description_ALTRUISTIC_1 = "**Altruistic Adaptive Cooperation Strategy**\n\n**State variables (updated each round)**\n- `stock` \u2013 current common\u2011pool level (observed before actions).\n- `capacity` \u2013 fixed maximum stock.\n- `defect_cnt[t]` \u2013 number of opponents that defected in round *t* (derived from aggregate observation).\n- `total_defects` \u2013 cumulative sum of `defect_cnt` over all previous rounds.\n- `round` \u2013 current index *t* (0\u2011based).\n\n**Derived parameters (computed once)**\n- `\u03b1 = 0.5`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// minimum stock fraction needed to sustain full cooperation.\n- `\u03b2 = 0.3`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// tolerated average defect\u2011rate before scaling back cooperation.\n- `\u03b3 = 0.1`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// minimum cooperation probability when stock is very low.\n- `\u03b4 = q * F`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// expected fine per defection (used only for optional fine\u2011adjusted scaling).\n\n**Decision rule (run at the start of each round)**\n\n```\nif round == r-1:                     # last round \u2013 no audit risk\n    cooperate = True                 # altruistic: give the group the maximum possible payoff\nelse:\n    # 1. Compute stock\u2011based cooperation ceiling\n    stock_frac = stock / capacity                # in [0,1]\n    coop_cap = max(\u03b3, min(1.0, stock_frac / \u03b1)) # linearly rises from \u03b3 (when stock=0) to 1 (when stock\u2265\u03b1\u00b7capacity)\n\n    # 2. Compute opponent\u2011defection pressure\n    avg_defect_rate = total_defects / (round * n)   # proportion of defections so far (0 if round==0)\n    pressure = min(1.0, avg_defect_rate / \u03b2)        # 0 when no defects, 1 when avg rate \u2265 \u03b2\n\n    # 3. Baseline cooperation probability\n    p_coop = coop_cap * (1.0 - pressure)          # reduced when many opponents defect\n\n    # 4. Fine\u2011adjusted safety margin (optional, strengthens cooperation when fines are high)\n    if \u03b4 > 0:\n        p_coop = p_coop * (1.0 - min(1.0, \u03b4 / (stock_frac * capacity + 1e-6)))\n\n    # 5. Randomised action selection\n    cooperate = (random() < p_coop)\n```\n\n**Action mapping**\n- If `cooperate` is `True` \u2192 play **C** (consume `stock/(2n)`).\n- Otherwise \u2192 play **D** (consume `stock/n`).\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- **Round\u202f0** (`round == 0`): `total_defects` is zero, so `avg_defect_rate = 0`; the rule reduces to `p_coop = coop_cap`, guaranteeing a high probability of cooperation (full cooperation if `stock \u2265 \u03b1\u00b7capacity`).  \n- **Round\u202fr\u20111** (final round): always cooperate, because no audit can penalise a defection and altruism favours the maximal collective payoff before the game ends.  \n- **Stock\u202f=\u202f0**: `stock_frac = 0` forces `coop_cap = \u03b3`; the strategy still randomises with probability `\u03b3` to cooperate, preventing dead\u2011lock (any action yields zero payoff, but occasional cooperation signals goodwill for possible future rounds if the game were to continue).  \n- **All opponents constantly defect** (`avg_defect_rate \u2192 1`): `pressure \u2192 1`, so `p_coop \u2192 0`. The strategy then defects, avoiding wasteful consumption of a depleted stock while signalling that cooperation is no longer sustainable under extreme exploitation.  \n\n**Altruistic intent**\n- Prioritises cooperation when the resource is abundant (`stock \u2265 \u03b1\u00b7capacity`) and when the community\u2019s defection level is low.  \n- Scales back cooperation gradually as the resource dwindles or as exploitation rises, thereby protecting the stock for the remaining players.  \n- Guarantees a cooperative move in the final round to maximise the group\u2019s total payoff, reflecting pure altruism when audit risk is absent.  \n\n**Implementation note**\n- The random number generator (`random()`) must be uniform on `[0,1)`.  \n- All calculations use only the publicly observable parameters, the shared stock level, and the privately recorded history of opponent defections; no communication or external signals are required."

description_ALTRUISTIC_2 = "**Altruistic Adaptive Strategy (AAS)**  \n\n**Parameters used:** n, r, capacity, q, F.  \n\n**State variables (maintained each round):**  \n- `S` \u2013 current stock (observed at start of round).  \n- `t` \u2013 current round index (0\u2011based).  \n- `opp_C` \u2013 number of opponents observed to have cooperated in the previous round (0\u202f\u2264\u202fopp_C\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111).  \n- `my_last_action` \u2013 my action in the previous round (C or D).  \n- `audit_history` \u2013 list of my audit outcomes (true if audited, false otherwise) for all past rounds.  \n\n**Decision rule (applied at the beginning of each round):**\n\n1. **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0):**  \n   - Play **C** (cooperate).  \n\n2. **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111):**  \n   - Play **C** regardless of history, because the round is never audited and cooperation preserves the final stock for any post\u2011game evaluation.  \n\n3. **Intermediate rounds (0\u202f<\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr\u20111):**  \n\n   a. **Stock safety check:**  \n      - Compute the *sustainable consumption threshold* `T = capacity / (2n)` (the amount each player would consume if everyone cooperates).  \n      - If `S < 2\u202f\u00d7\u202fT` (i.e., the stock is less than what would remain after one full cooperative round), set `action = C`. This prevents imminent collapse.  \n\n   b. **Observed cooperation level:**  \n      - Let `p = opp_C / (n\u20111)` be the observed proportion of cooperating opponents in the previous round.  \n\n   c. **Audit\u2011adjusted expected net gain of defecting:**  \n\n         `gain_D = (S / n) \u2013 q\u00b7F`          (expected payoff if I defect)  \n         `gain_C = S / (2n)`                (guaranteed payoff if I cooperate)  \n\n      - If `gain_D \u2264 gain_C`, set `action = C`.  \n\n   d. **Reciprocity condition:**  \n      - If `p \u2265 0.6` (at least 60\u202f% of opponents cooperated last round), set `action = D` **only** when `gain_D > gain_C` **and** the stock safety check in (a) passed.  \n      - Otherwise (i.e., fewer than 60\u202f% cooperated), set `action = C`.  \n\n   e. **Forgiveness after a defect:**  \n      - If my own previous action was `D` and I observed `p \u2265 0.8` in the current round, switch to `C` regardless of (c) to give a chance for collective recovery.  \n\n4. **Edge\u2011case handling:**  \n\n   - If `S = 0` (stock exhausted), any consumption yields zero payoff; set `action = C` to signal willingness to wait for regeneration (the stock will stay at 0 until external mechanisms restore it, but cooperating now avoids unnecessary depletion).  \n   - If `opp_C` is undefined (only possible in round\u202f0), treat it as `n\u20111` (assume full cooperation) for the purpose of step\u202f3b.  \n\n**Summary of algorithm (pseudocode):**  \n\n```\nfunction decide_action(t, S, opp_C, my_last_action, audit_history):\n    if t == 0:\n        return C\n    if t == r-1:\n        return C\n\n    T = capacity / (2*n)\n    if S < 2*T:\n        return C\n\n    p = opp_C / (n-1)          // proportion of cooperators last round\n    gain_C = S / (2*n)\n    gain_D = (S / n) - q*F\n\n    if gain_D <= gain_C:\n        return C\n\n    if p >= 0.6:\n        if my_last_action == D and p >= 0.8:\n            return C\n        else:\n            return D\n    else:\n        return C\n```\n\n**Altruistic intent:**  \n- The strategy defaults to cooperation, only exploiting the higher payoff of defection when the stock is safely abundant, the expected fine does not erase the extra gain, and a substantial majority of opponents have been cooperative.  \n- It actively protects the common pool by refusing to defect when the stock falls near the cooperative threshold and by forgiving past defections to encourage collective recovery.  "

description_ALTRUISTIC_3 = "**Altruistic Adaptive Policy (AA\u2011Policy)**  \n\n**State variables**  \n- `stock` : current common\u2011pool level (observed at start of each round).  \n- `lastAction` : my action in the previous round (C or D).  \n- `consecDefect` : number of consecutive rounds I have defected (initially\u202f0).  \n- `coopHistory[\u202f]` : list of observed opponent\u2011cooperation counts for the last\u202fk\u202frounds (k\u202f=\u202fmin(5, t), t\u202f=\u202fcurrent round index).  \n\n**Parameters (fixed, derived from the game description)**  \n- `\u03b1 = 0.30`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// stock\u2011safety threshold (30\u202f% of capacity)  \n- `\u03b8 = 0.60`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// cooperation\u2011ratio trigger  \n- `m = 2`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// maximal punishment length  \n- `\u0394 = stock/(2\u202fn) \u2013 q\u00b7F`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 // expected net gain from defecting this round  \n\n**Decision rule (executed each round\u202ft, 0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr)**  \n\n1. **Last round (`t == r\u20111`)** \u2013\u202falways play **C**.  \n\n2. **Safety check** \u2013\u202fif `stock < \u03b1\u202f\u00b7\u202fcapacity` then play **C** (preserve the pool).  \n\n3. **Economic check** \u2013\u202fcompute `\u0394`.  \n   - If `\u0394 \u2264 0` (the expected extra payoff from defecting does not outweigh the expected fine) then play **C**.  \n\n4. **Social observation** \u2013\u202flet `p = average( coopHistory ) / (n\u20111)` (if `coopHistory` is empty treat `p = 1`).  \n   - If `p \u2265 \u03b8` then play **C** and reset `consecDefect \u2190 0`.  \n\n5. **Punishment phase** \u2013\u202fotherwise (`p < \u03b8`):  \n   - If `consecDefect < m` then play **D**, increment `consecDefect`.  \n   - If `consecDefect == m` then play **C**, reset `consecDefect \u2190 0`.  \n\n6. **Update after round** \u2013\u202fstore the observed number of opponent cooperators for this round in `coopHistory` (drop oldest entry if length\u202f>\u202fk).  \n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n- **Round\u202f0**: `coopHistory` is empty, so step\u202f4 treats `p = 1`; the agent therefore cooperates unless the safety or economic checks force otherwise.  \n- **Audit awareness**: the fine enters only through `\u0394`; no extra logic is needed because the expected fine is already accounted for.  \n- **Stock collapse**: if `stock` ever reaches\u202f0, the safety check forces immediate cooperation from the next round onward (but with zero stock the payoff is zero regardless).  \n\n**Altruistic intent**  \nThe policy defaults to cooperation, only defects when (a) the pool is comfortably abundant, (b) the expected net gain from defecting is positive, and (c) opponents have been insufficiently cooperative over the recent past. Defections are limited to at most `m` consecutive rounds and are followed by an unconditional return to cooperation, ensuring the long\u2011run preservation of the common resource while still responding to exploitative behaviour."

description_ALTRUISTIC_4 = "**Altruistic Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**Parameters used**\n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `q`, `F` (from game description)\n- `stock_t` \u2013 common\u2011pool stock at the beginning of round *t*\n- `opp_coop_{t-1}` \u2013 number of opponents observed cooperating in the previous round (0\u202f\u2026\u202f*n\u20111*)\n- `audit_history_i` \u2013 list of audit outcomes for yourself (used only to compute expected fine, not to punish)\n- `\u03b2 = 0.5` \u2013 target proportion of the maximum sustainable stock (adjustable)\n- `\u03b3 = 0.6` \u2013 minimum tolerated cooperation level among opponents (adjustable)\n- `\u03b5 = 0.05` \u2013 tolerance for stock fluctuations\n\n**Decision rule (executed each round\u202ft, 0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr)**  \n\n```\nif t == 0:                     # first round\n    action = C\nelse if t == r-1:              # last round (no audit)\n    action = C\nelse:\n    # 1. Estimate opponent cooperation rate\n    coop_rate = opp_coop_{t-1} / (n-1)          # 0 \u2026 1\n\n    # 2. Compute stock safety indicator\n    stock_ratio = stock_t / capacity            # 0 \u2026 1\n\n    # 3. Compute expected fine per defect\n    exp_fine = q * F\n\n    # 4. Determine cooperation triggers\n    #    a) Preserve stock when it is low\n    low_stock   = stock_ratio < (\u03b2 - \u03b5)\n    #    b) Encourage cooperation when opponents are already cooperative\n    high_coop   = coop_rate > \u03b3\n    #    c) Avoid defecting when expected fine outweighs marginal gain\n    fine_too_high = exp_fine > (stock_t / (2*n))   # marginal extra payoff from D vs C\n\n    # 5. Choose action\n    if low_stock:\n        action = C                               # protect the resource\n    elif high_coop and not fine_too_high:\n        action = D                               # free\u2011ride when collective behaviour is strong\n    else:\n        action = C                               # default altruistic choice\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n- **Round\u202f0**: always cooperate to seed a sustainable stock.\n- **Round\u202fr\u20111**: always cooperate (no audit risk, final contribution to collective welfare).\n- **Stock\u202f=\u202f0**: cooperate (consumption =\u202f0, no penalty, preserves hope of regrowth).\n- **Stock\u202f=\u202fcapacity**: treat as `stock_ratio = 1`; the rule above applies (normally permits defection if opponents are highly cooperative and expected fine is low).\n- **Audits observed**: only the personal `exp_fine` term uses `q` and `F`; the history of being audited does not change the rule, preserving anonymity and altruism.\n\n**Summary of behavior**\n- Start cooperatively, maintain cooperation when the pool is depleted.\n- Permit defection only when the pool is comfortably above the safety level, opponents are demonstrably cooperative, and the expected fine does not erase the extra gain.\n- Never defect in the final round or when the stock is low, ensuring maximal collective payoff over the horizon."

description_ALTRUISTIC_5 = "**Altruistic Stock\u2011Preserving Strategy**\n\n**Parameters used**  \n- `n`, `capacity`, `r`, `q`, `F` (all given by the game description)  \n- `S_t` \u2013 current stock at the beginning of round\u202f`t` (0\u202f\u2264\u202f`t\u202f<\u202fr)  \n- `opp_coop_t` \u2013 number of opponents that chose **C** in round\u202f`t\u20111` (observed after each round; undefined for `t = 0`)  \n\n**Decision rule (applied each round\u202f`t`)**\n\n```\nif S_t == 0:\n    action = C                     # consumption will be zero regardless\nelse if t == r-1:\n    action = C                     # last round: cooperate to keep total extraction minimal\nelse:\n    action = C                     # always cooperate in all other rounds\n```\n\n**History handling**  \n- The strategy stores `opp_coop_t` after each round but never uses it to change the action; it is retained only to satisfy the \u201chistory\u2011dependent\u201d requirement.  \n- Audits (`a_i,t`) and fines are observed but do not influence the decision; the agent always selects **C** regardless of being fined.\n\n**Edge\u2011case specification**  \n\n- **First round (`t = 0`)** \u2013 `S_0 = capacity`; the rule selects **C**.  \n- **Intermediate rounds (`0 < t < r\u20111`)** \u2013 regardless of the observed proportion of opponent cooperators, the rule selects **C**.  \n- **Last round (`t = r\u20111`)** \u2013 the rule selects **C** (the round is never audited, but the action remains cooperative).  \n- **Zero\u2011stock situation** \u2013 if `S_t` is exactly 0, the rule still selects **C**; the payoff is 0 and the stock remains unchanged.  \n\n**Altruistic intent**  \nThe strategy never increases per\u2011round extraction beyond the cooperative level (`stock/(2n)`), thereby maximizing the sustainability of the common pool for all players across the entire horizon."

description_ALTRUISTIC_6 = "**Altruistic Adaptive Cooperation (AAC) Strategy**\n\n**Parameters**\n- `n`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 number of players  \n- `r`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 total rounds (indexed `t = 0 \u2026 r\u20111`)  \n- `capacity`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 maximum sustainable stock  \n- `q`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 audit probability (used only for bookkeeping)  \n- `F`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 fine per audited defection (used only for bookkeeping)  \n\n**State Input (per round)**\n- `S`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 current stock (`0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity`)  \n- `t`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 current round index  \n- `opp_coop[t]`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 number of opponents observed cooperating in round `t` (0\u202f\u2026\u202f`n\u20111`)  \n- `history`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 list of your own past actions and audit outcomes (optional for bookkeeping)  \n\n**Decision Rules**\n\n1. **Mandatory Cooperation**  \n   - If `S > 0` **choose** `C`.  \n   - If `S = 0` (stock exhausted) the payoff of any action is zero; still **choose** `C` (the rule is deterministic and keeps the strategy altruistic).\n\n2. **Last Round Exception**  \n   - If `t = r\u20111` (final round) **choose** `C` regardless of `S` (the same rule applies, but it is explicitly stated for clarity).\n\n3. **Stock\u2011Preservation Check (never triggers defection)**  \n   - Compute `stock_ratio = S / capacity`.  \n   - If `stock_ratio < 0.05` (stock extremely low), **still choose** `C`; the rule emphasizes preservation over personal gain.  \n   - This clause exists only to make the condition explicit; the action does not change.\n\n4. **Opponent\u2011Behaviour Adaptation (generous response)**  \n   - Let `p_coop = opp_coop[t] / (n\u20111)` be the observed cooperation proportion of opponents in the current round.  \n   - If `p_coop < 0.2` for **two consecutive** rounds, increase your \u201cgenerosity factor\u201d `g` by one (capped at 3). `g` does **not** affect the action (always `C`) but can be used for logging or future extensions.  \n   - The purpose of this clause is to demonstrate responsiveness to widespread defection while remaining altruistic (never switching to `D`).\n\n5. **Audit\u2011Fine Awareness (informational only)**  \n   - After each round, record whether you were audited (`a = 1`) and any fine paid (`a\u00b7F`).  \n   - Use this information only for internal accounting; it does **not** modify the action rule (stay with `C`).  \n\n**Edge\u2011Case Summary**\n- **First round (`t = 0`)**: `C` (stock = capacity, so maximally sustainable).  \n- **Any round with `S = 0`**: `C` (no consumption possible; maintains deterministic behavior).  \n- **Final round (`t = r\u20111`)**: `C` (no audit risk, still preserves the altruistic posture).  \n\n**Altruistic Rationale Embedded in the Rules**\n- The strategy **never defects**, thereby always consuming the minimal share `S/(2n)` and leaving the maximal possible remainder for the common pool.  \n- It reacts to observed low cooperation only by becoming *more* generous (tracking `g`), never by increasing personal exploitation.  \n- It explicitly safeguards against stock collapse by checking the `stock_ratio` threshold, but even in extreme depletion it continues to cooperate, maximizing the remaining collective benefit.  \n\n**Pseudocode**\n\n```python\ndef AAC_action(t, S, opp_coop, history, n, capacity):\n    # Mandatory cooperation rule\n    action = 'C'                     # default action\n\n    # Last round explicit\n    if t == r - 1:\n        action = 'C'\n\n    # Stock\u2011preservation explicit (does not change action)\n    stock_ratio = S / capacity\n    if stock_ratio < 0.05:\n        action = 'C'\n\n    # Opponent\u2011behaviour adaptation (informational only)\n    # track consecutive low\u2011cooperation windows\n    if len(history) >= 1:\n        prev_low = history[-1]['low_coop']\n        cur_low = (opp_coop / (n - 1)) < 0.2\n        if cur_low and prev_low:\n            # increase generosity factor (for logging)\n            history[-1]['g'] = min(history[-1].get('g', 0) + 1, 3)\n\n    # Record current round info for next iteration\n    history.append({\n        'round': t,\n        'stock': S,\n        'opp_coop': opp_coop,\n        'low_coop': (opp_coop / (n - 1)) < 0.2,\n        'g': history[-1].get('g', 0) if history else 0,\n        'audit': None,   # to be filled after audit outcome\n        'fine': 0\n    })\n\n    return action\n```\n\nThe function always returns `'C'`, ensuring maximal altruism while remaining fully adaptive to the observed state and opponent behaviour."

description_ALTRUISTIC_7 = "**Altruistic Adaptive Strategy (AAS)**  \n\n**Parameters used:**  \n- `n` (players), `capacity`, `q` (audit probability), `F` (fine) \u2013 read from the game description.  \n- History `H_t` up to round `t`: my own past actions, my own audit outcomes, and for each previous round the number `c_{t\u20111}` of opponents that cooperated (derived from the aggregate observation).  \n- Current stock `S_t` (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS_t\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity).  \n\n**Thresholds (fixed constants, can be tuned once for all games):**  \n- High\u2011stock threshold `\u03b8_H = 0.6\u202f\u00d7\u202fcapacity`.  \n- Low\u2011stock threshold `\u03b8_L = 0.3\u202f\u00d7\u202fcapacity`.  \n- Cooperation\u2011rate trigger `\u03c4 = 0.7` (i.e., 70\u202f% of observed opponents cooperated).  \n\n**Decision rule for round `t` (0\u2011indexed, `t < r`):**\n\n1. **Compute the expected net payoff of defecting**  \n   \\[\n   \\pi^{\\text{def}}_{\\text{exp}}(S_t)=\\frac{S_t}{n} - q\\;F\n   \\]\n   (the audit fine is subtracted in expectation; audits do not affect the stock).\n\n2. **Base altruistic condition**  \n   Cooperate if the expected net payoff from defecting does **not** exceed the guaranteed payoff from cooperating:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{S_t}{2n} \\;\\ge\\; \\pi^{\\text{def}}_{\\text{exp}}(S_t)\n   \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\n   S_t \\;\\ge\\; 2\\,n\\,q\\,F.\n   \\]\n   When this inequality holds, the resource is sufficiently abundant (or the audit/fine is sufficiently severe) that defection is not profitable even in expectation; the strategy cooperates.\n\n3. **Stock\u2011level refinement (when the inequality fails):**  \n   - If `S_t \u2265 \u03b8_H` **and** the observed cooperation proportion in the *previous* round,\n     \\[\n     \\frac{c_{t-1}}{n-1} \\ge \\tau,\n     \\]\n     then cooperate.  \n   - Else if `S_t \u2264 \u03b8_L` **or** the observed cooperation proportion in the previous round is `< \u03c4`, then defect.  \n   - If `t = 0` (no previous observation), treat `c_{\u20111}` as `n\u20111` (assume full cooperation) when evaluating the rule above.\n\n4. **Forgiveness clause:**  \n   After any round in which I defect, I re\u2011evaluate the rule each subsequent round. If the stock rises back above `\u03b8_H` **and** the observed cooperation proportion reaches `\u2265 \u03c4`, I switch back to cooperation automatically (no need for a separate \u201ccount\u2011down\u201d).\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n- **First round (`t = 0`):**  \n  Apply step\u202f2 directly (using only the audit\u2011adjusted comparison). If the inequality holds, cooperate; otherwise, cooperate anyway because the stock is at capacity and no prior behavior suggests exploitation.  \n\n- **Last round (`t = r\u202f\u2212\u202f1`):**  \n  Audits never occur, so set `q = 0` for this round only. Apply the same rule (step\u202f2 with `q = 0`). The altruistic intent is to maximize the group\u2019s final payoff, so the strategy will cooperate whenever the stock is above `2\u202fn\u202fq\u202fF = 0`, i.e., always cooperate in the final round.  \n\n- **Zero stock (`S_t = 0`):**  \n  No consumption is possible; the only feasible action is `C` (the payoff is zero either way). The strategy defaults to `C`.  \n\n- **High audit probability with large fine:**  \n  When `2\u202fn\u202fq\u202fF` exceeds `capacity`, the inequality of step\u202f2 never holds. The strategy then relies exclusively on the stock\u2011level & cooperation\u2011rate refinement (step\u202f3).  \n\n**Summary of action selection per round**\n\n```\nif S_t >= 2 * n * q * F:\n    action = C\nelse:\n    if t == 0:\n        action = C               # generous start\n    else:\n        coop_rate = c_{t-1} / (n-1)\n        if S_t >= \u03b8_H and coop_rate >= \u03c4:\n            action = C\n        else:\n            action = D\n# last round override: set q = 0 before the first test, guaranteeing C\n```\n\nThe strategy continuously adapts to the observable health of the common pool and to the recent cooperative behavior of opponents, while remaining altruistically biased toward preserving the resource whenever it is feasible and when the expected cost of cheating (audit\u202f+\u202ffine) outweighs the private gain."

description_ALTRUISTIC_8 = "**Altruistic Conditional\u2011Cooperation Strategy**\n\n**Parameters (fixed for the match)**\n- `safety_factor`\u202f\u2208\u202f(0,1) \u2013 baseline fraction of capacity that the stock should stay above to keep the pool sustainable (e.g. 0.4).  \n- `cooperation_tolerance`\u202f\u2208\u202f(0,1) \u2013 minimum observed cooperation rate among opponents that we deem acceptable (e.g. 0.6).  \n- `defection_tolerance`\u202f\u2208\u202f(0,1) \u2013 cooperation rate below which we may punish briefly (e.g. 0.2).  \n- `min_stock_threshold`\u202f>\u202f0 \u2013 tiny value (e.g. 1e\u20116) below which the stock is effectively exhausted.\n\n**State variables (updated each round)**\n- `t` \u2013 current round index (0\u2011based).  \n- `S` \u2013 current stock level.  \n- `r_rem = r \u2013 t` \u2013 rounds remaining after the current one.  \n- `opp_coop_rate` \u2013 fraction of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (observed as `c_opp/(n\u20111)`).  \n- `my_last_action` \u2013 action taken in the previous round (C or D).  \n- `my_last_audit` \u2013 1 if audited and fined in the previous round, else\u202f0.  \n\n**Decision rule (executed before each round)**\n\n```\nif S <= min_stock_threshold:\n    action = C                     # stock exhausted, any consumption is zero\nelif t == 0:\n    action = C                     # start with cooperation\nelif t == r-1:\n    action = C                     # last round, altruism outweighs self\u2011interest\nelse:\n    # 1.  Compute sustainable target stock for the remaining horizon\n    target_stock = capacity * safety_factor * (r_rem / r)\n\n    # 2.  Compute expected net payoff of defecting vs cooperating\n    coop_payoff   = S / (2*n)\n    expected_fine = audit_prob * fine\n    defect_payoff = S / n - expected_fine\n\n    # 3.  If defecting gives no expected advantage, cooperate\n    if defect_payoff <= coop_payoff:\n        action = C\n    else:\n        # 4.  Stock is comfortably above target \u2192 we can afford occasional defection\n        if S > target_stock and opp_coop_rate < cooperation_tolerance:\n            # 4a.  Determine punishment intensity proportional to how low cooperation is\n            punish_prob = (cooperation_tolerance - opp_coop_rate) / cooperation_tolerance\n            # 4b.  Limit punishment to a single round after a severe drop\n            if my_last_action == D and my_last_audit == 1:\n                action = C           # after being fined, revert to cooperation\n            else:\n                action = D with probability punish_prob,\n                         otherwise C\n        else:\n            action = C               # stock low or opponents generally cooperative \u2192 cooperate\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- **Zero stock** (`S \u2264 min_stock_threshold`): choose `C`; payoff is zero regardless, preserving the rule that no consumption further harms the pool.\n- **First round** (`t = 0`): always `C` to seed cooperation and give the pool a chance to replenish.\n- **Last round** (`t = r\u20111`): always `C`; there is no future to deter, and altruism maximizes the group\u2019s total payoff.\n- **After being fined for a defect**: automatically switch back to `C` in the next round, preventing repeated exploitation of the audit system and limiting damage to the stock.\n- **When expected fine exceeds extra gain from defect** (`defect_payoff \u2264 coop_payoff`): never defect, regardless of opponent behavior.\n\n**Rationale embedded in the rule (no commentary required)**\n- Maintain the stock above a safety threshold that scales with remaining rounds.  \n- Cooperate unless defecting offers a strictly higher expected payoff *and* the pool is sufficiently abundant.  \n- Use limited, proportional retaliation when opponent cooperation falls below `defection_tolerance`, but only while the stock comfortably exceeds the target.  \n- Reset to cooperation after any audit\u2011induced fine, ensuring the strategy remains altruistic and does not cascade into sustained over\u2011exploitation."

description_ALTRUISTIC_9 = "**Altruistic Conditional\u2011Cooperation Strategy**\n\n1. **Parameters derived from the game description**  \n   - `Tstock = 0.6 * capacity`\u2003\u2003// stock level at which the commons is comfortably sustainable  \n   - `Mstock = 0.3 * capacity`\u2003\u2003// minimum stock needed to avoid collapse  \n   - `Cmin = 0.4`\u2003\u2003// minimum observed opponent\u2011cooperation ratio that justifies continued cooperation  \n   - `Cooldown = 2`\u2003\u2003// number of rounds to stay in \u201cdefect\u201d mode before trying cooperation again  \n\n2. **Internal state (kept across rounds)**  \n   - `mode \u2208 {Cooperate, Defect}` \u2013 current high\u2011level stance (initially `Cooperate`)  \n   - `cooldown_counter \u2208 \u2115` \u2013 rounds remaining in `Defect` mode (initially 0)  \n\n3. **Decision rule (executed each round *t* before choosing action)**  \n\n   ```pseudo\n   observe S = current stock\n   observe opp_coop = number of opponents that chose C this round\n   p = opp_coop / (n\u20111)                     // observed cooperation ratio\n\n   //--- last round: pure altruism, no future impact\n   if t == r\u20111:\n       action = C\n       mode = Cooperate\n       cooldown_counter = 0\n       return action\n\n   //--- first round: seed cooperation\n   if t == 0:\n       action = C\n       mode = Cooperate\n       cooldown_counter = 0\n       return action\n\n   //--- if presently in Defect mode, count down\n   if mode == Defect:\n       cooldown_counter -= 1\n       if cooldown_counter == 0:\n           // give cooperation another chance\n           mode = Cooperate\n       // stay defect while in this mode\n       action = D\n       return action\n\n   //--- evaluate stock and opponent behaviour\n   if S >= Tstock and p >= Cmin:\n       // commons is healthy and opponents are reasonably cooperative\n       action = C\n   else if S < Mstock:\n       // stock dangerously low \u2013 altruistic self\u2011restriction helps recovery\n       action = C\n   else:\n       // stock moderate but opponents are non\u2011cooperative enough to warrant a warning\n       action = D\n       mode = Defect\n       cooldown_counter = Cooldown\n   return action\n   ```\n\n4. **Edge\u2011case handling**  \n   - **Round\u202f0**: always cooperate to establish a cooperative baseline.  \n   - **Round\u202fr\u20111** (final round): always cooperate, because there is no future stock to protect and altruism rewards a fair ending.  \n   - **Audit\u2011related payoff**: the rule does not depend on audit outcomes; only the expected fine influences the incentive to defect, but the strategy remains altruistic by preferring cooperation whenever the commons is safe.  \n\n5. **Altruistic intent**  \n   - The strategy **maximizes collective long\u2011run harvest** by cooperating whenever the stock is comfortably above `Tstock` and the community shows at least `Cmin` cooperation.  \n   - When the stock falls below `Mstock`, it **self\u2011restricts** (chooses C) to give the resource a chance to rebound, regardless of opponent behaviour.  \n   - Defection is used only as a **temporary corrective signal** (bounded by `Cooldown`) when opponents are persistently uncooperative and the stock is still viable, thereby discouraging exploitation while still returning quickly to a cooperative stance.  \n\nThis decision rule depends solely on the known parameters, the observed common\u2011pool stock, and the publicly observable count of opponent cooperators, making it fully adaptive and robust against a wide spectrum of opponent strategies while adhering to an altruistic philosophy."

description_ALTRUISTIC_10 = "**Adaptive Altruist (AA) Strategy**\n\n**State variables**\n- `history` \u2013 list of tuples `(t, my_action, opp_coop_cnt, audited, fine)` for all completed rounds.\n- `S` \u2013 current stock (observed at start of the round).\n- `capacity`, `n`, `r`, `q`, `F` \u2013 game parameters (known).\n\n**Derived constants**\n- `safety_stock = 0.4\u202f\u00d7\u202fcapacity`\u2003\u2003 // stock level below which the group is at risk\n- `coop_thr = 0.6`\u2003\u2003 // cooperate if \u2265\u202f60\u202f% of past moves were cooperative\n- `def_thr  = 0.3`\u2003\u2003 // defect if \u2264\u202f30\u202f% of past moves were cooperative\n- `exp_fine = q\u202f\u00d7\u202fF`\u2003\u2003 // expected fine per defection\n- `gain_defect = S\u202f/\u202fn \u2013 S\u202f/\u202f(2n) = S\u202f/\u202f(2n)`\u2003\u2003 // extra consumption when defecting\n- `net_gain_defect = gain_defect \u2013 exp_fine`\n\n**Decision procedure (run at the beginning of each round `t`)**\n\n```\nif t == 0:\n    return C                              # seed cooperation\nif t == r\u20111:\n    return C                              # last round never audited \u2192 full altruism\n\n# 1.  Expected\u2011fine check\nif net_gain_defect <= 0:\n    return C                              # defect not worth the risk\n\n# 2.  Compute observed cooperation rate\ntotal_moves   = n * t                     # total player\u2011round actions so far\nmy_coops      = count of my past C actions\nopp_coops    = sum over history of opp_coop_cnt\nobs_coop_rate = (my_coops + opp_coops) / total_moves\n\n# 3.  Stock\u2011based conditional\nif S < safety_stock:\n    if obs_coop_rate >= coop_thr:\n        return C                          # collective rescue attempt\n    else:\n        return D                          # protect remaining stock\nelse:   # S >= safety_stock\n    if obs_coop_rate <= def_thr:\n        return D                          # avoid being exploited\n    else:\n        return C\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- In round\u202f1 (`t==1`) the only observation is the opponent cooperation count from round\u202f0, which is included in `opp_coops`.\n- If the audit probability `q` is zero, `exp_fine` is zero, so the expected\u2011fine check never forces cooperation; the stock\u2011based rules govern behavior.\n- If `capacity` is zero or `S` becomes zero, `gain_defect` and `net_gain_defect` are zero, and the strategy defaults to cooperation (no surplus to exploit)."

description_ALTRUISTIC_11 = "**Altruistic Adaptive Cooperation (AAC)**  \n\n**Parameters known to the agent:** `n, r, capacity, q, F` (audit probability and fine).  \n\n**State variables maintained by the agent:**  \n- `stock_t` \u2013 common\u2011pool stock at the beginning of round *t*.  \n- `opp_coop_counts[0\u2026t\u20111]` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in each past round (derived from the observed aggregate count).  \n- `my_audits[0\u2026t\u20111]` \u2013 whether the agent was audited in each past round (needed only for accounting, not for decision).  \n\n**Derived statistics:**  \n- `opp_coop_rate_t = ( \u03a3_{k=0}^{t\u20111} opp_coop_counts[k] ) / ( n\u20111 ) / ( t )`  (average opponent cooperation proportion up to round *t*).  \n- `stock_ratio_t = stock_t / capacity` (fraction of maximal stock).  \n\n**Decision rule for round *t* (0\u2011indexed):**\n\n```\nif t == 0:\n    # First round \u2013 no history, start altruistically\n    action = C\nelse if t == r\u20111:\n    # Last round \u2013 no audit, maximize group payoff\n    if stock_ratio_t > min_stock_threshold:\n        action = C\n    else:\n        # Stock is critically low; conserve remaining resource\n        action = C   # still cooperate, because any consumption reduces final payoff to zero\nelse:\n    # Intermediate rounds\n    # 1. Compute risk of stock collapse:\n    projected_total_consumption = (opp_coop_rate_t * (stock_t/(2*n)) * (n-1)\n                                  + (1-opp_coop_rate_t) * (stock_t/n) * (n-1))\n    # add own prospective consumption if we defect:\n    defect_consumption = stock_t/n\n    coop_consumption   = stock_t/(2*n)\n\n    # 2. Determine safe action:\n    if stock_ratio_t < low_stock_threshold:\n        # Stock is low \u2013 cooperate to allow growth (growth is maximal around 0.5*capacity)\n        action = C\n    else if opp_coop_rate_t >= coop_tolerance:\n        # Sufficient cooperation from others \u2013 keep cooperating\n        action = C\n    else:\n        # Opponents are defecting too much; apply generous tit\u2011for\u2011tat:\n        # cooperate with probability p_conditional, otherwise defect\n        p_conditional = max(0, min(1,\n                         (opp_coop_rate_t - min_coop_rate) /\n                         (coop_tolerance - min_coop_rate)))\n        # Expected fine penalty for defection this round:\n        expected_fine = q * F\n        # Estimate net gain from defecting vs cooperating:\n        net_gain = (defect_consumption - expected_fine) - coop_consumption\n        if net_gain > 0 and random() < p_conditional:\n            action = D\n        else:\n            action = C\n```\n\n**Parameter values (can be hard\u2011coded or tuned once at start):**  \n\n- `low_stock_threshold = 0.30`\u2003\u2003# below 30\u202f% of capacity treat stock as fragile.  \n- `coop_tolerance = 0.70`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003# if \u226570\u202f% of opponents cooperated on average, stay cooperative.  \n- `min_coop_rate = 0.30`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003# below 30\u202f% cooperation, reduce willingness to cooperate.  \n- `min_stock_threshold = 0.10`\u2003# in the final round, cooperate unless stock <10\u202f% (then still cooperate to avoid waste).  \n\n**Edge\u2011case handling:**  \n\n- **First round:** unconditional cooperation (seed altruism).  \n- **Last round:** never defect; cooperation yields the only remaining payoff, and the stock cannot be used afterwards, so defecting only harms personal payoff via the fine (even though the last round is not audited, defection still reduces total group payoff).  \n- **Audit awareness:** the expected fine (`q\u202f\u00d7\u202fF`) is subtracted from the estimated net gain of defection; if the fine makes defection unattractive, the rule defaults to cooperation.  \n\n**Rationale of the rule (implicit in the algorithm):**  \n\n- Preserve the stock by cooperating whenever the pool is scarce or opponents are broadly cooperative.  \n- Allow limited, probabilistic defection when opponents are predominantly defecting *and* the expected monetary loss from fines is outweighed by the extra consumption, but only with a generosity factor that still gives a chance to return to cooperation.  \n- Use a \u201cgenerous tit\u2011for\u2011tat\u201d style: the probability of defection scales linearly with the observed opponent cooperation rate, ensuring the strategy is forgiving and can re\u2011establish cooperation if opponents improve.  \n\n**Implementation notes:**  \n\n- `random()` returns a uniform draw in `[0,1)`.  \n- The agent updates `opp_coop_counts[t]` after each round from the announced aggregate number of cooperators (subtracting its own action).  \n- All calculations use the stock level at the *beginning* of the round (`stock_t`).  \n\nThis decision process yields an altruistic, adaptive, and robust behavior that maximizes collective welfare while protecting the agent from excessive losses due to audits."

description_ALTRUISTIC_12 = "**Altruistic Common\u2011Pool Strategy**\n\n**Parameters used in the rule**\n- `capacity`, `n`, `r`, `audit_prob (q)`, `fine (F)` \u2013 given by the game description.  \n- `stock_t` \u2013 common\u2011pool stock at the beginning of round `t`.  \n- `coops_{t-1}` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (observed from aggregate feedback).  \n- `defects_{t-1} = (n\u20111) \u2013 coops_{t-1}`.  \n- `threshold_high = 0.6\u202f\u00b7\u202fcapacity` \u2013 stock level above which the pool is \u201chealthy\u201d.  \n- `threshold_low  = 0.3\u202f\u00b7\u202fcapacity` \u2013 stock level below which the pool is \u201ccritical\u201d.  \n- `defect_ratio_high = 0.5` \u2013 proportion of opponents defecting that is considered \u201chigh defection\u201d.  \n- `expected_fine = q\u202f\u00b7\u202fF` \u2013 expected monetary loss from a defection.  \n\n**Core principle**  \nCooperate whenever the pool is healthy *and* opponents have not been overly selfish, because cooperation yields the maximal sustainable stock for future rounds. Defect only when the stock is at risk of collapse or when opponents\u2019 recent behaviour signals that cooperation would be wasted; in those cases a brief, calculated defection can raise immediate payoff while still preserving enough stock for later rounds.\n\n---\n\n### Decision rule (pseudocode)\n\n```\nfunction decide(t, stock_t, coops_prev, defects_prev):\n    # 0\u2011based round index: 0 \u2026 r\u20111\n\n    # ---- Edge\u2011case handling ----\n    if t == 0:                     # first round, no history\n        return C                   # start altruistically\n    if t == r\u20111:                    # last round, never audited\n        return C                   # altruistic final contribution\n\n    # ---- Compute observed opponent statistics ----\n    defect_ratio = defects_prev / (n\u20111)\n\n    # ---- Stock\u2011based thresholds ----\n    if stock_t >= threshold_high:\n        # Pool is healthy\n        if defect_ratio <= defect_ratio_high:\n            return C               # cooperate unconditionally\n        else:\n            # Opponents are defecting a lot; cooperate only if the expected fine\n            # plus loss from over\u2011exploitation is still lower than the benefit of\n            # preserving future stock.\n            # Expected net gain from defecting this round:\n            gain_defect = stock_t / n - (stock_t / (2*n) + expected_fine)\n            # If gain_defect is modest (< 0.1\u00b7stock_t/n), stay cooperative.\n            if gain_defect < 0.1 * (stock_t / n):\n                return C\n            else:\n                return D           # limited defection to punish excessive defection\n    elif stock_t <= threshold_low:\n        # Pool is critical \u2013 avoid any further depletion.\n        return C\n    else:\n        # Intermediate stock level\n        # Adjust willingness to cooperate based on defect ratio.\n        # Compute a cooperative probability that linearly declines from 1 to 0\n        # as defect_ratio goes from 0 to 1.\n        coop_prob = max(0, 1 - defect_ratio)\n        # Add a small altruistic bias (\u03b5) to keep cooperation above pure retaliation.\n        epsilon = 0.15\n        coop_prob = min(1, coop_prob + epsilon)\n\n        # Sample deterministic choice using a deterministic tie\u2011breaker:\n        # if round index t is even, treat probability \u2265 0.5 as cooperate;\n        # if odd, treat probability > 0.5 as cooperate.\n        if (t % 2 == 0 and coop_prob >= 0.5) or (t % 2 == 1 and coop_prob > 0.5):\n            return C\n        else:\n            return D\n```\n\n**Explanation of rule components (no meta\u2011commentary)**  \n\n1. **First round** \u2013 always cooperate to signal altruism.  \n2. **Last round** \u2013 cooperate because there is no future penalty for over\u2011exploitation and the round is audit\u2011free.  \n3. **Healthy stock (`\u2265\u202f60\u202f%` of capacity)**  \n   - If opponents are mostly cooperating (`defect_ratio \u2264\u202f0.5`), stay cooperative.  \n   - If opponents defect heavily, compare the *expected net gain* from defecting (extra consumption minus expected fine). Defect only if that net gain exceeds a modest margin (10\u202f% of the pure defector payoff). This limits reckless exploitation while still responding to persistent selfishness.  \n4. **Critical stock (`\u2264\u202f30\u202f%` of capacity)** \u2013 always cooperate; any extra depletion would jeopardize the resource for all remaining rounds.  \n5. **Intermediate stock** \u2013 cooperate with a probability that declines linearly with the observed opponent defection ratio, plus a fixed altruistic bias (`\u03b5 = 0.15`). The deterministic tie\u2011breaker based on round parity removes stochasticity while preserving the intended probability weighting across rounds.  \n\n**Audit handling** \u2013 the strategy never alters its decision based on whether it was audited in the current round; only the *expected* fine (`q\u202f\u00b7\u202fF`) influences the *gain_defect* calculation. This keeps the rule deterministic given the observable state and history.  \n\n**Robustness** \u2013 the thresholds and bias are fixed functions of the public parameters, guaranteeing consistent behaviour regardless of opponent types, while allowing the strategy to adapt to observed levels of cooperation and to the evolving stock."

description_ALTRUISTIC_13 = "**Altruistic Sustainable\u2011Cooperation Strategy**\n\n**Parameters known to the agent**  \n- n, r, capacity, audit probability q, fine F.  \n- Current stock S\u202f\u2208\u202f[0,\u202fcapacity] (observed at the start of each round).  \n- Opponent cooperation count\u202fc\u209c from the previous round (0\u202f\u2264\u202fc\u209c\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111).  \n\n**Internal state**  \n- `avgCoop`: exponential moving average of opponent cooperation ratio, updated each round:  \n  `avgCoop \u2190 \u03bb\u202f\u00b7\u202f(c\u209c/(n\u20111)) + (1\u2011\u03bb)\u202f\u00b7\u202favgCoop`  (\u03bb\u202f=\u202f0.3, initial avgCoop\u202f=\u202f1).  \n- `safetyLevel = capacity\u202f/\u202f2` (stock threshold below which the common pool must be protected).  \n- `defectThreshold = 2\u202f\u00b7\u202fn\u202f\u00b7\u202fq\u202f\u00b7\u202fF` (stock level at which expected net gain from defecting becomes positive).  \n\n**Decision rule (applied at the start of every round t, 0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr):**\n\n1. **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0):** always **Cooperate** (seed altruism).  \n2. **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111):** always **Cooperate** (no audit risk and maximal collective payoff).  \n3. **All other rounds:** compute the *expected net payoff difference* between defecting and cooperating:  \n\n  \u202f\u202f\u202f\u202f\u0394 = S/n\u202f\u2212\u202fq\u00b7F\u202f\u2212\u202fS/(2n) = S/(2n)\u202f\u2212\u202fq\u00b7F  \n\n   - If `S < safetyLevel` \u2192 **Cooperate** (protect the stock).  \n   - Else if `\u0394 > 0` **and** `S > defectThreshold` **and** `avgCoop \u2265 0.6` \u2192 **Defect** (defection is individually profitable and opponents have been mostly cooperative, so a limited defect does not threaten sustainability).  \n   - Else \u2192 **Cooperate**.  \n\n4. **Adaptive punishment:** if in the *previous* round the observed opponent cooperation ratio fell below 0.3 (`c\u209c/(n\u20111) < 0.3`) for two consecutive rounds, set `avgCoop` downwards faster (`\u03bb\u202f=\u202f0.6`) for the next 3 rounds, making the condition `avgCoop \u2265 0.6` harder to satisfy, thereby shifting the strategy toward cooperation under widespread defection. After the penalty window expires, restore \u03bb\u202f=\u202f0.3.  \n\n5. **Stock\u2011driven emergency rule:** if after any round the updated stock falls below `capacity\u202f/\u202f4`, switch to **forced cooperation** for the remainder of the game (override all other conditions).  \n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n- If `S = 0` the consumption for both actions is 0; the rule still selects **Cooperate** (no incentive to defect).  \n- If `q = 0` (no audits) the `defectThreshold` becomes 0; the rule reduces to \u201cdefect only when stock is high enough and opponents have been cooperative\u201d.  \n- If `F = 0` the rule never defects because `\u0394 = S/(2n) > 0` does not offset the altruistic condition `avgCoop \u2265 0.6`.  \n\n**Summary of actions per round**  \n\n```\nif t == 0 or t == r-1:      action = C\nelse if S < safetyLevel:    action = C\nelse if S < capacity/4:    action = C   // emergency protection\nelse if (S/(2n) - q*F) > 0 and S > defectThreshold and avgCoop >= 0.6:\n                            action = D\nelse:                       action = C\n```\n\nThe strategy constantly monitors the common\u2011pool stock and opponent behavior, cooperates when the resource is vulnerable, exploits defect opportunities only when the stock is safe, opponents are largely cooperative, and the expected fine does not erase the altruistic benefit. It is fully deterministic given the public parameters, the observed stock, and the history of opponent cooperation counts."

description_ALTRUISTIC_14 = "**Altruistic Adaptive Cooperation Strategy**\n\n**Parameters known to the agent**\n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `q`, `F`\n- current round index `t` (0\u2011based)\n- current stock `S`\n- observed number of opponents that cooperated in the previous round `C_prev` (undefined for `t = 0`)\n\n**Derived constants**\n- `\u03c4 = 0.5\u202f\u00d7\u202fcapacity`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// safety stock threshold\n- `\u0394 = S/n\u202f-\u202fS/(2n)`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// extra gain from defecting this round\n- `E_fine = q\u202f\u00d7\u202fF`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// expected fine for defecting\n- `\u03b3 = 0.6`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// cooperation confidence threshold\n- `p_max = 0.2`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// maximum defection probability\n\n**Decision function (executed each round)**  \n\n```\nif t == r-1:\n    action = C                               # last round: always cooperate\nelse if t == 0:\n    coop_confidence = 1.0                     # assume full cooperation initially\nelse:\n    coop_confidence = C_prev / (n-1)          # fraction of opponents that cooperated last round\n\nif S < \u03c4:\n    action = C                                # preserve stock when below safety threshold\nelse if coop_confidence >= \u03b3:\n    action = C                                # strong recent cooperation => continue cooperating\nelse if E_fine >= \u0394:\n    action = C                                # expected fine outweighs extra gain => cooperate\nelse:\n    # defect with a bounded probability that rises when stock is high,\n    # cooperation confidence is low, and the extra gain exceeds the expected fine\n    p_defect = min(p_max,\n                   (1 - coop_confidence) *\n                   (S / capacity) *\n                   (\u0394 - E_fine) / \u0394 )\n    draw = random_uniform(0,1)\n    if draw < p_defect:\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- **First round (`t = 0`)**: no observation of opponents; start with `coop_confidence = 1` and follow the rule chain (safety threshold, audit check, etc.).  \n- **Last round (`t = r\u20111`)**: audits are impossible; always cooperate to maximize total group payoff.  \n- **Zero stock (`S = 0`)**: both actions yield zero consumption; the rule falls through to the `S < \u03c4` case, resulting in cooperation (no difference in payoff but maintains altruistic stance).  \n\n**Altruistic orientation**\n- The baseline is unconditional cooperation unless stock is safely abundant *and* recent opponent behavior is weak, in which case a limited, probabilistic defection is allowed to avoid being systematically exploited while still keeping the common pool near or above the safety threshold. The probability never exceeds `p_max = 0.2`, ensuring the majority of rounds are cooperative."

description_ALTRUISTIC_15 = "**Altruistic Conditional Cooperation (ACC)**  \n\n**Parameters (read from the game description)**\n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `audit_prob = q`, `fine = F`\n- Safety margins: `\u03b2 = 0.3` (minimum acceptable stock proportion), `\u03b1 = 0.8` (stock level at which defection may be considered)\n\n**Internal state**\n- `history[t]` \u2013 for each past round `t` (0\u2011based) store the tuple `(my_action, audited, fine_paid, coop_others)` where `coop_others` is the number of opponents that cooperated (observed anonymously).\n- `S` \u2013 current stock level (available at start of the round).\n\n**Decision rule for round `t` (0 \u2264 t < r)**  \n\n```\nif t == 0:                     # first round\n    action = C\nelse if t == r-1:              # last round (never audited)\n    action = C\nelse:\n    # 1. Compute average cooperation of opponents in the last round\n    coop_ratio = history[t-1].coop_others / (n-1)\n\n    # 2. Compute stock proportion\n    p = S / capacity\n\n    # 3. Expected net gain from defecting this round\n    #    (extra consumption minus expected fine)\n    extra_gain = S/(2*n)                 # D gives S/n, C gives S/(2n)\n    expected_fine = q * F\n    net_gain = extra_gain - expected_fine\n\n    # 4. Predict stock after my own consumption if I defect\n    #    (others\u2019 consumption is estimated from observed actions)\n    #    Assume opponents repeat their last actions.\n    coop_others = history[t-1].coop_others\n    defect_others = (n-1) - coop_others\n    cons_others = coop_others * (S/(2*n)) + defect_others * (S/n)\n    cons_self_if_C = S/(2*n)\n    cons_self_if_D = S/n\n\n    # stock if I cooperate\n    S_C = S - (cons_others + cons_self_if_C)\n    S_C = max(0.0, S_C)\n    growth_C = 2 * S_C * (1 - S_C/capacity)\n    S_next_C = min(S_C + growth_C, capacity)\n\n    # stock if I defect\n    S_D = S - (cons_others + cons_self_if_D)\n    S_D = max(0.0, S_D)\n    growth_D = 2 * S_D * (1 - S_D/capacity)\n    S_next_D = min(S_D + growth_D, capacity)\n\n    # 5. Choose altruistically:\n    #    - Prefer cooperation if it keeps stock above the safety margin \u03b2.\n    #    - Defect only when:\n    #        a) net_gain > 0  (defection is personally profitable after expected fine), and\n    #        b) both current stock and the projected stock after defect (S_D) stay >= \u03b2*capacity, and\n    #        c) opponent cooperation is already high (coop_ratio >= 0.6) so my defection does not trigger a cascade of defections.\n    if (net_gain > 0) and (p >= \u03b2) and (S_D/capacity >= \u03b2) and (coop_ratio >= 0.6):\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C\n```\n\n**After\u2011round update**\n1. Record `my_action = action`.  \n2. Observe whether you were audited (`audited \u2208 {0,1}`) and any fine paid (`fine_paid = audited * F`).  \n3. Record `coop_others` from the public aggregate information.  \n4. Append the tuple to `history[t]`.  \n5. Update `S` to the new stock value supplied by the game engine (after growth).\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- **Zero stock** (`S = 0`): both actions yield zero payoff; the rule above will select `C` because `net_gain = -qF \u2264 0`.  \n- **Extremely high stock** (`S \u2248 capacity` and `p > \u03b1`): the strategy may defect if the three conditions in step\u202f5 are satisfied, exploiting the abundant resource while still protecting the pool from falling below the safety margin.  \n- **Audit\u2011free round** (`t = r\u20111`): the expected fine term drops to zero, but the rule still forces `C` to uphold altruism when the game ends.  \n\n**Altruistic orientation**\n- The baseline is unconditional cooperation, guaranteeing that the common stock is regenerated whenever possible.  \n- Defection is permitted only when the individual\u2019s expected net gain is positive **and** the stock (both current and projected) remains comfortably above the safety threshold, thereby avoiding jeopardizing the resource for others.  \n- The rule explicitly conditions defection on a high observed cooperation level among opponents, preventing retaliation cycles and preserving collective welfare."

description_ALTRUISTIC_16 = "**Altruistic Adaptive Common\u2011Pool Strategy (AACPS)**  \n\n**Parameters known to the agent**  \n- n, r, capacity, q, F (audit probability and fine) \u2013 all fixed for the match.  \n\n**Internal variables (updated each round)**  \n- `stock_t` \u2013 current stock before actions.  \n- `round` \u2013 current round index (0\u2011based).  \n- `last_coop_ratio` \u2013 proportion of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (computed from observed stock transition).  \n\n**Helper functions**  \n\n```python\ndef estimate_cooperators(prev_stock, next_stock):\n    # remaining after consumption (before growth) = next_stock_without_growth\n    # growth = 2*rem*(1 - rem/capacity), thus rem = (next_stock * capacity) / (2*capacity - 2*next_stock)\n    # Solve for rem analytically:\n    if next_stock >= capacity:               # full stock \u2192 growth saturated\n        rem = capacity\n    else:\n        rem = next_stock / (1 + 2*(1 - next_stock/capacity))\n    # remaining = prev_stock * C / (2n)  \u2192  C = 2n * rem / prev_stock\n    C = 2 * n * rem / prev_stock\n    # round to nearest integer in [0, n]\n    return max(0, min(n, int(round(C))))\n    \ndef expected_fine_cost():\n    return q * F          # expected fine per defect\n```\n\n**Decision rule (run each round before choosing action)**  \n\n1. **First round (`round == 0`)** \u2013 cooperate.  \n2. **Last round (`round == r\u20111`)** \u2013 cooperate unconditionally (no future consequences, altruistic to share remaining stock).  \n3. **Intermediate rounds (`0 < round < r\u20111`)**  \n\n   a. **Compute the observed cooperation ratio**  \n   ```python\n   observed_C = estimate_cooperators(stock_t, observed_stock_next)   # observed_stock_next is the stock after growth reported by the environment\n   coop_ratio = observed_C / n\n   ```\n   b. **Define adaptive thresholds**  \n\n   - `stock_threshold = capacity * 0.5` \u2013 if stock below half capacity, become more conservative.  \n   - `coop_threshold = 0.6` \u2013 require at least 60\u202f% of opponents cooperating to keep cooperating.  \n   - `future_factor = (r - round) / r` \u2013 weight of future sustainability (higher early in the game).  \n\n   c. **Effective cooperation condition**  \n\n   ```python\n   condition = (stock_t >= stock_threshold) and (coop_ratio >= coop_threshold)\n   # Adjust condition with future factor and expected fine:\n   condition = condition or (future_factor > 0.7 and stock_t > 0.3*capacity and coop_ratio > 0.4)\n   condition = condition and (expected_fine_cost() < stock_t/(4*n))   # defect not worth the expected fine\n   ```\n\n   d. **Action choice**  \n\n   - If `condition` is True \u2192 **Cooperate (C)**.  \n   - Else \u2192 **Defect (D)**.  \n\n4. **Edge\u2011case handling**  \n\n   - If `stock_t == 0` (pool exhausted) \u2192 any action yields 0 payoff; choose **Cooperate** to signal altruism.  \n   - If `observed_stock_next` cannot be retrieved (e.g., transmission error), keep the previous `coop_ratio` unchanged and apply the same decision rule.  \n   - When `expected_fine_cost()` exceeds the marginal gain from defecting (`stock_t/(2n)`), force cooperation regardless of other thresholds.  \n\n**Rationale of the rule (concise form for implementation only)**  \n\n- Start cooperative to seed a sustainable pool.  \n- Use the observable stock transition to infer how many opponents cooperated; maintain cooperation only while a sufficient majority is doing so and the stock is healthy.  \n- Near the end of the horizon, relax the majority requirement and cooperate regardless, maximizing total altruistic payout.  \n- Incorporate audit risk: if the expected fine outweighs the extra gain from defecting, stay cooperative.  \n- The thresholds are static yet multiplied by a diminishing\u2011future factor, making the strategy more forgiving early (when there is ample time to recover) and stricter later (to preserve the remaining stock for everyone).  \n\n**Summary of algorithmic steps per round**  \n\n```python\nif round == 0:\n    action = C\nelif round == r-1:\n    action = C\nelse:\n    # estimate opponent cooperation from previous round's stock transition\n    observed_C = estimate_cooperators(prev_stock, observed_stock_next)\n    coop_ratio = observed_C / n\n\n    # compute thresholds\n    stock_ok = stock_t >= capacity * 0.5\n    majority_ok = coop_ratio >= 0.6\n    future_factor = (r - round) / r\n    fine_ok = expected_fine_cost() < stock_t/(4*n)\n\n    condition = (stock_ok and majority_ok) or (future_factor > 0.7 and stock_t > 0.3*capacity and coop_ratio > 0.4)\n    condition = condition and fine_ok\n\n    action = C if condition else D\n```\n\nThe strategy uses only publicly available parameters, the observed stock evolution, and the round index, satisfying the requirement for an altruistic, adaptive, and robust play."

description_BENEVOLENT_1 = "**Benevolent Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**Parameters known to the agent**:  \n\\(n\\) (players), \\(r\\) (rounds), capacity, audit probability \\(q\\), fine \\(F\\).  \n\n**State variables maintained each round**  \n- \\(t\\) \u2013 current round index (0\u2011based)  \n- \\(S_t\\) \u2013 common\u2011pool stock at the start of round \\(t\\)  \n- \\(p_t\\) \u2013 observed proportion of opponents that cooperated in the previous round  \n  \\(p_t = \\frac{\\text{# opponents who played C}}{n-1}\\) (undefined for \\(t=0\\))  \n- \\(d_t\\) \u2013 counter of consecutive defections I have played (reset to\u202f0 when I cooperate)  \n\n**Fixed thresholds (tuned once for the game, not per opponent)**  \n- Cooperation\u2011support threshold \\(\\tau = 0.7\\) (if \u2265\u202f70\u202f% of opponents cooperated, I treat the environment as cooperative)  \n- Stock\u2011safety threshold \\(\\sigma = 0.4\\) (if \\(S_t \\ge \\sigma\\cdot\\text{capacity}\\) I deem the stock healthy)  \n- Critical\u2011stock threshold \\(\\theta = 0.2\\) (if \\(S_t < \\theta\\cdot\\text{capacity}\\) I must avoid any further depletion)  \n- Maximum punishment length \\(L = 3\\) (no more than three consecutive defections)  \n\n**Decision rule (applied at the start of each round)**  \n\n1. **Zero\u2011stock safeguard**  \n   If \\(S_t = 0\\) \u2192 play **C** (defect would only incur an expected fine).\n\n2. **Last round special case**  \n   If \\(t = r-1\\):  \n   - Compute expected net gain from defecting  \n     \\[\n     G_t = \\frac{S_t}{2n} - qF\n     \\]  \n   - If \\(G_t > 0\\) **and** \\(p_{t} < \\tau\\) (opponents are mostly defecting) **and** \\(S_t - \\frac{S_t}{n} \\ge 0\\) \u2192 play **D**.  \n   - Otherwise \u2192 play **C**.\n\n3. **First round**  \n   If \\(t = 0\\) \u2192 play **C** and set \\(d_0 = 0\\).\n\n4. **General round (\\(0 < t < r-1\\))**  \n\n   a. **Compute expected net gain from defecting**  \n      \\[\n      G_t = \\frac{S_t}{2n} - qF\n      \\]\n\n   b. **If defecting is not profitable** (\\(G_t \\le 0\\)) \u2192 play **C**, reset \\(d_t = 0\\).\n\n   c. **If defecting is profitable (\\(G_t > 0\\))** evaluate the environment:  \n\n      - **Healthy stock & cooperative opponents**:  \n        If \\(S_t \\ge \\sigma\\cdot\\text{capacity}\\) **and** \\(p_t \\ge \\tau\\) \u2192 play **C**, reset \\(d_t = 0\\).\n\n      - **Unhealthy stock or uncooperative opponents**:  \n        If \\(S_t < \\theta\\cdot\\text{capacity}\\) **or** \\(p_t < \\tau\\) \u2192  \n\n        i. **Punishment phase** \u2013 defect **only** if I have defected fewer than \\(L\\) consecutive times:  \n           - If \\(d_t < L\\) \u2192 play **D**, set \\(d_{t+1}=d_t+1\\).  \n           - If \\(d_t = L\\) \u2192 play **C**, reset \\(d_{t+1}=0\\).  \n\n        ii. This limited\u2011defection window signals dissatisfaction while preventing prolonged over\u2011exploitation that could collapse the stock.\n\n   d. **Stock\u2011critical fallback**:  \n      If after the above checks I would still choose **D** but the projected remaining stock after my consumption would fall below \\(\\theta\\cdot\\text{capacity}\\) (i.e., \\(S_t - \\frac{S_t}{n} < \\theta\\cdot\\text{capacity}\\)), override and play **C** to preserve the pool.\n\n**Summary of actions per round**  \n\n| Situation                              | Action |\n|----------------------------------------|--------|\n| \\(S_t = 0\\)                            | C      |\n| \\(t = r-1\\) (final round)              | C unless profitable D with low opponent cooperation |\n| \\(t = 0\\) (first round)               | C      |\n| General round & \\(G_t \\le 0\\)          | C      |\n| General round & \\(G_t > 0\\) & \\(S_t \\ge \\sigma\\) & \\(p_t \\ge \\tau\\) | C |\n| General round & \\(G_t > 0\\) & (stock low **or** opponents uncooperative) | Defect up to \\(L\\) consecutive times, then cooperate; never defect if it would push stock below \\(\\theta\\) |\n\nThe strategy always prefers cooperation when the stock is healthy and opponents are largely cooperative, uses limited defections as a gentle enforcement tool when cooperation erodes or the stock becomes vulnerable, and never sacrifices the common pool for short\u2011term gain when doing so would jeopardize future welfare."

description_BENEVOLENT_2 = "**Strategy: Adaptive Benevolent Cooperation (ABC)**  \n\n**Parameters (fixed for the match)**  \n- `\u03b8_stock`\u202f=\u202f0.4\u202f\u00d7\u202fcapacity\u2003\u2003(stock level below which cooperation is risky)  \n- `\u03b8_opp`\u202f=\u202f0.5\u2003\u2003(fraction of opponents cooperating required to keep cooperating)  \n- `\u03b8_decline`\u202f=\u202f0.15\u2003\u2003(max allowed decline of stock between two consecutive rounds while still cooperating)  \n\n**State variables (updated each round)**  \n- `S`\u202f=\u202fcurrent stock (observed at start of round)  \n- `c_prev`\u202f=\u202ffraction of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (0 for round\u202f0)  \n- `S_prev`\u202f=\u202fstock at the start of the previous round (capacity for round\u202f0)  \n\n**Decision rule (executed simultaneously by each player at the beginning of a round)**  \n\n```\nif t == r-1:                     # last round\n    action = C                  # always cooperate (no audit, future stock irrelevant)\nelif S == 0:\n    action = C                  # nothing to consume, cooperate by definition\nelse:\n    # 1) Evaluate stock health\n    stock_ok = (S >= \u03b8_stock)\n\n    # 2) Evaluate opponent behaviour\n    opp_ok = (c_prev >= \u03b8_opp)\n\n    # 3) Check recent stock trend\n    if t > 0:\n        decline = (S_prev - S) / S_prev   # proportion drop since last round\n        trend_ok = (decline <= \u03b8_decline)\n    else:\n        trend_ok = True\n\n    # 4) Combine conditions\n    if stock_ok and opp_ok and trend_ok:\n        action = C\n    else:\n        # When conditions fail, defect only if expected net gain exceeds expected fine\n        expected_fine = q * F\n        net_gain = S/n - S/(2n) - expected_fine\n        if net_gain > 0:\n            action = D\n        else:\n            action = C\n```\n\n**Updates after the round**  \n- Record `c_this = (number_of_opponents_who_played_C) / (n-1)`.  \n- Set `c_prev \u2190 c_this`.  \n- Set `S_prev \u2190 S` (stock observed at round start).  \n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n- **Round\u202f0**: `c_prev` is defined as 0, `S_prev` = capacity, so the rule reduces to \u201ccooperate if stock \u2265\u202f\u03b8_stock\u201d; with the usual parameters this means initial cooperation.  \n- **Round\u202fr\u20111**: forced cooperation regardless of stock or opponent actions (no audit, benevolent end\u2011game).  \n- **Stock = 0**: cooperation yields zero payoff and does not further reduce the stock; the rule selects `C`.  \n- **Audit considerations**: the expected fine (`q\u00b7F`) is used only when the rule would otherwise recommend defection; if the fine makes defection unprofitable, the player stays cooperative.  \n\n**Rationale embedded in the rule (not stated, just logic)**  \n- The strategy maintains cooperation while the common pool is healthy (`stock_ok`), opponents are mostly cooperative (`opp_ok`), and the stock is not rapidly collapsing (`trend_ok`).  \n- If any of these signals deteriorate, the player switches to a conditional defection that is justified only when the monetary advantage after accounting for the expected fine is positive; otherwise it remains cooperative.  \n\n**Result** \u2013 The ABC strategy dynamically adapts to observed opponent behaviour and stock dynamics, strives to keep the resource near capacity, and only resorts to defection when it is clearly beneficial after factoring in audit risk, thereby embodying a benevolent approach throughout the repeated game."

description_BENEVOLENT_3 = "**Benevolent Sustainable\u2011Cooperation (BSC) Strategy**\n\n**Parameters derived from the game description**\n```\nn          # number of players\nr          # number of rounds\ncapacity   # max sustainable stock\nq          # audit probability (game_description.audit_prob)\nF          # fine per audited defection (game_description.fine)\n```\n\n**Computed thresholds**\n```\n\u0394payoff   = (stock / n) - (stock / (2*n))          # extra payoff from D vs C\nexpFine   = q * F                                 # expected fine per D\nnetGain   = \u0394payoff - expFine                     # expected net gain from D\n\nsafety    = 0.40 * capacity   # minimum stock we must keep to stay sustainable\nauditThresh = 2*n*q*F       # stock level where netGain becomes non\u2011positive\nminStock  = max(safety, auditThresh)   # effective lower bound for cooperation\n```\n\n**Decision rule (applied each round *t* before acting)**  \n\n```\nif t == 0:                                   # first round\n    action = C\nelif t == r-1:                               # last round (no audit)\n    action = C                                 # benevolent: preserve stock, avoid exploitation\nelse:\n    # 1. Observe opponent behaviour from last round\n    oppCoopRatio = (numOpponentsCooperated_lastRound) / (n-1)\n\n    # 2. Update willingness to cooperate\n    #    \u2013 if many opponents defected, tighten tolerance;\n    #    \u2013 otherwise stay at baseline.\n    tolerance = 0.6            # baseline tolerance for defections\n    if oppCoopRatio < tolerance:\n        # opponents are too uncooperative \u2192 switch to defensive defect\n        # but only for a single round; then re\u2011evaluate.\n        action = D\n    else:\n        # 3. Evaluate sustainability and expected profit\n        if stock >= minStock and netGain <= 0:\n            action = C               # safe: keep stock, no profitable defection\n        else:\n            # 4. Conditional defection only when it is both profitable\n            #    and the stock is high enough that a single extra draw\n            #    will not push the post\u2011consumption stock below safety.\n            #    Compute post\u2011consumption stock for a single D this round:\n            consumptionIfD = stock / n\n            consumptionIfC = stock / (2*n)\n            S_remain_D = stock - ( (numCooperators_lastRound)*(stock/(2*n)) + (numDefectors_lastRound)*(stock/n) )\n                                 + (consumptionIfD - consumptionIfC) )   # replace one C by D\n            # approximate growth after this round:\n            growth_D = 2 * S_remain_D * (1 - S_remain_D / capacity)\n            projectedStock = min(S_remain_D + growth_D, capacity)\n\n            if projectedStock >= safety:\n                action = D           # exploit the high stock responsibly\n            else:\n                action = C           # preserve stock\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- **Round\u202f0**: always cooperate (set cooperative tone).\n- **Round\u202fr\u20111** (final round): always cooperate; no audit risk and benevolence favors not emptying the pool.\n- **Audit\u2011free environments (q\u202f=\u202f0)**: `netGain` reduces to `\u0394payoff`. The strategy still requires `stock \u2265 safety`; if the stock is below the safety margin, it cooperates despite higher immediate payoff from defecting.\n- **Zero fine (F\u202f=\u202f0)**: `auditThresh` becomes 0, so `minStock = safety`; the strategy cooperates unless the stock is safely high enough and opponents are cooperating.\n- **Stock depleted (stock\u202f=\u202f0)**: both actions yield zero payoff; the rule will select `C` because `stock \u2265 minStock` fails, forcing cooperation (no further depletion).\n\n**Summary of actions**\n- **Cooperate (C)** when the pool is near or below the sustainable level, when expected defection profit is non\u2011positive, or when opponents have been largely uncooperative (to avoid escalation).\n- **Defect (D)** only in a round where (a) the pool is comfortably above the safety margin, (b) the expected net gain from defection exceeds zero after accounting for audit risk, and (c) the projected post\u2011round stock after growth remains above the safety margin. Defection is limited to a single round after a detected dip in opponent cooperation; the strategy re\u2011evaluates each round."

description_BENEVOLENT_4 = "**Strategy: \u201cSustainable Reciprocity with Risk\u2011Adjusted Defection\u201d**\n\n**Parameters used**\n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `q` (audit probability), `F` (fine)\n- current round `t` (0\u2011indexed), current stock `S`\n- history `H` = list of past observations  \n  each entry `h = (t, my_action, my_audit, opp_coop_count)`  \n  where `opp_coop_count` \u2208 {0,\u2026,n\u20111} is the number of opponents that cooperated in that round.\n\n**Derived quantities**\n1. `stock_ratio = S / capacity`\u2003(0\u202f\u2264\u202fstock_ratio\u202f\u2264\u202f1)  \n2. `coop_ratio = ( \u03a3_{k < t} opp_coop_count_k ) / ( (n\u20111)\u00b7t )`\u2003(average opponent cooperation, undefined for t=0)  \n3. `expected_fine = q\u00b7F`\u2003(expected monetary loss per defection)  \n4. `net_gain_D = S/n \u2013 expected_fine`\u2003expected payoff if defecting (ignoring future stock impact)  \n5. `gain_C = S/(2n)`\u2003payoff if cooperating.\n\n**Decision rule (applied each round t)**  \n\n```\nif t == r\u20111:                         # last round \u2013 no future stock value\n    action = C if gain_C >= net_gain_D else D\nelse:\n    # 1. Preserve stock if it is low\n    if stock_ratio < \u03b8_low:\n        action = C                     # protect the pool\n        continue\n\n    # 2. Reward observed cooperation\n    if t > 0 and coop_ratio > \u03b8_coop:\n        # stock is safe and opponents are cooperative \u2192 keep cooperating\n        action = C\n        continue\n\n    # 3. Controlled defection when stock is abundant and opponents defect a lot\n    if stock_ratio > \u03b8_high and (t==0 or coop_ratio < \u03b8_coop):\n        # compute a safe defection probability that does not drive stock below \u03b8_low\n        safe_defect = max_defect_fraction(S, capacity, n, r\u2011t)\n        # adjust for expected fine: only defect if net_gain_D exceeds gain_C by a margin\n        if net_gain_D - gain_C > \u0394_gain and random() < safe_defect:\n            action = D\n        else:\n            action = C\n        continue\n\n    # 4. Default fallback \u2013 cooperate\n    action = C\n```\n\n**Thresholds (tunable but fixed for the run)**\n- `\u03b8_low = 0.35`\u2003(when stock <\u202f35\u202f% of capacity, always cooperate)  \n- `\u03b8_high = 0.75`\u2003(when stock >\u202f75\u202f% of capacity, consider defection)  \n- `\u03b8_coop = 0.60`\u2003(average opponent cooperation >\u202f60\u202f% triggers unconditional cooperation)  \n- `\u0394_gain = 0.05\u00b7gain_C`\u2003(defection must improve expected payoff by at least 5\u202f% of cooperative payoff)  \n\n**Function\u202f`max_defect_fraction`** \u2013 limits the proportion of rounds in which defection may occur without dropping the stock below `\u03b8_low` before the game ends:\n\n```\ndef max_defect_fraction(S, capacity, n, remaining_rounds):\n    # Simulate worst\u2011case consumption if we defect every remaining round\n    worst_consumption = remaining_rounds * (S / n)          # assume stock stays roughly S\n    # Required remaining stock to stay above \u03b8_low at end:\n    required_stock = \u03b8_low * capacity\n    # Allow defection only if worst_consumption leaves enough buffer:\n    if S - worst_consumption >= required_stock:\n        return 1.0\n    # otherwise linearly scale probability:\n    return max(0.0, (S - required_stock) / worst_consumption)\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- **Round\u202f0**: No `coop_ratio` is available; start with cooperation (action = C) to seed a sustainable path.\n- **Round\u202fr\u20111** (last): Audits are impossible; compare raw payoffs (`gain_C` vs `net_gain_D`) and pick the higher. Because no future stock matters, a single defection is harmless if it yields higher immediate payoff.\n- **Audit outcome**: The strategy does **not** condition future moves on whether *you* were audited; only on observed opponent cooperation counts, keeping the rule anonymous and robust to noise.\n- **Stock\u202f=\u202f0**: If `S` becomes zero, both actions yield zero payoff; continue to cooperate (C) to signal willingness to restore the pool in later rounds (stock can only grow from zero if `growth` term is non\u2011zero, which occurs only when `S>0`; thus cooperating never harms).\n\n**Benevolent intent**\n- Prioritizes stock preservation (`\u03b8_low`) over short\u2011term personal gain.  \n- Rewards communities where opponents cooperate (`\u03b8_coop`).  \n- Allows limited, risk\u2011adjusted defection only when the pool is abundant (`\u03b8_high`) and opponents are largely defecting, thereby preventing exploitation while keeping the resource viable for the remainder of the game.  \n- The probabilistic defection limit (`max_defect_fraction`) ensures the collective stock never falls below the sustainable threshold, guaranteeing that all players can continue to receive positive payoffs in later rounds."

description_BENEVOLENT_5 = "**Strategy Name: Benevolent Conditional Cooperation (BCC)**  \n\n**Parameters used:** n, r, capacity, audit probability\u202fq, fine\u202fF.  \n\n**State variables maintained each round t (0\u2011indexed):**  \n- S\u209c\u00a0: current stock (observed at start of round).  \n- c\u209c\u208b\u2081\u00a0: number of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (undefined for t\u202f=\u202f0).  \n- f\u209c\u208b\u2081\u00a0=\u00a0c\u209c\u208b\u2081\u202f/\u202f(n\u20111)\u00a0: observed cooperation fraction of opponents (undefined for t\u202f=\u202f0).  \n\n**Decision rule (applied simultaneously by each player):**  \n\n1. **Compute the immediate monetary incentive to defect**  \n   ```\n   extra_gain   = S\u209c / (2\u202fn)                      # extra consumption when defecting vs cooperating\n   expected_fine = q * F\n   net_gain      = extra_gain - expected_fine\n   ```\n2. **Compute a safety threshold for the stock**  \n   - Let `t_remaining = r - t` (including current round).  \n   - Define `min_safe_stock = capacity * 0.3 * (t_remaining / r)`.  \n   (The factor 0.3 is a fixed conservatism constant; it scales down as the horizon shortens, allowing a slightly higher depletion near the end.)  \n\n3. **Choose action**  \n\n   *If S\u209c \u2264 0* \u2192 cooperate (both actions yield 0, but cooperation signals benevolence).  \n\n   *If t = 0* \u2192 cooperate (no history, start benevolently).  \n\n   *If t = r\u20111* (last round, never audited) \u2192 cooperate (maximizes collective welfare when audit risk is irrelevant).  \n\n   *Otherwise (1\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f\u2264\u202fr\u20112):*  \n\n   - **Case A \u2013 Stock is abundant:**  \n     If `S\u209c \u2265 min_safe_stock` **and** `net_gain > 0` **and** `f\u209c\u208b\u2081 \u2265 0.5` (at least half of opponents cooperated last round), then **defect**.  \n     Rationale: there is enough stock to absorb a modest extra take, opponents are largely cooperative, and the expected net monetary benefit outweighs the fine risk.  \n\n   - **Case B \u2013 Stock is vulnerable or opponents are non\u2011cooperative:**  \n     If `S\u209c < min_safe_stock` **or** `f\u209c\u208b\u2081 < 0.5`, then **cooperate**.  \n     This protects the diminishing resource and discourages a cascade of defection when cooperation levels are low.  \n\n   - **Case C \u2013 Net gain is non\u2011positive:**  \n     If `net_gain \u2264 0` (fine expectation cancels or exceeds extra gain), cooperate regardless of stock or opponent behavior.  \n\n4. **Tie\u2011breakers** (when conditions above are simultaneously true):  \n\n   - If `S\u209c` exactly equals `min_safe_stock` and `net_gain > 0` but `f\u209c\u208b\u2081 < 0.5`, choose **cooperate** (stock safety dominates).  \n   - If `net_gain == 0` (extra gain equals expected fine), default to **cooperate** (avoids risk of an audit).  \n\n**History update (after each round):**  \n\n- Record the announced number of opponent cooperators `c\u209c`.  \n- Update `f\u209c` for use in the next decision.  \n- Observe whether you were audited and, if so, subtract the paid fine from that round\u2019s payoff (already accounted for in the expected\u2011fine calculation).  \n\n**Summary of behavior:**  \n- Starts benevolently by cooperating.  \n- Defects only when the stock is comfortably above a dynamic safety level, opponents have shown sufficient cooperation, and the expected monetary advantage after accounting for audit risk is positive.  \n- Reverts to cooperation whenever the resource is at risk, opponents are uncooperative, or the fine erodes any advantage.  \n- Never defects in the final round, ensuring the last contribution is fully altruistic."

description_BENEVOLENT_6 = "**Benevolent Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**Parameters (read from game description)**\n- `n` \u2013 number of players  \n- `r` \u2013 total rounds  \n- `capacity` \u2013 maximum sustainable stock  \n- `q` \u2013 audit probability (0\u202f\u2264\u202fq\u202f\u2264\u202f1)  \n- `F` \u2013 fine per audited defection  \n\n**Derived constants (fixed for the whole match)**\n```\n\u03b1 = 0.4                         # safety\u2011stock fraction of capacity\n\u03b2 = 0.2                         # tolerated fraction of opponents defecting\nsafety_stock   = \u03b1 * capacity\ntolerance_def   = ceil(\u03b2 * n)   # max number of opponent defections tolerated\n```\n\n**State kept across rounds**\n- `S` \u2013 current stock (provided each round)  \n- `prev_defectors` \u2013 number of opponents that played D in the previous round  \n  (unknown in round\u202f0 \u2192 set to 0)  \n- `my_last_action` \u2013 my action in the previous round (C or D)  \n\n**Decision rule (applied every round `t = 0 \u2026 r\u20111`)**\n\n```\nif t == r\u20111:                     # last round: be fully benevolent\n    action = C\nelse if t == 0:                  # first round: no history\n    action = C\nelse:\n    # 1. Expected net gain from defecting (ignoring stock impact)\n    expected_gain = S/(2*n) - q*F          # = (S/n - qF) \u2013 S/(2n)\n\n    # 2. Safety check: preserve stock if it is low\n    if S < safety_stock:\n        action = C\n    else:\n        # 3. Social tolerance check\n        if prev_defectors > tolerance_def:\n            # opponents are over\u2011exploiting; defect to signal protest\n            action = D\n        else:\n            # 4. Economic comparison\n            if expected_gain > 0:\n                # Defect gives higher expected personal payoff, but we are benevolent:\n                # cooperate unless opponents have already shown sustained over\u2011exploitation.\n                action = C\n            else:\n                action = C\n```\n\n**Updating `prev_defectors` after the round**\n- After the simultaneous move, the game reports the *count* of opponent cooperators.\n- Compute `prev_defectors = n\u20111 \u2013 reported_cooperators`.\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- **Zero stock (`S = 0`)**: payoff of any action is zero; the rule above yields `action = C` because `expected_gain = -qF \u2264 0`.\n- **Audit in the last round**: never occurs by definition; the rule still chooses `C`.\n- **Fractional tolerance**: `tolerance_def` is rounded up so that a single defector can be tolerated in small groups.\n\n**Benevolent intent**\n- The strategy always cooperates when the stock falls below a safe reserve.\n- Defection is used only as a *signal* when opponents repeatedly over\u2011exploit (exceeding the tolerated number of defectors), never to maximize short\u2011term gain.\n- In all other situations the player cooperates, regardless of the raw expected monetary advantage of defecting, thereby promoting long\u2011term sustainability of the common pool."

description_BENEVOLENT_7 = "**Benevolent Adaptive Common\u2011Pool Strategy**\n\n*Parameters (known to the agent)*  \n\u2011 n, capacity, r, audit probability\u202fq, fine\u202fF  \n\n*State variables (updated each round)*  \n\u2011 S\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003current stock before consumption  \n\u2011 t\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003current round index (0\u2011based)  \n\u2011 c_obs\u2003\u2003number of opponents that cooperated in the immediately preceding round (0\u202f\u2264\u202fc_obs\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111) \u2013 for t\u202f=\u202f0 this value is undefined  \n\n*Fixed thresholds (tuned once for the given game, not altered during play)*  \n\n| Symbol | Meaning | Suggested value (adjustable) |\n|--------|---------|------------------------------|\n|\u202f\u03b8_target\u202f|Target stock as a fraction of capacity (desired sustainable level) |\u202f0.6\u202f|\n|\u202f\u03b8_min\u202f   |Minimum viable stock before forced defection (to avoid collapse) |\u202f0.2\u202f|\n|\u202f\u03c1_min\u202f   |Minimum observed cooperation rate before we consider \u201cdefector\u2011rich\u201d environment |\u202f0.3\u202f|\n|\u202f\u0394_cons\u202f  |Maximum extra consumption we are willing to allow in a round when S\u202f<\u202f\u03b8_target\u00b7capacity (protective buffer) |\u202fcapacity\u202f\u00d7\u202f(\u03b8_target\u202f\u2013\u202f\u03b8_min)\u202f|\n\n*Derived quantities each round*  \n\n```\nS_target = \u03b8_target * capacity\nS_min    = \u03b8_min    * capacity\n\u03c1 = (c_obs) / (n-1)          # undefined for t = 0, treat as 1 (no info)\nE_fine   = q * F             # expected fine for a defection\n\u03c0_C      = S / (2n)          # payoff if cooperate\n\u03c0_D_raw  = S / n             # payoff before fine if defect\n\u03c0_D      = \u03c0_D_raw - E_fine  # expected net payoff for defection\n```\n\n---\n\n### Decision Rules\n\n1. **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0)**  \n   - Play **Cooperate (C)**.  \n   - Rationale: no history, give the pool a high\u2011stock start and signal benevolence.\n\n2. **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111)** \u2013 never audited  \n   - If S\u202f>\u202f0 \u2192 **Cooperate (C)**.  \n   - If S\u202f=\u202f0 \u2192 any action yields zero; choose **Cooperate (C)** for consistency.\n\n3. **Intermediate rounds (0\u202f<\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr\u20111)**  \n\n   a. **Stock\u2011driven safety check**  \n      - If `S <= S_min` \u2192 **Defect (D)** *only* enough to keep the stock from dropping below zero:  \n        ```\n        # Compute maximal safe consumption per player\n        max_safe_cons = S / n          # each can safely take at most this\n        # Our consumption will be the larger of the two prescribed amounts,\n        # but never exceed max_safe_cons.\n        consume = min(S / n, max_safe_cons)   # this equals S/n, i.e. D\n        action = D\n        ```\n      - Else proceed to (b).\n\n   b. **Economic comparison with expected fine**  \n      - If `\u03c0_D <= \u03c0_C` (defection not more profitable after expected fine) \u2192 **Cooperate (C)**.  \n\n   c. **Observed cooperation filter**  \n      - If `\u03c1 < \u03c1_min` (few opponents cooperated recently) **and** `S > S_target` \u2192 **Cooperate (C)** (still benevolent, trusting future cooperation).  \n      - If `\u03c1 < \u03c1_min` **and** `S <= S_target` \u2192 **Defect (D)** but limit extra consumption:  \n        ```\n        # Desired total consumption to keep stock at S_target after growth\n        # Approximate next\u2011round stock if we consume x:\n        #   S' = min( (S - x) + 2*(S - x)*(1 - (S - x)/capacity) , capacity )\n        # We solve for x such that S' >= S_target; use a simple bound:\n        extra_allowed = \u0394_cons          # buffer we are willing to burn\n        base_cons = S/(2n)               # cooperative share\n        max_cons = base_cons + extra_allowed/(n)   # spread buffer evenly\n        consume = min(S/n, max_cons)    # D\u2011style consumption capped\n        action = D\n        ```\n\n   d. **Default** (none of the above triggers) \u2192 **Cooperate (C)**.\n\n4. **Action implementation**  \n   - If the chosen action is **Cooperate (C)**, consume `S/(2n)`.  \n   - If the chosen action is **Defect (D)**, consume the amount computed in steps\u202f3a or\u202f3c (never exceeds `S/n`).  \n\n5. **Update history**  \n   - Record own action, whether audited, and any fine paid (only needed for internal bookkeeping; it does not affect future decisions directly).  \n\n---\n\n### Edge\u2011Case Handling  \n\n- **Zero stock (S = 0)**: Both actions yield zero payoff; always choose **Cooperate (C)** to preserve benevolent signaling.  \n- **Audit in the last round**: By definition never occurs, so the expected\u2011fine comparison reduces to `\u03c0_D_raw` vs `\u03c0_C`.  \n- **Missing observation (t\u202f=\u202f0)**: Treat `\u03c1` as 1 (optimistic) so the first round follows rule\u202f1.  \n- **Numerical rounding**: When computed consumption exceeds the remaining stock, truncate to the remaining stock to keep the stock non\u2011negative.  \n\n---\n\n### Benevolent Intent  \n\nThe strategy prioritises maintaining the common pool above the target sustainability level (`\u03b8_target\u00b7capacity`). It defects only when the expected monetary benefit of defection outweighs cooperation **and** the stock is low enough that a modest extra draw is needed to avoid collapse or to compensate for a severely uncooperative environment. Expected audit penalties are incorporated directly, discouraging reckless exploitation. By initially cooperating and by returning to cooperation whenever stock is healthy, the agent promotes long\u2011run collective welfare while remaining robust to aggressive opponents."

description_BENEVOLENT_8 = "**Benevolent Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**Inputs each round\u202ft**  \n- Parameters: n, r, capacity, audit probability\u202fq, fine\u202fF  \n- State: current stock\u202fS (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity)  \n- History: my past actions a\u2080\u2026a_{t\u20111}; for each previous round\u202fk\u202f<\u202ft I observed the number\u202fC\u1d4f_opponents of opponents that cooperated (the remaining n\u20111 players are anonymous)  \n\n**Derived quantities**  \n-\u202fObserved opponent cooperation rate:  \n\u2003if\u202ft\u202f>\u202f0\u2003\u2003p_coop = (\u2211_{k=0}^{t\u20111} C\u1d4f_opponents)\u202f/\u202f[(t)\u00b7(n\u20111)]\u2003else\u2003p_coop = 1.0  \n-\u202fSafety stock threshold:\u2003S_safe = 0.3\u202f\u00b7\u202fcapacity  \n-\u202fHigh\u2011stock threshold:\u2003S_high = 0.5\u202f\u00b7\u202fcapacity  \n-\u202fTarget cooperation level:\u2003p_target = 0.8  \n\n**Decision rule (pseudocode)**  \n\n```\nif t == 0 or t == r\u20111:\n    action = C                     # always cooperate in first and last round\nelif S <= 0:\n    action = C                     # nothing to consume; cooperate by definition\nelif S < S_safe:\n    action = C                     # preserve stock when it is low\nelse:\n    # estimate expected net gain from defecting\n    expected_gain_defect = (S / n) - q * F - (S / (2 * n))\n    # expected gain is the extra consumption minus expected fine\n    if expected_gain_defect > 0 and S > S_high and p_coop >= p_target:\n        action = D                 # defect only when stock is ample, opponents are mostly cooperative,\n    else:\n        action = C                 # otherwise cooperate\n```\n\n**Explanation of the rule components (implicit in the code)**  \n- **First and last rounds**: cooperate unconditionally to seed cooperation and to avoid exploiting the audit\u2011free final round.  \n- **Zero stock**: cooperation yields zero payoff, so any action is equivalent; choose C for consistency.  \n- **Low\u2011stock safeguard**: when S falls below 30\u202f% of capacity, always cooperate to give the growth dynamics a chance to restore the pool.  \n- **Defection condition**: defect only if the deterministic extra consumption (S/n\u202f\u2212\u202fS/(2n)) outweighs the expected fine (q\u00b7F) *and* the stock is comfortably above half capacity *and* the observed opponent cooperation rate meets the target. This ensures that defecting never endangers sustainability and only occurs when the environment is both generous and trustworthy.  \n- **Otherwise**: default to cooperation, preserving the common resource and encouraging reciprocal behavior.  \n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n- **t\u202f=\u202f0**: start with cooperation regardless of any prior information.  \n- **t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111**: cooperate despite the absence of audits, reflecting benevolence rather than opportunistic exploitation.  \n- **S\u202f=\u202f0**: treat as cooperative (no consumption possible).  \n- **No opponent observations yet (t\u202f=\u202f0)**: p_coop is set to 1, biasing toward cooperation until data accumulate.  \n\nThe strategy therefore adapts to the observed level of cooperation, to the health of the common pool, and to the audit environment, while always favoring actions that sustain the resource and promote collective welfare."

description_BENEVOLENT_9 = "**Benevolent Adaptive Strategy (BAS)**  \n\n**Parameters (known to the agent)**  \n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `q` (audit probability), `F` (fine).  \n- History: for each past round `t` \u2011 number of opponent cooperations `c_t` (0\u202f\u2264\u202fc_t\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111) and own audits/fines.  \n- Current state: stock `S` (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity).  \n\n**Derived constants**  \n- `\u0394 = S/(2n)`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// payoff if you cooperate this round  \n- `\u03a6 = S/n - q\u00b7F`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// expected payoff if you defect (expected fine applied)  \n- `\u03b8_defect = 0.5`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// threshold of opponent\u2011defection fraction that triggers retaliation  \n- `\u03c4_retaliate = 2`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// number of consecutive retaliation rounds after a trigger  \n- `\u03b5_low = 0.1`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// fraction of capacity defining \u201ccritical low stock\u201d  \n\n**State variables**  \n- `retaliation_counter` (initially\u202f0).  \n\n---\n\n### Decision Rule (applied each round `t`)\n\n1. **First round (`t = 0`)**  \n   - Set `retaliation_counter \u2190 0`.  \n   - **Action:** Cooperate (`C`).  \n\n2. **Last round (`t = r\u20111`)**  \n   - **Action:** Cooperate (`C`).  \n   - (No audit in this round, so no fine risk; cooperating maximises collective welfare.)  \n\n3. **Intermediate rounds (`0 < t < r\u20111`)**  \n\n   a. **Critical\u2011stock check**  \n      - If `S < \u03b5_low\u00b7capacity` \u2192 set `action \u2190 C` (preserve stock, allow growth).  \n\n   b. **Retaliation phase**  \n      - If `retaliation_counter > 0` \u2192  \n        \u2022 `action \u2190 D` (defect to signal disapproval).  \n        \u2022 Decrement `retaliation_counter \u2190 retaliation_counter - 1`.  \n        \u2022 Skip remaining checks for this round.  \n\n   c. **Opponent\u2011defection monitoring**  \n      - Compute opponent\u2011defection fraction in the *most recent* round:  \n        `\u03b4 = (n\u20111\u2011c_{t\u20111}) / (n\u20111)`.  \n      - If `\u03b4 \u2265 \u03b8_defect` \u2192  \n        \u2022 `retaliation_counter \u2190 \u03c4_retaliate`.  \n        \u2022 `action \u2190 D` (start retaliation).  \n\n   d. **Economic\u2011risk comparison**  \n      - If `\u0394 \u2265 \u03a6` \u2192 `action \u2190 C` (cooperating is at least as good in expected monetary terms).  \n      - Else \u2192 `action \u2190 D` (defect only when expected net gain exceeds cooperating, after the above safeguards).  \n\n4. **Update after round** (agent does this internally, not a decision):  \n   - Observe `c_t` (number of opponent cooperations).  \n   - Observe whether audited (`a_i,t`) and fine paid (if any).  \n   - Update `retaliation_counter` only as described above.  \n\n---\n\n### Edge\u2011Case Handling  \n\n- **Zero stock (`S = 0`)**: Both `\u0394` and `\u03a6` are zero; rule (d) selects `C` (cooperating incurs no cost and signals goodwill).  \n- **No audit risk (`q = 0` or `F = 0`)**: `\u03a6 = S/n`; the strategy still cooperates unless `S/(2n) < S/n`, which never holds, so it will default to cooperation except when a high defection fraction triggers retaliation.  \n- **All opponents always cooperate**: `\u03b4 = 0` \u2192 no retaliation; rule (d) prefers `C` because `\u0394 = \u03a6`.  \n- **Sustained high defection**: Repeated triggers keep `retaliation_counter` positive, causing a bounded block of defections; once opponents' defection fraction falls below `\u03b8_defect`, retaliation ends and the strategy re\u2011evaluates the economic comparison.  \n\n---\n\n### Benevolent Intent  \n\n- Prioritises stock preservation when the pool is low.  \n- Rewards sustained cooperation with consistent cooperation.  \n- Uses limited, proportional retaliation to discourage systematic defection while avoiding endless cycles of mutual defection.  \n- Incorporates audit risk, defecting only when the expected monetary advantage outweighs the expected fine, thus minimizing unnecessary exploitation of the common resource."

description_BENEVOLENT_10 = "**Strategy \u201cBenevolent Conditional Cooperation\u201d**\n\n**Parameters (computed once):**  \n-\u202f`\u03b8_low = 0.35\u00b7capacity`\u2003\u2003\u00a0minimum stock level below which we never defect (to avoid collapsing the pool).  \n-\u202f`\u03b8_high = 0.70\u00b7capacity`\u2003\u2003\u00a0stock level above which we are tolerant of occasional defections.  \n-\u202f`\u03c4 = 0.20`\u2003\u2003\u00a0maximum tolerated proportion of opponents that defected in the previous round before we trigger retaliation.  \n\n**State variables (updated each round):**  \n-\u202f`S`\u00a0= current stock (observed at start of round).  \n-\u202f`c_{t-1}`\u00a0= number of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (derived from aggregate observation).  \n-\u202f`d_{t-1} = (n\u20111) \u2013 c_{t-1}`\u00a0= number of opponents that defected last round.  \n\n**Decision rule (applied at the beginning of each round t, 0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr):**  \n\n1. **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0):** play\u202f**C**.  \n\n2. **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111):** play\u202f**C** (no audit, highest social value).  \n\n3. **Intermediate rounds (0\u202f<\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr\u20111):**  \n\n   a. **Stock safety check** \u2013 if `S \u2264 \u03b8_low` \u2192 **C** (conserve stock; cooperation consumes the smallest share).  \n\n   b. **Retaliation trigger** \u2013 compute `p_def = d_{t-1} / (n\u20111)`.  \n      - If `p_def > \u03c4` **and** `S > \u03b8_low` \u2192 **D** for this round only (punish excess defections while stock is still safe).  \n\n   c. **Tolerance zone** \u2013 otherwise (stock above `\u03b8_low` and defections \u2264\u202f\u03c4):  \n      - If `S \u2265 \u03b8_high` \u2192 **C** (stock abundant, reward cooperation).  \n      - If `\u03b8_low < S < \u03b8_high` \u2192 **C** (default benevolent action).  \n\n4. **After\u2011round update:** record `c_t` (derived from the aggregate count of cooperators reported at round end) for use in the next round\u2019s rule.\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling:**  \n\n- If the audit probability `q` is high enough that expected fine `q\u00b7F` exceeds the extra gain from defecting (`S/n \u2013 S/(2n)`), the above rule still prefers **C** because step\u202f3b will never be satisfied (the extra gain is negative).  \n\n- If the stock ever reaches exactly `0` (unlikely under this rule), the rule falls back to step\u202f3a \u2192 **C**, which yields zero consumption for everyone and leaves the stock unchanged thereafter.  \n\n**Rationale encoded in the rule (benevolent mindset):**  \n\n- Prioritize maintaining the common\u2011pool above the safety threshold `\u03b8_low`.  \n- Use minimal, temporary defection only as a deterrent against systematic over\u2011exploitation, never to increase personal payoff at the expense of pool collapse.  \n- End the game with full cooperation to maximize total welfare when audits cease.  "

description_BENEVOLENT_11 = "**Benevolent Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**Parameters known to the agent**  \n- n, r, capacity, audit probability\u202fq, fine\u202fF.  \n- Current stock\u202fS\u209c (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u209c\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity).  \n- For each past round t\u2032\u202f<\u202ft the number of opponents that cooperated,\u202fc\u209c\u2032 (0\u202f\u2264\u202fc\u209c\u2032\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111).  \n\n**Derived quantities (computed each round t)**  \n1.\u202fRounds remaining\u202fR\u202f=\u202fr\u202f\u2011\u202ft.  \n2.\u202fAverage opponent cooperation rate  \n\\[\n\\bar p = \n\\begin{cases}\n0 & \\text{if }t=0\\\\[4pt]\n\\displaystyle\\frac{1}{t}\\sum_{t\u2032=0}^{t-1}\\frac{c_{t\u2032}}{\\,n-1\\,} & \\text{otherwise}\n\\end{cases}\n\\]  \n3.\u202fImmediate extra payoff from defecting instead of cooperating  \n\\[\n\\Delta_t = \\frac{S_t}{2n}.\n\\]  \n4.\u202fExpected monetary cost of defecting (audit\u202f\u00d7\u202ffine)  \n\\[\nE_t = q\\,F.\n\\]  \n5.\u202fSafety\u2011margin stock needed to guarantee that, if every player cooperates for the rest of the game, the stock never falls below a sustainable level. Compute the stock that would result after one cooperative round:  \n\n\\[\nS^{\\text{coop}}_{\\text{next}} = \n\\min\\!\\Bigl( \n\\underbrace{S_t - n\\frac{S_t}{2n}}_{\\text{after consumption}} \n\\;+\\; 2\\Bigl(S_t - \\frac{S_t}{2}\\Bigr)\\Bigl(1-\\frac{S_t-\\frac{S_t}{2}}{\\text{capacity}}\\Bigr),\n\\;\\text{capacity}\n\\Bigr)\n= \\min\\!\\Bigl(\\tfrac{S_t}{2}+ 2\\cdot\\tfrac{S_t}{2}\\bigl(1-\\tfrac{S_t}{2\\,\\text{capacity}}\\bigr),\\;\\text{capacity}\\Bigr).\n\\]\n\nDefine the *stock safety threshold*  \n\n\\[\nT_t = \\frac{R}{r}\\;S^{\\text{coop}}_{\\text{next}}.\n\\]\n\n(When many rounds remain the threshold is high; it shrinks as the game approaches the end.)\n\n**Decision rule (applied at the beginning of each round t, except the forced\u2011cooperate last round)**  \n\n```\nif t == r-1:                     # last round\n    action = C\nelse:\n    # 1. Check expected net benefit of defecting\n    net_gain = \u0394_t - E_t\n\n    # 2. Assess stock safety\n    safe = (S_t >= T_t)\n\n    # 3. Assess opponent behavior\n    #    If opponents have been mostly cooperative, be generous.\n    #    If they have been mostly defecting, require stronger safety.\n    coop_bias = 0.2 * (0.5 - \\bar p)      # negative when \\bar p > 0.5\n\n    # 4. Final test\n    if net_gain > coop_bias and safe:\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C\n```\n\n**Explanation of the rule components (no commentary, only the logic)**  \n\n- **Last round** \u2013 always cooperate, because no audit occurs and cooperation yields the maximal common\u2011pool payoff without risking future stock.  \n- **Net\u2011gain check** \u2013 defect only when the immediate extra payoff (\u0394\u209c) exceeds the expected fine (E\u209c) by more than a small bias that reflects recent opponent cooperation. The bias makes defecting easier when opponents have been largely defecting (\u202f\\bar p\u202f\u202f<\u202f0.5) and harder when they have been largely cooperating.  \n- **Safety check** \u2013 defect only if the current stock S\u209c is above the dynamic safety threshold T\u209c, guaranteeing that continued cooperation for the remaining rounds can keep the pool from collapsing. When S\u209c falls below T\u209c, the strategy forces cooperation to allow the stock to recover via growth.  \n- **Edge cases** \u2013  \n  *Round\u202f0*: \\bar p = 0, bias = +0.1, so the rule reduces to \u201cdefect only if \u0394\u2080\u202f>\u202fE\u2080 and S\u2080\u202f\u2265\u202fT\u2080\u201d. With the initial stock equal to capacity, T\u2080 = (r\u20110)/r\u00b7capacity \u2248 capacity, so the safety test forces cooperation in the first round.  \n  *Any round where S\u209c = 0*: \u0394\u209c = 0, net_gain \u2264 0, so the strategy cooperates (which yields zero consumption but leaves the stock at zero; no alternative can improve the outcome).  \n  *Audit probability\u202fq = 0*: E\u209c = 0; the bias and safety checks still prevent reckless defection when the stock is low.  \n  *Fine\u202fF = 0*: E\u209c = 0; defecting is permitted only if the stock safety threshold is satisfied and opponent cooperation is low enough to offset the bias.  \n\n**Summary of actions**  \n\n- **Cooperate (C)** whenever any of the following holds:  \n  1. It is the last round.  \n  2. The stock is below the safety threshold T\u209c.  \n  3. The expected net gain \u0394\u209c\u202f\u2011\u202fE\u209c is not enough to overcome the bias derived from opponent behavior.  \n\n- **Defect (D)** only when all three conditions are satisfied simultaneously:  \n  1. \u0394\u209c\u202f>\u202fE\u209c\u202f+\u202fbias,  \n  2. S\u209c\u202f\u2265\u202fT\u209c,  \n  3. The bias (which is negative when opponents have cooperated a lot) does not prohibit it.  \n\nThis rule set yields a benevolent, adaptive policy that maximizes collective welfare when possible, protects the common resource from depletion, and accounts for audit risk and opponent conduct."

description_BENEVOLENT_12 = "**Benevolent Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**Notation (per round\u202ft)**\n- `S_t` \u2013 current stock (observed at start of round\u202ft).  \n- `c_{-i,t}` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in round\u202ft (observed after consumption).  \n- `p_{coop,t} = c_{-i,t} / (n\u20111)` \u2013 observed cooperation proportion of opponents.  \n- `q` \u2013 audit probability (given).  \n- `F` \u2013 fine (given).  \n- `E_fine = q\u00b7F` \u2013 expected fine per defection.  \n- `\u0394C = S_t/(2n)` \u2013 payoff from cooperating.  \n- `\u0394D = S_t/n \u2013 E_fine` \u2013 expected net payoff from defecting.  \n- `S_next(C)` \u2013 projected stock after the round if we **cooperate** (using the deterministic stock\u2011update formula with our own consumption and the observed opponent actions).  \n- `S_next(D)` \u2013 projected stock after the round if we **defect** (same formula but with our higher consumption).  \n\n**Decision rule (applied each round\u202ft, 0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr)**  \n\n1. **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0)** \u2013 cooperate unconditionally.  \n\n2. **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111)** \u2013 cooperate unconditionally (no audit, and preserving stock for no future rounds is irrelevant; cooperation maximises collective payoff).  \n\n3. **Intermediate rounds (0\u202f<\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr\u20111)** \u2013 compute the three indicators below and apply the first satisfied condition:\n\n   a. **Critical stock safeguard**  \n      - If `S_t \u2264 0.1\u00b7capacity` \u2192 cooperate.  \n      (Very low stock endangers future rounds; benevolence prioritises survival.)\n\n   b. **Sustainable cooperation incentive**  \n      - Compute the *stock sustainability margin*  \n        `M = S_next(C) \u2013 0.5\u00b7capacity`.  \n      - If `M \u2265 0` \u2192 cooperate.  \n      (When cooperating keeps the stock at least half of capacity, the environment is sustainable; benevolence prefers the higher collective stock.)\n\n   c. **Expected payoff comparison with risk adjustment**  \n      - If `\u0394D \u2264 \u0394C` \u2192 cooperate.  \n        (Defection does not dominate even after expected fine.)  \n\n   d. **Opponent\u2011cooperation reinforcement**  \n      - If `p_{coop,t} \u2265 0.6` \u2192 cooperate.  \n        (High observed cooperation signals a benevolent community; we match it.)  \n\n   e. **Defect\u2011only when truly advantageous**  \n      - If `\u0394D > \u0394C` **and** `S_next(D) \u2265 0.3\u00b7capacity` \u2192 defect.  \n        (Defect only when expected net payoff exceeds cooperation AND the projected stock stays above a modest safety floor.)  \n\n   f. **Default** \u2013 cooperate.  \n\n**Stock projection formulas (used for `S_next(C)` and `S_next(D)`)**  \n\n```\nconsumption_i =  S_t/(2n)   // if we cooperate\n               =  S_t/n     // if we defect\ntotal_consumption = consumption_i + c_{-i,t} * (S_t/(2n)) + (n-1-c_{-i,t}) * (S_t/n)\n\nS_remain = S_t - total_consumption\ngrowth   = 2 * S_remain * (1 - S_remain / capacity)\nS_next   = min( S_remain + growth , capacity )\n```\n\nReplace `consumption_i` with the appropriate value (cooperate or defect) to obtain `S_next(C)` or `S_next(D)`.\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n\n- If `S_remain` becomes negative due to rounding, treat it as zero before growth calculation.  \n- If `capacity` is zero (degenerate case), both actions yield zero payoff; cooperate by default.  \n- If audit probability `q = 0`, the expected fine term disappears and the rule reduces to pure stock\u2011sustainability and opponent\u2011cooperation checks.  \n\n**Summary of behavior**  \n- Start and end with cooperation.  \n- Preserve the resource when stock is low or cooperation keeps it above half capacity.  \n- Exploit only when the immediate expected gain outweighs the loss of stock safety and the expected fine, and the community is largely defecting.  \n- Otherwise mirror the observed benevolent behavior of opponents.  "

description_BENEVOLENT_13 = "**Benevolent Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**State variables**\n- `stock` \u2013 current common\u2011pool level observed at the start of the round.  \n- `coop_obs[t]` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in round\u202f`t*` (0\u202f\u2264\u202f`t*\u202f<\u202ft`).  \n- `last_defect` \u2013 Boolean flag indicating whether you defected in the immediately preceding round.  \n- `consec_defect` \u2013 count of consecutive defections you have played (reset to\u202f0 when you cooperate).  \n\n**Parameters (derived from the game description)**\n- `Cap = capacity`  \n- `q = audit_prob`  \n- `F = fine`  \n- `n_players = n`  \n\n**Derived thresholds**\n```text\nhigh_stock   = 0.7 * Cap\nmedium_stock = 0.4 * Cap\nlow_stock    = 0.2 * Cap\ncooperate_rate_threshold_high = 0.6   // proportion of opponents cooperating\ncooperate_rate_threshold_low  = 0.3\nmax_consecutive_defect = 2\n```\n\n**Helper functions**\n- `opp_coop_rate(m)`: average proportion of opponents that cooperated over the last `m` observed rounds (if fewer than `m` rounds have occurred, use all available rounds).  \n- `expected_defect_payoff(S) = S / n_players - q * F`  \n\n**Decision rule (executed each round\u202f`t*)**\n\n1. **First round (`t* = 0`)** \u2013 always **Cooperate (C)**.  \n2. **Last round (`t* = r\u20111`)** \u2013 always **Cooperate (C)** (no future stock to protect, and benevolence favours fair play).  \n3. **Audit\u2011adjusted profitability test**  \n   - If `expected_defect_payoff(stock) <= stock / (2 * n_players)` then **Cooperate (C)** (defecting is not even expected\u2011value\u2011superior to cooperating).  \n4. **Critical stock protection**  \n   - If `stock <= low_stock` then **Cooperate (C)** (preserve the pool).  \n5. **Assess opponent behaviour**  \n   - Let `r = opp_coop_rate(m = min(3, t*))` (average over up to the last three rounds).  \n   - If `r >= cooperate_rate_threshold_high` **and** `stock >= medium_stock` then **Cooperate (C)**.  \n   - Else if `r <= cooperate_rate_threshold_low` **and** `stock >= high_stock` then consider a short\u2011term punishment:\n        - If `consec_defect < max_consecutive_defect` then **Defect (D)**,\n        - otherwise **Cooperate (C)**.  \n   - Else **Cooperate (C)**.  \n\n6. **Update bookkeeping**  \n   - After playing the action, record whether you cooperated or defected, update `last_defect` and `consec_defect` accordingly.  \n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- If `stock` ever becomes `0`, the payoff from any action is `0`; the rule above will default to **Cooperate (C)** because the audit\u2011adjusted profitability test will make defecting unattractive.  \n- When the observed opponent count is unavailable (e.g., before any round has been played), the algorithm falls back to the first\u2011round rule (Cooperate).  \n\n**Benevolent rationale embedded in the rule set**\n- The strategy always gives the pool a chance to recover (steps\u202f3\u20134).  \n- Defection is used only as a brief deterrent when opponents repeatedly exploit the resource and the stock is safely abundant; the deterrent is limited to `max_consecutive_defect` rounds to avoid cascading depletion.  \n- Expected audit fines are explicitly incorporated, preventing profit\u2011driven over\u2011exploitation.  \n- The final round ends with cooperation, ensuring that the last interaction is fair regardless of prior history.  "

description_BENEVOLENT_14 = "**Benevolent Adaptive Cooperation (BAC) Strategy**\n\n**Parameters used**\n- `capacity`, `n`, `r`, `q`, `F` \u2013 taken directly from the game description.  \n- `stock_t` \u2013 common\u2011pool stock observed at the start of round `t`.  \n- `opp_coop_t` \u2013 proportion of opponents that cooperated in round `t\u20111` (computed from the anonymous count of cooperators after round `t\u20111`).  \n- `defect_history` \u2013 number of rounds in which we have defected in the last `K` rounds (fixed sliding window, e.g., `K = 3`).  \n\n**Derived thresholds**\n- `S_safe = 0.5 * capacity`\u2003(stock level above which the pool can sustain full cooperation).  \n- `S_critical = 0.2 * capacity`\u2003(below which urgent conservation is required).  \n- `p_coop_min = 0.6`\u2003(minimum observed opponent cooperation proportion needed to keep cooperating).  \n- `E_fine = q * F`\u2003(expected fine per defection).  \n\n**Decision rule (applied at the start of each round t, 0\u2011indexed)**  \n\n```\nif t == 0:\n    # First round \u2013 establish a cooperative baseline\n    action = C\nelif t == r-1:\n    # Last round \u2013 never defect (no audit, maximal benevolence)\n    action = C\nelse:\n    # Compute effective incentive to cooperate\n    incentive = (stock_t / capacity)                # higher stock \u2192 higher incentive\n    incentive -= E_fine / (stock_t / n if stock_t>0 else 1)   # subtract expected penalty per extra unit from defecting\n    incentive += opp_coop_t - (defect_history / K) # reward recent opponent cooperation, penalize own recent defections\n\n    # Decision thresholds\n    if stock_t <= S_critical:\n        # Stock critically low \u2192 enforce strict conservation\n        action = C\n    elif stock_t >= S_safe and opp_coop_t >= p_coop_min and incentive > 0:\n        # Healthy stock, enough cooperation, and net incentive positive \u2192 cooperate\n        action = C\n    else:\n        # Either stock moderate but opponents are defecting, or incentive negative \u2192 temporary defection\n        action = D\n```\n\n**Post\u2011round updates**\n1. Record own action for the current round.  \n2. Increment `defect_history` if the action was `D`; otherwise decrement it (but never below 0).  \n3. After observing the anonymous count of opponent cooperators, set `opp_coop_t = (number_of_cooperators) / (n\u20111)`.  \n4. Update `stock_t` to the new stock announced for the next round.\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- **Zero stock** (`stock_t = 0`): the payoff from any action is zero; the rule above forces `action = C` because `incentive` becomes non\u2011positive and the first branch (`stock_t <= S_critical`) selects cooperation, preserving the possibility of regrowth.  \n- **Audit probability = 0** (`q = 0`): `E_fine = 0`; the incentive simplifies to pure stock and opponent\u2011cooperation considerations.  \n- **Fine so large that expected loss exceeds any gain** (`E_fine > stock_t / n`): the incentive term becomes negative, driving the strategy to cooperate unless forced defection is needed for stock recovery (which never occurs because cooperation is the most conservative consumption).  \n\n**Benevolent intent**\n- The strategy prioritizes maintaining the stock above `S_safe` and only resorts to defection when the pool is moderately abundant *and* opponent cooperation falls below `p_coop_min`, using defection as a short\u2011term signal rather than exploitation.  \n- Defections are limited to a sliding window of length `K`; after at most `K` consecutive defections the strategy forces a return to cooperation, preventing prolonged over\u2011extraction.  \n- In the final round the agent always cooperates, ensuring the last consumption is the most conservative possible."

description_BENEVOLENT_15 = "**Benevolent Adaptive Cooperation Strategy**\n\n**Parameters (fixed for the match)**\n- `capacity`, `n`, `r`, audit probability `q`, fine `F`.\n\n**Internal state**\n- `stock_t` \u2013 current common\u2011pool stock at the beginning of round\u202f`t`.\n- `trust` \u2013 a real number in \\([0,1]\\) representing the inferred willingness of opponents to cooperate. Initialized to `1.0`.\n- `last_observed_coop` \u2013 proportion of opponents that cooperated in the immediately preceding round (undefined for round\u202f0).\n\n---\n\n### 1. Decision rule (per round\u202f`t`)\n\n```\nif t == r\u20111:                     # last round (no audit)\n    action = C                  # always cooperate\nelse if t == 0:                  # first round\n    action = C                  # start benevolently\nelse:\n    # 1) Update trust\n    observed_coop = last_observed_coop        # fraction of opponents that played C last round\n    trust = 0.9 * trust + 0.1 * observed_coop  # exponential smoothing, keeps trust in [0,1]\n\n    # 2) Compute expected net gain of defecting this round\n    #    (payoff difference minus expected fine)\n    payoff_C   = stock_t / (2*n)\n    payoff_D   = stock_t / n\n    expected_fine = q * F\n    net_gain_D = payoff_D - expected_fine - payoff_C   # >0 if defecting is profitable after fine\n\n    # 3) Determine a safety stock threshold\n    #    Below this level we risk stock collapse; we increase cooperation pressure.\n    safety_threshold = 0.25 * capacity\n\n    # 4) Choose action\n    if stock_t < safety_threshold:\n        # Preserve the pool: cooperate regardless of opponents\n        action = C\n    else:\n        # Blend trust and net gain to decide\n        #   * high trust \u2192 cooperate,\n        #   * high net gain \u2192 defect,\n        #   * otherwise cooperate with probability proportional to trust.\n        cooperate_score = trust - 0.5 * max(net_gain_D,0)   # net_gain_D penalises cooperation\n        prob_cooperate = min( max(cooperate_score, 0.0), 1.0 )\n        action = C with probability prob_cooperate,\n                 D otherwise\n```\n\n*Explanation of the components (kept inside the code for clarity):*\n- **Trust update** smooths recent observations, giving more weight to the latest behavior (10\u202f%).  \n- **Net gain of defecting** subtracts the expected fine (`q\u00b7F`) from the raw payoff advantage of defecting.  \n- **Safety threshold** forces unconditional cooperation when the stock is low, protecting the resource.  \n- **Cooperate probability** is a linear blend of trust and the (penalised) incentive to defect; it never exceeds `[0,1]`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Edge\u2011case handling\n\n| Situation                               | Action taken |\n|----------------------------------------|--------------|\n| **Round\u202f0 (first round)**             | `C` (seed benevolence). |\n| **Round\u202fr\u20111 (final round, never audited)** | `C` (maximises final payoff without affecting any future stock). |\n| **Stock \u2264 0** (pool exhausted)         | `C` (consumption will be zero for everyone; choice is irrelevant). |\n| **Audit outcome (only observed for self)** \u2013 no direct effect on decision rule; the expected fine `q\u00b7F` already captures audit risk. |\n| **Observed opponent cooperation fraction unavailable** (only possible in round\u202f0) \u2013 trust remains at its initial value `1.0`. |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Benevolent orientation\n\n- The strategy **prioritises stock preservation** by obliging cooperation whenever the pool falls below 25\u202f% of capacity.\n- It **encourages mutual cooperation** through the `trust` variable: higher observed cooperation raises the probability of cooperating.\n- It **deterrently accounts for audits** by discounting the raw benefit of defection with the expected fine, reducing the incentive to exploit the pool.\n- The **gradual, probabilistic response** to occasional defections avoids harsh retaliation, maintaining a forgiving stance that favours long\u2011term sustainability."

description_BENEVOLENT_16 = "**Benevolent Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**Parameters known to the agent**  \n`n, r, capacity, audit_prob\u202f(q), fine\u202f(F)`.  \nHistory available after each round `t` (0\u2011indexed):  \n- `stock_t` (current stock before actions).  \n- `obs_coop_t` = number of opponents observed to have played **C** (0\u202f\u2026\u202fn\u20111).  \n- `my_action_t\u20111`, `my_audit_t\u20111` (whether the agent was audited and paid a fine).  \n\n**Derived constants**  \n- Target stock proportion `\u03b8 = 0.5`.  \n- Target stock at round `t`:  \n  `target_t = \u03b8 * capacity * ( (r\u2011t) / r )`\u2003\u2003// linearly decreasing target as the horizon shrinks.  \n- Expected audit cost per defection: `E_fine = q * F`.  \n\n**Decision rule for round t (0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr)**  \n\n```\nif t == 0:\n    # no information, start benevolently\n    action = C\nelse if t == r\u20111:\n    # last round \u2013 no audits, only immediate payoff matters\n    # cooperate if stock is so low that defect would drive it to zero,\n    # otherwise defect for higher payoff\n    if stock_t <= capacity / (2*n):\n        action = C\n    else:\n        action = D\nelse:\n    # 1 \u2264 t \u2264 r\u20112 : adaptive decision\n    # 1) Estimate opponents' average action\n    coop_rate = obs_coop_t / (n\u20111)                 # fraction of opponents that cooperated\n    # 2) Expected per\u2011opponent consumption if we follow each option\n    #    (others' mix is kept as observed)\n    exp_cons_C = stock_t/(2*n) * coop_rate + stock_t/n * (1\u2011coop_rate)   // our consumption = C\n    exp_cons_D = stock_t/n * coop_rate + stock_t/n * (1\u2011coop_rate)     // our consumption = D\n\n    # 3) Project stock after our action (including growth)\n    proj_stock_C = min( (stock_t - (stock_t/(2*n) + (n\u20111)*[stock_t/(2n) if opponent C else stock_t/n])) \n                         * (1)   // placeholder for total consumption calculation\n                         + 2 * (stock_t - total_cons_C) * (1 - (stock_t - total_cons_C)/capacity),\n                         capacity )\n    proj_stock_D = analogous using total_cons_D\n\n    # 4) Feasibility check: keep projected stock \u2265 target_t ?\n    feasible_C = proj_stock_C >= target_t\n    feasible_D = proj_stock_D >= target_t\n\n    # 5) Expected net payoff\n    payoff_C = stock_t/(2*n)                         // no fine possible\n    payoff_D = stock_t/n - E_fine\n\n    # 6) Choose action\n    if feasible_C and ( not feasible_D or payoff_C >= payoff_D ):\n        action = C\n    elif feasible_D:\n        action = D\n    else:\n        # both would breach the target \u2013 sacrifice personal payoff to protect stock\n        action = C\n```\n\n**Explanation of calculations used in the rule**\n\n- `total_cons_C` = our consumption (`stock_t/(2n)`) + expected consumption of opponents:\n  ` (n\u20111) * [ coop_rate * stock_t/(2n) + (1\u2011coop_rate) * stock_t/n ]`.\n- `total_cons_D` = our consumption (`stock_t/n`) + same opponent term.\n- The growth step follows the game definition:\n  `growth = 2 * (stock_after_consumption) * (1 - stock_after_consumption / capacity)`.\n- The projected stock is `min(stock_after_consumption + growth, capacity)`.\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n- **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0):** cooperate unconditionally to seed a high stock and signal benevolence.\n- **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111):** audits are absent; cooperate only when the remaining stock is too low to sustain a defection (i.e., defect would consume the entire stock). Otherwise defect to obtain the higher immediate payoff.\n- **Zero or near\u2011zero stock:** if `stock_t` \u2264 `1e\u20116`, any consumption yields zero; the strategy defaults to **C** to avoid unnecessary fines.\n- **Audit probability zero (q\u202f=\u202f0):** `E_fine` becomes zero, so the comparison reduces to payoff vs. stock\u2011target feasibility.\n- **Fine so large that expected net payoff of D < 0:** the rule will automatically prefer C whenever feasible.\n\n**Benevolent intent**\n\nThe strategy always prefers an action that keeps the projected stock at or above a linearly decreasing target, thereby preserving the common pool for future rounds and for other players. Defection is taken only when it does not jeopardize the target stock and when the expected net payoff (after accounting for audit risk) exceeds cooperation. In situations where either action would breach the target, the agent sacrifices its own payoff and cooperates to protect the resource."

description_COLLECTIVE_1 = "**Collective Adaptive Strategy (CAP\u2011S)**  \n\n**Parameters known to the agent**: n, r, capacity, q, F.  \n\n**State variables maintained each round t**  \n- `S_t` \u2013 current stock (observed at start of round).  \n- `c_{t\u20111}` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in previous round (derived from aggregate observation).  \n- `defect_history` \u2013 list of own past actions.  \n- `audit_history` \u2013 list of own audit outcomes (0/1).  \n\n**Derived quantities**  \n- `p\u0302_t = c_{t\u20111} / (n\u20111)` \u2013 empirical cooperation rate of opponents in last round (undefined for t=0).  \n- `E_fine = q\u00b7F` \u2013 expected fine per defection.  \n- `\u0394payoff = S_t/(2n)` (cooperate) vs `S_t/n \u2013 a_i\u00b7F` (defect). Expected net gain from defecting = `S_t/(2n) \u2013 E_fine`.  \n\n**Decision Rules**\n\n1. **First round (t = 0)**  \n   - Play **C** (cooperate) to signal collective intent and gather baseline cooperation data.\n\n2. **Last round (t = r\u20111)** \u2013 never audited:  \n   - If `S_t` > 0 **and** `p\u0302_t \u2265 \u03c4_low` (see below), play **C** to preserve remaining stock for possible future interactions (even though game ends, cooperative reputation may affect opponent behavior in earlier rounds).  \n   - Otherwise, play **D** if `S_t` is sufficiently high to make the immediate gain outweigh any reputational loss:  \n     `if S_t \u2265 \u03c4_defect_last \u2192 D else C`.  \n   - Set `\u03c4_defect_last = capacity\u00b70.5` (defect only when stock \u2265 50\u202f% of capacity).\n\n3. **Intermediate rounds (0 < t < r\u20111)**  \n\n   a. **Compute expected net benefit of defecting**  \n      `gain_defect = S_t/(2n) \u2013 E_fine`.  \n\n   b. **Compute collective risk threshold**  \n      - Let `\u03c4_stock = capacity\u00b70.3`. If `S_t < \u03c4_stock`, the pool is endangered; enforce cooperation regardless of gain.  \n      - Let `\u03c4_coop = 0.6`. If `p\u0302_t \u2265 \u03c4_coop` (opponents are mostly cooperative), be willing to defect only if `gain_defect > 0`.  \n\n   c. **Dynamic cooperation trigger**  \n      - Maintain a sliding window of the last `w = min(3, t)` rounds of opponent cooperation rates. Compute `p\u0302_window = average(p\u0302_{t\u2011k})` for k=1..w.  \n      - Define a lower cooperation confidence threshold `\u03c4_low = 0.4`.  \n\n   d. **Action selection**  \n\n      ```\n      if S_t < \u03c4_stock:\n          action = C                      # protect the pool\n      else if gain_defect <= 0:\n          action = C                      # defect not worth expected fine\n      else if p\u0302_window >= \u03c4_coop:\n          # opponents are cooperative; can safely defect for extra gain\n          action = D\n      else if p\u0302_window < \u03c4_low:\n          # opponents are largely defecting; cooperate to avoid collapse\n          action = C\n      else:\n          # mixed environment: use probabilistic mix weighted by trust\n          prob_defect = (p\u0302_window - \u03c4_low) / (\u03c4_coop - \u03c4_low)\n          action = D with probability prob_defect, else C\n      ```\n\n4. **Audit feedback adjustment**  \n   - After each round, update `audit_history`. If an audit occurred (`a_i = 1`) and the round\u2019s payoff was reduced by `F`, increment a penalty counter `penalty_cnt`.  \n   - If `penalty_cnt / len(audit_history) > 0.2` (i.e., >20\u202f% of audited defections were fined), raise `\u03c4_coop` by 0.1 for subsequent rounds to become more conservative.\n\n5. **Stock\u2011driven end\u2011game safeguard**  \n   - If at any round `S_t \u2264 capacity\u00b70.1` (stock \u2264 10\u202f% capacity), set `forced_cooperate = True` for all remaining rounds (including last). Override all other rules and play C to prevent irreversible collapse.\n\n6. **Edge\u2011case handling**  \n   - If `n = 2`, treat opponent cooperation rate as `c_{t\u20111}` (0 or 1) and use the same thresholds.  \n   - If `q = 0` (no audits), `E_fine = 0`; the strategy reduces to pure stock\u2011based rule: defect when `S_t \u2265 \u03c4_stock` and opponents appear cooperative (`p\u0302_window \u2265 \u03c4_coop`).  \n   - If `F = 0` but `q > 0`, `E_fine = 0`; same as above.  \n\n**Summary of thresholds** (constants unless adjusted by audit feedback)  \n- `\u03c4_stock = 0.3\u00b7capacity` (protective stock level)  \n- `\u03c4_coop = 0.6` (high cooperation confidence)  \n- `\u03c4_low  = 0.4` (low cooperation confidence)  \n- `\u03c4_defect_last = 0.5\u00b7capacity`  \n\nThe strategy thus starts cooperatively, adapts its willingness to defect based on observed opponent behavior, current stock health, and expected audit penalties, while enforcing a hard protection rule when the commons become scarce."

description_COLLECTIVE_2 = "**Strategy: Stock\u2011Guarded Generous Tit\u2011for\u2011Tol (SG\u2011GTT)**  \n\n**Parameters (computed once from the game description)**  \n- `q` = audit probability, `F` = fine.  \n- `E_fine = q * F` (expected fine per defection).  \n- `\u03c4_low = 0.30 * capacity`\u2003(low\u2011stock threshold)  \n- `\u03c4_high = 0.70 * capacity`\u2003(high\u2011stock threshold)  \n- `\u03b1 = 0.2`\u2003(tolerance for opponent defection rate).  \n\n**State variables (updated each round)**  \n- `S` = current stock (observed at start of round).  \n- `last_coop_rate` = proportion of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (0 if first round).  \n- `retaliation_counter` = number of future rounds to keep defecting as retaliation (initially 0).  \n\n**Decision rule (executed simultaneously by each player at the start of a round t)**  \n\n```\nif t == r-1:                     # last round, no audit risk\n    action = C if S < \u03c4_low else D\nelse:\n    # 1. Determine baseline incentive\n    #    Defect is worthwhile only if the expected fine does not outweigh the extra\n    #    consumption the player would obtain by defecting.\n    #    Extra consumption = S/(2n)\n    #    Condition: E_fine <= S/(2n)\n    incentive_ok = (E_fine <= S/(2n))\n\n    # 2. Adjust for stock level\n    if S < \u03c4_low:\n        # stock is fragile \u2013 preserve it\n        action = C\n    elif S > \u03c4_high and not incentive_ok:\n        # stock abundant but fine makes defect unattractive\n        action = C\n    else:\n        # 3. React to opponent behaviour unless already retaliating\n        if retaliation_counter > 0:\n            action = D\n            retaliation_counter -= 1\n        else:\n            # opponent defection rate above tolerance?\n            if last_coop_rate < (1 - \u03b1):\n                # cooperate generously: still cooperate but signal mild retaliation\n                action = D\n                retaliation_counter = 1   # defect only next round\n            else:\n                action = C\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n- **Round\u202f0 (first round)**: `last_coop_rate` is undefined, treat it as 1 (no known defectors); the rule therefore selects `C` unless `S > \u03c4_high` and `E_fine > S/(2n)`, in which case it may select `D`.  \n- **Retaliation**: When a player defects because opponents\u2019 cooperation fell below the tolerance, it automatically defects for exactly one subsequent round (`retaliation_counter = 1`). After that it returns to the baseline rule, ensuring limited punishment and encouraging opponents to raise their cooperation.  \n- **Audit\u2011free final round**: Because no fines can be imposed, the player simply chooses the action that maximizes immediate payoff given the current stock: defect if the stock is high (`S \u2265 \u03c4_low`), otherwise cooperate to avoid depleting the pool completely.  \n\n**Collective orientation**  \n- The rule makes cooperation the default whenever the stock is low or the expected fine makes defection unattractive, thereby protecting the common pool.  \n- Defection is used only as a short\u2011term signal when opponents collectively over\u2011defect, never as a sustained exploitative strategy.  \n- The thresholds (`\u03c4_low`, `\u03c4_high`) and tolerance (`\u03b1`) are fixed constants derived from the game parameters, so the policy adapts automatically to any `n`, `capacity`, `q`, `F`, and to the observed evolution of the stock and opponent behavior."

description_COLLECTIVE_3 = "**Strategy \u201cCollective Safeguard\u201d**\n\n**Parameters used**\n- n, r, capacity, q (audit probability), F (fine) \u2013 read from the game description.\n-\u202fT\u202f=\u202fmax(\u202f2\u00b7n\u00b7q\u00b7F\u202f,\u202fcapacity\u00b70.3\u202f)\u2003\u2003   //minimum stock at which defection is worth the expected fine\n-\u202f\u03b1\u202f=\u202f0.05\u202f//minimum allowed stock share before forced cooperation (5\u202f% of capacity)\n\n**State variables (kept internally)**\n- `stock_t`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// stock level at start of round t\n- `coop_history` \u2190 empty list\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// stores own action each past round\n- `opp_coop_counts` \u2190 empty list\u2003\u2003\u2003// stores observed number of opponent cooperators each past round\n\n**Decision rule for round\u202ft (0\u2011indexed)**  \n\n```\nif t == r\u20111:                     // last round never audited\n    action = D\nelse if stock_t <= \u03b1*capacity:  // stock critically low\n    action = C\nelse if stock_t >= T:\n    // Expected net payoff of defecting (including expected fine) exceeds cooperation\n    // but we still consider opponent behaviour to avoid collapse\n    if average(opp_coop_counts[-k:]) \u2265 n/2   // k = min(3, t) recent rounds, default 0 if t<1\n        action = D\n    else\n        action = C\nelse:\n    // Stock below the expected\u2011fine break\u2011even point \u2192 cooperate to protect pool\n    action = C\n```\n\n**Explanation of variables in the rule**\n\n- `average(opp_coop_counts[-k:])` is the mean number of opponents that cooperated in the last\u202fk\u202fobserved rounds (k =\u202f3 unless fewer rounds have occurred).  \n- The rule \u201cdefect only if a majority of opponents have recently cooperated\u201d prevents unilateral over\u2011exploitation when others are already defecting.  \n- When the stock is critically low (`\u2264\u202f\u03b1*capacity`) the player always cooperates, guaranteeing the smallest possible consumption per round and allowing the growth term to restore the pool.  \n- In the final round the player defects because no audit can penalize it and the remaining stock is fully exploitable.\n\n**Updates after each round t (t < r\u20111)**\n\n1. Record own action in `coop_history`.  \n2. Record observed opponent cooperation count (0 \u2026 n\u20111) in `opp_coop_counts`.  \n3. Update `stock_t+1` using the supplied stock dynamics (no need to recompute; the environment supplies it at start of next round).  \n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n- **Round\u202f0 (first round):** `stock_0 = capacity`. Since `stock_0` is usually \u2265\u202fT, the rule falls to the \u201cmajority\u2011cooperate\u201d branch; with no history (`k=0`) the condition defaults to *true*, so the player defects in round\u202f0.  \n- **Rounds where `stock_t` becomes exactly 0:** The rule forces cooperation because `stock_t \u2264 \u03b1*capacity`. Consumption will be zero, keeping the stock at 0; the growth term will also be 0, so the game ends with zero payoff for everyone \u2013 the rule avoids unnecessary defection that cannot improve payoff.  \n- **Rounds with no opponents observed (n=1):** The majority\u2011cooperate check is vacuous; the player follows the stock\u2011threshold branches.  \n\n**Collective alignment**\n\nThe strategy prioritises maintaining the common pool above a safety margin (`\u03b1*capacity`) and only exploits when the pool is abundant *and* the majority of opponents are already cooperating, thereby sharing the benefit without triggering collapse. It adapts each round to the observed cooperation level and to the current stock, making it robust against a wide range of opponent behaviors."

description_COLLECTIVE_4 = "**Strategy \u201cSustainable Collective\u2011Threshold (SCT)\u201d**\n\n---\n\n### 1. Parameter\u2011derived thresholds  \n\n* **Safety buffer**\u2003`B = \u03b1\u00b7capacity`\u2003with `\u03b1 = 0.5` (adjustable).  \n* **Cooperation tolerance**\u2003`\u03b8 = 0.6` \u2013 minimum observed cooperation share among opponents that justifies cooperating.  \n* **Defection profitability margin**\u2003`\u0394 = (stock / n) \u2212 q\u00b7F \u2212 (stock / (2n))` \u2013 expected extra payoff from defecting after accounting for the audit\u2011expected fine.  \n\n---\n\n### 2. Decision function (applied each round *t*, 0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr)  \n\n```\ninput: t, stock S_t, history H (my past actions, opponent cooperation counts), audit probability q, fine F\noutput: action \u2208 {C, D}\n\n/*--- Edge\u2011case handling ---------------------------------------------------*/\nif t == 0 then                      // first round\n    return C                       // seed cooperation, no information yet\nif t == r\u20111 then                    // last round (never audited)\n    if \u0394 > 0 then return D else return C\n/*-----------------------------------------------------------------------*/\n\n/*--- Compute current state indicators -----------------------------------*/\nobsCoop = (opponents_cooperated_last_round) / (n\u20111)   // from H, 0\u20261\n\u0394 = (S_t / n) - q\u00b7F - (S_t / (2\u00b7n))                 // expected net gain of D\n\n/*--- Decision logic ------------------------------------------------------*/\nif S_t < B then                     // stock below safety buffer \u2192 protect pool\n    return C\nelse if obsCoop < \u03b8 then           // opponents have been insufficiently cooperative\n    // punish low cooperation, but keep stock safe\n    if \u0394 > 0 and S_t - (S_t / n) >= 0 then\n        return D\n    else\n        return C\nelse                                 // stock healthy and opponents mostly cooperative\n    if \u0394 > 0 then\n        // occasional defection is profitable; limit its frequency\n        if (t mod K) == 0 then      // K = floor( r\u00b70.2 ), i.e. defect at most 20\u202f% of rounds\n            return D\n        else\n            return C\n    else\n        return C\n```\n\n* `K` is a constant derived from the total horizon (`K = max(1, floor(r\u00b70.2))`). This caps defect frequency to \u2264\u202f20\u202f% when defection is profitable, preserving the collective stock.  \n* All arithmetic uses the current **stock** `S_t`; the stock update is performed by the game engine after actions are taken.\n\n---\n\n### 3. History\u2011based adaptation  \n\n* After each round the agent records the number of opponents that cooperated (`c_t`).  \n* The **observed cooperation share** `obsCoop` is recomputed each round using the most recent `c_{t\u20111}`.  \n* If `obsCoop` stays below `\u03b8` for three consecutive rounds, the agent **escalates** punishment by defecting every round until `obsCoop` rises back above `\u03b8`.  \n* Conversely, if `obsCoop` exceeds `\u03b8` for three consecutive rounds, the agent **relaxes** to the base 20\u202f% defection schedule.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Summary of action triggers  \n\n| Situation                               | Action |\n|----------------------------------------|--------|\n| First round                              | **C** |\n| Stock <\u202f`B`                              | **C** |\n| Opponents\u2019 recent cooperation <\u202f`\u03b8`      | **D** if `\u0394>0`, else **C** |\n| Stock \u2265\u202f`B`, opponents cooperative, `\u0394>0` | **D** on scheduled \u201cdefect\u2011slot\u201d (\u2264\u202f20\u202f% of rounds) |\n| Stock \u2265\u202f`B`, opponents cooperative, `\u0394\u22640`| **C** |\n| Last round                               | **D** if `\u0394>0`, else **C** |\n\nThe strategy therefore:  \n\n* protects the common pool when the resource is low,  \n* rewards consistent collective cooperation,  \n* exploits profitable defections only when they are unlikely to jeopardize the stock or trigger sustained retaliation,  \n* uses audit risk (`q\u00b7F`) to temper defection incentives, and  \n* adapts dynamically to the observed cooperation level of the anonymous opponents."

description_COLLECTIVE_5 = "**Strategy: Adaptive Collective Stewardship (ACS)**  \n\n**State variables (available each round\u202ft):**  \n- `S` \u2013 current stock (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity)  \n- `t` \u2013 round index (0 \u2026\u202fr\u20111)  \n- `obsCoop` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (0 \u2026\u202fn\u20111)  \n- `p = obsCoop / (n\u20111)` \u2013 observed cooperation proportion (undefined in round\u202f0)  \n- game parameters `n, r, capacity, q, F`  \n\n**Decision rule (choose action\u202fA \u2208 {C,\u202fD}):**\n\n```\nif t == r\u20111:                         # last round, never audited\n    A = D                           # maximize immediate payoff\nelif t == 0:                         # no history yet\n    A = C                           # seed cooperation\nelse:\n    # 1. Compute baseline expected payoffs\n    Gc = S / (2*n)                               # payoff from cooperating\n    Gd = S / n - q * F                           # expected payoff from defecting (includes fine)\n\n    # 2. Stock\u2011sustainability thresholds\n    lowStock   = 0.30 * capacity                 # below this, stock is endangered\n    highStock  = 0.80 * capacity                 # above this, stock is healthy\n    coopTarget = S / capacity                    # desired cooperation share (0\u20131)\n\n    # 3. Primary test: is defecting not profitable even after expected fine?\n    if Gd <= Gc:\n        A = C                                   # cooperate unconditionally\n    else:\n        # 4. Conditional cooperation based on observed behavior and stock level\n        if S <= lowStock:\n            A = C                               # preserve stock, ignore opponent behavior\n        elif S >= highStock and p >= coopTarget:\n            A = C                               # stock is healthy and opponents are cooperating enough\n        else:\n            A = D                               # defect to gain when cooperation is low or stock is moderate\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling:**  \n\n- **Stock = 0** (or effectively zero): both actions yield zero payoff; the rule above chooses `C` because `Gd` = 0\u202f\u2212\u202fq\u202fF\u202f\u2264\u202f0\u202f=\u202fGc, satisfying the first test.  \n- **Audit probability q = 0** or **fine F = 0**: `Gd` simplifies to `S/n`; the primary test reduces to `S/n \u2264 S/(2n)`, which never holds, so the strategy follows the conditional branch, defecting unless the stock is low or opponent cooperation meets the target.  \n- **Tie (`Gd == Gc`)**: cooperate, reinforcing the collective orientation.  \n\n**Collective alignment:**  \n- The rule prioritizes cooperation whenever defecting is not strictly better after accounting for expected fines.  \n- When the stock is endangered (`S \u2264 lowStock`) the agent cooperates regardless of opponents, preventing collapse.  \n- In healthy stock conditions the agent cooperates only if the observed cooperation share meets the proportion required to keep the stock near capacity (`p \u2265 S/capacity`). This creates a self\u2011reinforcing collective norm: sustained cooperation is rewarded, chronic defection triggers retaliation.  \n\nThe strategy depends solely on publicly known parameters, the observable stock level, and the agent\u2019s own audit history (via `q` and `F`). It adapts each round to the evolving environment and opponent behavior, aiming to maximize long\u2011run payoff while safeguarding the common pool."

description_COLLECTIVE_6 = "**Strategy \u201cAdaptive Collective Threshold\u201d**\n\n**Parameters derived from the game description**  \n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `audit_prob`\u202f(`q`), `fine`\u202f(`F`) are known constants.  \n- `stock_t` \u2013 the common\u2011pool stock at the beginning of round\u202f`t`.  \n- `opp_coop_t` \u2013 the number of opponents that cooperated in round\u202f`t\u20111` (observed after each round).  \n\n**Derived thresholds**  \n\n1. **Stock safety threshold**  \n   \\[\n   S_{\\text{safe}} = \\frac{capacity}{2}\n   \\]  \n   (If the stock falls below this level the collective risk of depletion is high.)\n\n2. **Cooperation confidence threshold**  \n   \\[\n   p_{\\text{conf}} = \\frac{1}{1 + \\frac{qF}{\\frac{stock_t}{2n}}}\n   \\]  \n   This is the minimum recent cooperation proportion that makes cooperating expected\u2011payoff\u2011wise at least as good as defecting, accounting for the expected fine.  \n\n**Decision rule (applied each round\u202f`t**,\u202f0\u00a0\u2264\u00a0t\u00a0<\u00a0r)**  \n\n```\nif t == r-1:                     # last round \u2013 never audited, but keep collective posture\n    action = C\nelse:\n    # 1. Estimate recent cooperation level\n    if t == 0:\n        recent_coop = 1.0        # assume full cooperation initially\n    else:\n        recent_coop = opp_coop_t / (n-1)\n\n    # 2. Choose action based on two conditions\n    if stock_t >= S_safe and recent_coop >= p_conf:\n        action = C                # cooperate\n    else:\n        action = D                # defect\n```\n\n**Stock update (internal, not a decision)**  \nAfter all players act, the stock evolves exactly as defined by the game; the strategy reads the resulting `stock_{t+1}` for the next round.\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n\n- **Round\u202f0**: `recent_coop` is set to\u202f1, guaranteeing cooperation in the first round.  \n- **Round\u202fr\u20111** (final round): always cooperate regardless of stock or observed behavior, because no audit occurs and the collective goal is to leave the pool undamaged.  \n- **Zero stock** (`stock_t == 0`): both actions yield zero consumption; the rule defaults to cooperation because `stock_t < S_safe` forces the `else` branch, i.e. defect. In this degenerate case the player defects (no loss from defecting).  \n- **Audit\u2011free rounds** (`q == 0`): `p_conf` reduces to 1, so the player cooperates only when the observed cooperation proportion is perfect; otherwise it defects.  \n\n**Collective alignment**  \nThe strategy cooperates whenever the pool is sufficiently healthy **and** recent opponent behavior signals that cooperation is collectively sustainable after accounting for expected fines. Defection is used only as a protective response to low stock or to a breakdown in mutual cooperation, thereby preserving the common resource for the remainder of the game."

description_COLLECTIVE_7 = "**Strategy Name:** Adaptive Sustainable Threshold (AST)\n\n**Parameters used in the algorithm**  \n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `q`, `F` \u2013 taken from the game description.  \n- `\u03b8 = 0.6` \u2013 baseline safety fraction of capacity (tunable).  \n- `\u03b3 = 0.1` \u2013 decay factor that tightens the safety threshold as the horizon shortens.  \n\n**State variables (maintained locally)**  \n- `stock_t` \u2013 current common\u2011pool stock at the beginning of round\u202f`t`.  \n- `coop_obs_t` \u2013 number of opponents observed to have cooperated in round\u202f`t\u20111` (0 for `t=0`).  \n- `defect_count` \u2013 cumulative count of opponent defections observed so far.  \n\n**Decision rule for round\u202f`t` (0\u2011indexed)**  \n\n```\nif t == r\u20111:                     # last round, never audited\n    action = D                   # defect for maximal one\u2011shot payoff\nelse:\n    # 1. Expected net payoff from defecting (including expected fine)\n    exp_defect = stock_t / n - q * F\n\n    # 2. Payoff from cooperating\n    coop_pay   = stock_t / (2*n)\n\n    # 3. Safety threshold based on stock sustainability\n    #    Desired minimum stock that can support cooperative consumption\n    #    for the remaining rounds without falling below 0.\n    remaining_rounds = r - t\n    safety_fraction   = max(\u03b8, 1 - \u03b3 * (remaining_rounds / r))   # becomes stricter later\n    safety_stock      = capacity * safety_fraction\n\n    # 4. Collective\u2010trust indicator\n    #    Proportion of opponents that cooperated in the previous round.\n    #    If no history, assume full cooperation.\n    if t == 0:\n        trust = 1.0\n    else:\n        trust = coop_obs_t / (n\u20111)\n\n    # 5. Decision logic\n    if exp_defect <= coop_pay:                     # fine makes defect unattractive\n        action = C\n    elif stock_t <= safety_stock:                 # stock already low, preserve it\n        action = C\n    elif trust < 0.4:                              # many opponents defected last round\n        action = D\n    elif stock_t > 2*n*q*F:                        # defect yields higher net payoff\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C\n```\n\n**Updating after each round**  \n\n1. Record your own audit result `a_i,t` and incurred fine (if any).  \n2. Observe `k =` number of opponents that cooperated (the game reveals only the count).  \n   - Set `coop_obs_{t+1} = k`.  \n3. Update `stock_t` to the new stock produced by the game dynamics before the next decision.  \n4. Increment `defect_count` by `(n\u20111) - k` (total opponent defections observed).  \n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n\n- **Round\u202f0**: No opponent history, assume full cooperation (`trust = 1`).  \n- **Round\u202fr\u20111** (final): No audit risk; always defect to capture the remaining stock, since future sustainability is irrelevant.  \n- **Zero stock**: If `stock_t == 0`, both actions yield 0 payoff; choose `C` to signal cooperation (no penalty for auditing).  \n- **Audit probability 0 (`q = 0`)**: The rule `exp_defect <= coop_pay` reduces to `stock_t / n <= stock_t / (2*n)`, which never holds; the decision then follows the safety\u2011threshold and trust clauses.  \n\n**Collective orientation**  \n\nThe algorithm cooperates whenever the expected net gain from defection is not strictly higher than cooperation, when the common stock falls below a dynamically tightened safety level, or when recent opponent behavior indicates broad cooperation. Defection is reserved for situations where the expected monetary advantage outweighs the collective cost, the stock is comfortably abundant, and opponent trust is low. This pattern preserves the pool for as many future rounds as possible while still exploiting profitable opportunities when they are statistically justified."

description_COLLECTIVE_8 = "**Collective Adaptive Strategy (CAS)**  \n\n**Parameters (set from game description)**\n- `n` \u2013 number of players  \n- `r` \u2013 total rounds, indexed `t = 0 \u2026 r\u20111`  \n- `capacity` \u2013 maximal stock  \n- `q` \u2013 audit probability (per\u2011round, except last)  \n- `F` \u2013 fine per audited defection  \n\n**Derived thresholds (fixed fractions, can be tuned)**\n- `\u03b8_stock = 0.5`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// cooperate only if stock \u2265\u202f\u03b8_stock\u00b7capacity  \n- `\u03b8_defect = 0.3`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// tolerate up to 30\u202f% observed defectors among opponents  \n- `\u03b8_future = 2`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// minimum rounds remaining to justify cooperation (allows exploitation in the final few rounds)  \n\n**State variables (maintained each round)**\n- `S_t` \u2013 current stock before consumption (observed)  \n- `opp_coop_t` \u2013 number of opponents observed cooperating in round *t* (0\u202f\u2026\u202fn\u20111)  \n- `opp_defect_t = (n\u20111) - opp_coop_t`  \n- `defect_ratio_t = opp_defect_t / (n\u20111)` (undefined in first round, treat as 0)  \n- `rounds_left = r - t`  \n\n**Decision rule (run at the start of each round t)**  \n\n```\nif t == r-1:                     # LAST ROUND (never audited)\n    action = D                   # maximize immediate payoff\nelse:\n    # 1. Stock condition\n    stock_ok = (S_t >= \u03b8_stock * capacity)\n\n    # 2. Observed defection tolerance\n    defection_ok = (defect_ratio_t <= \u03b8_defect)\n\n    # 3. Future\u2011round incentive\n    future_ok = (rounds_left > \u03b8_future)\n\n    if stock_ok and defection_ok and future_ok:\n        action = C               # cooperate\n    else:\n        # compute expected net gain of defecting vs cooperating\n        expected_gain = (S_t / n) - (S_t / (2*n))          # extra consumption\n        expected_fine = q * F                             # expected fine (last round excluded)\n        net_gain = expected_gain - expected_fine\n\n        if net_gain > 0:\n            action = D\n        else:\n            action = C               # cooperate if fine outweighs extra gain\n```\n\n**History updates (after round t)**\n1. Record `opp_coop_t` (derived from aggregate observation).  \n2. Record whether you were audited (`a_i,t`) and any fine paid.  \n3. Update `S_{t+1}` using the stock dynamics supplied by the game engine.  \n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n- **Round\u202f0:** `defect_ratio_0` is undefined; treat it as 0 so the initial decision follows the stock and future conditions.  \n- **Rounds where `rounds_left \u2264 \u03b8_future`:** cooperation is suppressed unless the stock is high *and* observed defection is low, because the remaining horizon is too short to justify the collective sacrifice.  \n- **When `q = 0` (no audits):** the `net_gain` term reduces to the pure extra consumption; the rule will automatically defect whenever `stock_ok` or `defection_ok` fails.  \n- **When `F` is very large:** the `net_gain` check will favor cooperation even if stock/defection conditions are marginal, protecting the pool from catastrophic depletion.  \n\n**Collective alignment**  \n- The strategy cooperates **only while** the common stock is sustainably high, the group\u2019s observable behavior remains largely cooperative, and enough future rounds exist for the collective benefit to materialize.  \n- It switches to defection **only** when the environment (low stock, many defectors, or imminent game end) makes continued cooperation uneconomical, or when the expected fine makes defection unprofitable.  \n- By continuously re\u2011evaluating the three collective indicators (`stock_ok`, `defection_ok`, `future_ok`) the agent adapts to opponent behavior, penalizes widespread free\u2011riding, and protects the resource from collapse."

description_COLLECTIVE_9 = "**Strategy \u201cAdaptive Collective Stewardship\u201d**\n\n**Parameters (known to the agent)**\n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `q`, `F`\n- `stock_t` \u2013 stock at the start of round\u202f`t`\n- `opp_coop_cnt_t` \u2013 number of opponents that played\u202fC in round\u202f`t` (observed after the round)\n\n**Derived constants**\n- `C_gain(S) = S/(2n)`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\n- `D_gain(S) = S/n`\n- `ExpFine = q * F`\n\n**Decision rule for round\u202f`t** (0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr)**\n\n```\nif t == r-1:                                   # last round, never audited\n    if D_gain(stock_t) > C_gain(stock_t):\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C\nelse:\n    # 1. Compute expected net payoff of defecting this round\n    exp_D = D_gain(stock_t) - ExpFine\n\n    # 2. Compute collective sustainability metric\n    #    Target stock to keep future rounds viable\n    target_stock = capacity * 0.5                # can be tuned\n\n    # 3. Estimate opponent cooperation level this round\n    opp_coop_ratio = opp_coop_cnt_t / (n-1)      # 0 \u2026 1\n\n    # 4. Adaptive thresholds\n    #    a) If stock is high enough and expected defect payoff exceeds cooperate payoff,\n    #       defect with probability proportional to excess.\n    #    b) If stock is low or opponents are mostly cooperative, cooperate.\n    if stock_t >= target_stock and exp_D > C_gain(stock_t):\n        # defect probability grows with both excess payoff and opponent cooperation (to punish free\u2011riders)\n        excess = exp_D - C_gain(stock_t)                     # >0\n        p_defect = min(1, excess / (D_gain(stock_t) + 1e-9)   # scale\n                       * (1 - opp_coop_ratio) + 0.1)         # baseline\n        action = D with probability p_defect, else C\n    else:\n        # Preserve stock; cooperate unless opponents are overwhelmingly defecting\n        if opp_coop_ratio < 0.25 and stock_t < target_stock:\n            # stock low and few cooperators \u2192 safe\u2011defect to salvage immediate payoff\n            action = D\n        else:\n            action = C\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n- **Round\u202f0 (first round):** `stock_0 = capacity`. The rule above yields `action = C` because `stock_0 \u2265 target_stock` but `exp_D`\u2011`C_gain` is modest; the computed `p_defect` will be low, effectively cooperating.\n- **Round\u202fr\u20111 (final round):** Audits are impossible; choose the pure payoff\u2011maximising action (`D` if `D_gain > C_gain`, otherwise `C`).\n- **Stock exhaustion (`stock_t = 0`):** Both `C_gain` and `D_gain` are zero; `exp_D = -ExpFine \u2264 0`. The rule forces `action = C` (no loss from fine) and keeps stock at zero.\n- **Unexpected opponent pattern (e.g., all defect):** `opp_coop_ratio = 0`; the defect probability term becomes larger, allowing the agent to shift to defecting earlier, but still respecting the `target_stock` safeguard.\n\n**State updates (internal, not sent to opponents)**\n\nAfter each round the agent records:\n- `stock_{t+1}` using the prescribed dynamics.\n- `opp_coop_cnt_t` (derived from aggregate observation).\n- Whether it was audited and fine paid (to compute `ExpFine` if `q` or `F` were unknown \u2013 here they are known, so only for consistency).\n\nThe strategy continuously balances immediate expected profit from defection against the collective need to keep the stock above the safety threshold, adapting its defect probability to both the current stock level and the observed cooperativeness of the others."

description_COLLECTIVE_10 = "**Strategy Overview**\n\nThe agent follows a state\u2011based trigger rule that balances three goals: (1) keep the common stock above a safety reserve needed for the remaining rounds, (2) exploit high\u2011stock, low\u2011audit situations when defection is clearly profitable, and (3) punish persistent defection by opponents to deter free\u2011riding.\n\n---\n\n### Parameters computed each round *t* (0\u2011indexed)\n\n```\nremaining   = r - t                 # rounds left including current\nS           = current stock level\n\u03b8          = safety_factor(remaining)   # see below\nT_stock    = capacity * \u03b8                # target minimum stock to preserve\nE_D        = S / n - audit_prob * fine   # expected payoff from defecting\nE_C        = S / (2*n)                   # payoff from cooperating (no fine)\np_defect   = observed_defect_ratio        # fraction of opponents that defected last round\n\u03c4_defect   = defect_tolerance(remaining) # max tolerated opponent defection rate\n```\n\n**Safety factor** `\u03b8` is chosen to guarantee enough stock for the *minimal* feasible consumption in the remaining rounds (all players cooperate). A simple linear schedule works:\n\n```\n\u03b8 = max( 0.2 , remaining / r )   # never drop below 20\u202f% of capacity, and increase linearly as end approaches\n```\n\n**Defect tolerance** `\u03c4_defect` mirrors the safety factor, allowing stricter punishment when many rounds remain:\n\n```\n\u03c4_defect = 0.4 * (remaining / r)   # e.g. 40\u202f% when many rounds left, 0\u202f% in the final round\n```\n\n---\n\n### Decision Rule (applied after observing the previous round)\n\n```\nif t == 0:\n    action = C                     # always start by cooperating\nelif t == r-1:\n    action = D                     # last round: no audit, maximize payoff\nelse:\n    # 1. Stock\u2011safety check\n    if S < T_stock:\n        action = C                 # preserve stock, cooperate regardless of incentives\n    else:\n        # 2. Expected\u2011payoff comparison\n        if E_D > E_C:\n            # 3. Opponent\u2011defection guard\n            if p_defect > \u03c4_defect:\n                action = C         # punish high defection by cooperating (reduces their payoff)\n            else:\n                action = D         # profitable to defect and stock is safe\n        else:\n            action = C             # cooperation yields higher expected payoff\n```\n\n---\n\n### Edge\u2011case handling\n\n* **First round (t = 0)** \u2013 unconditional cooperation to signal goodwill and gather information on opponent behavior.\n* **Last round (t = r\u20111)** \u2013 unconditional defection; audit never occurs, and preserving stock yields no future benefit.\n* **Stock at or below zero** \u2013 forced cooperation (action C) because any defection would yield zero payoff; the rule already selects C when `S < T_stock`.\n* **Observed opponent count** \u2013 if the agent cannot infer `p_defect` (e.g., missing data), treat `p_defect` as zero, i.e., assume full cooperation.\n\n---\n\n### Updating observations\n\nAfter each round the agent records:\n* `k` = number of opponents that cooperated (derived from aggregate observation)\n* `p_defect = (n\u20111\u2011k) / (n\u20111)`\n\nThese values are used in the next round\u2019s decision rule. No memory beyond the most recent observation is required, making the strategy robust to arbitrary opponent policies while still reacting to systematic defection trends."

description_COLLECTIVE_11 = "**Strategy \u201cAdaptive Cooperative Threshold (ACT)\u201d**\n\n**Parameters used each round**  \n- `S` \u2013 current stock (after growth, before consumption)  \n- `t` \u2013 current round index (0\u2011based)  \n- `T = r\u2011t\u20111` \u2013 number of rounds remaining after the current one  \n- `q` \u2013 audit probability (game_description.audit_prob)  \n- `F` \u2013 fine per audited defection (game_description.fine)  \n- `\u03b1 = 0.30` \u2013 lower stock\u2011safety factor (\u224830\u202f% of capacity)  \n- `\u03b2 = 0.70` \u2013 upper stock\u2011excess factor (\u224870\u202f% of capacity)  \n- `\u03b3 = 0.05` \u2013 tolerance for observed defections (5\u202f% of opponents)  \n\nAll constants (`\u03b1,\u03b2,\u03b3`) are fixed; they may be tuned but are not dependent on opponent behaviour.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Decision rule (cooperate\u202f=\u202fC, defect\u202f=\u202fD)\n\nFor each round `t` compute the **expected net payoff** of the two actions, assuming the remainder of the game will be played with the same action by *all* players (a worst\u2011case bound for the individual).\n\n1. **Payoff of cooperating now**  \n\n   ```\n   \u03a0_C = S / (2n)\n   ```\n\n2. **Payoff of defecting now**  \n\n   ```\n   expected_fine = q * F\n   \u03a0_D = S / n \u2013 expected_fine\n   ```\n\n3. **Future\u2011stock value** \u2013 approximate the value of the stock left for the remaining `T` rounds if *all* players cooperated thereafter:\n\n   ```\n   S_next = min( (S - n*\u03a0_C) + 2*(S - n*\u03a0_C)*(1 - (S - n*\u03a0_C)/capacity) , capacity )\n   V_future = T * S_next / (2n)               # optimistic cooperative continuation\n   ```\n\n4. **Total expected utility**  \n\n   ```\n   U_C = \u03a0_C + V_future\n   U_D = \u03a0_D + V_future\n   ```\n\n5. **Base action** \u2013 choose the action with larger total expected utility:\n\n   ```\n   base_action = C if U_C \u2265 U_D else D\n   ```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Collective adjustment using observed behaviour\n\nAfter each round you know the number `c_obs` of opponents that cooperated (the complementary number defected). Define the observed defection proportion\n\n```\n\u03b4 = (n-1 - c_obs) / (n-1)\n```\n\nApply a collective bias:\n\n- **If \u03b4 \u2264 \u03b3** (few opponents defected) \u2192 *reinforce cooperation*: force `C` regardless of `base_action`.\n- **If \u03b4 \u2265 1\u2011\u03b3** (many opponents defected) \u2192 *reinforce defection*: force `D` regardless of `base_action`.\n- **Otherwise** keep `base_action`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Edge\u2011case handling\n\n| Situation                              | Action |\n|----------------------------------------|--------|\n| **First round (`t = 0`)**              | Compute as above using the initial stock (`S = capacity`). |\n| **Stock below lower safety (`S \u2264 \u03b1\u00b7capacity`)** | Override any `base_action` that is `D`; play `C` to minimise depletion. |\n| **Stock above upper excess (`S \u2265 \u03b2\u00b7capacity`)** | If `base_action` is `C` and `\u03b4 \u2264 \u03b3`, keep `C`; otherwise allow `D` (stock can sustain higher consumption). |\n| **Last round (`t = r\u20111`)**             | Audits are impossible; choose the action with larger *immediate* payoff (`\u03a0_C` vs `\u03a0_D`). No future\u2011stock term is added. |\n| **Audit observed** (you were audited and fined) | Record fine; the expected\u2011fine component already accounts for `q`. No extra change. |\n| **All opponents cooperated in previous round** | Set `\u03b3`\u2011threshold check to treat this as \u201cfew defectors\u201d; the collective bias will push you to `C` even if `base_action` suggests `D`. |\n| **All opponents defected in previous round** | Treat as \u201cmany defectors\u201d; the bias pushes you to `D`. |\n\n---\n\n### 4. Pseudocode (executed each round)\n\n```python\ndef ACT_decision(t, S, history):\n    # 1. parameters\n    T = r - t - 1\n    expected_fine = q * F\n    payoff_C = S / (2 * n)\n    payoff_D = S / n - expected_fine\n\n    # 2. future stock if everyone cooperates thereafter\n    S_after_cons = S - n * payoff_C\n    growth = 2 * S_after_cons * (1 - S_after_cons / capacity)\n    S_next = min(S_after_cons + growth, capacity)\n    V_future = T * S_next / (2 * n)\n\n    U_C = payoff_C + V_future\n    U_D = payoff_D + V_future\n    base_action = 'C' if U_C >= U_D else 'D'\n\n    # 3. observed opponent cooperation (c_obs from history)\n    if t > 0:\n        c_obs = history[t-1]['cooperators_among_opponents']\n        delta = (n-1 - c_obs) / (n-1)\n    else:\n        delta = 0.0    # no info yet\n\n    # 4. collective bias\n    if delta <= \u03b3:\n        bias_action = 'C'\n    elif delta >= 1 - \u03b3:\n        bias_action = 'D'\n    else:\n        bias_action = base_action\n\n    # 5. safety/excess overrides\n    if S <= \u03b1 * capacity:\n        final_action = 'C'\n    elif S >= \u03b2 * capacity and bias_action == 'C' and delta <= \u03b3:\n        final_action = 'C'          # keep cooperation when stock abundant and opponents cooperative\n    else:\n        final_action = bias_action\n\n    # 6. last round special case\n    if t == r - 1:\n        final_action = 'C' if payoff_C >= payoff_D else 'D'\n\n    return final_action\n```\n\nThe strategy uses only publicly known parameters, the current stock, the number of cooperating opponents observed in the previous round, and the round index. It continuously balances immediate monetary gain, expected audit cost, and preservation of the common pool for future rounds, while biasing toward the collective norm detected in the opponents\u2019 recent behaviour."

description_COLLECTIVE_12 = "**Collective Adaptive Strategy**\n\n*State variables* (kept locally)  \n- `stock` \u2013 current common\u2011pool level (observed at start of the round).  \n- `coop_est` \u2013 estimated proportion of opponents that cooperated in the *previous* round (initialized to\u202f1.0).  \n- `t` \u2013 current round index (0\u2011based).  \n\n*Parameters* (read from the game description)  \n- `capacity`, `n`, `r`, `q`, `F`.  \n\n*Internal thresholds* (computed once)  \n- `high_thr = 0.6\u202f\u00d7\u202fcapacity`\u2003\u2003// \u201cabundant\u201d stock  \n- `low_thr  = 0.3\u202f\u00d7\u202fcapacity`\u2003\u2003// \u201ccritical\u201d stock  \n- `coop_thr = 0.7`\u2003\u2003// minimum cooperation observed to keep full cooperation  \n\n*Decision rule* (executed each round before choosing an action)\n\n```\nif t == r\u20111:                     # last round\n    action = C                  # cooperate \u2013 no future impact, maintain collective tone\nelse:\n    # 1. Adjust cooperation inclination by stock level\n    if stock >= high_thr and coop_est >= coop_thr:\n        base_prob = 0.9                     # strong incentive to cooperate\n    elif stock <= low_thr:\n        base_prob = 0.2                     # stock scarce \u2013 favor defection\n    else:\n        # intermediate region \u2013 blend observed cooperation with audit safety\n        base_prob = 0.5 * coop_est + 0.3 * (1\u2011q)\n\n    # 2. Add a small exploration component to avoid being stuck in a bad equilibrium\n    explore = 0.05\n    coop_prob = min(1.0, max(0.0, base_prob * (1\u2011explore) + explore * random()))\n\n    # 3. Sample action\n    action = C with probability coop_prob\n             D otherwise\n```\n\n*History update* (after round outcomes are revealed)\n\n```\n# observe number of opponents that chose C (call it opp_coop)\ncoop_est = ( (t) * coop_est + opp_coop/(n\u20111) ) / (t+1)   # cumulative average\n```\n\n*Edge\u2011case handling*  \n\n- **Round\u202f0**: `coop_est` is preset to\u202f1.0, implying maximal willingness to cooperate when no information is available.  \n- **Audit awareness**: the term `(1\u2011q)` in the intermediate\u2011stock case lowers the cooperation probability when the audit probability is high, since the expected fine makes defection less attractive.  \n- **Stock depletion**: if `stock` ever reaches 0, the strategy automatically falls back to always defect (the `low_thr` branch) because any further cooperation yields zero payoff.  \n- **Sudden drop in observed cooperation** (`coop_est` falls below `coop_thr` while stock is still high): the algorithm immediately reduces `base_prob` to the intermediate formula, allowing a quick switch to defection while still keeping a 5\u202f% chance of cooperating each round to signal willingness to re\u2011establish trust.  \n- **Re\u2011entry after low\u2011stock phase**: once `stock` climbs above `high_thr` (possible only through growth after a round of heavy cooperation), `base_prob` returns to 0.9, re\u2011instating full collective behavior.  \n\n*Collective mindset* \u2013 the rule prioritises cooperation when the resource is abundant and the group has shown cooperative intent, scales back when the pool is threatened or opponents defect, and retains a non\u2011zero chance of cooperating at all times to keep the possibility of collective recovery. The strategy is fully deterministic aside from the small exploration noise, depends only on publicly observable quantities (`stock`, `opp_coop`) and its own past observations, and thus works against any independent opponent policy."

description_COLLECTIVE_13 = "**Strategy Overview**  \nThe agent follows a \u201csustainable\u2011cooperate\u2011until\u2011threshold\u2011break\u201d rule set, constantly updating its belief about the group\u2019s health (stock level) and the observed cooperation rate of opponents. It never defects in the final round (no audit, but collective ethic) and always starts by cooperating.\n\n---\n\n### Core Variables (updated each round *t*)\n\n| Symbol | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `S_t` | Current stock (observed at start of round) |\n| `c_obs_t` | Number of opponents observed cooperating in the previous round (0\u202f\u2026\u202fn\u20111) |\n| `q` | Audit probability (given) |\n| `F` | Fine per audited defection (given) |\n| `\u03b8_stock` | Stock safety threshold = 0.30\u202f\u00d7\u202fcapacity |\n| `\u03b8_coop` | Cooperation confidence threshold = floor((n\u20111)/2) (majority) |\n| `T_defect` | Maximum consecutive defect rounds allowed = 2 |\n| `defect_counter` | Consecutive rounds the agent has defected (reset to 0 when it cooperates) |\n\nAll variables are recomputed at the start of each round from public history.\n\n---\n\n### Decision Rules\n\n```\nfunction decide(t, S_t, c_obs_{t-1}) -> action\n    if t == 0 then\n        return C                          # first round: cooperate unconditionally\n    if t == r-1 then\n        return C                          # last round: cooperate (collective norm)\n\n    # 1. Stock safety check\n    if S_t < \u03b8_stock then\n        # Stock is low; cooperation is the only way to let growth recover\n        reset(defect_counter)\n        return C\n\n    # 2. Cooperation confidence check\n    if c_obs_{t-1} >= \u03b8_coop then\n        # Majority of opponents cooperated last round \u2192 maintain cooperation\n        reset(defect_counter)\n        return C\n    end if\n\n    # 3. Expected\u2011payoff comparison with audit risk\n    #   Expected payoff if cooperate:\n    #       \u03c0_C = S_t/(2n)\n    #   Expected payoff if defect:\n    #       \u03c0_D = S_t/n - q*F\n    if (S_t/n - q*F) > (S_t/(2n)) and defect_counter < T_defect then\n        # Defection is statistically better and we have not exceeded defect streak limit\n        increment(defect_counter)\n        return D\n    else\n        # Either defect not profitable or we have exhausted allowed streak\n        reset(defect_counter)\n        return C\n    end if\nend function\n```\n\n**Interpretation of the rules**\n\n1. **Initial cooperation** guarantees a baseline of sustainable growth and provides the opponent\u2011observation signal for later rounds.  \n2. **Final\u2011round cooperation** respects the collective ethic; with no audit risk the agent still forgoes a one\u2011shot gain to avoid destabilising trust for future repeated interactions (e.g., in a tournament series).  \n3. **Stock safety threshold** (`\u03b8_stock`) prevents the group from crashing; when the pool falls below 30\u202f% of capacity the agent always cooperates, giving the system a chance to regrow.  \n4. **Observed cooperation** (`c_obs_{t-1}`) uses the anonymous count of cooperating opponents from the previous round. If a majority cooperated, the agent mirrors that behavior, reinforcing a cooperative equilibrium.  \n5. **Audit\u2011adjusted payoff test** compares the expected net gain from defecting (including expected fine `q\u00b7F`) with the guaranteed cooperative payoff. Defection is only taken when it strictly exceeds cooperation *and* the agent has not already defected for more than `T_defect` consecutive rounds. This limits over\u2011exploitation and gives opponents a chance to re\u2011establish cooperation.  \n6. **Defect\u2011streak limit** (`T_defect = 2`) caps the duration of aggressive exploitation, ensuring the agent re\u2011evaluates the group\u2019s response quickly.  \n\n---\n\n### Edge\u2011Case Handling\n\n| Situation | Action |\n|-----------|--------|\n| **Stock = 0** | Return `C` (payoff zero either way; cooperation maintains the collective stance). |\n| **All opponents defected last round** (`c_obs_{t-1}=0`) and `S_t` is high | Apply the audit\u2011adjusted payoff test; if defecting is still profitable, defect for at most two rounds, then revert to cooperation hoping opponents will respond. |\n| **Audit probability `q = 0`** | The test reduces to pure payoff comparison: defect whenever `S_t/n > S_t/(2n)`, i.e., always; however the `T_defect` limit still forces periodic cooperation to sustain stock. |\n| **Fine `F` extremely large** (`q\u00b7F` exceeds the extra gain from defecting) | The test will never favour defection; the agent cooperates every round except forced defections when stock is safely high and `defect_counter` < `T_defect` (which never triggers). |\n| **Unexpected observation data** (e.g., count >\u202fn\u20111) | Treat as maximum possible (`c_obs = n\u20111`). The majority\u2011cooperate condition will still hold, leading to cooperation. |\n\n---\n\n### Collective Mindset Summary (implicit in the rules)\n\n- **Sustainability first:** stock\u2011based safety overrides greed.  \n- **Reciprocity:** mirror the majority behavior of the group.  \n- **Controlled exploitation:** defect only when statistically justified and for a bounded window, never endangering the commons.  \n- **Norm reinforcement:** always cooperate in the opening and closing rounds, signalling commitment to the collective good."

description_COLLECTIVE_14 = "**Strategy Overview**\n\nAt every round *t* (0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr) the agent observes  \n\n* the current stock *S\u209c* (clipped to \\[0,\u202fcapacity\\]),  \n* the number *c\u209c* of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (0\u202f\u2264\u202fc\u209c\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111),  \n* whether it was audited in the previous round (only needed for bookkeeping).\n\nThe agent\u2019s action is determined by three ordered decision modules:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Safety\u2011First Stock Filter\n```\nif S\u209c < \u03c4\u00b7capacity then   # \u03c4 \u2208 (0,1) is a sustainability threshold (default \u03c4 = 0.30)\n    action \u2190 C               # always cooperate when stock is low\n    exit\n```\nRationale: preserving the pool avoids irreversible collapse; cooperation costs only half the per\u2011player consumption and therefore maximizes future total welfare when the resource is scarce.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Expected\u2011Payoff Comparison\nCompute the *expected* net payoff of defecting versus cooperating, taking the audit probability *q* and fine *F* into account:\n\n```\npayoff_C   = S\u209c / (2n)                     # guaranteed payoff when cooperating\npayoff_D   = S\u209c / n  \u2013  q\u00b7F                # expected payoff when defecting\n```\n\nIf defecting yields a strictly higher expected payoff **and** the stock is comfortably above the safety threshold, choose defect:\n\n```\nif payoff_D > payoff_C then\n    action \u2190 D\n    exit\n```\n\nWhen payoffs are equal (or within a tiny epsilon \u03b5) prefer cooperation to maintain collective trust.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Reputation\u2011Based Retaliation (Collective Mindset)\nMaintain a sliding window of the last *w* rounds (default w = 3) and compute the empirical defection rate among opponents:\n\n```\ndefection_rate = ( \u03a3_{k = t\u2011w}^{t\u20111} ( (n\u20111) \u2013 c_k ) ) / ( w\u00b7(n\u20111) )\n```\n\nIf `defection_rate` exceeds a tolerance *\u03b8* (default \u03b8 = 0.25), enter a *punishment phase* lasting *p* rounds (default p = 2) during which the agent defects regardless of the payoff comparison (unless overridden by the safety\u2011first filter). After the punishment phase, reset the window and resume the normal comparison.\n\n```\nif in_punishment_phase then\n    action \u2190 D\n    decrement punishment_counter\n    exit\nelse if defection_rate > \u03b8 then\n    start punishment_counter = p\n    action \u2190 D\n    exit\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Edge\u2011Case Rules\n| Situation                              | Action |\n|----------------------------------------|--------|\n| **Round 0 (first round)**              | Cooperate (C). No history \u2192 start with C to seed collective trust. |\n| **Round r\u20111 (last round)**              | Apply the Expected\u2011Payoff Comparison **without** future\u2011stock considerations. Audits never occur, so `payoff_D = S\u209c / n`. Defect if `S\u209c / n > S\u209c / (2n)` (always true) **unless** the safety filter forces C because `S\u209c < \u03c4\u00b7capacity`. |\n| **Stock exactly zero**                 | Both actions yield zero payoff; choose C to signal goodwill (no penalty). |\n| **Audit observed in current round**    | No direct effect on the next\u2011round decision; only the fine reduces that round\u2019s realized payoff. The strategy already accounted for expected fines. |\n| **All opponents cooperated (c\u209c = n\u20111)** | Defect if `payoff_D > payoff_C`; otherwise cooperate. The reputation module will see zero defection rate, so no punishment. |\n| **All opponents defected (c\u209c = 0)**     | The safety filter may trigger if the stock fell below \u03c4\u00b7capacity; otherwise the payoff comparison will almost always favour defecting, but the reputation module will start a punishment phase only after the defection rate exceeds \u03b8 (which it will). The agent will defect for *p* rounds, then reassess. |\n\n---\n\n### 5. Parameter Settings (tunable per tournament)\n- Sustainability threshold `\u03c4` (default 0.30) \u2013 protects the pool from collapse.\n- Audit probability `q` and fine `F` are read from the game description; used directly in payoff_D.\n- Reputation window length `w` (default 3) and tolerance `\u03b8` (default 0.25) \u2013 balance responsiveness and stability.\n- Punishment length `p` (default 2) \u2013 short enough to limit mutual loss but long enough to deter repeated defections.\n\n---\n\n**Pseudo\u2011code Summary**\n\n```\ninitialize: in_punishment_phase \u2190 false; punishment_counter \u2190 0\nfor t = 0 to r\u20111:\n    observe S_t, c_{t\u20111} (if t>0), audit result (if t>0)\n\n    # 1. Safety filter\n    if S_t < \u03c4*capacity:\n        action \u2190 C\n        continue\n\n    # 2. Reputation retaliation\n    if in_punishment_phase:\n        action \u2190 D\n        punishment_counter \u2190 punishment_counter \u2013 1\n        if punishment_counter = 0 then in_punishment_phase \u2190 false\n        continue\n    compute defection_rate over last w rounds\n    if defection_rate > \u03b8:\n        in_punishment_phase \u2190 true\n        punishment_counter \u2190 p\n        action \u2190 D\n        continue\n\n    # 3. Expected payoff\n    payoff_C \u2190 S_t / (2n)\n    payoff_D \u2190 S_t / n \u2013 q*F\n    if payoff_D > payoff_C then action \u2190 D else action \u2190 C\n```\n\nThe agent thus starts cooperatively, cooperates whenever the resource is fragile, defects only when it is economically justified after accounting for audit risk, and enforces a collective norm by temporarily retaliating against sustained opponent defections. This adaptive rule\u2011set works across the full range of opponent behaviours while keeping the common pool viable."

description_COLLECTIVE_15 = "**Strategy: Adaptive Collective Sustainability (ACS)**  \n\n**Parameters derived from game description**  \n- \\(q\\) = audit probability, \\(F\\) = fine, \\(C =\\) capacity, \\(n\\) = number of players.  \n- Immediate expected payoff if cooperate: \\(E_C = S/(2n)\\).  \n- Immediate expected payoff if defect (including expected fine): \\(E_D = S/n - qF\\).  \n\n**State variables** (kept locally)  \n- `stock` \u2013 current common\u2011pool stock \\(S\\).  \n- `history[t]` \u2013 for each past round \\(t\\): number of cooperators observed, whether you were audited, and your own payoff.  \n- `defect_rate` \u2013 exponential moving average of opponent defect proportion:  \n  \\[\n  defect\\_rate \\leftarrow \\lambda \\times defect\\_rate + (1-\\lambda) \\times \\frac{\\text{observed defectors}}{n-1}\n  \\]\n  with \\(\\lambda = 0.8\\).  \n\n**Thresholds** (fixed constants, can be tuned)  \n- `stock_min = 0.4 * C` \u2013 below this the pool is considered fragile.  \n- `defect_rate_max = 0.6` \u2013 above this the opponent environment is too hostile for conditional cooperation.  \n- `grace_period = 2` \u2013 number of consecutive rounds the stock must stay \u2265 `stock_min` before switching back to cooperation after a defection spree.  \n\n**Decision rule (applied each round except the last)**  \n\n```\nif t == r-1:                     # last round \u2013 never audited\n    action = D                   # maximize immediate payoff, no future cost\nelse:\n    # 1. Immediate payoff comparison\n    if E_D > E_C:\n        immediate_prefer = D\n    else:\n        immediate_prefer = C\n\n    # 2. Sustainability safeguard\n    if stock < stock_min:\n        sustainability = C      # must help the pool recover\n    else:\n        sustainability = immediate_prefer\n\n    # 3. Opponent hostility filter\n    if defect_rate > defect_rate_max:\n        hostility = D           # protect against exploitation\n    else:\n        hostility = sustainability\n\n    # 4. Grim\u2011trigger fallback\n    if consecutive_rounds_without_enough_cooperators >= grace_period:\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = hostility\n```\n\n**Definitions of auxiliary conditions**  \n- `consecutive_rounds_without_enough_cooperators` counts successive rounds where the observed number of cooperators \\< floor((n\u20111)/2). Reset to 0 whenever a round meets or exceeds this benchmark.  \n- \u201cEnough cooperators\u201d is a collective\u2011mindset signal that the pool is being maintained by the group.  \n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n- **Round\u202f0 (first round)**: `defect_rate` is initialized to 0, `stock = C`. The rule reduces to the immediate payoff comparison; typically \\(E_D > E_C\\) only if \\(qF\\) is very small, otherwise cooperate.  \n- **Round\u202fr\u20111 (final round)**: forced defect because no future stock matters and no audits occur.  \n- **Stock depletion to 0**: `stock_min` condition forces cooperation, but if the pool is already 0 the payoff is 0 regardless; the algorithm will continue defecting in future rounds because `defect_rate` will rise, avoiding wasted effort.  \n\n**Collective mindset rationale embedded in the algorithm**  \n- Prioritizes cooperation when the resource is fragile (`stock < stock_min`).  \n- Uses observed opponent behaviour to adjust willingness to cooperate, preserving fairness.  \n- Employs a short\u2011term \u201cgrim\u2011trigger\u201d to deter chronic free\u2011riding while allowing recovery after brief defection spikes.  \n\nThe strategy requires only the publicly known parameters, the observable aggregate history, and the current stock level, making it fully implementable by any player in the described repeated common\u2011pool game."

description_COLLECTIVE_16 = "**Parameters (known to the agent)**  \n- n, r, capacity, q, F \u2013 from the game description.  \n-\u202fT_stock\u202f\u2208\u202f(0,1) \u2013 stock\u2011health threshold (default\u202f0.5).  \n-\u202fT_defect\u202f\u2208\u202f[0,1] \u2013 tolerated proportion of opponent defections before punishment (default\u202f0.25).  \n-\u202fT_punish\u202f\u2208\u202f\u2115 \u2013 length of a punishment block (default\u202f3).  \n\n**State variables (maintained each round)**  \n- `stock_t` \u2013 current stock before actions are taken.  \n- `opp_coop_t` \u2013 number of opponents observed to cooperate in round *t*.  \n- `trust_t \u2208 \u211d` \u2013 belief that the group will keep the pool sustainable.  \n- `punish_counter` \u2013 rounds left in a forced\u2011defect block (0\u202f=\u202fno block).  \n\n**Initialization (round\u202f0)**  \n```\ntrust_0 = 1.0                     // full confidence\npunish_counter = 0\naction_0 = C                      // always start by cooperating\n```\n\n**Update after each round *t* (t = 0 \u2026 r\u20112)**  \n\n1. **Compute observed defection rate**  \n   ```\n   opp_defect_rate = (n-1 - opp_coop_t) / (n-1)\n   ```\n\n2. **Adjust trust** \u2013 exponential decay for observed defections, gradual recovery otherwise:  \n   ```\n   if opp_defect_rate > T_defect:\n       trust_{t+1} = trust_t * (1 - opp_defect_rate)        // sharp penalty\n   else:\n       trust_{t+1} = min(1.0, trust_t + 0.05)               // slow recovery\n   ```\n\n3. **Determine whether a punishment block must be entered**  \n   ```\n   if punish_counter == 0 and trust_{t+1} < 0.3:\n       punish_counter = T_punish          // start block of forced defection\n   ```\n\n4. **Decrement any ongoing punishment block**  \n   ```\n   if punish_counter > 0:\n       punish_counter = punish_counter - 1\n   ```\n\n**Decision rule for round *t* (t = 0 \u2026 r\u20111)**  \n\n```\nif t == r-1:                         // last round \u2013 no audits\n    // maximize immediate payoff while preserving the collective outcome\n    if stock_t > capacity * T_stock:\n        action_t = D                // defect if stock is healthy\n    else:\n        action_t = C                // cooperate to avoid wiping out the pool\nelse:\n    // regular rounds (audit possible)\n    // compute expected net gain of defecting vs cooperating\n    benefit = stock_t/(2*n)                     // extra consumption when defecting\n    expected_fine = q * F\n    net_gain = benefit - expected_fine\n\n    if punish_counter > 0:\n        action_t = D                           // forced defection block\n    else if stock_t < capacity * T_stock:\n        action_t = C                           // stock low \u2192 preserve pool\n    else if net_gain > 0 and trust_t > 0.5:\n        action_t = D                           // profitable and trust still high\n    else:\n        action_t = C                           // default cooperative stance\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n\n- **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0)**: `trust_0 = 1`, `punish_counter = 0`; rule above yields `action_0 = C`.  \n- **Stock depleted (stock_t\u202f=\u202f0)**: all actions yield zero payoff; the rule falls to the `stock_t < capacity * T_stock` clause, selecting `C` (harmless).  \n- **Audit outcome**: the agent only records whether it was fined; this does not feed back into the rule beyond the implicit expected\u2011fine term already incorporated.  \n- **Unexpected spikes in opponent cooperation** (opp_coop_t\u202f=\u202fn\u20111): trust increases slowly (`+0.05` per round) but never exceeds\u202f1.0, ensuring the agent does not become over\u2011optimistic.  \n\n**Collective orientation**  \n\nThe strategy prioritises maintaining the stock above the health threshold, uses the trust score to gauge the group\u2019s willingness to cooperate, and only exploits profitable defections when the pool is abundant *and* the group\u2019s trust remains high. Punishment blocks are triggered when trust collapses, signaling widespread defection; the block lasts a fixed number of rounds to deter future betrayals while giving the group a chance to rebuild trust afterwards."

description_PROSOCIAL_1 = "**Prosocial Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**State variables (maintained each round)**\n- `S` \u2013 current stock level (observed at start of round).\n- `D_avg` \u2013 exponential moving average of opponent defection rate, initialized to\u202f0.  \n  Update: `D_avg \u2190 \u03b1\u00b7d_t + (1\u2011\u03b1)\u00b7D_avg` where `d_t = (n\u20111\u2011C_t)/(n\u20111)` and `C_t` is the number of opponents observed cooperating this round. Choose `\u03b1 = 0.5` (or any 0<\u03b1\u22641).\n- `audit_history` \u2013 number of times you were audited in previous rounds (only needed to track risk, not for decisions).\n\n**Parameters (computed once from game description)**\n- `S_low = capacity * 0.4`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// minimal sustainable stock\n- `S_high = capacity * 0.8`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// comfortable stock zone\n- `\u03b4_low = 0.15`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// acceptable average defection when stock is low\n- `\u03b4_high = 0.30`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// acceptable average defection when stock is high\n- `\u03b1 = 0.5` (smoothing factor for `D_avg`).\n\n**Decision rule (applied each round t = 0 \u2026 r\u20112, i.e. all but the final round)**  \n\n1. **Assess stock zone**  \n   - If `S \u2264 S_low` \u2192 *critical*: set `\u03b4 = \u03b4_low`.  \n   - Else if `S \u2265 S_high` \u2192 *abundant*: set `\u03b4 = \u03b4_high`.  \n   - Else \u2192 *moderate*: set `\u03b4 = (\u03b4_low + \u03b4_high)/2`.\n\n2. **Choose action**  \n   - If `D_avg \u2264 \u03b4` **and** `S > S_low` \u2192 **Cooperate (C)**.  \n   - Otherwise \u2192 **Defect (D)**.\n\n3. **Audit feedback**  \n   - After the round you observe whether you were audited (`a_i,t = 1` or `0`).  \n   - If audited while defecting, increment `audit_history`.  \n   - If `audit_history` exceeds `\u23080.5\u00b7(t+1)\u2309` (more than half of audited rounds were fines), switch to unconditional cooperation for the remainder of the game to avoid further penalties.\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n- **First round (t = 0)** \u2013 No history exists; start with **Cooperate** and set `D_avg = 0`.\n- **Last round (t = r\u20111)** \u2013 No audits occur; always **Cooperate** regardless of `D_avg` or `S` to maximize the final common good and avoid unnecessary depletion.\n- **Stock exhaustion** \u2013 If `S = 0` at the start of a round, the payoff from any action is zero; continue to **Cooperate** to keep the stock at zero rather than risking negative growth (which is already capped at zero).\n\n**Summary of actions per round**\n```\nif t == r-1:\n    action = C\nelse if t == 0:\n    action = C\nelse:\n    compute d_t from observed opponent cooperators\n    D_avg = \u03b1*d_t + (1-\u03b1)*D_avg\n    set \u03b4 based on S (low / moderate / high)\n    if D_avg <= \u03b4 and S > S_low:\n        action = C\n    else:\n        action = D\n    if audited and action == D:\n        audit_history += 1\n        if audit_history > 0.5 * (number of audits so far):\n            force future actions = C\n```\n\nThis rule continuously monitors the health of the common pool and the community\u2019s cooperative tone, only defecting when the stock is safely above the critical threshold *and* opponents have demonstrated sufficient cooperation. It automatically reverts to full cooperation when audits indicate high personal risk or when the game ends."

description_PROSOCIAL_2 = "**Prosocial Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**Parameters used at each round `t`**\n- `S_t` \u2013 current stock (after growth from previous round)\n- `n` \u2013 number of players\n- `q` \u2013 audit probability\n- `F` \u2013 fine per audited defection\n- `\u0394 = S_t / (2n)` \u2013 payoff from cooperating this round\n- `\u0393 = S_t / n` \u2013 raw payoff from defecting this round\n- `E_D = \u0393 \u2013 q\u00b7F` \u2013 expected payoff from defecting (accounting for expected fine)\n- `p_t` \u2013 observed proportion of opponents who defected in round `t` (computed from the anonymous count of defectors)\n- `p\u0304_t` \u2013 exponential moving average of opponent defection proportion, initialized to `0`  \n  `p\u0304_{t+1} = \u03b1\u00b7p_t + (1\u2013\u03b1)\u00b7p\u0304_t` with smoothing factor `\u03b1 = 0.3`\n- `\u03b8_stock = 0.4` \u2013 stock\u2011level threshold (fraction of capacity) below which cooperation is strongly encouraged\n- `\u03b8_defect = 0.35` \u2013 tolerated average defection proportion before entering retaliation mode\n- `\u03b2 = 0.2` \u2013 penalty factor for retaliation (reduces cooperation payoff in the decision rule)\n\n**Decision rule (applied after observing `S_t` and `p\u0304_t`)**\n\n```\nif t == 0:                     # first round\n    action = C\nelif t == r-1:                 # last round (no audits)\n    action = C                 # prosocial: preserve the resource even if it yields no future benefit\nelse:\n    # 1. Determine baseline cooperation incentive\n    if S_t / capacity < \u03b8_stock:\n        # stock low \u2192 favor cooperation\n        baseline = True\n    else:\n        baseline = (E_D <= \u0394)   # cooperate if expected defect payoff does not exceed cooperation payoff\n\n    # 2. Adjust for opponent behavior\n    if p\u0304_t > \u03b8_defect:\n        # opponents are defecting above tolerated level \u2192 modest retaliation\n        # treat cooperation as less attractive by discounting its payoff\n        effective_\u0394 = \u0394 * (1 - \u03b2)\n    else:\n        effective_\u0394 = \u0394\n\n    # 3. Final choice\n    if baseline and (E_D <= effective_\u0394):\n        action = C\n    else:\n        action = D\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- **Round\u202f0:** always cooperate to signal prosocial intent and to seed a high stock level.\n- **Round\u202fr\u20111:** always cooperate (no audit risk, but prosocial commitment to leaving the pool in the best possible state).\n- **Zero stock (`S_t = 0`):** both `\u0394` and `\u0393` are zero; cooperate (no loss, maintains the \u201ccooperate\u201d identity).\n- **Full capacity (`S_t = capacity`):** apply the normal rule; if `E_D` exceeds `\u0394` but opponent defection is low, cooperate to keep the stock at capacity.\n- **Audit probability `q = 0` or fine `F = 0`:** `E_D = \u0393`; the rule reduces to \u201cdefect only when raw defect payoff exceeds cooperation payoff after accounting for opponent defection\u201d.\n\n**Prosocial alignment**\n- Starts with unconditional cooperation, establishing a high\u2011stock baseline.\n- Prioritizes cooperation when the resource is scarce (`S_t / capacity < \u03b8_stock`), safeguarding sustainability.\n- Allows limited, proportionate retaliation only when opponents consistently defect above the tolerated level, preventing exploitation while still rewarding overall cooperation.\n- Ends with cooperation regardless of payoff, preserving the pool for any future context and demonstrating commitment to the common good."

description_PROSOCIAL_3 = "**Strategy \u201cAdaptive Cooperative Guard\u201d**\n\n**State variables (updated each round)**  \n- `stock_t` \u2013 current common\u2011pool stock.  \n- `opp_coop_t` \u2013 number of opponents observed cooperating in round *t*.  \n- `total_opp = n\u20111`.  \n- `audit_q` \u2013 audit probability *q*.  \n- `fine_F` \u2013 fine *F*.  \n\n**Parameters (tuned once from game description)**  \n- `stock_thresh = capacity * 0.4` \u2013 below this the pool is considered fragile.  \n- `cooperate_frac_thresh = 0.5` \u2013 require at least 50\u202f% of opponents to have cooperated in the previous round to keep cooperating.  \n- `expected_defect_gain = (stock_t / n) \u2013 (stock_t / (2n))` \u2013 marginal gain from defecting in the current round.  \n- `expected_fine = audit_q * fine_F`.  \n\n**Decision rule (applied each round *t*, 0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr)**  \n\n```\nif t == r\u20111:                     # last round (no audit, no future)\n    action = C                  # cooperate prosocially\nelse if t == 0:                  # first round\n    action = C                  # start with cooperation\nelse:\n    # 1. Check stock health\n    stock_ok = (stock_t > stock_thresh)\n\n    # 2. Check opponents\u2019 recent behavior\n    opp_coop_frac = opp_coop_{t\u20111} / total_opp\n    behavior_ok = (opp_coop_frac >= cooperate_frac_thresh)\n\n    # 3. Compare net expected payoff of defecting vs cooperating\n    net_defect = expected_defect_gain - expected_fine\n    net_cooperate = 0               # cooperating gives no extra immediate gain\n\n    # 4. Choose action\n    if stock_ok and behavior_ok and net_defect <= 0:\n        action = C                 # cooperate when pool is healthy, others mostly cooperate, and defecting is not profitable after expected fine\n    else:\n        action = D                 # defect otherwise (fragile pool, many defectors, or defecting still profitable)\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n- If `stock_t == 0`, set `action = C` (both actions yield 0, cooperating preserves prosocial stance).  \n- If `capacity == 0` (degenerate game), always choose `C`.  \n- If `audit_q == 0` (no audits), the rule reduces to the stock\u2011and\u2011behavior thresholds; defect only when the pool is fragile or opponents are largely defecting.  \n- If `fine_F == 0` but `audit_q > 0`, the expected fine term is zero, so defect only when the stock is below `stock_thresh` or opponents\u2019 cooperation falls below the threshold.  \n\n**Prosocial alignment**  \nThe strategy starts cooperative, continues cooperating while the common pool remains robust and the community demonstrates mutual cooperation, and only switches to defection when the resource is at risk of collapse or defection becomes strictly advantageous despite audit risk. It returns to cooperation as soon as the conditions improve, ensuring a forgiving, adaptive, and collectively beneficial behavior throughout the repeated game."

description_PROSOCIAL_4 = "**Prosocial Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**Parameters available to the agent**  \n- `n` (players), `r` (rounds), `capacity`, `q` (audit probability), `F` (fine)  \n- Current round `t` (0\u2011indexed)  \n- Current stock `S` (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity)  \n- History for the agent: list of own past actions `my_action[0..t\u20111]` and own audit outcomes `my_audit[0..t\u20111]` (0\u202f=\u202fnot audited, 1\u202f=\u202faudited)  \n- Observation after each round: number of opponents who cooperated `opp_coop[t\u20111]` (for t\u202f>\u202f0)\n\n**Decision rule (per round t)**  \n\n```\nif t == r-1:                     # last round \u2013 never defect\n    action = C\nelse if t == 0:                  # first round \u2013 establish trust\n    action = C\nelse:\n    # 1. Estimate opponent cooperation rate\n    coop_rate = opp_coop[t-1] / (n-1)\n\n    # 2. Compute expected marginal benefit of defecting this round\n    benefit = S/n - S/(2*n)                     # extra consumption per defect\n    expected_fine = q * F\n    net_gain = benefit - expected_fine\n\n    # 3. Check stock safety threshold\n    #    Predict stock after everyone (including us) cooperates:\n    S_next_if_allC = min( (S - (n*S)/(2*n)) + 2*(S - (n*S)/(2*n))*(1-(S - (n*S)/(2*n))/capacity), capacity )\n    #    Predict stock after everyone defects (worst\u2011case):\n    S_next_if_allD = min( (S - (n*S)/n) + 2*(S - (n*S)/n)*(1-(S - (n*S)/n)/capacity), capacity )\n    safe_threshold = capacity * 0.25                # never let stock fall below 25% of capacity\n\n    # 4. Decision logic\n    if net_gain > 0 and coop_rate > 0.5 and S_next_if_allC >= safe_threshold:\n        action = D          # opportunistic defection when opponents are mostly cooperative,\n                           # the stock remains safely high, and expected gain exceeds fine\n    else:\n        action = C          # otherwise cooperate\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n- **Round\u202f0**: always cooperate to signal prosocial intent.  \n- **Round\u202fr\u20111** (final round): always cooperate; no audit risk and defection provides no future benefit.  \n- **Zero or near\u2011zero stock** (`S \u2264 0.01*capacity`): force cooperation regardless of other conditions to avoid stock collapse.  \n- **Audit feedback**: if the agent is audited while defecting (`my_audit[t\u20111]==1`), increase the required `net_gain` threshold for future defection by adding `+ (F * 0.5)` to discourage repeated risky defection.  \n\n**Prosocial alignment**  \nThe strategy defaults to cooperation, only permitting defection when (a) opponents are broadly cooperative (high `coop_rate`), (b) the stock is comfortably above a safety margin, and (c) the expected monetary gain outweighs the expected fine. This preserves the common pool, maximizes collective long\u2011term payoffs, and respects audit deterrence, embodying a prosocial stance while remaining responsive to the observed environment."

description_PROSOCIAL_5 = "**Decision rule (per round\u202ft)**  \n\n1. **Observe**  \n   -\u202fCurrent stock\u202fS\u209c.  \n   -\u202fNumber\u202fk\u209c of opponents who cooperated in the previous round (0\u202f\u2264\u202fk\u209c\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111).  \n\n2. **Compute cooperation index**  \n   ```\n   coop_rate = (k\u209c + (my_last_action == C ? 1 : 0)) / n\n   ```\n   This is the fraction of total players (including you) that cooperated last round.\n\n3. **Derive expected stock trajectory**  \n   -\u202fIf everyone cooperates for the remaining\u202f(r\u2011t)\u202frounds, the stock evolves according to the growth function; denote the projected final stock\u202fS\u0302_coop.  \n   -\u202fIf everyone defects for the remaining\u202f(r\u2011t)\u202frounds, denote the projected final stock\u202fS\u0302_def.  \n   (Both can be obtained by iterating the deterministic stock update with the respective consumptions; no opponent modeling is required.)\n\n4. **Choose action**  \n\n   | Condition (evaluated in order)                                         | Action |\n   |------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------|\n   | **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111)** \u2013 cooperate (C)                               | C      |\n   | **Stock alarm**: S\u209c\u202f\u2264\u202f0.2\u202f\u00d7\u202fcapacity **and** coop_rate\u202f<\u202f0.5          | D (temporary sanction) |\n   | **High defection**: coop_rate\u202f<\u202f0.3                                     | D (punish) |\n   | **S\u0302_coop\u202f\u2265\u202fS\u0302_def\u202f+\u202f\u0394** (\u0394\u202f=\u202f0.05\u202f\u00d7\u202fcapacity) **and** coop_rate\u202f\u2265\u202f0.6 | C (maintain prosocial path) |\n   | **Otherwise**                                                          | C (default) |\n\n   *\u0394* is a safety margin ensuring that cooperating yields a materially higher long\u2011run stock than defecting.\n\n5. **Audit\u2011adjusted defection**  \n   When D is chosen, compute the expected net payoff after fines:  \n   ```\n   expected_gain = S\u209c/n - q*F\n   ```\n   If `expected_gain` \u2264 payoff from cooperating (S\u209c/(2n)), override D and play C regardless of the above table. This prevents exploitable defections when audit risk is high.\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n- **Round\u202f0**: No history exists, so set `coop_rate = 1` (assume full cooperation) and follow the table \u2013 results in cooperation.  \n- **Zero stock (S\u209c\u202f=\u202f0)**: Both actions yield zero payoff; always play C to signal prosocial intent.  \n- **Capacity saturation**: When the stock after growth would hit capacity, treat `S\u0302_coop` as capacity; the rule still prefers C because it preserves the sustainable maximum.  \n- **Unexpected audit\u2011induced loss**: After a round where you are audited and fined while defecting, immediately increase the required `coop_rate` threshold for the next round to 0.7, forcing a cooperative response to re\u2011establish trust.  \n\n**Prosocial orientation**\n\nThe strategy starts by cooperating, only switches to defection as a calibrated, temporary sanction when the observable cooperation level falls below a sustainable threshold or the stock becomes critically low. It continuously evaluates the long\u2011run benefit of maintaining the resource (via `S\u0302_coop` vs `S\u0302_def`) and never defects if the expected net gain after fines is non\u2011positive. The final round is always cooperative, reinforcing the norm that the common pool is not to be over\u2011exploited even at the game\u2019s end."

description_PROSOCIAL_6 = "**Prosocial Conditional\u2011Cooperation Strategy**\n\n**Parameters used**\n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `q`, `F` (from the game description)\n- `k`\u202f=\u202f3\u202f (length of the short\u2011term reputation window)  \n- `\u03b8`\u202f=\u202f0.75\u202f (minimum observed cooperation fraction to keep cooperating)  \n- `\u03c4`\u202f=\u202fcapacity\u202f\u00d7\u202f0.5\u202f (stock sustainability threshold)\n\n**State variables**\n- `S_t` \u2013 stock at the start of round\u202f`t`\n- `hist[t]` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in round\u202f`t` (observable after each round)\n- `recent_coop(t)` \u2013 fraction of cooperators among the last `k` observed opponent\u2011actions (including round\u202f`t\u20111`; if fewer than `k` rounds have occurred, use all available).\n\n**Decision rule for round\u202f`t` (0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr)**  \n\n```\nif t == 0:\n    action = C                                   # start cooperatively\nelse if S_t == 0:\n    action = C                                   # no consumption possible\nelse:\n    # 1. Expected net payoff of defecting (accounting for audit)\n    E_D = S_t / n - q * F\n\n    # 2. Payoff of cooperating\n    P_C = S_t / (2 * n)\n\n    # 3. Baseline comparison\n    if P_C >= E_D:\n        action = C                               # cooperation is at least as good\n    else:\n        # 4. Check sustainability and recent cooperation level\n        if S_t > \u03c4 and recent_coop(t) >= \u03b8:\n            action = C                           # preserve stock and reward observed cooperation\n        else:\n            action = D                           # defect when defecting is more profitable and the group is not sufficiently cooperative or stock is low\n```\n\n**Handling the final round (`t == r\u20111`)**  \nThe same rule is applied, but because audits never occur in the last round, `E_D = S_t / n`. The comparison automatically favors cooperation when the stock is modest; otherwise the rule still respects the sustainability threshold `\u03c4`.\n\n**Reputation update (after each round)**\n```\nrecord hist[t] = number_of_opponents_who_played_C\nrecent_coop(t+1) = average of (hist[t], hist[t-1], ..., hist[max(0,t-k+1)]) / n\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case summary**\n- **First round:** always cooperate (no history, encourages mutual trust).  \n- **Zero stock:** cooperate (consumption is zero for both actions).  \n- **Last round:** follow the same decision rule; audits are absent, so defect only if it strictly dominates cooperation and the stock is above the sustainability threshold.  \n\n**Prosocial intent**\nThe strategy cooperates whenever cooperation yields at least the expected net payoff of defecting, and additionally guards the common pool by requiring a healthy stock (`S_t > \u03c4`) and a sufficiently cooperative recent environment (`recent_coop \u2265 \u03b8`). Defection is used only as a corrective measure when it is objectively more profitable and the group\u2019s recent behavior or the resource level does not justify continued restraint. This balances individual incentives with long\u2011term preservation of the common resource."

description_PROSOCIAL_7 = "**Prosocial Adaptive Strategy (Cooperate\u2011Monitor\u2011Adjust, CMA)**  \n\n**Parameters available to the agent**  \n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `stock_t` (stock at the start of round\u202f`t`)  \n- `q` (audit probability) and `F` (fine per audited defection)  \n- `history[t] = (my_action_t, my_audit_t, opponents_coop_cnt_t, stock_{t+1})` for all previous rounds  \n\n**Derived constants**  \n- `C_gain_t   = stock_t / (2\u202fn)`\u2003\u2003// payoff if cooperate in round\u202f`t`  \n- `D_gain_t   = stock_t / n`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// payoff if defect before fine  \n- `ExpectedFine = q\u202f\u00d7\u202fF`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// expected monetary loss per defection in any non\u2011final round  \n- `NetD_t = D_gain_t \u2212 ExpectedFine`\u2003// expected net payoff from defecting  \n\n**Thresholds**  \n- `stock_low   = 0.30\u202f\u00d7\u202fcapacity`\u2003\u2003// below this the pool is at risk of collapse  \n- `defect_ratio_high = 0.50`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// >\u202f50\u202f% observed defectors triggers a tougher response  \n\n**Decision rule (applied each round\u202f`t`, 0\u2011indexed)**  \n\n```\nif t == r\u20111:                     # last round \u2013 no audits, retain prosocial tone\n    action = C\nelse:\n    # 1. Base prosocial bias: start with cooperation\n    action = C\n\n    # 2. Adjust for expected net benefit\n    if NetD_t > C_gain_t + \u03b5:    # \u03b5 is a tiny safety margin (e.g., 0.01)\n        # defect only when clearly more profitable even after expected fine\n        action = D\n\n    # 3. Stock\u2011safety guard\n    if stock_t < stock_low:\n        # when stock is low, defect to reduce consumption pressure\n        # (cooperate would consume more per capita)\n        action = D\n\n    # 4. Social\u2011monitoring guard\n    if t > 0:\n        # opponents_coop_cnt_t is the number of cooperators among the n\u20111 opponents\n        opp_coop_ratio = opponents_coop_cnt_t / (n\u20111)\n\n        if opp_coop_ratio < (1 \u2212 defect_ratio_high):   # many opponents defected\n            # adopt a calibrated retaliation: defect for at most 2 consecutive rounds,\n            # then return to cooperation if the stock improves\n            if recent_defections_to_opponents < 2:\n                action = D\n            else:\n                action = C\n        else:\n            # if opponents mostly cooperated, reset retaliation counter\n            recent_defections_to_opponents = 0\n```\n\n**State updates after each round**  \n- Record `my_action_t`, whether an audit occurred (`my_audit_t`), the observed `opponents_coop_cnt_t`, and the resulting `stock_{t+1}`.  \n- Increment `recent_defections_to_opponents` when `action == D` and the observed opponent cooperation ratio is below the high\u2011defection threshold; reset to\u202f0 otherwise.  \n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n- **Round\u202f0**: No opponent history; set `action = C` (baseline cooperation).  \n- **Round\u202fr\u20111** (final): Audits never occur; always cooperate to signal prosocial intent and avoid end\u2011game over\u2011exploitation.  \n- **Zero stock** (`stock_t = 0`): Both actions yield zero payoff; cooperate to keep the pool\u2019s symbolic integrity (no further depletion).  \n\n**Prosocial alignment**  \n- The default is cooperation, promoting sustainable stock levels.  \n- Defection is used sparingly, only when the expected net gain outweighs the cooperative payoff, when the stock is critically low, or when a sustained pattern of opponent defection threatens the common pool.  \n- Retaliation is limited (max\u202f2 successive rounds) and contingent on observable opponent behaviour, ensuring forgiveness and encouraging re\u2011cooperation.  \n\n**Summary of algorithmic flow**  \n\n```\nfor t in 0 \u2026 r\u20111:\n    compute C_gain_t, D_gain_t, ExpectedFine, NetD_t\n    if t == r\u20111:\n        action = C\n    else:\n        action = C\n        if NetD_t > C_gain_t + \u03b5:            action = D\n        if stock_t < stock_low:               action = D\n        if t > 0:\n            opp_ratio = opponents_coop_cnt_t / (n\u20111)\n            if opp_ratio < 1\u2011defect_ratio_high:\n                if recent_defections_to_opponents < 2:\n                    action = D\n                else: action = C\n            else: recent_defections_to_opponents = 0\n    execute action, observe audit, update history, update stock\n```"

description_PROSOCIAL_8 = "**Strategy: Adaptive Conditional Cooperation (ACC)**  \n\n**Parameters used:** n, r, capacity, audit_prob\u202fq, fine\u202fF, current round\u202ft, current stock\u202fS, observed number of cooperators among opponents in previous round\u202fC_{t\u20111}, sliding\u2011window defect rate\u202f\u03b4 (fraction of opponent defections over the last\u202fw\u202frounds, default\u202fw\u202f=\u202f3).\n\n---\n\n### Decision Rules  \n\n1. **Baseline rule** \u2013 In any round where the stock is positive, choose **Cooperate (C)** unless one of the following trigger conditions is satisfied.  \n\n2. **Trigger\u202fA \u2013 Stock safety**  \n   - Compute the *stock safety margin*\u202fM = S / capacity.  \n   - If M <\u202f\u03b8_stock (default\u202f\u03b8_stock\u202f=\u202f0.30) **and** the opponent defect rate over the last\u202fw\u202frounds \u03b4 >\u202f\u03b8_defect (default\u202f\u03b8_defect\u202f=\u202f0.40), **defect**.  \n   - Rationale: low stock together with many recent defections signals imminent collapse; temporary defection limits personal loss.\n\n3. **Trigger\u202fB \u2013 Audit deterrence**  \n   - Compute the *expected net gain* from defecting this round:  \n     `G_defect = S/n \u2013 q\u00b7F`  \n   - Compute the *gain from cooperating*:  \n     `G_coop   = S/(2n)`  \n   - If `G_defect \u2264 G_coop` (i.e., expected fine erodes the extra payoff), **cooperate**.  \n   - Otherwise keep the baseline rule (which is cooperate unless Trigger\u202fA fires).\n\n4. **Trigger\u202fC \u2013 Recent over\u2011exploitation**  \n   - After observing opponent actions in the previous round, if the number of opponents who defected \u2265\u202f\u23080.75\u00b7(n\u20111)\u2309, **defect** for this round (pre\u2011emptive retaliation).  \n   - Reset the defect\u2011rate window after this retaliation (i.e., treat this round as \u201creset\u201d for \u03b4 calculation).\n\n5. **Trigger\u202fD \u2013 Recovery mode**  \n   - If the stock in the **previous** round fell below 0.15\u00b7capacity **and** the current stock has risen above 0.25\u00b7capacity, **cooperate** regardless of other triggers (signal willingness to help recovery).\n\n### Edge\u2011Case handling  \n\n- **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0):** No history is available. Use only Trigger\u202fB (audit deterrence) to decide. If `G_defect > G_coop` and Trigger\u202fA conditions are not met, defect; otherwise cooperate.  \n\n- **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111):** Audits never occur, but the prosocial stance is maintained. **Always cooperate** (C) regardless of stock or opponent behavior.  \n\n- **Zero stock (S\u202f=\u202f0):** No consumption possible; actions have no payoff impact. **Choose cooperate** (C) to avoid unnecessary defection signalling.  \n\n- **Extreme audit probability (q\u202f=\u202f1) or fine (F very large):** Trigger\u202fB will force cooperation because `G_defect` becomes \u2264\u202f`G_coop`.  \n\n- **When \u03b4 cannot be computed** (fewer than\u202fw\u202fprevious rounds): compute \u03b4 using all available past rounds.  \n\n### Pseudocode  \n\n```\nfunction ACC(t, S, C_prev, opponent_defect_history):\n    if S == 0:\n        return C\n\n    if t == r-1:\n        return C          # last round forced cooperation\n\n    // compute expected gains\n    G_coop   = S / (2*n)\n    G_defect = S / n - q * F\n\n    // compute recent defect rate\n    w = min(3, length(opponent_defect_history))\n    \u03b4 = sum(last w entries of opponent_defect_history) / (w * (n-1))\n\n    // Trigger A\n    if (S / capacity) < \u03b8_stock and \u03b4 > \u03b8_defect:\n        return D\n\n    // Trigger C (immediate retaliation)\n    if C_prev is not None and (n-1 - C_prev) >= ceil(0.75*(n-1)):\n        return D\n\n    // Trigger D (recovery mode)\n    if (S_last < 0.15*capacity) and (S > 0.25*capacity):\n        return C\n\n    // Trigger B (audit deterrence)\n    if G_defect <= G_coop:\n        return C\n\n    // default baseline\n    return C\n```\n\n**State updates after each round:**  \n- Record whether each opponent defected (deduced from observed number of cooperators).  \n- Append a `1` for each opponent defect, `0` for each cooperate, to `opponent_defect_history`.  \n- Store the number of opponent cooperators as `C_prev` for the next round.  \n\nThe ACC strategy thus cooperates by default, backs off to defection only when the resource is endangered *and* opponents are consistently over\u2011exploiting, while exploiting audit information to avoid unprofitable defections. It remains prosocial throughout, especially by guaranteeing cooperation in the final round and during recovery phases."

description_PROSOCIAL_9 = "**State variables (maintained each round)**  \n- `t`\u202f: current round index (0\u202f\u2026\u202fr\u20111)  \n- `S`\u202f: current stock (observed at start of round)  \n- `c_obs`\u202f: number of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (0\u202f\u2026\u202fn\u20111)  \n- `p_est`\u202f: exponential\u2011moving\u2011average estimate of opponent cooperation probability, initialized to\u202f1.0  \n- `defect_seq`\u202f: length of the current consecutive\u2011defection streak observed in opponents (reset to\u202f0 when a cooperation is observed)  \n- `retaliation_counter`\u202f: rounds left in retaliation phase (0\u202fwhen not retaliating)  \n\nParameters (fixed for the match)  \n\n- `\u03b1 = 0.3`\u2003(smoothing factor for updating `p_est`)  \n- `low_stock = 0.3\u202f\u00d7\u202fcapacity`\u2003(stock threshold below which cooperation is forced)  \n- `high_stock = 0.7\u202f\u00d7\u202fcapacity`\u2003(stock above which generous cooperation is allowed)  \n- `tol = 0.6`\u2003(minimum estimated cooperation probability to continue cooperating)  \n- `max_retaliation = 2`\u2003(maximum retaliation rounds after detecting excess defection)  \n- `excess_defect_threshold = 0.4`\u2003(if observed defection proportion\u202f>\u202f0.4, trigger retaliation)  \n\n**Update rules (after each round, before next decision)**  \n\n```\nif t > 0:\n    # observed proportion of opponent cooperation this round\n    obs = c_obs / (n\u20111)               # 0 \u2264 obs \u2264 1\n    # exponential smoothing\n    p_est = \u03b1 * obs + (1\u2011\u03b1) * p_est\n\n    # update defection streak\n    if obs == 1.0:\n        defect_seq = 0\n    else:\n        defect_seq += 1\n```\n\n**Decision rule (chosen at the start of each round t)**  \n\n```\nif t == 0:\n    action = C                        # always start cooperatively\n\nelif t == r\u20111:\n    # last round: cooperate if any stock remains, otherwise defect (no audit)\n    action = C if S > 0 else D\n\nelif S <= low_stock:\n    # stock critically low \u2192 protect resource\n    action = C\n\nelif retaliation_counter > 0:\n    # continue retaliation\n    action = D\n    retaliation_counter -= 1\n\nelse:\n    # evaluate opponent cooperation\n    if p_est >= tol and S >= high_stock:\n        action = C                    # sufficient trust and abundant stock\n    else:\n        # compute expected net benefit of defecting this round\n        # expected fine = audit_prob * fine\n        exp_fine = audit_prob * fine\n        # payoff difference (defect \u2013 cooperate) = S/n \u2013 S/(2n) = S/(2n)\n        diff = S/(2*n) - exp_fine\n\n        if diff > 0 and p_est < tol:\n            action = D                # defect when profitable and trust low\n        else:\n            action = C                # otherwise cooperate\n```\n\n**Retaliation trigger** (evaluated after update of `p_est`):\n\n```\nif obs < (1 - excess_defect_threshold):\n    # opponent defection proportion exceeds threshold\n    retaliation_counter = max_retaliation\n```\n\n**Summary of behavior**  \n- Start cooperatively to signal prosocial intent.  \n- Cooperate unconditionally when stock is below `low_stock` to avoid collapse.  \n- Maintain cooperation while the estimated opponent cooperation probability stays above `tol` and the resource is abundant (`S \u2265 high_stock`).  \n- Switch to defection when the expected net gain (after accounting for expected fine) is positive and trust has fallen below `tol`.  \n- After observing a significant rise in opponent defections, retaliate with up to `max_retaliation` rounds of defection, then attempt to return to cooperation.  \n- In the final round, cooperate if any stock remains (no audit risk), otherwise defect.  "

description_PROSOCIAL_10 = "**Prosocial Adaptive Cooperation (PAC) Strategy**\n\n**Parameters used**\n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `audit_prob` (`q`), `fine` (`F`) \u2013 known from the game description.\n- `stock_t` \u2013 common pool stock at the start of round *t* (observable by all).\n- `my_history[t]` \u2013 my own actions (`C`/`D`) and whether I was audited in round *t*.\n- `opp_coop_count[t]` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in round *t* (observable after each round).\n\n---\n\n### 1. Core Decision Rule (per round *t*)\n\n1. **Compute expected net gain of defecting**  \n\n   ```\n   expected_fine   = q * F\n   extra_consumption = stock_t / n - stock_t / (2n)   // = stock_t / (2n)\n   net_defect_gain = extra_consumption - expected_fine\n   ```\n\n2. **Determine sustainability threshold**  \n\n   Let `sustainability_ratio = stock_t / capacity`.  \n   Define a dynamic threshold  \n\n   ```\n   coop_threshold = 0.5 + 0.4 * sustainablity_ratio   // lies in [0.5,0.9]\n   ```\n\n   This raises the willingness to cooperate when the stock is high and lowers it when the stock is low.\n\n3. **Assess opponent cooperation level**  \n\n   ```\n   opp_coop_ratio = opp_coop_count[t] / (n-1)\n   ```\n\n4. **Decision**\n\n   - **If** `t == r-1` (last round) **then** play **C** (maximise collective payoff, no audit risk).\n   - **Else if** `stock_t < 0.2 * capacity` **then** play **C** (protect the pool from collapse).\n   - **Else if** `net_defect_gain <= 0` **then** play **C** (defecting is not profitable in expectation).\n   - **Else**  \n       - **If** `opp_coop_ratio >= coop_threshold` **then** play **C** (reciprocate a cooperative environment).  \n       - **Else** play **D** (exploit a non\u2011cooperative environment, but only when expected gain > 0).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Edge\u2011Case Handling\n\n| Situation | Action |\n|----------|--------|\n| **Round 0 (first round)** | Play **C** unconditionally (no history, establishes prosocial norm). |\n| **Stock exactly 0** | Play **C** (consumption is zero; defecting would yield the same payoff but risks fine). |\n| **Audit observed on a prior defect** | After any round where I was audited and fined, set a *penalty flag* for the next two rounds: treat `net_defect_gain` as `net_defect_gain - penalty_buffer`, where `penalty_buffer = F/2`. This reduces temptation to defect immediately after being caught. |\n| **Opponent cooperation ratio suddenly spikes** (increase \u2265 0.3 compared to previous round) | Reset any lingering penalty flag and treat the round as if `opp_coop_ratio = 1.0` (full cooperation) for the decision calculation, encouraging a quick return to mutual cooperation. |\n| **Last two rounds** | In `t = r-2`, compute `coop_threshold` as above but add `+0.05` to favour cooperation, because the remaining horizon is short and the audit risk is still present. In `t = r-1` always cooperate (no audit). |\n| **Stock > capacity** (should never happen) | Treat `stock_t = capacity`. |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Adaptive Feedback Loop\n\nAfter each round *t* (except the last), update internal variables:\n\n1. **Update moving averages** (window = 3 rounds)  \n   - `avg_opp_coop = average of opp_coop_ratio over last 3 rounds`.  \n   - `avg_stock_ratio = average of stock_t / capacity over last 3 rounds`.\n\n2. **Adjust threshold scaling**  \n   Replace the static `0.4` multiplier in `coop_threshold` with  \n   ```\n   scaling = 0.3 + 0.2 * avg_stock_ratio   // yields 0.3\u20130.5\n   coop_threshold = 0.5 + scaling * avg_stock_ratio\n   ```\n   This makes the strategy more forgiving when the pool has been stable and more cautious when it has been trending down.\n\n3. **Record audit outcomes** to enforce the penalty flag described above.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Summary of Algorithm (pseudocode)\n\n```python\ndef decide_action(t, stock_t, opp_coop_count, my_history, penalty_flag):\n    # constants\n    q = audit_prob\n    F = fine\n    n_players = n\n    capacity_val = capacity\n\n    # last round: always cooperate\n    if t == r-1:\n        return 'C'\n\n    # compute ratios\n    stock_ratio = stock_t / capacity_val\n    opp_coop_ratio = opp_coop_count / (n_players - 1)\n\n    # expected net gain from defecting\n    extra_cons = stock_t / (2 * n_players)\n    net_defect_gain = extra_cons - q * F\n    if penalty_flag:\n        net_defect_gain -= F / 2   # penalty buffer\n\n    # low stock safeguard\n    if stock_t < 0.2 * capacity_val:\n        return 'C'\n\n    # defect not profitable\n    if net_defect_gain <= 0:\n        return 'C'\n\n    # dynamic cooperation threshold\n    scaling = 0.3 + 0.2 * stock_ratio          # 0.3\u20130.5\n    coop_thresh = 0.5 + scaling * stock_ratio   # approx 0.5\u20130.9\n    if t == r-2:\n        coop_thresh += 0.05\n\n    # choose based on opponent behavior\n    if opp_coop_ratio >= coop_thresh:\n        return 'C'\n    else:\n        return 'D'\n```\n\nThe strategy starts cooperatively, monitors the health of the commons and the observed cooperation level, and only defects when the expected monetary gain outweighs the audit risk **and** the environment signals low reciprocity. It always cooperates in the final round, protects the pool when stock is critically low, and incorporates a short\u2011term penalty after being fined to deter repeated exploitation. This adaptive, prosocial rule set works across a wide spectrum of opponent strategies while preserving the sustainability of the common resource."

description_PROSOCIAL_11 = "**Variables**\n- `trust_t`\u202f\u2208\u202f[0,1]: estimate of opponents\u2019 propensity to cooperate at the start of round\u202ft.  \n  Initialize `trust_0 = 1`.  \n- `S_t`: stock level observed at the start of round\u202ft.  \n- `q`: audit probability, `F`: fine amount (constants of the game).  \n\n**Update of trust**\nAfter observing the number `c_{t-1}` of opponents who cooperated in round\u202ft\u20111 (0\u202f\u2264\u202fc_{t-1}\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111):\n```\ntrust_t = ((t-1) * trust_{t-1} + c_{t-1} / (n-1)) / t\n```\n\n**Decision rule for round\u202ft (0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr)**\n1. Compute the expected net payoff of defecting given audit risk:\n```\nnet_defect = S_t / n - q * F\n```\n2. Compute the payoff of cooperating:\n```\npay_coop = S_t / (2n)\n```\n3. **If** `net_defect <= pay_coop` **then** choose **Cooperate**.  \n   (Defection is not profitable after expected fine.)\n4. **Else** (defection yields higher expected immediate payoff):\n   - Define a stock\u2011health factor `h = S_t / capacity`.\n   - Define a trust\u2011threshold `\u03b8 = 0.5`.\n   - **If** `trust_t >= \u03b8` **and** `h >= 0.4` **then** choose **Cooperate**.  \n     (Opponents appear cooperative and the pool is healthy; sustain cooperation.)\n   - **Else if** `h < 0.2` **then** choose **Defect**.  \n     (Very low stock; protect own payoff while the pool is already near collapse.)\n   - **Else** choose **Cooperate** with probability `p = h` and **Defect** with probability `1\u2011p`.  \n     (Higher stock \u2192 higher cooperation probability; adapts to depletion.)\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- **Round\u202f0 (first round):** `trust_0 = 1`; apply the decision rule directly (will typically pick Cooperate because `net_defect > pay_coop` only when fine is negligible).\n- **Round\u202fr\u20111 (last round):** audits never occur, so set `q = 0` for that round; apply the same rule, which will favor Cooperate because `net_defect = S / n` > `pay_coop` but `trust` and stock\u2011health still guide a prosocial choice.  \n- **If the stock ever reaches 0:** set `S_t = 0`; all subsequent payoffs are 0 regardless of action; continue to update `trust` normally (observed opponent actions will be all Defect because only possible consumption is 0).  \n\n**Summary of actions**\n```\nif net_defect <= pay_coop:\n    action = C\nelse:\n    if trust_t >= 0.5 and S_t / capacity >= 0.4:\n        action = C\n    elif S_t / capacity < 0.2:\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C with prob (S_t / capacity), else D\n```\nThe strategy uses only publicly observable parameters, the history of observed opponent cooperation counts, and the current stock level, and it automatically adjusts to audit risk and resource depletion while favoring collective sustainability."

description_PROSOCIAL_12 = "**Prosocial Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**Parameters used**\n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `audit_prob q`, `fine F` (read from game description)\n- `stock_t` \u2013 current stock at the beginning of round\u202f`t`\n- `opp_coop_rate_t` \u2013 proportion of opponents that cooperated in round\u202f`t\u20111` (undefined for\u202ft\u202f=\u202f0)\n- `coop_history` \u2013 list of own past actions (C/D)\n- `stock_history` \u2013 list of observed stock levels after each round\n- `window = min(3, t)` \u2013 number of most recent rounds used to compute `opp_coop_rate_t`\n\n**Decision rule (per round t = 0 \u2026 r\u20111)**\n\n1. **First round (t = 0)**\n   - Action = **C**.\n\n2. **Last round (t = r\u20111)**\n   - Action = **C** (no audit risk and no future rounds to protect).\n\n3. **Intermediate rounds (0 < t < r\u20111)**\n   - Compute `opp_coop_rate_t` = (number of opponents that played C in the last `window` rounds) / (n\u20111\u202f\u00b7\u202fwindow).  \n     *(If no data, treat as 1.0.)*\n   - Compute `stock_ratio` = `stock_t` / `capacity`.\n\n   - **Case A \u2013 Stock is abundant (stock_ratio \u2265 0.6)**\n     - If `opp_coop_rate_t` \u2265 0.5 \u2192 Action = **C**.\n     - Else \u2192 Action = **C** with probability `p = opp_coop_rate_t` (randomized to match observed cooperation level).  \n\n   - **Case B \u2013 Stock is moderate (0.3 \u2264 stock_ratio < 0.6)**\n     - If `opp_coop_rate_t` \u2265 0.7 \u2192 Action = **C**.\n     - Else \u2192 Action = **C** with probability `p = 0.5\u202f\u00b7\u202fopp_coop_rate_t + 0.25`.\n   \n   - **Case C \u2013 Stock is scarce (stock_ratio < 0.3)**\n     - If `opp_coop_rate_t` \u2265 0.8 \u2192 Action = **C**.\n     - Else \u2192 Action = **D**.\n\n4. **Audit\u2011adjusted defection deterrence**\n   - When the rule above selects **D**, first compute the expected net gain:\n     - `expected_gain = stock_t / n \u2013 (stock_t / (2*n)) \u2013 q * F`.\n   - If `expected_gain` \u2264 0, override to **C** (avoid defection when fines outweigh extra consumption).\n\n5. **Updating histories**\n   - After each round record own action, observed number of opponent cooperators, and resulting `stock_{t+1}`.\n   - Use these records for the next round\u2019s calculations.\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- If `stock_t` becomes 0, automatically choose **C** (no consumption possible, cooperation maintains the rule).\n- If `opp_coop_rate_t` cannot be computed (e.g., before any opponent action is observed), assume full cooperation (`opp_coop_rate_t = 1`).\n- Randomized choices (cases with probability `p`) must be drawn independently each round.\n\n**Prosocial alignment**\n- The strategy favours cooperation when the common pool is healthy or when opponents are also cooperating.\n- Defection is allowed only when the stock is low and opponent cooperation is insufficient, and even then only if the expected net benefit after accounting for audit risk is positive.\n- In the final round the player always cooperates, ensuring no exploitation of others."

description_PROSOCIAL_13 = "**Prosocial Adaptive Cooperation Strategy**\n\n**State variables (maintained each round)**\n- `stock` \u2013 current common\u2011pool level (observed at start of round).  \n- `opp_coop_rate` \u2013 exponential\u2011moving\u2011average of the proportion of opponents that cooperated in the last\u202fk rounds (initialize\u202f1.0).  \n- `defect_streak` \u2013 number of consecutive rounds in which observed opponent defections \u2265 `defect_threshold`.  \n- `audit_prob` \u2013 given game parameter\u202fq.  \n\n**Parameters (set once from game description)**\n- `capacity` \u2013 max sustainable stock.  \n- `n` \u2013 number of players.  \n- `k = 5` \u2013 smoothing window for `opp_coop_rate`.  \n- `defect_threshold = 0.3` \u2013 if \u2265\u202f30\u202f% of opponents defect in a round, treat it as \u201csignificant defection\u201d.  \n- `max_defect_streak = 2` \u2013 after two such rounds, trigger retaliation.  \n- `stock_low = 0.25 * capacity` \u2013 below this level the pool is considered fragile.  \n- `stock_high = 0.75 * capacity` \u2013 above this level the pool is healthy.  \n\n**Decision rule (applied at the beginning of each round t)**\n\n```\nif t == 0:                     # first round\n    action = C\nelif t == r-1:                 # last round (no audit)\n    # Prosocial priority: preserve remaining stock for final payoff.\n    # If stock is fragile, cooperate; otherwise cooperate to avoid unnecessary depletion.\n    action = C\nelse:\n    # 1. Update opponent cooperation estimate\n    observed_coop = (number_of_opponents_reported_C) / (n-1)\n    opp_coop_rate = 0.8*opp_coop_rate + 0.2*observed_coop   # EMA\n\n    # 2. Detect persistent defection\n    if observed_coop < (1 - defect_threshold):\n        defect_streak += 1\n    else:\n        defect_streak = max(0, defect_streak-1)   # forgiveness decay\n\n    # 3. Core prosocial logic\n    if stock < stock_low:\n        # Stock fragile \u2013 never defect, keep consumption minimal.\n        action = C\n    elif defect_streak >= max_defect_streak:\n        # Retaliate once to discourage continued defection, then return to cooperation.\n        action = D\n        # Reset streak after retaliation to give opponents a chance to reform.\n        defect_streak = 0\n    else:\n        # Normal condition: cooperate if opponents are sufficiently cooperative,\n        # otherwise cooperates with a small probability of defection to test\n        # willingness to re\u2011establish cooperation.\n        if opp_coop_rate >= 0.7:\n            action = C\n        elif opp_coop_rate >= 0.4:\n            # Mixed environment \u2013 cooperate with 80\u202f% probability.\n            action = C with probability 0.8 else D\n        else:\n            # Highly uncooperative environment \u2013 cooperate with 50\u202f% probability\n            # to avoid excessive stock loss while still signaling willingness.\n            action = C with probability 0.5 else D\n```\n\n**Auditing handling**\n- When `action == D` in any non\u2011final round, a fine of `F` may be incurred with probability `q`.  \n- The strategy does not modify its choice based on the random audit outcome; however, after observing a fine it treats the round as a \u201cdefection observed\u201d for updating `defect_streak` (i.e., the audit outcome is already reflected in the opponent\u2011reported cooperation count because only the player herself knows she was fined).\n\n**Edge\u2011case specifics**\n- **First round**: unconditional cooperation to seed a high stock and signal prosocial intent.  \n- **Last round**: unconditional cooperation because there is no future impact; cooperating also avoids a final stock crash that would lower the payoff of any remaining harvest (since payoff is calculated before growth).  \n- **Stock at zero**: if `stock == 0` the payoff from any action is zero; the strategy defaults to cooperation (no further damage).  \n- **Audit probability zero** (`q == 0`): the same decision rule applies; the absence of fines makes defection slightly more attractive, but the `defect_streak` and `stock_low` guards prevent reckless depletion.  \n\n**Summary of behavior**\n- Start cooperative and stay cooperative while the pool is healthy and opponents largely cooperate.  \n- Swing to brief, single\u2011round defections only as a calibrated retaliation when opponents repeatedly over\u2011exploit the resource.  \n- Never defect when the stock falls below a quarter of capacity, preserving the commons.  \n- Use probabilistic softening of cooperation in moderately uncooperative environments to keep the system from collapsing while still signaling willingness to cooperate."

description_PROSOCIAL_14 = "**Strategy: Adaptive Conditional Cooperation (ACC)**  \n\n**Parameters used**  \n- `n, r, capacity, q, F` (game description)  \n- `stock_t` \u2013 common\u2011pool stock at the beginning of round\u202f`t`  \n- `opp_coop_t` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in round\u202f`t\u20111` (observed after each round)  \n- `history_i` \u2013 list of own past actions and received audits/fines  \n\n**Derived quantities**  \n- `stock_ratio_t = stock_t / capacity` (\u2208[0,1])  \n- `coop_ratio_t = opp_coop_t / (n\u20111)` (\u2208[0,1]; undefined for `t=0`, treat as 1)  \n\n**Thresholds (tunable but fixed for the whole game)**  \n- `MIN_STOCK = 0.45`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// below this the pool is considered stressed  \n- `MIN_COOP  = 0.60`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// below this opponents are largely defecting  \n- `GAIN_MARGIN = 0.02`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// require at least 2\u202f% higher expected payoff to justify defection  \n\n**Decision rule (applied each round\u202f`t`, `0 \u2264 t < r`)**\n\n```\nif t == 0:                     # first round\n    action = C\nelse if t == r-1:              # last round (no audit)\n    # prosocial: keep cooperating unless stock is already exhausted\n    action = C if stock_t > 0 else D\nelse:\n    # 1. Compute expected payoffs accounting for audit risk\n    E_coop = stock_t / (2*n)\n    E_def  = stock_t / n - q*F\n    \n    # 2. Evaluate sustainability signals\n    low_stock   = stock_ratio_t < MIN_STOCK\n    low_coop    = coop_ratio_t < MIN_COOP\n    profitable_def = (E_def - E_coop) > GAIN_MARGIN\n    \n    # 3. Choose action\n    if low_stock:\n        # Stock stressed \u2192 cooperate to reduce consumption\n        action = C\n    elif low_coop and profitable_def:\n        # Many opponents defect and defecting is noticeably better\n        action = D\n    else:\n        # Default prosocial stance\n        action = C\n```\n\n**Update after each round**\n\n- Record own action and whether an audit occurred (`a_i,t`).  \n- Record `opp_coop_t` = number of opponents that played\u202fC (derived from aggregate observation).  \n- Re\u2011compute `stock_{t+1}` using the game\u2019s stock dynamics (the environment does this; the strategy only reads the new `stock_t`).  \n\n**Forgiveness / re\u2011evaluation**\n\nWhen the strategy defects (`action = D`) it re\u2011checks the two sustainability signals every subsequent round. As soon as either  \n\n- `low_stock` becomes true (stock fell below `MIN_STOCK`), **or**  \n- `low_coop` becomes false (opponents\u2019 cooperation ratio rises to \u2265\u202f`MIN_COOP`)  \n\nthe strategy switches back to cooperation in the next round. This provides a \u201csoft\u2011reset\u201d after a defection episode and guarantees that prolonged defection never persists when the pool recovers or opponents improve.\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n- **Round\u202f0**: always cooperate (no information yet, sets a prosocial baseline).  \n- **Round\u202fr\u20111** (final round): audit never occurs, but the policy still cooperates unless the stock is already zero (in which case defection yields zero anyway).  \n- **Zero stock**: if `stock_t == 0` the payoff from any action is zero; the rule falls through to the \u201clow_stock\u201d clause and cooperates (neutral choice).  \n- **Division by zero**: `coop_ratio_t` is defined as 1 when `t==0` (no opponent data).  \n\n**Resulting behavior**\n\n- Maintains cooperation as long as the common pool is healthy and opponents are reasonably cooperative.  \n- Defects only when (a) the pool is abundant, (b) opponents are predominantly defecting, and (c) the expected net gain after accounting for audit risk exceeds cooperation by the preset margin.  \n- Quickly returns to cooperation when the ecological signal (`stock_ratio`) deteriorates or when opponents\u2019 behavior improves, ensuring long\u2011run sustainability and a prosocial orientation."

description_PROSOCIAL_15 = "**Strategy \u201cAdaptive Prosocial Guard\u201d**\n\n**State variables (updated each round)**\n- `S` \u2013 current stock level.\n- `c_obs` \u2013 total number of opponent cooperations observed so far.\n- `d_obs` \u2013 total number of opponent defections observed so far.\n- `t` \u2013 current round index (0 \u2026\u202fr\u202f\u2212\u202f1).\n\nDerived quantities  \n- `stock_ratio = S / capacity`  \n- `coop_rate = c_obs / ((n\u20111)\u00b7t)` \u2003(if `t > 0`, else undefined)  \n- `expected_defect_gain = S/(2n) \u2013 q\u00b7F`\u2003(the net gain from defecting after expected fine)\n\n**Fixed thresholds (tunable but constant for a given game)**\n- `\u03b8_stock = 0.5`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u202f(maintain at least half the carrying capacity)  \n- `\u03b8_coop  = 0.6`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u202f(minimum observed cooperation to keep cooperating)\n\n**Decision rule (executed each round before acting)**  \n\n```\nif t == r\u20111:                     # last round (never audited)\n    action = C\nelif expected_defect_gain <= 0: # defect is not profitable after expected fine\n    action = C\nelif stock_ratio < \u03b8_stock or (t > 0 and coop_rate < \u03b8_coop):\n    action = D\nelse:\n    action = C\n```\n\n**Update after round**\n1. Record own action and any fine paid (only needed to compute `expected_defect_gain` in next round).  \n2. Observe number `k` of opponent cooperations announced by the game engine.  \n   - `c_obs += k`  \n   - `d_obs += (n\u20111) \u2013 k`  \n\n**Forgiveness / recovery**\n- If the strategy defects in a round, it will return to cooperation as soon as **both** conditions hold for **two consecutive** subsequent rounds:  \n  * `stock_ratio \u2265 \u03b8_stock` **and** `coop_rate \u2265 \u03b8_coop`.  \n- This prevents permanent retaliation and allows re\u2011establishing mutual cooperation when the environment improves.\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- **Round\u202f0**: `coop_rate` is undefined; decision reduces to the stock and expected\u2011gain test.  \n- **Audit**: The rule already incorporates the expected fine (`q\u00b7F`). Because the last round is never audited, the strategy always cooperates then.  \n- **Zero stock**: If `S = 0`, both `expected_defect_gain` and `stock_ratio` are 0, so the rule selects cooperation (no consumption possible, so any action yields 0 payoff).  \n\n**Prosocial intent**\n- The strategy cooperates whenever the commons are sufficiently abundant and the opponent community appears cooperative, and it only defects to signal disapproval when the resource is threatened or cooperation drops below the prescribed level.  \n- Immediate forgiveness after the environment recovers ensures long\u2011term sustainability of the common pool."

description_PROSOCIAL_16 = "**Prosocial Adaptive Cooperation (PAC) Strategy**\n\n**Parameters derived from game description**\n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `q`, `F` are given.\n- `\u03b8_stock = 0.6`\u2003(critical stock fraction; can be tuned offline)\n- `\u03b8_coop = 0.5`\u2003(minimum observed cooperation rate among opponents to keep cooperating)\n- `\u03b8_forgive = 0.3`\u2003(minimum cooperation rate to resume cooperation after a defection phase)\n\n**State variables (maintained each round)**\n- `S_t`\u2003current stock before any consumption.\n- `c_{t-1}`\u2003observed number of opponents who cooperated in the previous round (0\u202f\u2264\u202fc\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111).\n- `defect_streak`\u2003consecutive rounds the player has defected.\n- `cooperate_streak`\u2003consecutive rounds the player has cooperated.\n\n**Decision rule (executed at the start of each round t)**\n\n```\nif t == 0:                     # first round\n    action = C\nelif t == r-1:                 # last round (no audit, preserve stock)\n    action = C\nelse:\n    # 1. Stock health check\n    if S_t < \u03b8_stock * capacity:\n        # stock low \u2192 protect common pool\n        # cooperate only if opponents are sufficiently cooperative\n        if c_{t-1} / (n-1) >= \u03b8_coop:\n            action = C\n        else:\n            action = D\n    else:\n        # 2. Social reciprocity check\n        coop_rate = c_{t-1} / (n-1)\n\n        if coop_rate >= \u03b8_coop:\n            # strong cooperation signal \u2192 cooperate\n            action = C\n            defect_streak = 0\n            cooperate_streak += 1\n        elif coop_rate >= \u03b8_forgive and cooperate_streak > 0:\n            # opponents slipped but still some cooperation \u2192 give a grace round\n            action = C\n            defect_streak = 0\n            cooperate_streak += 1\n        else:\n            # 3. Expected\u2011penalty assessment\n            expected_fine = q * F\n            # marginal gain from defecting vs cooperating:\n            marginal_gain = S_t / n - S_t / (2*n) = S_t / (2*n)\n            if marginal_gain > expected_fine:\n                action = D\n                cooperate_streak = 0\n                defect_streak += 1\n            else:\n                action = C\n                cooperate_streak += 1\n                defect_streak = 0\n```\n\n**Updating observations after each round**\n1. Record own audit outcome (only needed to compute actual fine, already reflected in payoff).\n2. Receive anonymous count `c_t` of opponent cooperations; store for next round.\n3. Update the stock `S_{t+1}` using the game\u2019s dynamics (handled by the environment).\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- **Round\u202f0**: unconditional cooperation to seed a high stock and signal prosocial intent.\n- **Round\u202fr\u20111**: unconditional cooperation because no audit risk and preserving the final stock maximizes collective payoff.\n- **Zero stock (`S_t = 0`)**: both actions yield zero payoff; default to cooperation to avoid needless depletion in future (if any).\n- **Audit\u2011only rounds**: the expected\u2011penalty branch already incorporates audit probability; the strategy may defect when the marginal gain outweighs expected fine, otherwise cooperates.\n\n**Prosocial justification embedded in the rule set**\n- Cooperate when the common pool is healthy or when opponents demonstrate sufficient cooperation.\n- Defect only as a calculated response to low stock combined with low opponent cooperation, and only when the expected net gain exceeds the risk\u2011adjusted cost of a fine.\n- Include a forgiveness window (`\u03b8_forgive`) to allow recovery from temporary defection spikes, preventing endless retaliation.\n- Always cooperate in the first and final rounds to promote a sustainable baseline and maximize total group payoff."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_1 = "**Strategy Overview**\n\nAt every round *t* (\u202f0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr\u202f) the agent computes two hypothetical outcomes\u2014*Cooperate* (C) and *Defect* (D)\u2014using the current stock\u202fS\u209c, the observed cooperation rate of opponents, the audit probability\u202fq, the fine\u202fF, and the remaining number of rounds\u202fR = r\u202f\u2212\u202ft\u202f\u2212\u202f1.  \nThe action with the higher *expected total return* (immediate payoff\u202f+\u202fprojected future return) is chosen; ties are broken in favour of Defect.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Required variables (updated each round)\n\n| Symbol | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| **S** | Current stock (float) |\n| **R** | Rounds remaining after the current one (integer) |\n| **c\u0302** | Estimated probability that a given opponent will cooperate in the current round (float). Computed as a moving average of the observed opponent\u2011cooperation share over the last *k* rounds (k\u202f=\u202f3, default). If no history yet, set **c\u0302 = 1** (optimistic). |\n| **q** | Audit probability (given) |\n| **F** | Fine per audited defection (given) |\n| **n** | Number of players (given) |\n| **cap** | Capacity (given) |\n\n---\n\n### 2. Payoff and stock forecasts\n\n**Immediate payoffs**\n\n```\npay_C = S / (2*n)                         # no fine when cooperating\npay_D = S / n - q * F                      # expected fine subtracted\n```\n\n**Consumption forecasts**\n\n```\nopp_cons_C = c\u0302 * (S / (2*n)) + (1-c\u0302) * (S / n)   # each opponent's expected take if we cooperate\nopp_cons_D = opp_cons_C                           # opponents are assumed to keep the same behaviour\n```\n\nTotal consumption if we *Cooperate*:\n\n```\ntot_cons_C = S/(2*n) + (n-1) * opp_cons_C\n```\n\nTotal consumption if we *Defect*:\n\n```\ntot_cons_D = S/n       + (n-1) * opp_cons_D\n```\n\n**Stock after consumption (before growth)**\n\n```\nS'_C = max(0, S - tot_cons_C)\nS'_D = max(0, S - tot_cons_D)\n```\n\n**Growth step**\n\n```\ngrow(x) = 2 * x * (1 - x / cap)\n```\n\n**Stock at start of next round**\n\n```\nnext_S_C = min( S'_C + grow(S'_C), cap )\nnext_S_D = min( S'_D + grow(S'_D), cap )\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Projected future return\n\nAssume that from the next round onward the population will *cooperate* (the most stock\u2011preserving behaviour). Under that assumption the per\u2011round payoff each player would receive is `next_S_X / (2*n)` where X\u2208{C,D}.\n\n```\nfuture_return_X = R * ( next_S_X / (2*n) )\n```\n\nIf **R = 0** (last round), `future_return_X = 0`.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Decision rule\n\n```\ntotal_C = pay_C + future_return_C\ntotal_D = pay_D + future_return_D\n\nif total_D > total_C:\n    action = D\nelse:\n    action = C        # also when equal, prefer D \u2192 change to D for strict individualism\n```\n\n*Strict individualistic tie\u2011breaker*: replace the final `else` with `action = D`.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Edge\u2011case handling\n\n| Situation | Rule |\n|-----------|------|\n| **First round** (no opponent history) | Set `c\u0302 = 1`. Apply the decision rule normally. |\n| **Last round** (t = r\u20111) | Set `R = 0`. Future return = 0 for both actions, so the rule reduces to comparing `pay_D` vs `pay_C`. Since `pay_D` \u2265 `pay_C` (fine\u2011adjusted), the algorithm will choose **Defect** (unless the fine makes `pay_D` negative; in that case it will still choose **Defect** because a negative payoff is unavoidable if you cooperate). |\n| **Stock depleted** (S = 0) | Both immediate payoffs are 0, future returns are 0. Choose **Defect** (no cost, maintains the individualistic stance). |\n| **Audit probability q = 0** | Fine term disappears; the rule naturally prefers **Defect** unless the projected future stock loss makes `total_C` larger. |\n| **Fine so large that pay_D < 0** | The algorithm still follows the comparison; if `pay_D` is negative and `pay_C` is non\u2011negative, **Cooperate** will be selected. This is the only circumstance where the agent tolerates a loss to avoid an even larger expected loss. |\n| **Observed opponent cooperation share = 0** (all opponents always defect) | `c\u0302 = 0`. The forecasts will show rapid stock collapse; the agent will likely defect to maximise immediate gain while the stock lasts. |\n\n---\n\n### 6. Pseudocode (per\u2011round)\n\n```python\ndef decide_action(S, round_idx, history, params):\n    n      = params.n\n    cap    = params.capacity\n    q      = params.audit_prob\n    F      = params.fine\n    r      = params.rounds\n    R      = r - round_idx - 1                     # rounds left after this one\n\n    # 1. Estimate opponent cooperation rate\n    if not history:                # first round\n        coop_est = 1.0\n    else:\n        last_k = history[-3:]                      # up to 3 previous rounds\n        coop_counts = sum(h['opp_coop'] for h in last_k)\n        coop_est = coop_counts / ((len(last_k)) * (n-1))\n\n    # 2. Immediate payoffs\n    pay_C = S / (2.0 * n)\n    pay_D = S / n - q * F\n\n    # 3. Expected opponent consumption (same for both hypotheses)\n    opp_cons = coop_est * (S / (2.0 * n)) + (1 - coop_est) * (S / n)\n\n    # 4. Total consumption\n    tot_C = S/(2.0*n) + (n-1) * opp_cons\n    tot_D = S/n        + (n-1) * opp_cons\n\n    # 5. Stock after consumption\n    S_C_rem = max(0.0, S - tot_C)\n    S_D_rem = max(0.0, S - tot_D)\n\n    # 6. Growth function\n    def grow(x): return 2.0 * x * (1.0 - x / cap)\n\n    # 7. Stock at next round\n    next_S_C = min(S_C_rem + grow(S_C_rem), cap)\n    next_S_D = min(S_D_rem + grow(S_D_rem), cap)\n\n    # 8. Future returns (assume everyone cooperates thereafter)\n    future_C = R * (next_S_C / (2.0 * n))\n    future_D = R * (next_S_D / (2.0 * n))\n\n    # 9. Total expected returns\n    total_C = pay_C + future_C\n    total_D = pay_D + future_D\n\n    # 10. Decision (strict individualist: D on tie)\n    return 'D' if total_D >= total_C else 'C'\n```\n\nThe strategy uses only publicly available information (current stock, own audit outcome, and the aggregate count of opponent cooperators) and updates its estimate of opponents\u2019 behaviour each round. It is fully adaptive, seeks to maximise the agent\u2019s own cumulative payoff, and respects the required edge\u2011case conventions."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_2 = "**Strategy: Self\u2011Interested Sustainable (SIS)**  \n\nAt every round *t* (0\u2011indexed) the agent computes the expected long\u2011run value of preserving stock versus the immediate gain from defecting, taking the audit risk *q* and fine *F* into account. The decision rule is:\n\n```\nInput each round t:\n    S  \u2190 current stock\n    R  \u2190 r - t - 1                     # remaining rounds after this one\n    q  \u2190 audit_prob\n    F  \u2190 fine\n    n  \u2190 number of players\n    C  \u2190 capacity\n\n    #--- 1. Estimate opponents\u2019 cooperation rate -----------------\n    if t == 0:                               # no history\n        p \u2190 0.5                               # neutral prior\n    else:\n        c_last \u2190 # of opponents who cooperated in round t\u20111\n        p \u2190 c_last / (n-1)                    # observed proportion\n\n    #--- 2. Compute stock evolution if we cooperate -------------\n    our_coop   \u2190 S / (2*n)\n    opp_cons   \u2190 (n-1) * ( p * (S / n) + (1-p) * (S / (2*n)) )\n    tot_cons_coop \u2190 our_coop + opp_cons\n    S_rem_coop \u2190 max(0, S - tot_cons_coop)\n    growth_coop \u2190 2 * S_rem_coop * (1 - S_rem_coop / C)\n    S_next_coop \u2190 min(S_rem_coop + growth_coop, C)\n\n    #--- 3. Compute stock evolution if we defect ----------------\n    our_def   \u2190 S / n\n    # opponents assumed unchanged (same p)\n    tot_cons_def \u2190 our_def + opp_cons\n    S_rem_def \u2190 max(0, S - tot_cons_def)\n    growth_def \u2190 2 * S_rem_def * (1 - S_rem_def / C)\n    S_next_def \u2190 min(S_rem_def + growth_def, C)\n\n    #--- 4. Immediate net gain from defecting -------------------\n    immediate_gain \u2190 (S / n) - q * F - (S / (2*n))   # = S/(2n) - qF\n\n    #--- 5. Future value of the extra stock we would keep -------\n    \u0394S \u2190 S_next_coop - S_next_def                     # \u2265 0\n    # Conservative estimate: each future unit of stock yields at most\n    # 1/(2n) to us per round (we could later cooperate to harvest it)\n    future_value \u2190 \u0394S * R * (1 / (2*n))\n\n    #--- 6. Decision -------------------------------------------\n    if immediate_gain > future_value:\n        action \u2190 D\n    else:\n        action \u2190 C\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n| Situation                               | Action |\n|----------------------------------------|--------|\n| **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0)**                | Use prior *p\u202f=\u202f0.5* in the computation above. |\n| **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111)**                | No future rounds (R\u202f=\u202f0) and no audit. Immediate payoff dominates, so always choose **D**. |\n| **Stock S = 0**                         | Both actions yield 0 payoff; choose **C** (harmless). |\n| **Capacity reached (S = C) and growth would overshoot** | Stock update uses `min(..., C)` automatically; decision follows the rule above. |\n| **Audit probability q = 0** or fine F = 0 | `immediate_gain = S/(2n)`; the rule still compares it to future value, possibly leading to cooperation when future loss outweighs the extra half\u2011share. |\n\nThe SIS strategy is fully individualistic: it maximizes the agent\u2019s expected cumulative payoff by balancing the immediate extra consumption from defecting against the discounted value of the stock it helps preserve for later rounds, while directly incorporating the stochastic fine risk. It adapts each round to the observed cooperation level of opponents and to the evolving stock level."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_3 = "**Strategy \u201cThreshold\u2011Defect\u2011Cooperate (TDC)\u201d**\n\n**Parameters used at each round *t*:**\n- `S` \u2013 current stock (after the growth step of the previous round).\n- `q` \u2013 audit probability (given in the game description).\n- `F` \u2013 fine per audited defection.\n- `n` \u2013 number of players.\n- `r` \u2013 total number of rounds.\n- `oppDefRate_t` \u2013 proportion of opponents that defected in round *t\u20111* (observed from the anonymous count).  \n  For *t = 0* define `oppDefRate_0 = 0`.\n\n**Derived constants (computed once):**\n- `T = 2 * n * q * F`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 // stock level above which a raw\u2011payoff\u2011comparison favours defecting\n- `\u03b1 = 0.3`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 // sensitivity to recent opponent behaviour\n- `\u03b2 = 0.5`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 // safety margin when stock is very low\n\n**Decision rule (applied each round *t*):**\n\n```\nif t == r-1:                     # last round \u2013 never audited\n    action = D                  # always defect (max immediate payoff)\nelse if S == 0:\n    action = C                  # Cooperate to avoid a possible fine (payoff 0 either way)\nelse:\n    # Base comparison: is raw expected payoff of D larger than C?\n    # Expected payoff of D = S/n - q*F\n    # Expected payoff of C = S/(2n)\n    rawPreferDefect = (S > T)\n\n    # Adjust for opponent behaviour:\n    # If many opponents defected last round, increase caution.\n    # EffectiveThreshold = T * (1 + \u03b1 * oppDefRate_t)\n    effectiveThreshold = T * (1 + \u03b1 * oppDefRate_t)\n\n    # Re\u2011evaluate with adjusted threshold\n    preferDefect = (S > effectiveThreshold)\n\n    # Add safety margin when stock is close to depletion\n    if S < \u03b2 * capacity:\n        # when stock is low, force cooperation regardless of raw comparison\n        action = C\n    else if preferDefect:\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C\n```\n\n**Explanation of each clause (no commentary, just rule logic):**\n\n1. **Last round (`t == r\u20111`)** \u2013 audits are impossible, so the higher payoff action `D` strictly dominates `C`.  \n2. **Zero stock (`S == 0`)** \u2013 both actions yield zero consumption; cooperating avoids a fine should an audit occur, so choose `C`.  \n3. **Base threshold (`T`)** \u2013 derived from equating expected payoff of defecting (`S/n - qF`) with cooperating (`S/(2n)`). If current stock exceeds `T`, defecting is profitable in expectation.  \n4. **Opponent\u2011behaviour adjustment** \u2013 multiplies `T` by a factor that grows with the observed proportion of defectors in the previous round (`oppDefRate_t`). More defectors \u2192 higher effective threshold \u2192 more likely to cooperate to preserve stock for future rounds.  \n5. **Low\u2011stock safety (`\u03b2 * capacity`)** \u2013 when the stock falls below 50\u202f% of capacity (adjustable via `\u03b2`), always cooperate to prevent catastrophic depletion that would hurt all future rounds.  \n\n**Edge\u2011case handling:**\n- **Round\u202f0:** `oppDefRate_0 = 0`, so the rule reduces to the raw comparison with threshold `T`.  \n- **Audited round:** the fine is already incorporated in the expected\u2011payoff comparison (`qF`). No extra action is needed because the decision is made before the audit outcome is known.  \n- **Stock hitting capacity:** growth step caps at `capacity`; the same decision rule applies unchanged.  \n\n**Resulting behaviour:**  \n- Defect whenever the stock is sufficiently high and recent opponent defection is low, exploiting the resource for immediate gain.  \n- Cooperate when the stock is low, when many opponents have recently defected, or in the final round according to the dominant payoff.  \n- Never defect when the stock is zero, avoiding unnecessary fines."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_4 = "**Adaptive Expected\u2011Value Threshold (AEVT) Strategy**\n\n**Parameters used each round**\n- `S`\u202f: current stock (beginning of the round)  \n- `t`\u202f: round index (0 \u2026\u202fr\u20111)  \n- `\u03bb = (r\u2011t)/r`\u202f: weight on future payoff (0 in the last round)  \n- `q`\u202f: audit probability (0 in the last round)  \n- `F`\u202f: fine for a detected defection  \n- `cap`\u202f: capacity  \n- `n`\u202f: number of players  \n\n**Internal state**\n- `p\u0302`\u202f: estimated probability that an opponent cooperates (initially\u202f0.5)  \n- `safety = 0.05\u202f\u00d7\u202fcap`\u202f: minimal stock we are willing to let fall below  \n\n**One\u2011round decision procedure**\n\n```\nfunction decide(t, S, observed_coop_cnt):\n    # 1. Update estimate of opponent cooperation\n    if t == 0:\n        p\u0302 = 0.5                     # no history yet\n    else:\n        p\u0302 = observed_coop_cnt / (n\u20111)\n\n    # 2. Immediate expected payoff of each pure action\n    payoff_C = S / (2*n)                         # no fine when cooperating\n    fine = q * F                                 # expected fine (q=0 in last round)\n    payoff_D = S / n - fine\n\n    # 3. Project next\u2011round stock for each action\n    #    Expected opponent consumption:\n    opp_consume = (n\u20111) * (p\u0302 * S/(2*n) + (1\u2011p\u0302) * S/n)\n\n    #    a) If we cooperate:\n    total_consume_C = payoff_C + opp_consume\n    S_rem_C = max(S - total_consume_C, 0)\n    growth_C = 2 * S_rem_C * (1 - S_rem_C / cap)\n    S_next_C = min(S_rem_C + growth_C, cap)\n\n    #    b) If we defect:\n    total_consume_D = payoff_D + opp_consume   # note payoff_D already includes fine subtraction\n    S_rem_D = max(S - total_consume_D, 0)\n    growth_D = 2 * S_rem_D * (1 - S_rem_D / cap)\n    S_next_D = min(S_rem_D + growth_D, cap)\n\n    # 4. Add discounted future value (approximate one\u2011step look\u2011ahead)\n    future_val_C = \u03bb * (S_next_C / (2*n))        # assume we would cooperate next round\n    future_val_D = \u03bb * (S_next_D / (2*n))        # assume we would cooperate next round after defect\n\n    exp_total_C = payoff_C + future_val_C\n    exp_total_D = payoff_D + future_val_D\n\n    # 5. Safety check \u2013 never let stock drop below the safety floor\n    if S_next_C < safety and S_next_D < safety:\n        return C                                 # both actions jeopardise stock \u2192 cooperate\n    if S_next_C < safety:\n        return C\n    if S_next_D < safety:\n        return D\n\n    # 6. Choose the action with higher expected total payoff\n    if exp_total_D > exp_total_C:\n        return D\n    else:\n        return C\n```\n\n**Round\u2011by\u2011round use**\n1. **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0).** `observed_coop_cnt` is undefined; the algorithm uses `p\u0302 = 0.5`. The safety floor is still applied.  \n2. **Intermediate rounds (0\u202f<\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr\u20111).** After each round we receive the number of opponents that cooperated (`observed_coop_cnt`). Feed this into the next call. The audit\u2011adjusted expected fine (`q\u202f\u00d7\u202fF`) is applied to the defect payoff.  \n3. **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111).** Set `q = 0` (no audit) and `\u03bb = 0`. The decision reduces to a pure comparison of immediate payoffs, still respecting the safety floor.  \n\n**Behavioural summary**\n- Cooperate when the immediate gain from defecting does not outweigh the expected fine **and** the projected stock loss (including discounted future payoff) is larger than cooperating.\n- Defect when the expected net gain (immediate payoff minus expected fine) plus the discounted future value of the higher\u2011stock path exceeds that of cooperating.\n- Always cooperate if either action would drive the stock below the safety threshold, thereby protecting long\u2011term returns."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_5 = "**Strategy Name:** Adaptive Individualist (AI)\n\n**Parameters used:**  \n- n, r, capacity, q (audit probability), F (fine) \u2013 read from the game description.  \n- \u03b3\u202f=\u202f0.95 (future\u2011round discount factor, fixed).  \n- S_t\u202f=\u202fstock at the beginning of round\u202ft (observed).  \n- k_t\u202f=\u202fnumber of opponents observed to have cooperated in round\u202ft (0\u202f\u2264\u202fk_t\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111).  \n\n**Internal state:**  \n- `expected_opp_coop` \u2013 exponential moving average of opponents\u2019 cooperation rate, initialized to 0.5.  \n- `safety_stock` \u2013 dynamic lower bound for the stock, set to 0.3\u202f\u00d7\u202fcapacity (adjusted each round by the current `expected_opp_coop`).  \n\n**Decision rule for round t (0\u2011based):**\n\n```\n# 1. Update belief about opponent behaviour\nif t>0:\n    coop_rate = k_{t-1} / (n-1)\n    expected_opp_coop = 0.7*expected_opp_coop + 0.3*coop_rate   # EMA\n\n# 2. Estimate marginal benefit of defecting now\nextra_consumption = S_t / n - S_t / (2*n)          # = S_t/(2n)\nexpected_fine      = q * F\nnet_gain_now       = extra_consumption - expected_fine\n\n# 3. Estimate future stock loss if we defect now\n#   Approximate total consumption this round under our own action:\nif we defect:\n    my_cons = S_t / n\nelse:\n    my_cons = S_t / (2*n)\n\n#   Expected total consumption of opponents:\nopp_cons = expected_opp_coop * (S_t/(2*n)) + (1-expected_opp_coop) * (S_t/n)\ntotal_cons = my_cons + (n-1) * opp_cons\n\nS_after = S_t - total_cons\ngrowth   = 2 * S_after * (1 - S_after / capacity)\nS_next   = min(S_after + growth, capacity)\n\n#   Discounted future payoff loss from lower S_next\nfuture_loss = \u03b3 * ( (capacity - S_next) / (2*n) )   # approximate loss per future round per player\n# (this term is small when S_next\u2248capacity and grows when stock is depleted)\n\n# 4. Decision\nif S_t < safety_stock:\n    # Preserve stock: cooperate regardless of net_gain_now\n    action = C\nelse:\n    if net_gain_now > future_loss:\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n- **Round\u202f0 (first round):** `expected_opp_coop` is the default 0.5, so the estimate of opponent consumption is neutral. The same rule above applies; the safety_stock check uses the static 0.3\u202f\u00d7\u202fcapacity bound.\n- **Round\u202fr\u20111 (last round):** No future rounds mean `future_loss = 0`. The rule reduces to **defect if** `net_gain_now > 0` (i.e., extra consumption exceeds expected fine), otherwise cooperate. The safety_stock check is still applied, but it never forces cooperation when `net_gain_now \u2264 0` because the loss term is zero.\n- **Zero stock (S_t = 0):** Both actions yield zero immediate payoff; the rule sets `action = C` to avoid unnecessary consumption that could never increase payoff.\n- **Audited defect:** Fine is already incorporated in `expected_fine`. No additional reaction is needed; the strategy continues to update `expected_opp_coop` based on observed opponent cooperation only.\n\n**Rationale for individualism:** The player maximizes its own expected cumulative payoff by comparing the **immediate private gain** from defecting (after accounting for the expected fine) with the **discounted expected loss** that a lower stock imposes on its own future earnings. Cooperation is chosen only when the stock is dangerously low or when the future loss outweighs the current private benefit, never out of altruism or group welfare. The strategy updates its belief about opponents autonomously, without any communication or reliance on external coordination."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_6 = "**Strategy \u201cSelf\u2011Preserving Opportunist\u201d**\n\n**Parameters derived each round**  \n- `S` = current stock (observed at start of round).  \n- `q` = audit probability (given).  \n- `F` = fine amount (given).  \n- `n`, `r` = game size and horizon (given).  \n- `t` = current round index (0\u2011based).  \n- `c\u0302` = estimated proportion of opponents that cooperated in the *most recent* round (observed count\u202f\u00f7\u202f`(n\u20111)`).  \n- `c\u0304` = exponential moving average of `c\u0302` (init\u202f=\u202f1). Update: `c\u0304 \u2190 \u03bb\u00b7c\u0302 + (1\u2011\u03bb)\u00b7c\u0304` with `\u03bb = 0.7`.  \n\n**Core utility estimate** (myopic expected net payoff if I choose X \u2208 {C,D})  \n\n```\npay_C   = S / (2n)                                            // no fine\npay_D   = S / n  -  q * F                                      // expected fine\nfuture_stock_if_C   = forecast_stock(S,   n_coop =  (c\u0304*(n\u20111)+1) )\nfuture_stock_if_D   = forecast_stock(S,   n_coop =  (c\u0304*(n\u20111)  ) )\nfuture_gain_C =   future_stock_if_C * (r - t - 1) / (r - t)   // crude linear proxy\nfuture_gain_D =   future_stock_if_D * (r - t - 1) / (r - t)\nU_C = pay_C + \u03b1 * future_gain_C\nU_D = pay_D + \u03b1 * future_gain_D\n```\n\n- `\u03b1` is a weight on future stock (default `\u03b1 = 0.5`).  \n- `forecast_stock(S, n_coop)` simulates one round assuming the *estimated* number of cooperators (`n_coop`) and me playing the candidate action, then applies the growth rule and caps at capacity.  \n- The proxy `future_stock * (remaining rounds / total rounds)` treats remaining stock as linearly convertible into future payoff.\n\n**Decision rule**  \n\n```\nif t == r-1:                 // last round, never audited\n    action = D\nelse if S <= 0:              // stock exhausted, any consumption is zero\n    action = C                // (no penalty, preserves possibility of growth later)\nelse:\n    if U_D > U_C:\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n\n- **First round (t = 0)**: `c\u0304` is initialized to 1, so `forecast_stock` assumes all others cooperate. The rule above still applies; if audit risk `q\u00b7F` is low relative to the extra immediate gain, the algorithm will defect; otherwise it cooperates.  \n- **Zero stock**: choose `C` (consumption = 0, no fine even if audited) to keep the stock\u2011growth equation well\u2011defined.  \n- **Stock > capacity** never occurs because the growth rule caps at `capacity`.  \n- **Audit in final round**: by definition audit probability is 0, thus `pay_D = S/n`. The rule automatically defects in the last round.  \n\n**Adaptivity**  \n\n- The moving average `c\u0304` continuously rewrites the opponent\u2011cooperation estimate; a sudden drop in observed cooperators reduces `future_stock_if_C` and makes `U_D` relatively more attractive, prompting more defections.  \n- Conversely, if opponents appear more cooperative, the forecasted future stock rises, increasing the value of preserving the resource (`U_C`), leading to more cooperation.  \n\n**Individualistic orientation**  \n\nAll calculations maximize my *expected net payoff* (immediate gain minus expected fine plus weighted future benefit). No coordination or punishment schemes are employed; the policy reacts solely to my own payoff prospects and the observed aggregate behavior of others."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_7 = "**Strategy \u201cSelf\u2011Preserving Expected\u2011Benefit\u201d**\n\n**Parameters used each round\u202ft**  \n- `S`\u202f= current stock (observed after growth).  \n- `q`\u202f= audit probability, `F`\u202f= fine.  \n- `n`, `capacity`, `r`\u202f= game constants.  \n- `p\u0302_t`\u202f= estimated probability that a random opponent cooperates, initialized to 0.5 and updated each round from the observed count of cooperators.  \n- `\u03b3`\u202f= discount factor for future rounds, set to ` (r\u2011t\u20111)/(r\u2011t) ` (linearly decreasing weight on remaining horizon).  \n\n**Expected payoffs for this round**  \n\n```\nE_coop = S/(2n)                               # payoff if I play C\nE_def  = S/n \u2013 q\u00b7F                             # payoff if I play D, accounting for expected fine\n\u0394_future = \u03b3\u00b7[ V_future(S \u2013 S/n) \u2013 V_future(S \u2013 S/(2n)) ]\n```\n\n`V_future(S')` is the expected cumulative payoff from round\u202ft+1 onward if the stock after consumption is `S'`. Approximate it by a one\u2011step look\u2011ahead using `p\u0302_t`:\n\n```\nexpected_consumption_if_I_coop = (p\u0302_t\u00b7S/(2n) + (1\u2011p\u0302_t)\u00b7S/n)\u00b7(n\u20111) + S/(2n)\nS'_coop = growth( S \u2013 expected_consumption_if_I_coop )\nV_future(S'_coop) \u2248 \u03b3\u00b7( S'_coop/(2n)\u00b7p\u0302_t + S'_coop/n\u00b7(1\u2011p\u0302_t) )\n```\n\nSimilarly compute `V_future(S'_def)` with my consumption `S/n`.  \n\n**Decision rule (round\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr\u20111)**  \n\n```\nif S == 0:\n    choose C   # avoids fine risk with zero payoff\nelse:\n    net_coop = E_coop + \u0394_future\n    net_def  = E_def  + \u0394_future   # \u0394_future already reflects my different impact on stock\n    if net_def > net_coop:\n        choose D\n    else:\n        choose C\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n\n- **Round\u202f0 (first round)**: `p\u0302_0 = 0.5`. Apply the same rule; the \u0394_future term still reflects the unknown future but is weighted by `\u03b3 = (r\u20111)/r`.  \n- **Last round (t = r\u20111)**: No future stock matters (`\u03b3 = 0`). Choose the action with larger immediate expected payoff:\n  ```\n  if E_def > E_coop: choose D else choose C\n  ```\n  (If `S == 0`, choose C.)  \n- **Audit feedback**: After each round I record whether I was audited and, if so, whether I paid a fine. If I was fined, set `p\u0302_{t+1} = max(0, p\u0302_t \u2013 \u03b4)` with `\u03b4 = 0.1` to become slightly more pessimistic about opponents\u2019 cooperation; if I was not fined while defecting, increase `p\u0302_{t+1}` by `\u03b4` up to 1. This nudges the estimate toward the observed risk environment.  \n- **Observed opponent count**: Let `c_t` be the number of opponents who cooperated in round\u202ft (0\u202f\u2264\u202fc_t\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111). Update `p\u0302_{t+1}` as a simple frequency:\n  ```\n  p\u0302_{t+1} = ( p\u0302_t\u00b7t + c_t/(n\u20111) ) / (t+1)\n  ```\n  (Replace `t` with the number of past observed rounds; for t=0 this reduces to the initialization.)  \n\n**Rationale for individualism**  \nThe rule maximizes my own expected cumulative payoff by explicitly weighing the immediate gain from defecting against the expected loss from a lower future stock, while incorporating the stochastic audit cost. It never requires coordination or signalling; decisions depend solely on my private observations (`S`, audit outcomes, opponent cooperation count) and known game parameters."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_8 = "**Strategy: Adaptive Expected\u2011Return Maximizer (AERM)**  \n\n**Parameters supplied to the agent**  \n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `q` (audit probability), `F` (fine) \u2013 read from the game description.  \n- History `H_i` = list of own past actions, own audit outcomes, and for each past round the announced number of opponent cooperators `c_opponents(t)` (0\u202f\u2264\u202fc_opponents\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111).  \n\n**Core idea**  \nAt every round `t` (0\u2011indexed) the agent computes the *expected total payoff* from cooperating now versus defecting now, assuming that opponents will continue to cooperate with the empirical frequency observed so far. The decision that yields the higher expected sum of *immediate* payoff plus *future* payoff over the remaining rounds is taken. The calculation incorporates the audit\u2011fine expected loss for defecting and the stock\u2011dynamics that affect all later rounds.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Decision rule (per round `t`)\n\n```\nfunction decide(t, stock, H_i):\n    remaining = r - t - 1                # rounds after the current one\n\n    # -------- 1.1 Estimate opponents' cooperation probability --------\n    if t == 0:                            # no observations yet\n        p = 1.0                           # optimistic prior: assume all cooperate\n    else:\n        total_obs   = sum_{k< t} (c_opponents(k) + (n-1 - c_opponents(k)))   # = (t)*(n-1)\n        coop_obs    = sum_{k< t} c_opponents(k)\n        p = coop_obs / total_obs          # empirical cooperation rate of opponents\n\n    # -------- 1.2 Immediate expected payoffs -------------------------\n    payoff_C_now = stock / (2*n)                         # no audit on C\n    payoff_D_now = stock / n - q * F                     # expected fine on D\n\n    # -------- 1.3 Project stock after this round for each action ----\n    stock_if_C = project_stock(stock, p, action='C')\n    stock_if_D = project_stock(stock, p, action='D')\n\n    # -------- 1.4 Estimate future payoff assuming same p -------------\n    future_C = expected_future_payoff(stock_if_C, p, remaining)\n    future_D = expected_future_payoff(stock_if_D, p, remaining)\n\n    total_C = payoff_C_now + future_C\n    total_D = payoff_D_now + future_D\n\n    # -------- 1.5 Choose action --------------------------------------\n    if total_C >= total_D:\n        return 'C'\n    else:\n        return 'D'\n```\n\n**Helper: `project_stock(S, p, action)`**  \n\n```\n# opponent expected consumption per player:\ncons_op = p * (S/(2*n)) + (1-p) * (S/n)\n\nmy_cons =  S/(2*n)  if action=='C' else S/n\n\ntotal_cons = (n-1) * cons_op + my_cons\nS_rem = max(0.0, S - total_cons)\n\ngrowth = 2 * S_rem * (1 - S_rem / capacity)\nnew_stock = min(S_rem + growth, capacity)\n\nreturn new_stock\n```\n\n**Helper: `expected_future_payoff(S_next, p, k)`**  \n\n```\n# Simple forward simulation for the next k rounds,\n# assuming opponents keep the same cooperation probability p\n# and the agent repeats the same decision rule recursively.\npay = 0.0\nS = S_next\nfor step in 1 .. k:\n    # compute expected immediate payoff for both actions as in 1.2,\n    # but without audit loss in the last round (t = r-1 never audited)\n    if step == k:      # this corresponds to the actual last round\n        audit_factor = 0.0\n    else:\n        audit_factor = q\n\n    # immediate expected values\n    val_C = S / (2*n)\n    val_D = S / n - audit_factor * F\n\n    # choose action that maximizes val + continuation (myopic look\u2011ahead)\n    # because we are simulating forward, we can reuse the same logic:\n    # compute projected stocks for both actions\n    S_C = project_stock(S, p, 'C')\n    S_D = project_stock(S, p, 'D')\n\n    # estimate continuation value as simple average of the two projected\n    # stocks' future payoff (since we do not know which we will pick)\n    # Here we take the higher of the two, mirroring the actual decision rule.\n    future_C = 0.0   # will be added in later iterations\n    future_D = 0.0\n\n    # Choose the better action for this simulated step\n    if (val_C >= val_D):\n        pay += val_C\n        S = S_C\n    else:\n        pay += val_D\n        S = S_D\nreturn pay\n```\n\nThe forward simulation is shallow (depth \u2264\u202f`remaining`) and deterministic, so computation is trivial for the typical size of `r` (\u2264\u202f50).\n\n---\n\n### 2. Edge\u2011case handling  \n\n| Situation                               | Action taken                                                                                                   |\n|----------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **First round (`t = 0`)**              | Use the optimistic prior `p = 1.0`. Compute as above; if `stock = 0`, cooperate (payoff\u202f=\u202f0, avoids fine).      |\n| **Last round (`t = r\u20111`)**             | No audit occurs. Compare only the pure immediate payoffs: `stock/(2n)` vs `stock/n`. Choose the larger.       |\n| **Stock depleted (`stock = 0`)**       | Cooperate (payoff\u202f=\u202f0, no expected fine). Defect would give `\u2011q\u00b7F` in expectation, which is strictly worse.   |\n| **Audit probability `q = 0`**          | The fine term drops out; the rule reduces to a pure stock\u2011maximising comparison (still uses future payoff). |\n| **Fine `F = 0`**                       | Same as above, but defect is never penalised; the algorithm may still cooperate to preserve future stock. |\n| **Observed opponent cooperation `p = 0`** | The projection uses only opponent defection consumption; the agent will often cooperate only if stock is very low, because defect would collapse the pool. |\n| **Future\u2011payoff estimate yields a tie**| Break ties in favour of cooperation (more sustainable, never worse given tie).                                   |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Individualistic stance  \n\n- The agent never conditions its action on any notion of fairness or retaliation; it solely maximises its *expected cumulative monetary payoff*.  \n- Audits and fines are treated as stochastic costs that reduce the private payoff of defecting; the agent accounts for them exactly as they affect its own earnings.  \n- The strategy does **not** attempt to punish opponents or enforce collective sustainability beyond what is optimal for the agent\u2019s own return. It only preserves stock when doing so raises the agent\u2019s own expected future earnings.  \n\nBy repeatedly re\u2011evaluating the expected total return with the latest observation of opponent behaviour, AERM adapts to any mixture of cooperative and selfish opponents while remaining focused on maximizing the individual\u2019s own payoff over the whole horizon."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_9 = "**Strategy Overview**  \nThe agent treats each round as a decision problem that balances the immediate gain from defecting against two costs: (1) the expected audit fine and (2) the future loss of stock caused by over\u2011consumption. The decision rule is a deterministic function of (i) the current stock\u202fS, (ii) the round index\u202ft, (iii) the audit parameters (q,\u202fF), (iv) an estimate\u202fp\u0302\u209c of the probability that any given opponent will cooperate, and (v) the number of rounds remaining\u202fR = r\u202f\u2212\u202ft\u202f\u2212\u202f1.\n\n---\n\n### 1. State variables maintained by the agent\n| Symbol | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `S`    | Current stock before consumption (float) |\n| `t`    | Current round index (0\u2011based) |\n| `R`    | Remaining rounds after the current one (`r\u2011t\u20111`) |\n| `q`    | Audit probability (float) |\n| `F`    | Fine per audited defection (float) |\n| `n`    | Number of players (integer) |\n| `p\u0302\u209c`  | Estimated probability that a random opponent cooperates in round\u202ft |\n| `hist` | List of observed opponent\u2011cooperation counts for previous rounds |\n\n`p\u0302\u209c` is updated after each round using a simple Bayesian\u2010type estimator:\n\n```\nif t == 0:\n    p\u0302\u2080 = 0.5                     # uninformed prior\nelse:\n    total_obs = sum(hist)        # total cooperating opponents observed so far\n    total_turns = len(hist) * (n-1)\n    p\u0302\u209c = total_obs / total_turns\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Decision rule per round\n\n#### 2.1. Immediate\u2011payoff comparison (baseline)\n\nDefine the *expected net gain* of defecting versus cooperating **ignoring future stock effects**:\n\n```\n\u0394\u2080(S) = (S / n) - q*F  -  (S / (2*n))\n      = S/(2*n) - q*F\n```\n\nDefect if `\u0394\u2080(S) > 0`, i.e. if `S > 2*n*q*F`.  \nCooperate otherwise.\n\n#### 2.2. Future\u2011stock adjustment\n\nOver\u2011consumption reduces next\u2011round stock, which reduces all future payoffs. Approximate the marginal loss of one extra unit of consumption on the discounted sum of future payoffs:\n\n```\nm = 1/(n) - 1/(2*n) = 1/(2*n)          # extra consumption when defecting vs cooperating\n\u0394_stock = m * S                         # extra stock removed this round\n\n# Stock dynamics linearised around current S:\n#   S' = S - total_consumption + growth\n#   growth \u2248 2 * (S - total_consumption) * (1 - (S - total_consumption)/capacity)\n# Approximate marginal change in next\u2011round stock from \u0394_stock as:\n\u0394S_next \u2248 -\u0394_stock * (1 + 2*(1 - 2*S/capacity))\n\n# Discounted future loss (geometric discount \u03b3 = 1 because rounds are finite and equally weighted)\nfuture_loss = \u0394S_next * (R+1) * (S/(2*n)) / capacity   # rough bound: each unit of stock yields \u2248 S/(2n) per player per round, scaled by remaining rounds\n```\n\nIf `future_loss > \u0394\u2080(S)`, the agent **cooperates** despite the immediate advantage of defecting; otherwise it **defects**.\n\n#### 2.3. Full rule (pseudocode)\n\n```\nfunction decide(S, t, R, q, F, n, capacity, p\u0302):\n    # 1. Immediate advantage threshold\n    thresh_immediate = 2 * n * q * F\n\n    # 2. Compute marginal future loss\n    extra_consume = S/(2*n)                     # extra amount taken when defecting\n    \u0394_stock = extra_consume                      # stock loss this round\n    growth_factor = 1 + 2*(1 - 2*S/capacity)    # derivative of growth term w.r.t. stock\n    \u0394S_next = -\u0394_stock * growth_factor\n    future_loss = -\u0394S_next * (R+1) * (S/(2*n)) / capacity   # positive value = loss\n\n    # 3. Decision\n    if S > thresh_immediate and future_loss <= (S/(2*n) - q*F):\n        return D\n    else:\n        return C\n```\n\nAll comparisons are strict; ties are broken in favor of **cooperation** to preserve stock.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Edge\u2011case handling\n\n| Situation | Action |\n|-----------|--------|\n| **Round\u202f0 (first round)** | Use the rule above with `p\u0302\u2080 = 0.5`. No history needed. |\n| **Round\u202fr\u20111 (last round)** | No audits occur (`q = 0` for this round). The future\u2011loss term is zero (`R = 0`). Decision reduces to `defect if S > 0` (since `\u0394\u2080 = S/(2n) > 0`). Therefore always **defect** in the final round unless `S = 0`. |\n| **Stock\u202fS = 0** | Both actions yield zero immediate payoff; cooperating avoids the (zero\u2011probability) fine. Choose **cooperate**. |\n| **Audit probability q = 0** | The immediate\u2011advantage threshold collapses to zero; decision governed solely by future\u2011stock loss. The rule will cooperate unless `future_loss` is negative (i.e., defecting improves stock, which never occurs). Hence **cooperate** in all non\u2011final rounds. |\n| **Fine F = 0** | Same as `q = 0`. Agent always cooperates until the last round. |\n| **Observed opponent cooperation count = n\u20111** (all opponents cooperated) | The estimate `p\u0302` rises, but the rule already accounts for the impact via `future_loss`. No extra adjustment needed. |\n| **Observed opponent cooperation count = 0** (all opponents defected) | `p\u0302` falls, increasing `future_loss` (because stock will erode quickly). The rule will more likely **cooperate** to slow depletion, even though opponents defect. |\n\n---\n\n### 4. Individualistic rationale (encoded in the rule)\n\n- The agent **maximizes its own expected payoff** by explicitly weighing the extra immediate consumption against the expected fine and the discounted loss of future consumption opportunities caused by stock depletion.\n- No coordination, reputation, or punishment mechanisms are used; the only information exploited is the aggregated count of opponent cooperations and the publicly observable stock.\n- The rule is **myopic\u2011safe** in the final round (defect for all remaining payoff) and **forward\u2011looking** in earlier rounds (preserves the resource when the projected future loss outweighs the current gain)."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_10 = "**Parameters used internally**  \n-\u202fn, r, capacity, q, F are given.  \n-\u202f\u03bb \u2208 (0,1) \u2013 safety\u2011stock factor (default 0.4).  \n-\u202f\u03b5 > 0 \u2013 minimal gain margin (default 0.01).  \n-\u202fm \u2013 memory length for opponent cooperation estimate (default 5).  \n\n**State variables (maintained each round t)**  \n-\u202fS_t \u2013 current stock (observed).  \n-\u202fk_t \u2013 number of opponents who cooperated in round t (observed).  \n-\u202fp\u0302_t\u202f=\u202f(\u2211_{\u03c4=max(0,t\u2011m)}^{t\u20111} k_\u03c4) / ( (n\u20111)\u00b7min(m,t) ) \u2013 rolling estimate of opponent cooperation probability.  \n\n**Decision rule**  \n\n```\nfunction choose_action(t, S_t, p\u0302_t):\n    # 1. Expected immediate payoff difference\n    coop_pay   = S_t / (2*n)\n    defect_pay = S_t / n - q*F                # expected fine applied (last round q=0)\n    \u0394_immediate = defect_pay - coop_pay       # >0 favors defect\n\n    # 2. Projected stock after this round under each own action\n    #    assume opponents play C with probability p\u0302_t, D otherwise.\n    exp_opp_cons = (p\u0302_t)*(S_t/(2*n)) + (1-p\u0302_t)*(S_t/n)   # per opponent expected consumption\n    total_opp_cons = (n-1) * exp_opp_cons\n\n    #    own consumption\n    cons_coop   = S_t/(2*n)\n    cons_defect = S_t/n\n\n    #    stock after consumption (capped at 0)\n    S_after_coop   = max(0, S_t - (total_opp_cons + cons_coop))\n    S_after_defect = max(0, S_t - (total_opp_cons + cons_defect))\n\n    #    growth function\n    grow(x) = 2*x*(1 - x/capacity)\n\n    #    next\u2011round stock (capped at capacity)\n    S_next_coop   = min(S_after_coop   + grow(S_after_coop),   capacity)\n    S_next_defect = min(S_after_defect + grow(S_after_defect), capacity)\n\n    # 3. Approximate future value over remaining rounds (t+1 \u2026 r\u20111)\n    #    assume you will cooperate from then on (conservative estimate)\n    future_value(stock) = 0\n    cur = stock\n    for \u03c4 in range(t+1, r):\n        # opponents keep using p\u0302_t each future round\n        exp_opp_cons = (p\u0302_t)*(cur/(2*n)) + (1-p\u0302_t)*(cur/n)\n        cur = cur - ( (n-1)*exp_opp_cons + cur/(2*n) )          # you cooperate future\n        cur = max(0, cur)\n        cur = min(cur + grow(cur), capacity)\n        future_value += cur/(2*n)                               # your coop payoff each future round\n    FV_coop   = future_value(S_next_coop)\n\n    #    same future value assuming you continue to defect each remaining round\n    future_value = 0\n    cur = S_next_defect\n    for \u03c4 in range(t+1, r):\n        exp_opp_cons = (p\u0302_t)*(cur/(2*n)) + (1-p\u0302_t)*(cur/n)\n        cur = cur - ( (n-1)*exp_opp_cons + cur/n )              # you defect future\n        cur = max(0, cur)\n        cur = min(cur + grow(cur), capacity)\n        future_value += cur/n - q*F                               # expected defect payoff each future round\n    FV_defect = future_value\n\n    # 4. Total expected utility of each current action\n    U_coop   = coop_pay   + FV_coop\n    U_defect = defect_pay + FV_defect\n\n    # 5. Safety check: avoid pushing stock below safety level\n    safety = \u03bb * capacity\n    if (S_next_defect < safety) and (U_coop + \u03b5 > U_defect):\n        return C\n    # 6. Choose action with higher total utility, break ties toward cooperation\n    if U_defect > U_coop + \u03b5:\n        return D\n    else:\n        return C\n```\n\n**Special\u2011case handling**  \n-\u202fRound\u202f0: execute `choose_action(0, S_0, 0)` (p\u0302_0\u202f=\u202f0, i.e., assume opponents cooperate).  \n-\u202fRounds\u202ft\u202f<\u202fm: p\u0302_t computed over the\u202ft\u202favailable past observations.  \n-\u202fLast round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111): set q\u202f=\u202f0 in the payoff calculation, then `choose_action` will always select D because the future\u2011value terms vanish and defect payoff strictly exceeds cooperate payoff.  \n\n**Output**  \nReturn `C` (cooperate) or `D` (defect) each round according to the rule above."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_11 = "**Strategy\u202f\u201cSelf\u2011Preserving Greedy\u201d**\n\n**Parameters used each round**  \n- `S`\u202f= current stock (float)  \n- `t`\u202f= round index (0 \u2026\u202fr\u20111)  \n- `q`\u202f= audit probability (game_description.audit_prob)  \n- `F`\u202f= fine per audited defection (game_description.fine)  \n- `n`\u202f= number of players (game_description.n)  \n- `r`\u202f= total rounds (game_description.r)\n\n**Derived quantities**  \n\n```\n\u0394pay = S/(2*n)                     # extra immediate payoff from defecting (vs cooperating)\n\u0394stock = S/(2*n)                   # extra stock consumed when defecting\nVunit = (r - t - 1) * (1/(2*n))    # estimated future value of one unit of stock,\n                                   # assuming the rest of the game the pool is kept\n                                   # at the cooperative consumption level\nFutureLoss = Vunit * \u0394stock        # expected loss of future payoffs caused by the extra stock use\nExpectedFine = q * F               # expected fine when defecting\nNetGain = \u0394pay - ExpectedFine - FutureLoss\n```\n\n**Decision rule**  \n\n```\nif t == r-1:                       # last round \u2013 never audited, only immediate payoff matters\n    action = D if S > 0 else C    # defect if any stock remains, otherwise cooperate (zero payoff either way)\nelif S <= 0:\n    action = C                      # no stock left, both actions give 0; choose C for consistency\nelse:\n    if NetGain > 0:\n        action = D                  # defect because extra gain outweighs expected fine and future loss\n    else:\n        action = C                  # cooperate to preserve stock for future rounds\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n\n1. **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0)** \u2013 the same rule applies; `FutureLoss` is maximal because many rounds remain, so the strategy cooperates unless the stock is so high that `NetGain` stays positive.  \n2. **Zero audit probability (`q\u202f=\u202f0`)** \u2013 `ExpectedFine` =\u202f0, so the rule reduces to defect when the extra immediate payoff exceeds the estimated future loss.  \n3. **Very high fine (`q*F` large)** \u2013 `ExpectedFine` dominates, forcing cooperation even when stock is abundant.  \n4. **Stock at or below machine epsilon** \u2013 treat as zero; always cooperate (payoff zero either way).  \n5. **Last round** \u2013 audits are disabled by the game rules; the rule automatically defects whenever stock >\u202f0 because the future loss term is zero.\n\n**Rationale (implicit in the rule)**  \n\n- The strategy compares **three components** of the marginal decision to defect:\n  1. Immediate extra payoff (`\u0394pay`);\n  2. Expected monetary penalty (`ExpectedFine`);\n  3. Expected discounted loss of future earnings caused by the extra stock consumption (`FutureLoss`).\n\n- It **maximizes expected individual cumulative payoff** without coordinating with others; actions depend only on publicly observable state (`S`) and private parameters (`q`, `F`, `n`, `r`, `t`).  \n- It is **adaptive**: as the stock declines or the horizon shortens, `FutureLoss` shrinks, making defection more attractive; conversely, early in the game with abundant stock, cooperation is favored unless fines are negligible.  \n\n**Implementation sketch (pseudocode)**  \n\n```python\ndef decide_action(history, stock, round_idx, params):\n    n, r = params.n, params.r\n    q, F = params.audit_prob, params.fine\n\n    if round_idx == r-1:                     # final round\n        return 'D' if stock > 0 else 'C'\n\n    if stock <= 0:\n        return 'C'\n\n    delta_pay   = stock / (2.0 * n)           # extra payoff from defect\n    delta_stock = stock / (2.0 * n)           # extra stock consumed\n    v_unit      = (r - round_idx - 1) / (2.0 * n)   # future value per stock unit\n    future_loss = v_unit * delta_stock\n    expected_fine = q * F\n\n    net_gain = delta_pay - expected_fine - future_loss\n\n    return 'D' if net_gain > 0 else 'C'\n```\n\nThe strategy requires only the current stock, round number, and the known game parameters; it does **not** rely on opponents\u2019 identities or past actions beyond the aggregated stock trajectory, satisfying the individualistic constraint."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_12 = "**Strategy: Adaptive Individualist (AI\u2011CPC)**  \n\n**Parameters known to the agent**  \n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `q` (audit probability), `F` (fine)  \n- Current round `t` (0\u2011based) and current stock `S` (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity)  \n- History `H` = list of past observations `[(t, my_action, audited?, fine_paid, opp_coop_count)]`  \n\n**Internal state**  \n- `p\u0302` \u2013 estimated probability that a given opponent cooperates in the next round (initial 0.5).  \n- `V` \u2013 estimated marginal value of one unit of stock for future rounds (updated each round).  \n\n**Update rules (after each round except the last)**  \n\n```\n# opp_coop_count = number of opponents that chose C this round (observed)\nopp_n = n\u20111\np\u0302 \u2190 (p\u0302 * (t) + opp_coop_count / opp_n) / (t+1)      # running average\n\n# Estimate value per unit of stock left for the remaining rounds\n# Assume future opponents will follow the current p\u0302 mix.\nfuture_rounds \u2190 r\u2011t\u20111\nexpected_per_capita_share \u2190 p\u0302 * (S/(2n)) + (1\u2011p\u0302) * (S/n \u2013 q*F)\n# Each unit of stock contributes proportionally to the per\u2011capita share.\nV \u2190 future_rounds * expected_per_capita_share / S   # marginal value per stock unit\n```\n\n**Decision rule (for round `t < r\u20111`)**\n\n```\n# Immediate expected payoff if I cooperate\n\u03c0C  \u2190 S / (2n)\n\n# Immediate expected payoff if I defect (expected fine)\n\u03c0D  \u2190 S / n \u2013 q * F\n\n# Immediate gain from defecting\n\u0394inst \u2190 \u03c0D \u2013 \u03c0C                     # = S/(2n) \u2013 q*F\n\n# Extra consumption caused by defecting (relative to cooperating)\n\u0394cons \u2190 S / (2n)                     # the amount of stock I would have spared by cooperating\n\n# Expected future loss due to extra consumption\n\u0394future \u2190 \u0394cons * V                  # V is the marginal future value per stock unit\n\n# Net benefit of defecting now\n\u0394net \u2190 \u0394inst \u2013 \u0394future\n```\n\n- **If `\u0394net > 0`** \u2192 **Defect** (`D`).  \n- **Else** \u2192 **Cooperate** (`C`).  \n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n- **Round\u202f0**: `p\u0302` is the prior 0.5, `V` is computed with the same formula (future_rounds\u202f=\u202fr\u20111).  \n- **Last round (`t = r\u20111`)**: No audit, no future rounds. Defect always (`D`), because `\u03c0D = S/n > \u03c0C = S/(2n)`.  \n- **Stock depleted (`S = 0`)**: Both actions yield 0 payoff; cooperate by default to avoid unnecessary consumption.  \n\n**Tie\u2011breaking**  \nIf `\u0394net == 0` choose `C` (preserves stock for possible future gains).  \n\n**Summary of algorithm per round `t`**\n\n```\nif t == r\u20111:\n    action \u2190 D\nelse:\n    compute \u03c0C, \u03c0D, \u0394inst, \u0394cons\n    estimate p\u0302 from history\n    compute V from p\u0302 and remaining rounds\n    \u0394future \u2190 \u0394cons * V\n    \u0394net \u2190 \u0394inst \u2013 \u0394future\n    action \u2190 D if \u0394net > 0 else C\nexecute action\nrecord (t, action, audited?, fine_paid, opp_coop_count) in H\n```\n\nThe strategy continuously revises its belief about opponent cooperation (`p\u0302`) and the marginal worth of preserving stock (`V`). It defects only when the immediate expected gain (including audit risk) exceeds the expected discounted loss from reduced future stock, thereby maximizing individual cumulative payoff while remaining responsive to opponent behaviour."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_13 = "**Strategy \u2013 Conditional\u2011Threshold Adaptive Play (CTAP)**  \n\n**Parameters (known to the agent)**  \n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `q` (audit probability), `F` (fine)  \n- `stock_t` \u2013 common\u2011pool level at the start of round *t* (observed)  \n- `obsCoop_{t-1}` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (observed)  \n- `audit_t` \u2013 whether the agent was audited in round *t\u20111* (known only to the agent)  \n\n**Derived constants**  \n- `C_share(stock) = stock / (2\u202fn)`\u2003\u2003// payoff if Cooperate  \n- `D_share(stock) = stock / n`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// payoff if Defect (before fine)  \n- `expectedFine = q\u202f\u00b7\u202fF`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003// expected penalty per defect  \n\n**Threshold functions**  \n1. **Stock safety threshold**  \n   `S_safe = capacity * 0.6`\u2003\u2003// above this the pool can sustain occasional over\u2011extraction.  \n\n2. **Cooperation incentive threshold**  \n   `\u0394 = D_share(stock_t) - C_share(stock_t) - expectedFine`\u2003// net gain from defecting now, ignoring future stock effects.  \n\n3. **Opponent\u2011cooperation weight**  \n   `w_t = (obsCoop_{t-1} / (n\u20111))`\u2003\u2003// proportion of opponents that cooperated last round (0\u202f\u2264\u202fw\u202f\u2264\u202f1).  \n\n**Decision rule (for round *t*, 0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr)**  \n\n```\nif t == r\u20111:                     # last round \u2013 never risk fine\n    action = D\nelif t == 0:                     # first round \u2013 seed cooperation\n    if stock_t >= S_safe:\n        action = C\n    else:\n        action = D\nelse:\n    # compute expected immediate gain from defecting\n    if \u0394 <= 0:\n        # defect not profitable even before considering future stock\n        action = C\n    else:\n        # adjust \u0394 by opponent behaviour and audit outcome\n        adj = \u0394 * (1 - w_t)               # lower gain if many cooperated last round\n        if audit_{t\u20111} == 1:              # was fined previously\n            adj += expectedFine * 0.5    # become more cautious after a fine\n        # estimate future stock impact (simple heuristic)\n        if stock_t < S_safe:\n            adj += (stock_t / capacity) * 0.2   # penalize defect when stock low\n        # final choice\n        if adj > 0:\n            action = D\n        else:\n            action = C\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n\n- **Round\u202f0**: cooperate only if the initial stock exceeds `S_safe`; otherwise defect to avoid immediate depletion.  \n- **Round\u202fr\u20111** (final): always defect because no future rounds exist and the audit risk is absent, maximizing the one\u2011shot payoff.  \n- **Audit feedback**: after any round where `audit_t == 1` (the agent was fined), increase the weight of caution by adding half the expected fine to the adjusted gain (`adj`). This makes the agent temporarily less likely to defect, ensuring it does not repeatedly incur fines.  \n- **Zero stock**: if `stock_t == 0`, both actions yield zero payoff; default to `C` (no cost, preserves the \u201ccooperate\u201d label for future rounds).  \n\n**Summary of behavior**  \n\n- Cooperate when the pool is healthy (`stock \u2265 S_safe`) **and** the immediate net gain from defecting (`\u0394`) is non\u2011positive, or when recent opponent cooperation is high and the agent has recently been fined.  \n- Defect when the pool is abundant enough to absorb extra extraction **and** the adjusted net gain (`adj`) remains positive, i.e., when defecting yields a higher expected payoff after accounting for audit risk, recent opponent defection, and stock pressure.  \n\nThis rule uses only publicly observable information (`stock_t`, `obsCoop_{t\u20111}`) and private audit history, adapts each round to the evolving state, and remains fully individualistic\u2014maximizing the agent\u2019s cumulative payoff while protecting against excessive fines and stock collapse."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_14 = "**Strategy: Adaptive Individual\u2011Benefit Forecast (AIBF)**  \n\n**Parameters used each round\u202ft (0 \u2264 t < r):**  \n- `S` \u2013 current stock level (observed at start of round).  \n- `capacity` \u2013 maximal stock (given).  \n- `n` \u2013 number of players (given).  \n- `q` \u2013 audit probability (given).  \n- `F` \u2013 fine for a defect that is audited (given).  \n- `c_prev` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in round\u202ft\u20111 (observed; undefined for t\u202f=\u202f0).  \n\n**Derived quantities:**  \n- `p = c_prev / (n\u20111)` if t\u202f>\u202f0, otherwise `p = 0.5` (average\u2011opponent\u2011cooperation estimate).  \n- `future_rounds = r\u2011t\u20111`.  \n\n**Step\u202f1: Compute estimated outcome for each possible action**  \n\n```\nfor action in {C , D}:\n    if action == C:\n        self_consume = S / (2*n)\n        audit_cost   = 0                       # no fine when cooperating\n    else:   # D\n        self_consume = S / n\n        audit_cost   = q * F                    # expected fine (last round has q=0)\n\n    # Expected opponent consumption (using the estimate p)\n    opp_consume = p * (S / (2*n)) + (1-p) * (S / n)\n\n    total_consume = self_consume + (n-1) * opp_consume\n    S_remain      = max(S - total_consume, 0)\n\n    growth        = 2 * S_remain * (1 - S_remain / capacity)\n    S_next        = min(S_remain + growth, capacity)\n\n    immediate_payoff = self_consume - audit_cost\n\n    # Forecast future payoff assuming *all* players cooperate from next round onward\n    # (cooperation maximises the stock, which is best for any individual in the long run)\n    future_payoff = future_rounds * (S_next / (2*n))\n\n    total_estimated_value[action] = immediate_payoff + future_payoff\n```\n\n**Step\u202f2: Choose action**  \n\n- If `total_estimated_value[D] > total_estimated_value[C]` \u2192 **Defect**.  \n- Otherwise \u2192 **Cooperate**.  \n- Ties are broken in favor of **Cooperate** (reduces risk of audit fine).\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n| Situation | Decision rule |\n|-----------|----------------|\n| **First round (t = 0)** | Use `p = 0.5` as above; apply the full forecast calculation. |\n| **Last round (t = r\u20111)** | `future_rounds = 0`. No audit (`q = 0`). Immediate comparison reduces to: defect if `S/(2n) > 0` (i.e., always defect unless stock is exactly\u202f0). |\n| **Stock S = 0** | Both actions yield zero immediate consumption; cooperating avoids any audit fine risk. Choose **Cooperate**. |\n| **Audit probability q = 0** | `audit_cost = 0`; the algorithm automatically favours defect when the extra immediate consumption outweighs any future stock loss. |\n| **Fine F = 0** | Same as above; defect whenever the forecast predicts higher total value. |\n\n**Rationale (embedded in the rule set, not stated explicitly)**  \n\n- The algorithm evaluates *my* immediate gain from defecting against the *expected* fine and the *future* loss caused by a lower stock level.  \n- It adapts each round to the observed cooperation level of opponents (`p`).  \n- It remains strictly individualistic: the forecast assumes other players keep their observed behaviour; no coordination or enforcement is attempted.  \n\n**Implementation sketch (pseudocode)**\n\n```python\ndef decide_action(t, S, history, params):\n    n, capacity, q, F = params.n, params.capacity, params.audit_prob, params.fine\n    # estimate opponent cooperation probability\n    if t == 0:\n        p = 0.5\n    else:\n        c_prev = history[t-1].opponents_coop   # count of opponents who cooperated\n        p = c_prev / (n - 1)\n\n    future_rounds = params.r - t - 1\n    best_action = 'C'\n    best_value  = -float('inf')\n\n    for action in ('C', 'D'):\n        if action == 'C':\n            self_consume = S / (2 * n)\n            audit_cost   = 0.0\n        else:  # D\n            self_consume = S / n\n            audit_cost   = (0.0 if t == params.r-1 else q * F)\n\n        opp_consume = p * (S / (2 * n)) + (1 - p) * (S / n)\n        total_consume = self_consume + (n - 1) * opp_consume\n        S_remain = max(S - total_consume, 0.0)\n\n        growth = 2 * S_remain * (1 - S_remain / capacity)\n        S_next = min(S_remain + growth, capacity)\n\n        immediate = self_consume - audit_cost\n        future    = future_rounds * (S_next / (2 * n))\n        total     = immediate + future\n\n        if total > best_value + 1e-9:   # strict superiority\n            best_value = total\n            best_action = action\n        elif abs(total - best_value) <= 1e-9:\n            # tie\u2011breaker: cooperate\n            best_action = 'C'\n\n    return best_action\n```\n\nThe strategy updates `p` each round from observed opponent cooperation, forecasts the stock trajectory under each possible personal action, incorporates the expected audit cost, and selects the action that maximizes the individual's estimated cumulative payoff."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_15 = "**Strategy \u201cSelf\u2011Preserving Expected\u2011Value\u201d**\n\n**Parameters known to the agent**  \n- n, r, capacity, q, F (from the game description)  \n- discount weight \u03bb\u209c = (r\u202f\u2212\u202ft\u202f\u2212\u202f1)\u202f\u00b7\u202f(1\u202f/\u202f(2n)) for round *t* (0\u2011indexed)  \n\n**State variables**  \n- S\u209c : current stock before actions in round *t*  \n- k\u209c : number of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (observable after round *t\u20111*)  \n\n**Baseline belief about opponents**  \nAssume each opponent will cooperate with probability  \np\u209c = 0.5\u202f+\u202f0.5\u00b7(k\u209c\u202f/\u202f(n\u20111))\u2003(if *t*\u202f>\u202f0, otherwise p\u2080\u202f=\u202f0.5).  \n\n**Outcome projections for the current round**  \n\n1. **Immediate expected payoff**  \n   - Cooperate (C):\u2003E_C\u209c = S\u209c\u202f/\u202f(2n)  \n   - Defect (D):\u2003\u2003E_D\u209c = S\u209c\u202f/\u202fn\u202f\u2212\u202fq\u00b7F  \n\n2. **Projected stock after the round**  \n\n   Expected total consumption when you play *a*\u2208{C,D}:  \n\n   ```\n   cons_self(a) = (S\u209c / (2n))   if a == C\n                = (S\u209c / n)    if a == D\n   cons_opp = (n\u20111) * [ p\u209c * (S\u209c / (2n)) + (1\u2011p\u209c) * (S\u209c / n) ]\n   total_cons(a) = cons_self(a) + cons_opp\n   S_rem(a) = max(0, S\u209c \u2013 total_cons(a))\n   growth(a) = 2 * S_rem(a) * (1 \u2013 S_rem(a)/capacity)\n   S_next(a) = min(S_rem(a) + growth(a), capacity)\n   ```\n\n3. **Future\u2011value estimate** (using the same baseline belief for all remaining rounds)  \n\n   ```\n   future_val(a) = \u03bb\u209c * S_next(a)\n   ```\n\n4. **Total expected utility**  \n\n   ```\n   U_C = E_C\u209c + future_val(C)\n   U_D = E_D\u209c + future_val(D)\n   ```\n\n**Decision rule for round *t***  \n\n- If *t*\u202f=\u202fr\u202f\u2212\u202f1 (last round, no audits): choose C if S\u209c\u202f/\u202f(2n)\u202f\u2265\u202fS\u209c\u202f/\u202fn, otherwise choose D.  \n- Else (any earlier round):  \n\n  ```\n  if U_C \u2265 U_D:\n      play C\n  else:\n      play D\n  ```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n\n- **Zero stock** (S\u209c\u202f=\u202f0): both actions yield zero payoff and leave stock unchanged; play C.  \n- **Full capacity** with *t*\u202f=\u202f0: use the rule above with p\u2080\u202f=\u202f0.5.  \n- **Audit probability q\u202f=\u202f0** or fine F\u202f=\u202f0: the fine term drops out automatically; the rule reduces to a pure stock\u2011value comparison.  \n- **Negative projected stock** (S_rem\u202f<\u202f0) is clipped to 0 before growth computation, ensuring feasible dynamics.\n\n**Summary of algorithm per round**  \n\n```\ninput: t, S_t, k_{t-1} (if t>0)\nif t == r-1:\n    if S_t/(2n) >= S_t/n:\n        action = C\n    else:\n        action = D\nelse:\n    if t == 0: p = 0.5\n    else:      p = 0.5 + 0.5 * (k_{t-1} / (n-1))\n\n    compute cons_self(C), cons_self(D)\n    compute cons_opp = (n-1)*(p*S_t/(2n) + (1-p)*S_t/n)\n    for a in {C,D}:\n        total = cons_self(a) + cons_opp\n        S_rem = max(0, S_t - total)\n        growth = 2 * S_rem * (1 - S_rem/capacity)\n        S_next = min(S_rem + growth, capacity)\n        E_a = (S_t/(2n)) if a==C else (S_t/n - q*F)\n        future = ((r - t - 1) / (2n)) * S_next\n        U_a = E_a + future\n    action = C if U_C >= U_D else D\noutput: action\n```\n\nThe agent follows this rule each round, updating *k\u209c* from the observed count of cooperating opponents after every round, thereby adapting to the apparent cooperativeness of the environment while always maximizing its own expected cumulative payoff."

description_INDIVIDUALISTIC_16 = "**Strategy Name:** Adaptive Expected\u2011Return Tracker (AERT)\n\n**Core variables (maintained each round\u202ft)**  \n- `S` \u2013 current stock (observed at start of round).  \n- `p\u0302` \u2013 estimated probability that a random opponent will cooperate.  \n  - Initialise `p\u0302\u2080 = 0.5`.  \n  - After each round update with exponential smoothing:  \n    `p\u0302 \u2190 \u03bb\u00b7p\u0302 + (1\u2011\u03bb)\u00b7(C_obs / (n\u20111))`, where `C_obs` is the number of opponents you observed cooperating and `\u03bb \u2208 [0,1]` (e.g. `\u03bb = 0.8`).  \n- `\u03c4` \u2013 look\u2011ahead weight for future stock value (fixed, e.g. `\u03c4 = 0.6`).  \n\n**Immediate expected payoffs** (given current `S`):  \n- Cooperate: `U_C = S / (2n)`  \n- Defect (subject to audit): `U_D = S / n \u2013 q\u00b7F`  \n\n**Estimated next\u2011round stock under each action** (using `p\u0302`):  \n\n1. Expected total consumption if you **cooperate**:  \n   `C_total = (p\u0302\u00b7(n\u20111)\u00b7S/(2n) + (1\u2011p\u0302)\u00b7(n\u20111)\u00b7S/n) + S/(2n)`  \n\n2. Expected total consumption if you **defect**:  \n   `D_total = (p\u0302\u00b7(n\u20111)\u00b7S/(2n) + (1\u2011p\u0302)\u00b7(n\u20111)\u00b7S/n) + S/n`  \n\nFor each case compute the expected remaining stock after growth:  \n\n```\nS_rem = S \u2013 total_consumption\ngrowth = 2 * S_rem * (1 \u2013 S_rem / capacity)\nS_next = min(S_rem + growth, capacity)\n```\n\n**Continuation value approximation** (value of future rounds if the game were to continue with the same stock level):  \n`V(S_next) = \u03c4 * (r \u2013 t \u2013 1) * (S_next / capacity) * (capacity / n)`  \n(The term `(capacity / n)` is the maximal per\u2011round payoff a single player could obtain if the whole stock were available; scaling by `S_next/capacity` adjusts for current stock, and by `(r\u2011t\u20111)` discounts by remaining rounds.)\n\n**Decision rule (round\u202ft, 0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr\u20111):**  \n\n```\nif S == 0:\n    action = C            # no consumption possible, avoid unnecessary audit risk\nelse:\n    EV_coop = U_C + V(S_next_coop)\n    EV_def  = U_D + V(S_next_def)\n    action = D if EV_def > EV_coop else C\n```\n\n**Last round (t = r\u20111):** No audits occur, so only immediate payoff matters.  \n```\nif S == 0: action = C\nelse:     action = D    # higher immediate payoff, no future penalty\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling:**  \n\n- **Zero stock:** Choose `C` (consumption = 0, avoids potential audit fine).  \n- **Negative expected payoff from defecting** (possible if `q\u00b7F > S/n`): the rule automatically selects `C` because `EV_def` will be lower than `EV_coop`.  \n- **Capacity overflow:** The stock update formula already caps at `capacity`; no additional action needed.  \n\n**Parameter choices (can be tuned once at start):**  \n\n- Smoothing factor `\u03bb` (e.g. `0.8`) \u2013 balances responsiveness vs stability of the cooperation estimate.  \n- Look\u2011ahead weight `\u03c4` (e.g. `0.6`) \u2013 controls how much future stock matters to the agent; higher values make the agent more conservation\u2011oriented.  \n\n**Summary of behaviour:**  \n- The agent continuously infers the cooperativeness of the population, projects the stock trajectory under each possible own action, and selects the action that maximizes the sum of its immediate expected return and a discounted estimate of future returns.  \n- It never defects when the stock is depleted, and defects in the final round to capture the last\u2011round surplus, reflecting a purely individualistic payoff maximization."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_1 = "**Opportunistic Common\u2011Pool Strategy**\n\n**Notation (available to the agent each round\u202ft)**  \n*\u202fn\u202f\u2013 number of players*  \n*\u202fr\u202f\u2013 total rounds*  \n*\u202fcapacity\u202f\u2013 maximum sustainable stock*  \n*\u202fq\u202f\u2013 audit probability (0\u202f\u2264\u202fq\u202f\u2264\u202f1)*  \n*\u202fF\u202f\u2013 fine for a detected defection*  \n*\u202fS\u209c\u202f\u2013 stock level at the beginning of round\u202ft* (observed after the growth step of round\u202ft\u20111)  \n*\u202fk\u209c\u202f\u2013 number of opponents observed cooperating in round\u202ft\u20111* (0\u202f\u2264\u202fk\u209c\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111)  \n*\u202f\u03b1\u202f\u2208\u202f(0,\u202f1) \u2013 learning rate (fixed, e.g.\u202f0.5)*  \n\n**Estimated opponent cooperation rate**  \nMaintain a running estimate \\(p_t\\) of the probability that a randomly chosen opponent cooperates:\n\n```\nif t == 0:\n    p_0 = 0.5                # neutral prior\nelse:\n    obs = k_t / (n-1)        # observed cooperation frequency this round\n    p_t = \u03b1 * p_{t-1} + (1-\u03b1) * obs\n```\n\n**Expected one\u2011shot payoff (ignoring stock dynamics)**  \n\n```\nE_C(S) = S / (2n)                                 # cooperate\nE_D(S) = S / n - q * F   (if q > 0) else S / n   # defect, expected fine subtracted\n```\n\n**Forecasted stock after this round** (used only for a safety check)\n\n```\ndef forecast_stock(S, action, p):\n    # Expected total consumption this round\n    coop_opp = (n-1) * p           # expected cooperating opponents\n    def_opp  = (n-1) - coop_opp   # expected defecting opponents\n\n    cons_self = S/(2n) if action == 'C' else S/n\n    cons_opp  = coop_opp * (S/(2n)) + def_opp * (S/n)\n\n    S_rem = S - (cons_self + cons_opp)\n    growth = 2 * S_rem * (1 - S_rem / capacity)\n    return min(S_rem + growth, capacity)\n```\n\n**Safety stock threshold** \u2013 the minimum stock that still yields a positive cooperative payoff for each remaining round if everyone were to cooperate:\n\n```\nmin_needed(t) = (r - t - 1) * (capacity / (2n))\n```\n\n**Decision rule (applied each round\u202ft)**  \n\n```\nif t == r-1:                     # LAST ROUND (never audited)\n    action = 'D'                 # pure defection, maximizes immediate payoff\nelif S_t <= 0:                   # STOCK DEPLETED\n    action = 'D'                 # any action yields 0; choose D to keep logic simple\nelse:\n    # Compare expected immediate payoffs\n    coop_val = E_C(S_t)\n    def_val  = E_D(S_t)\n\n    if def_val > coop_val:                       # defect is strictly better now\n        # Safety check: will stock stay above the minimal needed level?\n        S_next = forecast_stock(S_t, 'D', p_t)\n        if S_next >= min_needed(t):\n            action = 'D'                         # defect opportunistically\n        else:\n            action = 'C'                         # sacrifice this round to preserve future gains\n    elif coop_val > def_val:                     # cooperation dominates even with fine\n        action = 'C'\n    else:                                        # indifference (difference within \u03b5)\n        # bias toward defection but allow occasional cooperation\n        action = 'D' with probability 0.7 else 'C'\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n* **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0)** \u2013 the estimate `p_0` is set to 0.5, so the rule above applies directly. No audit history is needed.\n* **Rounds where audit probability q\u202f=\u202f0** \u2013 the fine term drops out, `E_D(S)=S/n`. The same decision logic applies; the safety check prevents reckless depletion.\n* **When the stock becomes exactly capacity after growth** \u2013 treat `S_t = capacity` normally; the rule already accounts for the full\u2011stock case.\n* **If the forecasted stock after defecting would be <\u202f0** (possible when S_t is tiny) \u2013 the safety condition forces cooperation (or defection if already zero, which yields no loss).\n\n**Summary of opportunistic stance**\n\n* Defect whenever the expected immediate gain (net of expected fine) exceeds cooperation **and** the stock forecast indicates we can still afford to keep the commons productive for the remaining rounds.  \n* Cooperate when defection would jeopardize future earning potential or when cooperation already yields the higher immediate payoff.  \n* Always defect in the final round, exploiting the lack of audit and the absence of future consequences.  \n\nThe strategy updates its belief about opponent behaviour each round, reacts to the current stock level, and balances short\u2011term profit with a minimal sustainability safeguard\u2014exactly the opportunistic, adaptive behavior required."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_2 = "**Opportunistic Adaptive Strategy (OAS)**  \n\n---\n\n### 1. Internal State  \n| Variable | Meaning |\n|----------|---------|\n| `t` | current round index (0 \u2026 r\u20111) |\n| `S` | current stock (observed at start of round) |\n| `opp_coop_avg` | exponential moving average of the proportion of opponents that cooperated in the last\u202fk\u202fobserved rounds (default\u202fk\u202f=\u202f3) |\n| `defect_score` | cumulative expected gain from defecting versus cooperating, updated each round |\n| `remaining = r\u2011t` | number of rounds left including the current one |\n| `\u03c4(S, remaining)` | stock\u2011safety threshold: `\u03c4 = capacity * (remaining / r) * \u03b1`, with `\u03b1 \u2208 [0.5,1]` (tuned offline) |\n\nAll variables are recomputed at the start of each round from the public history (your own action, the public count of opponent cooperators, and the observed stock).  \n\n---\n\n### 2. Decision Rule  \n\nAt the beginning of round\u202f`t` compute the **expected net benefit of defecting**:\n\n```\n# 2.1 Expected immediate payoff\npay_C = S / (2n)                                 # payoff if you cooperate\npay_D = S / n                                     # payoff if you defect\n\n# 2.2 Expected fine for defecting\nexp_fine = q * F                                   # audit probability \u00d7 fine\n\n# 2.3 Immediate gain from defecting (after expected fine)\ngain_now = (pay_D - exp_fine) - pay_C\n```\n\nCompute the **expected future stock impact** of your current action under the assumption that opponents continue to behave as indicated by `opp_coop_avg`:\n\n```\n# 2.4 Estimate opponent average consumption per player\nexp_opp_cons_per = opp_coop_avg * (S / (2n)) + (1\u2011opp_coop_avg) * (S / n)\n\n# 2.5 Stock after round if you cooperate\nstock_C = S - (pay_C + n * exp_opp_cons_per)               # total consumption\nstock_C = stock_C + 2 * stock_C * (1 - stock_C / capacity) # growth\nstock_C = min(stock_C, capacity)\n\n# 2.6 Stock after round if you defect\nstock_D = S - (pay_D + n * exp_opp_cons_per)               # total consumption\nstock_D = stock_D + 2 * stock_D * (1 - stock_D / capacity)\nstock_D = min(stock_D, capacity)\n```\n\nEstimate **future payoffs** for the remaining\u202f`remaining\u20111`\u202frounds assuming the stock evolves with the corresponding `stock_C` or `stock_D` and the same opponent cooperation level:\n\n```\nfuture_C = (remaining\u20111) * (stock_C / (2n))                # optimistic bound: you keep cooperating\nfuture_D = (remaining\u20111) * (stock_D / n) - (remaining\u20111) * q * F   # optimistic bound: you keep defecting\n```\n\nNow compute the **total expected advantage of defecting**:\n\n```\ntotal_gain = gain_now + (future_D - future_C)\n```\n\n#### Action selection  \n\n```\nif S < \u03c4(S, remaining):                # stock dangerously low \u2192 preserve\n    action = C\nelif total_gain > 0 and S > \u03c4(S, remaining):\n    action = D\nelse:\n    action = C\n```\n\n*Interpretation*:  \n- Defect only when the immediate extra consumption outweighs the expected fine **and** the projected stock remains above the safety threshold, guaranteeing that the future loss from stock depletion does not cancel the gain.  \n- When the stock is below the safety threshold, cooperate to allow regeneration even if opponents are likely to defect; this avoids a catastrophic collapse that would hurt all future rounds.  \n\n---\n\n### 3. Edge\u2011case Handling  \n\n| Situation | Rule |\n|----------|------|\n| **Round\u202f0 (first round)** | Initialise `opp_coop_avg = 1` (optimistic) and `defect_score = 0`. Apply the decision rule; the safety threshold is `\u03c4 = \u03b1\u00b7capacity` (typically >\u202f0.5\u202fcapacity), so early\u2011round defecting is allowed only if `total_gain > 0`. |\n| **Round\u202fr\u20111 (last round)** | Audits are impossible\u202f\u2192\u202f`exp_fine = 0`. Future payoff terms are zero, so `total_gain = (pay_D \u2013 pay_C)`. Choose `D` iff `pay_D > pay_C` **and** `S \u2265 \u03c4(S,1)` (the threshold for the final round is usually low, e.g., `\u03b1\u00b7capacity * (1/r)`). |\n| **Audited after a defect** | Subtract the realized fine `F` from this round\u2019s payoff (already accounted for in expected value). Do **not** modify the decision rule; the audit outcome only updates `defect_score` (optional) and `opp_coop_avg` if the audit reveals your own action (you already know it). |\n| **Observed zero opponents cooperating** | `opp_coop_avg` drops sharply \u2192 future stock after any defect will be very low. The rule will likely set `action = C` because `total_gain` becomes negative or the safety threshold is breached. |\n| **Stock hits 0** | The safety threshold forces cooperation (`action = C`) but any consumption yields zero payoff; the game ends effectively. The strategy continues to output `C` for remaining rounds. |\n| **Capacity reached (S = capacity)** | The growth term is zero, but the stock is maximal; the safety threshold is easily satisfied, so the rule evaluates `total_gain` normally. |\n\n---\n\n### 4. Updating Beliefs  \n\nAfter each round:\n\n```\n# observed number of opponent cooperators = coop_cnt\nopp_coop_now = coop_cnt / (n\u20111)\n\n# exponential moving average (smoothing factor \u03b2 \u2208 [0.1,0.3] tuned offline)\nopp_coop_avg = (1\u2011\u03b2) * opp_coop_avg + \u03b2 * opp_coop_now\n```\n\nOptionally update a cumulative `defect_score`:\n\n```\ndefect_score += gain_now          # tracks net advantage accumulated by defecting\n```\n\nIf `defect_score` becomes strongly negative (e.g., < \u2013threshold), force cooperation for the next few rounds to allow stock recovery, then resume normal evaluation.  \n\n---\n\n### 5. Summary of the Opportunistic Mindset  \n\n- **Exploit** any observable tendency of opponents to cooperate by defecting when the expected extra consumption (minus expected fine) yields a positive net gain and the stock remains safely above the regeneration threshold.  \n- **Preserve** the resource when the stock is low or when future loss would outweigh the immediate profit, thereby keeping the game alive for later exploitation.  \n- **Adapt** continuously via `opp_coop_avg` and the stock\u2011safety function, ensuring the strategy reacts to sudden shifts in opponent behaviour or unexpected stock collapses.  \n\nThe algorithm relies only on publicly available parameters, the observed stock level, and the counted number of opponent cooperators\u2014fulfilling the requirement of being **purely state\u2011 and history\u2011based**."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_3 = "**Opportunistic Common\u2011Pool Strategy**  \n\n**Parameters known to the agent**  \n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `q` (audit probability), `F` (fine)  \n- Current round `t` (0\u2011indexed) and current stock `S` (clamped to `[0,capacity]`)  \n- Observation after each round: `c_obs` = number of opponents that cooperated in that round  \n\n**Internal state**  \n- `coop_est` = Bayesian estimate of the probability that a random opponent cooperates in the next round. Initialise with a uniform Beta(1,1). After each observation update:  \n  `\u03b1 \u2190 \u03b1 + c_obs` , `\u03b2 \u2190 \u03b2 + (n\u20111\u2011c_obs)` , `coop_est = \u03b1/(\u03b1+\u03b2)`  \n\n- `future_value_est` = discounted expected gain from a higher stock in later rounds (simple exponential decay with discount factor `\u03b4 = 0.95`). Updated each round by:  \n  `future_value_est \u2190 \u03b4 * future_value_est + (S - S_prev) * (r\u2011t\u20111)/r`  \n  (captures that increasing the stock now yields extra payoff in remaining rounds).\n\n**Decision rule (per round)**  \n\n1. **Compute immediate expected payoff of cooperating**  \n   - `pay_C = S / (2*n)`  \n\n2. **Compute immediate expected payoff of defecting**  \n   - Base payoff: `base_D = S / n`  \n   - Expected fine: `E_fine = q * F` (last round `q = 0`)  \n   - `pay_D = base_D - E_fine`  \n\n3. **Adjust defect payoff for future stock impact**  \n   - Expected stock after round if cooperate:  \n     `S_C = min( (S - n*pay_C) + 2*(S - n*pay_C)*(1-(S - n*pay_C)/capacity) , capacity )`  \n   - Expected stock after round if defect (assuming all opponents follow current `coop_est`):  \n     `exp_opponent_cons = coop_est * (S/(2*n)) + (1\u2011coop_est) * (S/n)`  \n     `total_cons_D = pay_D + (n\u20111)*exp_opponent_cons`  \n     `S_D = min( (S - total_cons_D) + 2*(S - total_cons_D)*(1-(S - total_cons_D)/capacity) , capacity )`  \n\n   - Future value differential:  \n     `\u0394_future = future_value_est * (S_D - S_C) / capacity`  \n\n   - Effective defect payoff: `eff_D = pay_D + \u0394_future`  \n\n4. **Choose action**  \n   - If `eff_D > pay_C` \u2192 **Defect** (`D`)  \n   - Else \u2192 **Cooperate** (`C`)  \n\n5. **Edge cases**  \n   - **Round 0**: `\u03b1=\u03b2=1` \u2192 `coop_est = 0.5`. Apply the rule above (no history yet).  \n   - **Last round (`t == r\u20111`)**: set `q = 0` (no audit) and treat `future_value_est = 0` (no future). Choose `D` if `S/n > S/(2n)` (always true when `S>0`), otherwise `C` if `S==0`.  \n   - **Stock depleted (`S <= 0`)**: both actions yield zero immediate payoff; keep `coop_est` unchanged and randomly pick `C` (harmless) to avoid unnecessary risk of fine.  \n\n6. **Robustness tweak** (optional but part of the opportunistic mindset):  \n   - If `coop_est` falls below a low threshold `\u03b8_low = 0.2`, treat opponents as effectively all defectors and set `pay_C = 0` (since cooperating would be wasteful). The rule then defaults to `D`.  \n   - If `coop_est` rises above a high threshold `\u03b8_high = 0.8` **and** the stock is above `0.5*capacity`, boost `future_value_est` by a factor of `1.2` to exploit the long\u2011run benefits of preserving the pool, making cooperation temporarily more attractive.  \n\n**Summary of algorithm per round**  \n\n```\nfunction decide(t, S, c_obs):\n    update Beta(\u03b1,\u03b2) with c_obs\n    coop_est = \u03b1/(\u03b1+\u03b2)\n\n    if t == r-1:\n        q_eff = 0\n        future_value_est = 0\n    else:\n        q_eff = q\n\n    pay_C = S/(2*n)\n    pay_D = S/n - q_eff*F\n\n    # stock forecasts\n    S_C = min( (S - n*pay_C) + 2*(S - n*pay_C)*(1-(S - n*pay_C)/capacity), capacity )\n    exp_op_cons = coop_est * (S/(2*n)) + (1-coop_est) * (S/n)\n    total_cons_D = pay_D + (n-1)*exp_op_cons\n    S_D = min( (S - total_cons_D) + 2*(S - total_cons_D)*(1-(S - total_cons_D)/capacity), capacity )\n\n    \u0394_future = future_value_est * (S_D - S_C) / capacity\n    eff_D = pay_D + \u0394_future\n\n    if coop_est < \u03b8_low:   # opportunistic defection floor\n        action = D\n    elif coop_est > \u03b8_high and S > 0.5*capacity:\n        future_value_est *= 1.2   # amplify cooperation incentive\n        action = C if eff_D <= pay_C else D\n    else:\n        action = D if eff_D > pay_C else C\n\n    # edge: zero stock\n    if S <= 0: action = C\n\n    return action\n```\n\nThe strategy constantly evaluates whether the immediate gain from defection (after accounting for expected fines) outweighs the combined immediate gain from cooperation plus the projected future benefit of a healthier stock. It adapts its belief about opponent cooperation, becomes aggressively exploitative when opponents appear mostly selfish, and leverages the last\u2011round audit exemption to maximize payoff."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_4 = "**Opportunistic Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**Inputs (available each round t)**  \n- Parameters: n, r, capacity, audit_prob\u202fq, fine\u202fF.  \n- Current stock\u202fS (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity).  \n- History for self: past actions a_i,0\u2026a_i,t\u20111, own audit outcomes, own received payoffs.  \n- Aggregate observation: number of opponents that cooperated in previous round, k_{t\u20111} (0\u202f\u2264\u202fk_{t\u20111}\u2264\u202fn\u20111).  \n\n**Core idea**  \nDefect whenever the expected marginal return from defecting exceeds the expected marginal return from cooperating, taking into account (1) the audit risk, (2) the impact of current consumption on future stock, and (3) the observed level of cooperation among opponents. Cooperate only when the stock is sufficiently abundant *and* opponents are collectively cooperating enough that preserving the stock yields higher future returns than the one\u2011shot gain from defecting.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Expected immediate net payoff\n\n- If I cooperate:\u2003E[\u03c0^C]\u202f=\u202fS\u202f/\u202f(2n)  \n- If I defect:\u2003E[\u03c0^D]\u202f=\u202fS\u202f/\u202fn\u202f\u2212\u202fq\u00b7F  \n\nDefine **\u0394 = E[\u03c0^D] \u2212 E[\u03c0^C] = S/(2n)\u202f\u2212\u202fq\u00b7F**.  \n- \u0394\u202f>\u202f0\u202f \u21d2 immediate incentive to defect.  \n- \u0394\u202f\u2264\u202f0\u202f \u21d2 immediate incentive to cooperate.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Expected impact on future stock\n\nTotal consumption in round t if I choose action x\u202f\u2208\u202f{C,D} and opponents\u2019 observed cooperation level is k_{t\u20111}:\n\n- Expected number of cooperating opponents for this round:  \n\n  `k_est = k_{t\u20111}` (use the last round\u2019s aggregate count as a predictor).  \n\n- Expected total consumption if I **cooperate**:  \n\n  `C_total = (k_est+1) * (S/(2n)) + (n\u2011k_est\u20111) * (S/n)`  \n\n- Expected total consumption if I **defect**:  \n\n  `D_total = (k_est) * (S/(2n)) + (n\u2011k_est) * (S/n)`  \n\n(If I defect, I replace my own C\u2011consumption with D\u2011consumption; opponents keep the same mix.)\n\nCompute the expected remaining stock after growth for each alternative:\n\n```\nfunction post_stock(consumption):\n    S_rem = max(0, S - consumption)\n    growth = 2 * S_rem * (1 - S_rem / capacity)\n    return min(S_rem + growth, capacity)\n```\n\n- `S_next_C = post_stock(C_total)`\n- `S_next_D = post_stock(D_total)`\n\nDefine the **future value term** as the discounted expected payoff in the next round, using the same \u0394\u2011logic applied to the projected stock:\n\n```\n\u0394_next_C = S_next_C / (2n) - q * F\n\u0394_next_D = S_next_D / (2n) - q * F\n```\n\nAssume a one\u2011step horizon (myopically estimate future gain) and weight it by a factor `\u03b3 \u2208 (0,1]` (default \u03b3\u202f=\u202f0.5).  \n\nCompute **net advantage** of defecting now:\n\n```\nAdv = \u0394                         // immediate advantage\n      + \u03b3 * (\u0394_next_D - \u0394_next_C)   // expected change in next\u2011round advantage\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Decision rule per round\n\n```\nif t == r-1:                     // last round, no future stock value\n    action = (\u0394 > 0) ? D : C\nelse:\n    if Adv > 0:\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Edge\u2011case handling\n\n| Situation | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0)** | No opponent history; set `k_est = n\u20111` (assume maximal cooperation) to avoid premature depletion. Apply the decision rule using this estimate. |\n| **Stock depleted (S\u202f=\u202f0)** | Both actions yield 0 payoff; choose **C** (conserves the \u201ccooperate\u201d label for audit\u2011free reputation, though irrelevant). |\n| **Audit probability zero (q\u202f=\u202f0)** | `\u0394 = S/(2n)`. Defect whenever `S/(2n)\u202f>\u202f0` \u2192 always defect (opportunistic). |\n| **Fine so large that q\u00b7F\u202f\u2265\u202fS/(2n)** | `\u0394\u202f\u2264\u202f0` \u2192 always cooperate while stock remains positive. |\n| **Observed zero opponents cooperating (k_{t\u20111}=0)** and stock low (S\u202f<\u202fcapacity/4) | The projected `S_next_D` will likely collapse; `Adv` becomes negative \u2192 cooperate to keep stock from hitting zero and preserve any future payoff. |\n| **Detected repeated audits on self (a_i,t\u20111\u202f=\u202f1 for several consecutive rounds)** | Implicitly captured by q\u00b7F; no extra rule needed. |\n\n---\n\n### 5. Parameter `\u03b3` (future\u2011value weight)\n\n- Set `\u03b3 = 0.5` by default for a balanced opportunistic stance.  \n- If the game horizon is long (`r`\u202f\u2265\u202f10) and stock growth is strong, increase `\u03b3` (e.g., 0.7) to value future sustainability.  \n- If the horizon is short (`r` \u2264\u202f3) or fine is negligible, keep `\u03b3` low (e.g., 0.3) to prioritize immediate gain.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Summary of algorithm (pseudocode)\n\n```python\ndef decide_action(t, S, capacity, n, q, F, k_last, gamma=0.5):\n    # immediate advantage\n    delta = S/(2*n) - q*F\n\n    # estimate opponents' cooperation count\n    k_est = k_last if t > 0 else n-1\n\n    # consumption totals\n    coop_cons = (k_est+1)*(S/(2*n)) + (n-k_est-1)*(S/n)\n    defect_cons = (k_est)*(S/(2*n)) + (n-k_est)*(S/n)\n\n    def post_stock(cons):\n        S_rem = max(0.0, S - cons)\n        growth = 2 * S_rem * (1 - S_rem / capacity)\n        return min(S_rem + growth, capacity)\n\n    S_next_C = post_stock(coop_cons)\n    S_next_D = post_stock(defect_cons)\n\n    # next\u2011round advantage\n    delta_next_C = S_next_C/(2*n) - q*F\n    delta_next_D = S_next_D/(2*n) - q*F\n\n    # total advantage of defecting now\n    Adv = delta + gamma * (delta_next_D - delta_next_C)\n\n    if t == r-1:                     # final round, no future term\n        return 'D' if delta > 0 else 'C'\n    else:\n        return 'D' if Adv > 0 else 'C'\n```\n\nExecute this function each round, feeding it the observed number of cooperating opponents from the previous round (`k_last`). The strategy automatically adapts to stock fluctuations, audit risk, and opponent behavior while always seeking the highest expected personal payoff\u2014embodying an opportunistic stance."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_5 = "**Opportunistic Threshold\u2011Defect Strategy**\n\n**Parameters needed each round**\n- `t`\u202f: current round index (0 \u2026\u202fr\u20111)  \n- `S`\u202f: current stock level  \n- `q`\u202f: audit probability  \n- `F`\u202f: fine amount  \n- `n`\u202f: number of players  \n- `capacity`\u202f: maximum stock  \n- `last_opponents_coop`\u202f: number of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (undefined for round\u202f0)  \n\n**Decision rule**\n\n```\nfunction decide(t, S, last_opponents_coop):\n    // 1. Last round \u2013 no audit, pure exploitation\n    if t == r-1:\n        return D\n\n    // 2. Immediate expected payoff comparison\n    immediate_defect = S / n       - q * F          // expected net payoff if I defect\n    immediate_coop   = S / (2 * n)                   // payoff if I cooperate\n    if immediate_defect <= immediate_coop:\n        return C        // cooperation is already at least as good\n\n    // 3. Estimate opponents\u2019 defect probability\n    if t == 0:\n        p_def = 0.5                         // no information, assume 50\u202f%\n    else:\n        p_def = ( (n-1) - last_opponents_coop ) / (n-1)   // fraction of opponents that defected\n\n    // 4. Project stock after this round if I defect\n    //    Expected consumption of each opponent:\n    //        defect \u2192 S / n\n    //        cooperate \u2192 S / (2n)\n    exp_consumption_opponents = (n-1) * ( p_def * S / n + (1-p_def) * S / (2*n) )\n    exp_consumption_self      = S / n                     // I defect\n    total_exp_consumption    = exp_consumption_self + exp_consumption_opponents\n\n    S_rem   = max(S - total_exp_consumption, 0)          // stock after consumption\n    growth  = 2 * S_rem * (1 - S_rem / capacity)        // logistic growth\n    S_next  = min(S_rem + growth, capacity)              // stock at start of next round\n\n    // 5. Sustainability threshold\n    //    Below this stock, the expected fine from defecting outweighs the extra\n    //    immediate gain (derived from immediate_defect > immediate_coop):\n    //        S_thresh = 2 * n * q * F\n    S_thresh = 2 * n * q * F\n\n    // 6. Choose action\n    if S_next < S_thresh:\n        return C        // defect would drive stock below the safe threshold \u2192 cooperate\n    else:\n        return D        // stock remains healthy enough \u2192 exploit\n```\n\n**Handling edge cases**\n- **Round\u202f0**: No history, use the 50\u202f% defect estimate; apply the immediate\u2011payoff comparison and the sustainability check.\n- **Round\u202fr\u20111** (last round): Always defect, because there is no future stock value and no audit risk.\n- **Stock\u202f=\u202f0**: Both actions yield zero payoff; the rule will return\u202fC because `S_next = 0 < S_thresh`. This conserves the (non\u2011existent) resource without loss.\n\n**Opportunistic mindset**\n- Defect whenever the immediate expected gain exceeds cooperation *and* the projected stock stays above the sustainability threshold.\n- Switch to cooperation only when defecting would risk depleting the stock below the level at which future fines erode the advantage, or when the audit\u2011adjusted immediate gain is non\u2011positive. This maximizes short\u2011term exploitation while preserving enough resource to keep future exploitation profitable."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_6 = "**Opportunistic Expected\u2011Gain Strategy**\n\n**Parameters known to the agent**  \n- n, r, capacity, audit probability q (zero in the final round), fine F.  \n- Current stock S (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity).  \n- Observation after each round: number of opponents that cooperated,\u202fc\u209c (so defectors\u202f=\u202fn\u20111\u2011c\u209c).\n\n---\n\n### Core decision rule (round\u202ft, 0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr)\n\n1. **Compute the expected marginal profit of defecting**  \n\n   ```\n   profit_D = S/n                     // payoff if D, before fine\n   profit_C = S/(2n)                  // payoff if C\n   expected_fine = q * F               // zero when t = r\u20111\n   net_gain = profit_D - profit_C - expected_fine\n   ```\n\n2. **If net_gain > 0** \u2192 **Defect**.  \n   *(The expected extra consumption outweighs the expected fine.)*\n\n3. **If net_gain \u2264 0** \u2192 **Cooperate**, **unless** the observed opponent behaviour in the previous round suggests an exploitable surplus (see step\u202f4).\n\n---\n\n### Opportunistic exploitation of opponent weakness  \n\nWhen net_gain \u2264 0 the agent still looks for a short\u2011term exploitation window:\n\n*Let\u202fp\u209c\u208b\u2081 = (n\u20111\u2011c\u209c\u208b\u2081)/(n\u20111) be the observed defection rate among opponents in the preceding round (undefined for t\u202f=\u202f0).*\n\n- If *p\u209c\u208b\u2081\u202f\u2265\u202f\u03b8* (\u03b8\u202f=\u202f0.6 by default) **and** *S\u202f\u2265\u202f\u03b1\u00b7capacity* (\u03b1\u202f=\u202f0.5 by default) **and** *net_gain + \u0394\u202f>\u202f0*, then **Defect**, where \u0394\u202f=\u202f(p\u209c\u208b\u2081\u202f\u2212\u202f\u03b8)\u00b7S/(2n) is a bonus term reflecting that many opponents are already over\u2011exploiting the resource.\n\n- Otherwise follow the core rule (step\u202f2\u20133).\n\n---\n\n### Edge\u2011case handling  \n\n- **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0)**: No opponent history; set p\u208b\u2081\u202f=\u202f0. Apply the core rule directly.  \n- **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111)**: Audits never occur, so set q\u202f=\u202f0 (expected_fine\u202f=\u202f0). The core rule reduces to \u201cdefect if S\u202f>\u202f0\u201d, which will always be true unless the stock is already exhausted; consequently **always defect** in the final round.  \n- **Stock depleted (S\u202f=\u202f0)**: Both actions yield zero payoff and consumption; choose **Cooperate** (any action is equivalent, but C conserves the formal rule).  \n- **Stock near capacity**: No special handling; the core rule already captures the higher marginal gain from defecting when S is large.\n\n---\n\n### Pseudocode (per round)\n\n```python\ndef decide_action(t, S, q, F, n, capacity, history):\n    # history holds list of opponent coop counts per past round\n    if t == r-1:                     # last round\n        return 'D' if S > 0 else 'C'\n\n    expected_fine = q * F\n    profit_D = S / n\n    profit_C = S / (2 * n)\n    net_gain = profit_D - profit_C - expected_fine\n\n    if net_gain > 0:\n        return 'D'\n\n    # opportunistic bump when opponents over\u2011defect\n    if t > 0:\n        c_prev = history[-1]                     # cooperators among opponents\n        p_prev = (n-1 - c_prev) / (n-1)\n        theta = 0.6\n        alpha = 0.5\n        if p_prev >= theta and S >= alpha * capacity:\n            delta = (p_prev - theta) * S / (2 * n)\n            if net_gain + delta > 0:\n                return 'D'\n\n    return 'C'\n```\n\nThe strategy continuously re\u2011evaluates the expected net gain of defecting, exploits rounds where opponents are already over\u2011defecting, and defaults to cooperation only when the expected fine erodes any advantage or when preserving the stock yields higher future returns."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_7 = "**Strategy Overview**  \nAt every round\u202ft (0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr) the agent computes the *expected marginal gain* from defecting versus cooperating given the current stock\u202fS\u209c, the audit probability\u202fq, and the fine\u202fF. It then decides based on a dynamic threshold that balances immediate profit against the risk of depleting the pool for future rounds.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Decision rule per round  \n\n1. **Compute deterministic payoffs**  \n   -\u202fc_pay = S\u209c\u202f/\u202f(2n)\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 (cooperate)  \n   -\u202fd_pay = S\u209c\u202f/\u202fn\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003 (defect, before fine)\n\n2. **Expected fine**  \n   -\u202fexp_fine = q\u202f\u00d7\u202fF  \n\n3. **Net expected payoff from defecting**  \n   -\u202fd_exp = d_pay\u202f\u2212\u202fexp_fine  \n\n4. **Assess stock\u2011preservation risk**  \n   -\u202fprojected_stock = min( (S\u209c\u202f\u2212\u202f( (k_c\u202f\u00d7\u202fc_pay)\u202f+\u202f(k_d\u202f\u00d7\u202fd_pay) ) )\u202f+\u202f2\u202f\u00d7\u202f(S\u209c\u202f\u2212\u202fconsumed)\u202f\u00d7\u202f(1\u202f\u2212\u202f(S\u209c\u202f\u2212\u202fconsumed)/capacity) , capacity )  \n   where k_c and k_d are the *expected* numbers of cooperating and defecting opponents in this round.  \n   -\u202frisk_factor = 1\u202f\u2212\u202f(projected_stock\u202f/\u202fcapacity)\u2003\u2003(0\u202f=\u202ffull stock, 1\u202f=\u202fempty)  \n\n5. **Opportunity score**  \n   -\u202fscore = d_exp\u202f\u2212\u202fc_pay\u202f\u2212\u202f\u03b1\u202f\u00d7\u202frisk_factor  \n\n   \u03b1 is a small constant (e.g. \u03b1\u202f=\u202f0.1\u202f\u00d7\u202fmax(d_pay,c_pay)) that penalises aggressive defection when the pool is already low.\n\n6. **Action selection**  \n   - If **score\u202f>\u202f0** \u2192 **Defect**  \n   - Else \u2192 **Cooperate**  \n\n   When the score is exactly zero, break ties in favor of defection (opportunistic bias).\n\n---\n\n### 2. History\u2011driven estimation of opponents  \n\n- Maintain rolling averages **p_C** and **p_D** = proportion of cooperators/defectors observed so far (excluding own action).  \n- Update each round:  \n  ```\n  p_C = (p_C * (t) + observed_cooperators) / (t+1)\n  p_D = 1 - p_C\n  ```\n- Use these to set **k_c = (n\u20111)\u202f\u00d7\u202fp_C**, **k_d = (n\u20111)\u202f\u00d7\u202fp_D** in the projection step.  \n- If the history window is empty (t\u202f=\u202f0) assume **p_C = 1** (optimistic baseline) to avoid premature depletion.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Edge\u2011case handling  \n\n| Situation | Action |\n|-----------|--------|\n| **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0)** | Use the decision rule with **p_C\u202f=\u202f1** (i.e., assume everyone will cooperate). If **score\u202f>\u202f0**, defect immediately; otherwise cooperate. |\n| **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111)** | Audits are impossible, so set **exp_fine\u202f=\u202f0**. Apply the decision rule without the fine term; defect if **d_pay\u202f>\u202fc_pay**, else cooperate. |\n| **Stock\u202fS\u209c\u202f=\u202f0** | No payoff possible; cooperate (action irrelevant) and wait for growth (which will stay zero). |\n| **Projected_stock\u202f\u2264\u202f0** (i.e., total expected consumption would exhaust the pool) | Force **Cooperate** regardless of score to avoid a zero\u2011stock dead\u2011end, because any defection would guarantee zero future payoffs. |\n| **Audit probability q\u202f=\u202f0** | Treat **exp_fine\u202f=\u202f0**; the rule reduces to pure profit comparison with risk penalty. |\n| **Fine F\u202f=\u202f0** | Same as above; defection is chosen whenever **d_pay\u202f>\u202fc_pay\u202f+\u202f\u03b1\u202f\u00d7\u202frisk_factor**. |\n\n---\n\n### 4. Opportunistic bias  \n\n- The constant **\u03b1** is deliberately modest, so the agent only backs off from defection when the pool is critically low.  \n- When the expected net gain from defection (after accounting for audit risk) exceeds cooperation by any margin, the agent seizes the opportunity, even if opponents are predominantly cooperators.  \n- The tie\u2011break rule (\u201cfavor defection when score\u202f=\u202f0\u201d) ensures the strategy leans toward maximal extraction whenever profitability is marginally equal.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Pseudocode (per round)  \n\n```\nfunction decide_action(t, S, history):\n    if S == 0: return C               // nothing to take\n    if t == r-1:                       // final round, no audit\n        exp_fine = 0\n    else:\n        exp_fine = q * F\n\n    c_pay = S / (2*n)\n    d_pay = S / n\n\n    // estimate opponent composition\n    if t == 0:\n        p_C = 1.0\n    else:\n        p_C = average_coop_fraction_up_to(t-1)\n    p_D = 1 - p_C\n    k_c = (n-1) * p_C\n    k_d = (n-1) * p_D\n\n    // projected stock after this round\n    expected_consumption = k_c * c_pay + k_d * d_pay + c_pay   // include self if cooperate\n    S_remain = S - expected_consumption\n    growth = 2 * S_remain * (1 - S_remain / capacity)\n    projected_stock = min(S_remain + growth, capacity)\n\n    risk = 1 - projected_stock / capacity\n    \u03b1 = 0.1 * max(c_pay, d_pay)\n\n    d_exp = d_pay - exp_fine\n    score = d_exp - c_pay - \u03b1 * risk\n\n    if score > 0 or (score == 0 and t != r-1):\n        return D\n    else:\n        return C\n```\n\nThe **average_coop_fraction_up_to** routine uses the anonymous count of cooperating opponents observed after each round (available by the game\u2019s observation rule). This yields a fully adaptive, opportunistic policy that exploits profitable defection while retreating only when the common pool is in danger of collapse."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_8 = "**Opportunistic Common\u2011Pool Strategy**\n\n---\n\n### 1. Core decision rule (round\u202ft, current stock\u202fS)\n\n1. **Never cooperate in the last round** (`t == r\u20111`).  \n   *No future value to preserve, and audits are impossible.*\n\n2. **Otherwise compute the \u201caudit\u2011adjusted defect value\u201d**  \n\n   ```\n   expected_defect_payoff   = S / n                # raw consumption\n                              - q * F               # expected fine\n   coop_payoff              = S / (2 * n)          # consumption if C\n   ```\n\n3. **If defecting would leave the pool dangerously low, force cooperation**  \n\n   ```\n   S_after_defect = S - S/n                # stock after consumption, before growth\n   S_after_coop   = S - S/(2*n)\n\n   # Project one step of natural growth (the same for C or D)\n   grow(x) = min( x + 2*x*(1 - x/capacity), capacity )\n\n   projected_stock_defect = grow(S_after_defect)\n   projected_stock_coop   = grow(S_after_coop)\n\n   # \u201cdanger threshold\u201d \u2013 we never let the stock drop below this fraction\n   danger_threshold = capacity * 0.10\n   ```\n\n   *If* `projected_stock_defect < danger_threshold` **and** `projected_stock_coop \u2265 danger_threshold` \u2192 **Cooperate**.\n\n4. **Otherwise compare immediate expected payoffs**  \n\n   *If* `expected_defect_payoff > coop_payoff` \u2192 **Defect**,  \n   *else* \u2192 **Cooperate**.\n\n   This captures the opportunistic trade\u2011off: defect whenever the extra immediate gain (after accounting for the audit risk) exceeds the cooperation payoff, unless doing so would threaten the pool\u2019s survival.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Edge\u2011case handling\n\n| Situation                               | Action                                                                 |\n|----------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Round\u202f0 (first round)**               | Apply the core rule using the initial stock (`S = capacity`).       |\n| **Round\u202fr\u20111 (final round)**             | Always **Defect** (no audit, no future rounds).                      |\n| **Stock already at 0**                 | Payoff is 0 for any action; play **Cooperate** to avoid unnecessary fines (optional). |\n| **Audit probability q = 0**            | The rule reduces to `expected_defect_payoff = S/n`; defect unless the danger\u2011threshold rule forces cooperation. |\n| **Fine F = 0**                          | Same as above; defect whenever `S/n > S/(2n)`, i.e. always except when danger\u2011threshold forces cooperation. |\n| **Projected stock after both actions \u2264 danger_threshold** | Choose the action with the higher immediate expected payoff (the core comparison in step\u202f4). |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Opportunistic mindset rationale (embedded in the rule)\n\n* **Maximize immediate gain** \u2013 Defect whenever the audit\u2011adjusted immediate payoff exceeds the cooperative payoff.  \n* **Preserve future extraction opportunities** \u2013 Switch to cooperation only when defecting would push the common pool below a safe level, thereby jeopardising all future rounds.  \n* **Exploit audit uncertainty** \u2013 The expected fine (`q\u202f\u00d7\u202fF`) is subtracted only from the defect payoff; when audits are rare or fines small, defecting dominates.  \n* **Self\u2011contained adaptation** \u2013 The decision uses only observable quantities (`S`, `t`, `n`, `capacity`, `q`, `F`) and the player\u2019s own audit history (implicitly through `q`). No assumptions about opponent strategies are required.  \n\n---\n\n### 4. Pseudocode (full per\u2011round algorithm)\n\n```python\ndef decide_action(t, S, params):\n    n, r, capacity, q, F = params['n'], params['r'], params['capacity'], params['audit_prob'], params['fine']\n    # 1. Last round \u2192 defect\n    if t == r - 1:\n        return 'D'\n\n    # 2. Immediate expected payoffs\n    exp_defect = S / n - q * F\n    coop       = S / (2 * n)\n\n    # 3. Projected stocks after one round (growth step same for C/D)\n    S_after_def = S - S / n\n    S_after_coop= S - S / (2 * n)\n\n    def grow(x):\n        return min(x + 2 * x * (1 - x / capacity), capacity)\n\n    proj_def  = grow(S_after_def)\n    proj_coop = grow(S_after_coop)\n\n    danger = capacity * 0.10\n\n    # 4. Survival safeguard\n    if proj_def < danger and proj_coop >= danger:\n        return 'C'\n\n    # 5. Opportunistic payoff comparison\n    if exp_defect > coop:\n        return 'D'\n    else:\n        return 'C'\n```\n\nThe strategy is applied independently each round, using the observed common\u2011pool stock `S` and the round index `t`. It is fully deterministic given the parameters and history, opportunistically exploiting audit risk while protecting the resource when collapse would eliminate all future gains."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_9 = "**Opportunistic Adaptive Strategy**\n\n---\n\n### 1. Core decision rule (per round\u202ft)\n\n```\ninput:  n, r, capacity, q, F,   // game parameters\n        S_t (current stock),   // 0 \u2264 S_t \u2264 capacity\n        k_t (number of opponents that cooperated in round t\u20111)\n        t (round index, 0\u2011based)\n\nremaining   = r - t          // rounds left including current\ndiscount    = 1.0            // no explicit discount, can be changed later\n\n// ---------- 1) Estimate opponents\u2019 cooperation probability ----------\nif t == 0:\n    // no history \u2013 assume neutral baseline\n    p_coop = 0.5\nelse:\n    // opponents are anonymous; k_t out of (n\u20111) opponents cooperated last round\n    p_coop = k_t / (n\u20111)\n\n// ---------- 2) Compute expected immediate payoff ----------\npayoff_C = S_t / (2*n)                       // certain when you cooperate\npayoff_D = S_t / n - q*F                     // expectation when you defect\n\n// ---------- 3) Estimate stock after this round under each own action ----------\nexpect_coop_consumption  = payoff_C + (n\u20111) * ( p_coop * payoff_C + (1\u2011p_coop) * payoff_D )\nexpect_defect_consumption = payoff_D + (n\u20111) * ( p_coop * payoff_C + (1\u2011p_coop) * payoff_D )\n\nS_if_C = S_t - expect_coop_consumption\nS_if_D = S_t - expect_defect_consumption\n\n// apply growth function (same for both cases)\ngrow = \u03bb -> 2*\u03bb*(1 - \u03bb/capacity)\n\nS_next_C = min( S_if_C + grow(S_if_C), capacity )\nS_next_D = min( S_if_D + grow(S_if_D), capacity )\n\n// ---------- 4) Project future value of the remaining stock ----------\nvalue_per_unit_stock = (remaining-1) * (1/(2*n))   // each unit of stock can yield at most 1/(2n) per player per future round if all cooperate\nfuture_val_C = (S_next_C - S_t) * value_per_unit_stock\nfuture_val_D = (S_next_D - S_t) * value_per_unit_stock\n\n// ---------- 5) Total expected utility for each own action ----------\nU_C = payoff_C + future_val_C\nU_D = payoff_D + future_val_D\n\n// ---------- 6) Choose action ----------\nif U_D > U_C:\n    action = D\nelse:\n    action = C\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Edge\u2011case handling\n\n| Situation                               | Forced decision |\n|----------------------------------------|------------------|\n| **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0)**                 | Use the rule above with `p_coop = 0.5`. |\n| **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111)**                | **Always defect** (no audit risk, no future stock value). |\n| **Stock exhausted (S_t\u202f=\u202f0)**           | Payoffs are zero regardless; play **defect** to avoid any future penalty (no stock to preserve). |\n| **Audit probability q = 0**           | The rule reduces to pure payoff comparison; defect if `S_t/n > S_t/(2n)`. |\n| **Fine F = 0**                         | Same as q\u202f=\u202f0 case; defect dominates. |\n| **Remaining rounds = 1 (penultimate round)** | Future\u2011value term is zero; choose action that gives higher immediate expected payoff (`payoff_C` vs `payoff_D`). |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Opportunistic rationale embedded in the rule\n\n* **Immediate gain vs risk** \u2013 The expected payoff of defecting includes the audit\u2011adjusted fine (`q\u00b7F`).  \n* **Stock preservation** \u2013 The algorithm values any increase in future stock (`future_val_*`) using the marginal payoff a fully cooperative future would generate.  \n* **Opponent inference** \u2013 `p_coop` continuously updates from the observed count of cooperators, allowing the agent to exploit a cooperative environment (defect) or to cooperate when many opponents already cooperate (to keep stock high for later exploitation).  \n* **Last\u2011round exploitation** \u2013 With no audit and no future stock, the strategy always defects to maximize final\u2011round earnings.  \n\nThe described decision procedure is deterministic given the observable history, requires only the public parameters and the per\u2011round observations, and adapts automatically to any opponent mixture while always biasing toward the action that maximizes the player\u2019s own expected cumulative payoff."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_10 = "**Opportunistic Common\u2011Pool Strategy**\n\n---\n\n**1. Core decision rule (per round\u202ft, stock\u202fS\u209c)**  \n\n```\nif t == r\u20111:                     # last round, no audit\n    action = D                  # always defect\nelse:\n    # 1) Estimate opponent cooperation rate\n    if t == 0:\n        coop_rate = 1.0         # assume full cooperation initially\n    else:\n        coop_rate = observed_cooperators_{t\u20111} / (n\u20111)\n\n    # 2) Compute expected one\u2011shot payoffs\n    coop_pay   = S\u209c / (2*n)                       # payoff if I cooperate\n    defect_pay = S\u209c / n - q * F                    # expected payoff if I defect (audit risk)\n\n    # 3) Safety\u2011stock check\n    safety_thresh = capacity * 0.25                # never let stock drop below 25\u202f% of capacity\n    if S\u209c < safety_thresh:\n        action = C                                 # cooperate to preserve stock\n        continue\n\n    # 4) Opportunistic gain check\n    if defect_pay > coop_pay:\n        # 4a) Anticipate future stock loss from widespread defection\n        projected_stock = S\u209c - (n-1)*(coop_rate*S\u209c/(2*n) + (1\u2011coop_rate)*S\u209c/n) - S\u209c/n\n        # If projected stock stays above safety_thresh, defect now\n        if projected_stock >= safety_thresh:\n            action = D\n        else:\n            action = C\n    else:\n        action = C\n```\n\n*Explanation of the rule components (kept in code only, not narrative):*  \n\n- **Last round:** No audit, so defect maximizes payoff.  \n- **Cooperation\u2011rate estimate:** Uses the anonymous count of cooperating opponents from the previous round; initial assumption of full cooperation encourages a high starting stock.  \n- **Payoff comparison:** Defection is chosen only when its expected net payoff (including expected fine\u202f=\u202fq\u00b7F) exceeds cooperation\u2019s guaranteed payoff.  \n- **Safety\u2011stock threshold:** Prevents the stock from collapsing below a quarter of capacity; whenever the stock is under this bound the strategy forces cooperation regardless of payoff comparison.  \n- **Future\u2011stock projection:** Calculates the stock that would remain after this round assuming opponents continue their estimated mix of C/D. If that projection stays above the safety threshold, the immediate gain from defecting is taken; otherwise the strategy cooperates to avoid end\u2011game depletion.\n\n---\n\n**2. Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n| Situation                               | Action taken |\n|-----------------------------------------|--------------|\n| **t = 0 (first round)**                 | Compute `coop_pay` and `defect_pay` with `coop_rate = 1.0`. Follow core rule; typically cooperate unless `q\u00b7F` is very low and `S\u2080` is large enough that `defect_pay > coop_pay`. |\n| **t = r\u20111 (final round)**               | Always defect (no audit, no future rounds). |\n| **S\u209c \u2264 safety_thresh**                  | Force cooperation to keep stock above the minimum viable level. |\n| **Observed auditors for self** `a_i,t` | No direct effect on the choice; fine already accounted for in `defect_pay`. |\n| **All opponents defect in previous round** (`coop_rate = 0`) | Projection yields rapid stock decline; the safety check will dominate, causing cooperation until stock recovers enough to make defection profitable again. |\n\n---\n\n**3. Opportunistic mindset**\n\n- **Maximize immediate net gain** whenever the expected benefit of defection (including audit risk) exceeds the safe cooperative payoff.  \n- **Exploit high\u2011stock phases**: When the pool is abundant, the extra consumption from defecting is large, so the strategy readily defects.  \n- **Retreat only when stock threatens collapse**: The safety threshold enforces a fallback to cooperation, preserving the resource so future opportunistic defections remain possible.  \n- **Adapt to opponent behavior** through the rolling estimate of their cooperation rate; if opponents become more selfish, the projected stock drops and the strategy automatically shifts back toward cooperation until the pool recovers.  \n\nThis decision process uses only publicly known parameters, the observed count of cooperating opponents each round, and the current stock level, making it fully compliant with the game\u2019s information constraints while remaining aggressively opportunistic."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_11 = "**Opportunistic Common\u2011Pool Strategy**\n\n```\ninput: n, r, capacity, q (audit probability), F (fine)\nstate variables per round t:\n    S          \u2013 current stock (float, 0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity)\n    coop_cnt   \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in round t\u20111\n    total_coop \u2013 cumulative opponent cooperations seen so far\n    opp_rounds \u2013 number of opponent observations (t) so far\n    last_action \u2013 my action in round t\u20111  (C/D/None)\n\nderived constants:\n    THRESH = 2 * n * q * F          # stock level above which defecting is EV\u2011wise\n    MIN_SAFE = capacity * 0.05      # avoid draining stock below 5\u202f% unless forced\n    LAST_ROUND = r\u20111\n```\n\n---\n\n### 1. Decision rule for a generic round `t` (0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr\u20111)\n\n```\nif t == 0:                         # first round, no opponent history\n    # use pure EV comparison\n    if S > THRESH and S > MIN_SAFE:\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C\nelse:\n    # 1) Expected\u2011value check (same as first round)\n    ev_defect = S / n - q * F\n    ev_coop   = S / (2 * n)\n\n    # 2) Anticipated stock if I defect vs cooperate today\n    cons_def = S / n                # my consumption when defecting\n    cons_coop = S / (2 * n)         # my consumption when cooperating\n    S_rem_def  = max(0, S - (cons_def + (coop_cnt * S/(2*n) + (n-1-coop_cnt) * S/n)))   # opponent consumption assumed from last\u2011round mix\n    S_rem_coop = max(0, S - (cons_coop + (coop_cnt * S/(2*n) + (n-1-coop_cnt) * S/n)))\n\n    grow_def  = 2 * S_rem_def * (1 - S_rem_def / capacity)\n    grow_coop = 2 * S_rem_coop * (1 - S_rem_coop / capacity)\n\n    S_next_def  = min(S_rem_def  + grow_def,  capacity)\n    S_next_coop = min(S_rem_coop + grow_coop, capacity)\n\n    # 3) Opportunistic weighting\n    #   - Give extra weight to immediate payoff when stock is abundant\n    #   - Give extra weight to future stock when stock is scarce\n    weight_future = 1.0 - (S / capacity)   # high when stock low\n\n    score_def = ev_defect + weight_future * (S_next_def - S_next_coop)\n    score_coop = ev_coop\n\n    # 4) Choose action\n    if score_def > score_coop and S > MIN_SAFE:\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C\n```\n\n**Explanation of the components (kept internal, not output):**\n- *EV check* guarantees defecting only when the expected net gain exceeds cooperating after accounting for the expected fine (`q\u00b7F`).\n- *Future\u2011stock estimate* uses the opponent cooperation count from the previous round (`coop_cnt`). It assumes opponents repeat the same mix in the current round, which is a reasonable short\u2011term predictor in an anonymous setting.\n- *Weight_future* biases the decision toward preserving the stock when it is already low (\u2264\u202f5\u202f% of capacity we treat as \u201ccritical\u201d). When the stock is high, the weight shrinks, letting the immediate payoff dominate.\n- The `MIN_SAFE` floor prevents a reckless defect that would push the stock below a critical level, which would catastrophically reduce all future returns.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Edge\u2011case handling\n\n| Situation                     | Action |\n|-------------------------------|--------|\n| **Round `t = 0` (first round)** | Apply the EV\u2011only rule (step\u202f1). |\n| **Round `t = r\u20111` (last round)**| **Always defect** (`action = D`). No audit risk, and preserving stock gives no future benefit. |\n| **Stock `S = 0`**                | Either action yields 0 payoff; choose `C` to avoid unnecessary fine risk (if `q>0`). |\n| **Audit probability `q = 0`**    | `THRESH = 0`; the EV check always favors defect (`action = D`) except when `S \u2264 MIN_SAFE`, in which case cooperate to keep the pool alive for the final round. |\n| **Fine `F = 0`**                 | Same as `q = 0`; always defect unless stock is critically low (`S \u2264 MIN_SAFE`). |\n| **Observed opponent count `coop_cnt = n\u20111`** (all opponents cooperated) | The future\u2011stock estimate will be high; the algorithm will likely select `D` (maximizing opportunistic gain). |\n| **Observed opponent count `coop_cnt = 0`** (all opponents defected) | Future\u2011stock estimate will be low; the algorithm will likely select `C` to avoid collapsing the pool. |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Summary of the opportunistic mindset encoded\n\n- **Maximize immediate net payoff** whenever the expected gain from defecting (including expected fine) exceeds cooperating.\n- **Exploit abundant cooperation**: if opponents cooperated heavily in the previous round, the algorithm assumes the stock will stay high and defects aggressively.\n- **Preserve the resource when scarce**: as the stock falls toward a critical threshold, the decision weight shifts to future stock, prompting cooperation even if the EV of defecting is still slightly higher.\n- **Never risk a fine in the final round** (no audit) and never sacrifice a sure payoff when the pool is already depleted.\n\nThe above deterministic rule uses only publicly known parameters (`n, r, capacity, q, F`), the observable stock `S`, and the aggregate opponent cooperation count from the last round\u2014fulfilling the requirement of being fully adaptive, history\u2011dependent, and opportunistic."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_12 = "**Opportunistic Common\u2011Pool Strategy**\n\n*Parameters supplied to the agent*  \n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `q`, `F` (from the game description)  \n- `stock_t` \u2013 current stock at the beginning of round\u202f`t` (0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr)  \n- `history` \u2013 for each previous round\u202f`s\u202f<\u202ft` the agent knows: its own action `a_i,s` (C/D), whether it was audited, and the number `k_s` of opponents that cooperated (0\u202f\u2264\u202fk_s\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111).\n\n*Derived values*  \n- `remaining = r\u2011t\u20111`\u2003\u2003(rounded\u2011down number of future rounds)  \n- `pCoop = ( \u03a3_{s< t} k_s ) / ( (n\u20111)\u00b7t )`\u2003\u2003(if `t==0` set `pCoop = 0.5`)  \n- `gain_defect = stock_t / (2\u00b7n)`\u2003\u2003(immediate payoff difference D\u202f\u2212\u202fC)  \n- `expected_fine = q\u00b7F`\u2003\u2003(only in rounds\u202f`t\u202f<\u202fr\u20111`)  \n- `net_immediate = gain_defect \u2013 expected_fine`  \n- `extra_consumption = stock_t / (2\u00b7n)`\u2003\u2003(amount of stock removed when defecting instead of cooperating)  \n\n*Future\u2011stock loss estimate*  \n\n```text\n# Assume the stock would evolve with the average opponent behaviour observed so far.\n# Expected per\u2011opponent consumption if we cooperate:\n   coop_cons = stock_t/(2\u00b7n)\n# Expected per\u2011opponent consumption if we defect:\n   defect_cons = stock_t/n\n# Weighted expected consumption of opponents in the next round:\n   opp_cons = (pCoop)\u00b7coop_cons + (1\u2011pCoop)\u00b7defect_cons\n# Total expected consumption next round if we cooperate now:\n   total_next_coop = opp_cons + coop_cons\n# Total expected consumption next round if we defect now:\n   total_next_def  = opp_cons + defect_cons\n# Stock after consumption (before growth) difference:\n   delta_S = total_next_coop \u2013 total_next_def = extra_consumption\n# Approximate growth function G(S) = 2\u00b7S\u00b7(1\u2011S/capacity)\n# Approximate future loss over remaining rounds (linearized):\n   future_loss \u2248 remaining \u00b7 ( delta_S * ( 1 \u2013 G'(stock_t) ) )\n# where G'(S) = 2\u00b7(1\u20112\u00b7S/capacity)\n# For simplicity we bound future_loss by:\n   future_loss = remaining * extra_consumption * (1 \u2013 2\u00b7(1\u20112\u00b7stock_t/capacity))\n```\n\n*Decision rule (applied each round `t`)*  \n\n```\nif stock_t <= 0:\n    action = C                         # zero payoff, avoid fine\nelif t == r\u20111:                         # last round \u2013 never audited\n    action = D if stock_t > 0 else C\nelse:\n    # compute a weighted threshold for opportunism\n    threshold = \u03b3 * future_loss       # \u03b3 \u2208 [0,1] is a risk\u2011adjustment constant (default 0.7)\n    if net_immediate > threshold:\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C\n```\n\n*Edge\u2011case handling*  \n\n- **First round (`t==0`)**: `pCoop` is set to 0.5, `remaining = r\u20111`. The same rule above applies, giving a baseline aggressiveness when no information is available.  \n- **Zero or negligible stock** (`stock_t < 1e\u20116`): always cooperate to avoid paying a fine that would yield a negative payoff.  \n- **High audit probability / high fine** (`q\u00b7F` exceeds `gain_defect`): the rule automatically yields `net_immediate \u2264 0`, so the agent cooperates.  \n- **Stock near capacity** (`stock_t \u2265 0.9\u00b7capacity`): growth term is small; `future_loss` is low, making defection more attractive if `net_immediate` is positive.  \n\n*Opportunistic tuning*  \n\n- The constant `\u03b3` controls how aggressively the agent weighs future stock damage versus immediate gain.  \n  * `\u03b3 = 0` \u2192 pure myopic profit (defect whenever `net_immediate > 0`).  \n  * `\u03b3 = 1` \u2192 fully forward\u2011looking (defect only if immediate profit outweighs the maximal estimated future loss).  \n- The agent may adapt `\u03b3` online: after each round, compute the realized stock change; if the stock falls faster than the growth prediction, increase `\u03b3` slightly to become more conservative, otherwise decrease `\u03b3` to exploit.  \n\n*Summary of the algorithm*  \n\n1. Observe `stock_t` and `k_{t\u20111}` (number of cooperating opponents).  \n2. Update `pCoop`.  \n3. Compute `gain_defect`, `expected_fine`, `net_immediate`.  \n4. Estimate `future_loss` using the linearized stock\u2011growth approximation.  \n5. Set `threshold = \u03b3\u00b7future_loss`.  \n6. Choose **Defect** if `net_immediate > threshold`, otherwise **Cooperate** (with the special cases above).  \n\nThe strategy iterates this rule each round, constantly adapting to the observed cooperation level of opponents, the current stock level, and the audit\u2011fine environment, thereby maximizing short\u2011term profit while opportunistically avoiding catastrophic stock collapse."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_13 = "**Decision rule (per round\u202ft,\u202f0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr)**  \n\nInputs:  \n- current stock\u202fS (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity)  \n- number of opponents that cooperated in the previous round\u202fC_obs (if\u202ft\u202f=\u202f0, set\u202fC_obs\u202f=\u202fn\u20111, i.e. assume all opponents cooperated)  \n- remaining rounds\u202fR\u202f=\u202fr\u202f\u2011\u202ft  \n\nConstants (known from the game description):  \n- n,\u202fcapacity,\u202fq,\u202fF  \n\n1. **Compute the audit\u2011adjusted defect advantage**\n\n\\[\n\\Delta(S)=\\frac{S}{n}-qF\\;-\\;\\frac{S}{2n}\n       =\\frac{S}{2n}\\;-\\;qF\n\\]\n\nDefecting gives a higher *immediate* expected payoff iff\u202f\u0394(S)\u202f>\u202f0, i.e.  \n\n\\[\nS > \\theta_0\\quad\\text{with}\\quad\\theta_0 = 2n\\,qF .\n\\]\n\n2. **Adjust the threshold for observed opponent behaviour**  \n\nLet  \n\n\\[\np_{\\text{def}} = \\frac{(n-1)-C_{\\text{obs}}}{\\,n-1\\,}\\qquad(0\\le p_{\\text{def}}\\le1)\n\\]\n\nbe the fraction of opponents that defected last round.  \nRaise the threshold proportionally:\n\n\\[\n\\theta = \\theta_0\\,(1+\\alpha\\,p_{\\text{def}}),\n\\]\n\nwhere\u202f\u03b1\u202f>\u202f0 is a fixed aggressiveness factor (e.g.\u202f\u03b1\u202f=\u202f1).  \nWhen opponents are already defecting, it becomes easier for us to join them.\n\n3. **Take stock sustainability into account**  \n\nIf there are future rounds (R\u202f>\u202f1), we protect the stock when it is low.  \nDefine a safety floor\n\n\\[\nS_{\\min}= \\beta\\,\\theta,\n\\]\n\nwith\u202f\u03b2\u202f\u2265\u202f1 (e.g.\u202f\u03b2\u202f=\u202f1.5).  \n\n- If\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fS_min, cooperate to avoid driving the stock toward collapse.  \n- Otherwise, follow the profit\u2011threshold test.\n\n4. **Last round exception**  \n\nThe final round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111) is never audited, so the fine term disappears.  \nDefecting always yields a larger immediate payoff (S/n\u202f>\u202fS/(2n)) and does not affect future rounds. Hence **always defect** in the last round.\n\n5. **Algorithm**\n\n```\nfunction decide(t, S, C_obs):\n    R = r - t                     # rounds left including current\n    if t == r-1:                  # last round, no audit\n        return D\n\n    theta0 = 2 * n * q * F\n    p_def = ((n-1) - C_obs) / (n-1)      # proportion of opponents who defected last round\n    theta = theta0 * (1 + alpha * p_def) # audit\u2011adjusted threshold\n    S_min = beta * theta                  # safety floor\n\n    if S > theta and S > S_min:\n        return D        # opportunistically defect\n    else:\n        return C        # cooperate to preserve stock\n```\n\n**Parameter defaults (can be hard\u2011coded):**  \n-\u202f\u03b1\u202f=\u202f1 (makes the threshold fully responsive to opponent defections)  \n-\u202f\u03b2\u202f=\u202f1.5 (requires the stock to be comfortably above the defect\u2011profit threshold before we risk defection).\n\n**Summary of actions**  \n- **First round**: C_obs\u202f=\u202fn\u20111 \u2192\u202fp_def\u202f=\u202f0 \u2192\u202f\u03b8\u202f=\u202f\u03b8\u2080. Decision follows the profit test with the safety floor.  \n- **Intermediate rounds**: adjust \u03b8 based on observed opponent behaviour, respect the safety floor, defect only when the stock is high enough to absorb the extra consumption without endangering future payoffs.  \n- **Final round**: always defect.  "

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_14 = "**Opportunistic Common\u2011Pool Strategy**\n\n1. **Notation (for the current round\u202ft)**\n   * `S` \u2013 current stock level (observed at start of round).\n   * `R = r\u2011t` \u2013 number of rounds remaining after this one (including the current round).\n   * `q` \u2013 audit probability, `F` \u2013 fine amount.\n   * `p\u0302` \u2013 empirical estimate of the proportion of opponents that cooperated in the **most recent** round (if no past round, set `p\u0302 = 0.5`).\n   * `\u0394 = S/(2n)` \u2013 extra consumption a defector obtains over a cooperator.\n   * `E_fine = q\u00b7F` \u2013 expected fine per defection.\n\n2. **Immediate\u2011gain check**\n   * Compute **net immediate gain** of defecting versus cooperating:\n     \n     `G = \u0394 \u2013 E_fine`\n     \n   * If `G \u2264 0` \u2192 **Cooperate** (defection is not worth the expected fine).\n\n3. **Stock\u2011safety check**\n   * Predict the stock that would result if you defect **and** opponents continue to behave as estimated by `p\u0302`:\n     \n     ```\n     # expected opponent consumption per opponent\n     opp_cons = p\u0302 * (S/(2n)) + (1\u2011p\u0302) * (S/n)\n\n     # total consumption this round under each of your two choices\n     total_cons_coop = (S/(2n)) + (n\u20111) * opp_cons\n     total_cons_def  = (S/n)     + (n\u20111) * opp_cons\n\n     # stock after consumption\n     S_rem_coop = S \u2013 total_cons_coop\n     S_rem_def  = S \u2013 total_cons_def\n\n     # growth function\n     growth(x) = 2 * x * (1 \u2013 x/capacity)\n\n     # resulting stock after growth (capped by capacity)\n     S_next_coop = min( S_rem_coop + growth(S_rem_coop), capacity )\n     S_next_def  = min( S_rem_def  + growth(S_rem_def ), capacity )\n     ```\n\n   * **Critical\u2011stock threshold**: `\u03c4 = capacity * 0.05` (5\u202f% of capacity).  \n     If `S_next_def < \u03c4` **and** `R > 1` \u2192 **Cooperate** (protect the pool so future rounds are not worthless).\n\n4. **Future\u2011value comparison (optional look\u2011ahead)**\n   * Approximate the *value* of the next\u2011round stock as its linear contribution to payoffs (because each round\u2019s payoff is proportional to the stock at the start of that round).  \n     Let `V_coop = S_next_coop` and `V_def = S_next_def`.\n   * Choose the action that maximizes the sum of **immediate payoff** plus **future\u2011value estimate**:\n     \n     ```\n     payoff_coop = S/(2n)                     # no fine\n     payoff_def  = S/n \u2013 E_fine                # expected fine deducted\n\n     score_coop = payoff_coop + V_coop\n     score_def  = payoff_def  + V_def\n     ```\n\n   * If `score_def > score_coop` \u2192 **Defect**, else \u2192 **Cooperate**.\n\n5. **Edge\u2011case handling**\n   * **First round** (`t = 0`): no opponent history, set `p\u0302 = 0.5` and follow the rules above.  \n   * **Last round** (`t = r\u20111`): no audit, no future rounds.  \n     * Compute `G = \u0394` (no fine).  \n     * If `G > 0` \u2192 **Defect**, else \u2192 **Cooperate**.\n   * **Audit observed**: after each round you learn whether you were audited and the fine paid. Update nothing else; the strategy already incorporates the expected fine.  \n\n6. **Summary decision flow (pseudocode)**\n\n   ```python\n   def decide(S, t, history):\n       R = r - t                     # rounds left including current\n       if t == r-1:                  # last round, no audit\n           return 'D' if S/(2*n) > S/(2*n) else 'C'  # always D because extra gain >0\n       \n       # estimate opponent cooperation rate\n       if t == 0:\n           p_hat = 0.5\n       else:\n           p_hat = history[-1]['opp_coop_frac']   # fraction observed last round\n       \n       delta = S/(2*n)\n       G = delta - q*F\n       if G <= 0:\n           return 'C'\n       \n       # expected opponent consumption per opponent\n       opp_cons = p_hat * (S/(2*n)) + (1-p_hat) * (S/n)\n       \n       total_coop = (S/(2*n)) + (n-1)*opp_cons\n       total_def  = (S/n)     + (n-1)*opp_cons\n       \n       S_rem_coop = S - total_coop\n       S_rem_def  = S - total_def\n       \n       def growth(x):\n           return 2 * x * (1 - x/capacity)\n       \n       S_next_coop = min(S_rem_coop + growth(S_rem_coop), capacity)\n       S_next_def  = min(S_rem_def  + growth(S_rem_def ), capacity)\n       \n       # critical stock protection\n       if S_next_def < 0.05*capacity and R > 1:\n           return 'C'\n       \n       payoff_coop = S/(2*n)\n       payoff_def  = S/n - q*F\n       \n       score_coop = payoff_coop + S_next_coop\n       score_def  = payoff_def  + S_next_def\n       \n       return 'D' if score_def > score_coop else 'C'\n   ```\n\nThe strategy **defects whenever the expected immediate gain outweighs the expected fine and the resulting stock remains safely above a low\u2011stock threshold**, otherwise it cooperates to keep the pool viable for future exploitation. It adapts each round to observed opponent cooperation levels, uses audit risk opportunistically, and maximizes short\u2011term profit while averting catastrophic depletion."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_15 = "**Strategy \u201cOpportunistic Stock\u2011Preserving Defector\u201d**\n\n**Parameters used each round**  \n- `S` \u2013 current stock (observed)  \n- `t` \u2013 current round index (0\u2011based)  \n- `m = r\u2011t` \u2013 rounds remaining (including the current one)  \n- `q` \u2013 audit probability, `F` \u2013 fine amount  \n- `k_last` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (if `t>0`; otherwise unknown)  \n\n**Derived constants**  \n- `\u0394_immediate = S/(2n) \u2013 q\u00b7F`\u2003\u2003 // expected net gain of defecting vs cooperating (last round audit\u2011free, `q=0`)  \n- `Safety = capacity\u00b7\u03c3(m)`\u2003\u2003 // minimum stock to keep alive for the rest of the game, with  \n\u2003\u2003`\u03c3(m) = max( 0.05 ,  (m\u20111)/(r) )`\u2003\u2003 // never below 5\u202f% of capacity, otherwise proportional to remaining horizon  \n\n**Decision rule (applied each round)**  \n\n1. **Final round (`t == r\u20111`)** \u2013 no audits.  \n   *Always defect* (`D`), because `S/n > S/(2n)` and there is no future to protect.\n\n2. **First round (`t == 0`)** \u2013 no opponent history.  \n   - If `\u0394_immediate > 0` **and** `S \u2013 expected_consumption_if_D \u2265 Safety` \u2192 `D`  \n   - else \u2192 `C`  \n\n   `expected_consumption_if_D = S/n + (n\u20111)\u00b7(S/(2n))` (assume opponents start cooperative).  \n\n3. **Intermediate rounds (`0 < t < r\u20111`)**  \n\n   a. **Estimate opponents\u2019 behavior**  \n      - Let `p_coop = k_last / (n\u20111)` (empirical cooperation probability from the last round).  \n      - Expected opponent consumption if we cooperate:  \n        `E_cons_opponents_C = (n\u20111)\u00b7[ p_coop\u00b7(S/(2n)) + (1\u2011p_coop)\u00b7(S/n) ]`  \n      - Expected opponent consumption if we defect: same `E_cons_opponents_C` (opponents are assumed to keep their last\u2011round pattern).  \n\n   b. **Project stock after our action**  \n\n      - If we cooperate:  \n        `Total_cons_C = S/(2n) + E_cons_opponents_C`  \n        `S'_C = S \u2013 Total_cons_C`  \n\n      - If we defect:  \n        `Total_cons_D = S/n + E_cons_opponents_C`  \n        `S'_D = S \u2013 Total_cons_D`  \n\n      - Apply growth:  \n        `S_next_C = min( S'_C + 2\u00b7S'_C\u00b7(1 \u2013 S'_C/capacity) , capacity )`  \n        `S_next_D = min( S'_D + 2\u00b7S'_D\u00b7(1 \u2013 S'_D/capacity) , capacity )`  \n\n   c. **Choose action**  \n\n      - **Defect** if **both** conditions hold:  \n        1. `\u0394_immediate > 0`\u2003\u2003 (expected immediate profit net of fines is positive)  \n        2. `S_next_D \u2265 Safety`\u2003 (projected stock after defecting stays above the safety threshold)  \n\n      - **Otherwise cooperate**.  \n\n4. **Update history** after the round: record the observed number of cooperating opponents (`k_last`) for use in the next round.\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n- If at any point `S \u2264 0`, all future payoffs are zero; the strategy defaults to cooperating (no further loss).  \n- If `q = 0` (no audits) the rule reduces to \u201cdefect unless it would drive the stock below `Safety`\u201d.  \n- If `F` is so large that `\u0394_immediate \u2264 0`, the strategy cooperates regardless of stock level.  \n\n**Opportunistic character**  \nThe algorithm defects whenever the expected immediate gain (after accounting for audit risk) outweighs the cost of possibly reducing future stock, and only cooperates to preserve enough stock to keep earning in later rounds. It continuously adapts to observed opponent cooperation levels, making it responsive to a wide spectrum of opponent behaviours."

description_OPPORTUNISTIC_16 = "**Opportunistic Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**Parameters needed each round**  \n- `n, r, capacity, q, F` (game constants)  \n- `S` \u2013 current stock (float)  \n- `t` \u2013 current round index (0\u2011based)  \n- `oppCoops[t']` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in round `t'` (observed after each round) for all `t' < t`  \n- `myActions[0 \u2026 t\u20111]` \u2013 own past actions (C/D)  \n\n**Derived quantities**  \n\n```\np_coop = ( \u03a3_{\u03c4=0}^{t-1} oppCoops[\u03c4] ) / ( (n\u20111) * t )   # empirical opponent cooperation probability\nlow_stock   = 0.20 * capacity                           # safety threshold\nhigh_stock  = 0.80 * capacity                           # when stock is abundant\n```\n\n**Decision rule (pseudocode)**  \n\n```\nfunction choose_action(t, S):\n    # 1. Last round \u2013 no audit, pure opportunism\n    if t == r\u20111:\n        return D\n\n    # 2. First round \u2013 need a baseline signal\n    if t == 0:\n        return C\n\n    # 3. Stock safety check\n    if S < low_stock:\n        return C                     # protect the pool when it is precarious\n\n    # 4. Compute immediate expected payoffs\n    coop_pay   = S / (2*n)\n    defect_pay = S / n - q*F          # expected fine only when not last round\n\n    # 5. Estimate expected total consumption for the round\n    opp_expected_cons = (p_coop) * S/(2*n) + (1\u2011p_coop) * S/n\n    total_cons_coop   = (n\u20111) * opp_expected_cons + S/(2*n)   # if we cooperate\n    total_cons_defect = (n\u20111) * opp_expected_cons + S/n      # if we defect\n\n    # 6. Project stock after growth for each of our two possible actions\n    function project_stock(consumed):\n        S_rem = max(0.0, S - consumed)\n        growth = 2 * S_rem * (1 - S_rem / capacity)\n        return min(S_rem + growth, capacity)\n\n    stock_next_if_C = project_stock(total_cons_coop)\n    stock_next_if_D = project_stock(total_cons_defect)\n\n    # 7. Opportunistic preference:\n    #    a) Defect if immediate expected net gain exceeds cooperation,\n    #    b) and the projected stock stays above the safety threshold,\n    #    c) otherwise cooperate.\n    if defect_pay > coop_pay and stock_next_if_D >= low_stock:\n        # 8. Add a \u201crevenge\u201d boost when opponents have recently defected heavily\n        recent_defect_ratio = 1 - ( \u03a3_{\u03c4=max(0,t\u20113)}^{t\u20111} oppCoops[\u03c4] ) / ( (n\u20111) * min(3,t) )\n        if recent_defect_ratio > 0.6:          # three\u2011round window, >60% defections\n            return D                          # exploit their lack of cooperation\n        else:\n            return D\n    else:\n        return C\n```\n\n**Summary of the rule set**\n\n1. **Round\u202f0** \u2013 start with `C` to collect a baseline of opponent behavior.  \n2. **Round\u202fr\u20111** \u2013 always `D` (no audit, maximum immediate payoff).  \n3. **Stock below 20\u202f% of capacity** \u2013 force `C` to avoid collapse, regardless of expectations.  \n4. **Otherwise** evaluate the expected net payoff of `D` (including expected fine) versus `C`.  \n5. Defect when it strictly dominates *and* the resulting projected stock stays at least at the safety threshold.  \n6. If opponents have shown a sharp recent rise in defections (\u2265\u202f60\u202f% in the last three rounds), bias toward `D` even when the payoff margin is marginal, exploiting the weakness of the opponent pool.  \n7. In all other circumstances cooperate.  \n\nThe strategy solely uses publicly known parameters, the observable aggregate opponent cooperation counts, and the current stock level, making it fully adaptive to any opponent mix while remaining aggressively opportunistic."

description_SELFINTERESTED_1 = "**Strategy name:** Adaptive Expected\u2011Value with Defection\u2011Retaliation (AEV\u2011DR)\n\n**Parameters (fixed for the agent):**  \n-\u202f`\u03b1 \u2208 [0,1]` \u2013 weight given to future stock value (default\u202f0.6).  \n-\u202f`\u03b2 \u2208 (0,1]` \u2013 tolerance for observed defections (default\u202f0.5).  \n-\u202f`\u03b3 \u2208 \u2115` \u2013 retaliation length after a breach (default\u202f2 rounds).  \n\n**Internal state:**  \n- `stock` \u2013 current common\u2011pool level (observed at start of each round).  \n- `t` \u2013 current round index (0\u2011based).  \n- `r` \u2013 total number of rounds.  \n- `audit_q` \u2013 audit probability `q`.  \n- `fine_F` \u2013 fine `F`.  \n- `last_defect_round` \u2013 last round in which we observed a defection proportion >\u202f\u03b2 (initial\u202f\u2212\u221e).  \n- `retaliation_counter` \u2013 rounds left in retaliation mode (initial\u202f0).  \n\n**Decision rule (executed each round before action):**\n\n```\nif t == r-1:                     # last round, no audits and no future\n    action = D if (stock / n - audit_q * fine_F) > (stock / (2n)) else C\nelse:\n    # 1. Immediate expected payoff\n    coop_now   = stock / (2n)                     # no fine when cooperating\n    defect_now = stock / n - audit_q * fine_F    # expected fine for D\n\n    # 2. Approximate future stock impact\n    #    Assume other players keep their last\u2011observed cooperation rate p_obs\n    #    (p_obs = #cooperators_last_round / (n-1), with 0 if no data).\n    if t == 0:  p_obs = 0.5                     # neutral prior before any observation\n    else:       p_obs = cooperators_last_round / (n-1)\n\n    #    Expected total consumption next round if we cooperate now:\n    #        cons_coop = (p_obs * (stock/(2n))) + ((1-p_obs) * (stock/n))\n    #    Expected total consumption next round if we defect now:\n    #        cons_def  = (p_obs * (stock/(2n))) + ((1-p_obs) * (stock/n))\n    #    (Both are identical because our own action only changes total consumption by \u0394 = stock/(2n))\n    #    Hence future stock difference \u0394S = stock/(2n) (the extra amount saved by cooperating).\n\n    delta_stock = stock / (2n)                 # extra stock retained by cooperating this round\n\n    #    Project stock after one more round using growth rule (linearized):\n    S_future_coop = min( (stock - (n*stock/(2n) + (n-1)*p_obs*stock/(2n) + (n-1)*(1-p_obs)*stock/n) )\n                         + delta_stock\n                         + 2*(stock - delta_stock)*(1-(stock - delta_stock)/capacity), capacity)\n\n    S_future_def  = min( (stock - (n*stock/(2n) + (n-1)*p_obs*stock/(2n) + (n-1)*(1-p_obs)*stock/n) )\n                         , capacity)\n\n    #    Future expected per\u2011round payoff (ignoring future audits) for a representative opponent:\n    future_val_coop = (S_future_coop/(2n)) * (r - t - 1)\n    future_val_def  = (S_future_def/( n))   * (r - t - 1)\n\n    #    Combine immediate and future components\n    ev_coop = coop_now   + \u03b1 * future_val_coop\n    ev_def  = defect_now + \u03b1 * future_val_def\n\n    # 3. Retaliation trigger\n    if observed_defection_ratio > \u03b2:\n        last_defect_round = t\n        retaliation_counter = \u03b3\n\n    # 4. Final action choice\n    if retaliation_counter > 0:\n        action = D                               # enforce retaliation\n        retaliation_counter -= 1\n    else:\n        action = C if ev_coop >= ev_def else D\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n| Situation | Action taken |\n|-----------|--------------|\n| **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0)** \u2013 no opponent history | Use neutral prior `p_obs = 0.5`. Compute `ev_coop` vs `ev_def` as above; if `ev_coop`\u202f\u2265\u202f`ev_def` cooperate, else defect. |\n| **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111)** \u2013 no audits, no future | Choose the higher of the raw immediate payoffs (`stock/(2n)` vs `stock/n - audit_q\u00b7F`). |\n| **Stock exhausted (`stock \u2264 0`)** | Both actions yield zero; cooperate to avoid unnecessary fine risk (no audit benefit). |\n| **Observed defectors ratio exactly \u03b2** | Treat as non\u2011breach (retain normal evaluation). |\n| **Retaliation counter active** | Force defection regardless of EV calculation; decrement counter each round. |\n| **Audit probability `q = 0`** | Fine term drops out; the EV comparison reduces to the classic commons dilemma, still using future\u2011stock weighting. |\n| **Fine `F = 0`** | Same as above; retaliation still applies when opponents\u2019 defection ratio exceeds \u03b2. |\n\n**Self\u2011interest justification embedded in the rule**\n\n- The agent maximizes a weighted sum of *expected immediate* profit (adjusted for audit risk) and *projected future profit* from a higher stock.\n- Retaliation is triggered only when opponents collectively over\u2011defect beyond a tolerance, protecting the agent\u2019s long\u2011run payoff by discouraging exploitation.\n- In the terminal round the agent ignores future considerations and simply extracts the maximum feasible payoff."

description_SELFINTERESTED_2 = "**Self\u2011Interested Adaptive Strategy**\n\n---\n\n### 1. Overview  \nAt each round *t* (0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr) the agent computes the *total expected discounted payoff* of cooperating (C) versus defecting (D) for the *current* round **plus** the *remaining* rounds, using only observable information (current stock\u202fS, number of opponents that cooperated in the last round\u202fk, audit probability\u202fq, fine\u202fF, and the round index). The action with the larger expected total is taken.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Notation (local to the algorithm)\n\n* n \u2013 number of players  \n* r \u2013 total rounds  \n* t \u2013 current round index (0\u2011based)  \n* S \u2013 current stock before consumption (float, 0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity)  \n* k \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in the *previous* round; if t\u202f=\u202f0 set k\u202f=\u202fn\u20111 (optimistic seed)  \n* q \u2013 audit probability (0\u202f\u2264\u202fq\u202f\u2264\u202f1)  \n* F \u2013 fine for a defected audit (\u2265\u202f0)  \n* \u03bb\u202f=\u202f(r\u202f\u2011\u202ft\u202f\u2011\u202f1)/(r\u202f\u2011\u202ft) \u2013 weighting factor for future rounds (\u2248\u202ffraction of game left)  \n\nDerived quantities  \n\n* **Opponent\u2011cooperation probability estimate**  \n  \\[\n  \\hat p = \\frac{k}{\\,n-1\\,}\\quad (0\\le\\hat p\\le1)\n  \\]\n\n* **Consumption amounts** (per player)  \n  \\[\n  c_C = \\frac{S}{2n},\\qquad c_D = \\frac{S}{n}\n  \\]\n\n* **Total consumption if we play C** (assuming opponents repeat the observed mix)  \n  \\[\n  C_{\\text{tot}} = c_C \\;+\\; k\\;c_C \\;+\\; (n-1-k)\\;c_D\n                = \\frac{S}{2n}\\,\\bigl(2n-1-k\\bigr)\n  \\]\n\n* **Total consumption if we play D**  \n  \\[\n  D_{\\text{tot}} = c_D \\;+\\; k\\;c_C \\;+\\; (n-1-k)\\;c_D\n                = \\frac{S}{2n}\\,\\bigl(2n-k\\bigr)\n  \\]\n\n* **Stock after consumption** (cannot be negative)  \n  \\[\n  S'_X = \\max\\bigl(0,\\;S - X_{\\text{tot}}\\bigr),\\qquad X\\in\\{C,D\\}\n  \\]\n\n* **Growth function** (applied after consumption)  \n  \\[\n  g(S') = 2\\,S'\\,\\Bigl(1-\\frac{S'}{\\text{capacity}}\\Bigr)\n  \\]\n\n* **Stock at the start of the next round**  \n  \\[\n  S_{next}^X = \\min\\bigl(S'_X + g(S'_X),\\; \\text{capacity}\\bigr)\n  \\]\n\n* **Immediate monetary payoff** (before fine)  \n  \\[\n  \\pi_C^{\\text{imm}} = c_C,\\qquad\n  \\pi_D^{\\text{imm}} = c_D - \\mathbf{1}_{t<r-1}\\,q\\,F\n  \\]\n\n* **Estimated per\u2011round payoff for the remaining horizon** (assuming we continue to cooperate after this round)  \n  \\[\n  \\pi_{\\text{future}}^X = \\frac{S_{next}^X}{2n}\n  \\]\n\n* **Total expected payoff for each candidate action**  \n  \\[\n  \\Pi_C = \\pi_C^{\\text{imm}} \\;+\\; \\lambda\\;(r-t-1)\\,\\pi_{\\text{future}}^C\n  \\]\n  \\[\n  \\Pi_D = \\pi_D^{\\text{imm}} \\;+\\; \\lambda\\;(r-t-1)\\,\\pi_{\\text{future}}^D\n  \\]\n\n---\n\n### 3. Decision Rule (per round)\n\n```\nif S == 0:\n    action = C                # no payoff either way; choose the low\u2011impact action\nelif t == r-1:\n    action = D                # last round never audited; D always yields higher immediate payoff\nelse:\n    # compute the quantities above\n    compute c_C, c_D\n    compute C_tot, D_tot\n    compute S'_C, S'_D\n    compute S_next_C, S_next_D\n    compute \u03c0_imm_C = c_C\n    compute \u03c0_imm_D = c_D - q*F\n    compute \u03c0_future_C = S_next_C / (2*n)\n    compute \u03c0_future_D = S_next_D / (2*n)\n    \u03bb = (r - t - 1) / (r - t)          # weight for future rounds\n    \u03a0_C = \u03c0_imm_C + \u03bb * (r - t - 1) * \u03c0_future_C\n    \u03a0_D = \u03c0_imm_D + \u03bb * (r - t - 1) * \u03c0_future_D\n\n    if \u03a0_D > \u03a0_C:\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. Edge\u2011Case Handling  \n\n| Situation                               | Prescribed Action | Rationale (self\u2011interest) |\n|----------------------------------------|-------------------|---------------------------|\n| **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0)**                | Compute using k\u202f=\u202fn\u20111 (pretend everyone cooperated last round) | Gives a cooperative baseline; the formula still compares immediate vs future payoffs |\n| **Stock is zero (S\u202f=\u202f0)**              | Play C            | No consumption possible, payoff zero; C avoids unnecessary audit risk in non\u2011final rounds |\n| **Final round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111)**              | Play D            | No audit, D strictly dominates C for any S\u202f>\u202f0 |\n| **Audit probability q\u202f=\u202f0**            | Decision reduces to comparing c_D vs c_C plus future stock impact | The same rule automatically ignores fines |\n| **Fine F\u202f=\u202f0**                         | Same as above, but D may be chosen more often because the fine term disappears |\n| **Remaining rounds = 1 (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20112)**       | \u03bb\u202f=\u202f0\u202f\u2192\u202ffuture term drops; decision is purely based on immediate payoff (with expected fine) | Maximizes payoff for the last two rounds |\n\n---\n\n### 5. Self\u2011Interest Alignment  \n\n* The algorithm **maximizes expected own monetary payoff** by explicitly accounting for the audit\u2011induced expected fine, the immediate consumption benefit, and the **impact of the chosen action on future stock**, which directly influences the agent\u2019s future consumption opportunities.  \n* It never sacrifices current payoff for an abstract \u201cfairness\u201d goal; any cooperation is undertaken only when the projected future gain outweighs the immediate loss from defecting.  \n* The strategy is **deterministic given the observable state** and thus robust to stochastic opponent behavior: it continuously re\u2011estimates opponents\u2019 cooperation level from the most recent observable count (k) and adapts accordingly.  \n\n---"

description_SELFINTERESTED_3 = "**Self\u2011interested Adaptive Strategy**\n\n---\n\n### Parameters (available to the agent)\n\n* `n` \u2013 number of players  \n* `r` \u2013 total rounds, indexed `t = 0 \u2026 r\u20111`  \n* `capacity` \u2013 maximal stock  \n* `q` \u2013 audit probability (0\u202f\u2264\u202fq\u202f\u2264\u202f1)  \n* `F` \u2013 fine for a defected audit  \n* `\u03b8` \u2013 safety\u2011stock fraction (default 0.3)  \n* `\u03b1` \u2013 defect\u2011share trigger (default 0.5)  \n* `m` \u2013 punishment length after trigger (default 2)\n\n### Observables each round `t`\n\n* `S_t` \u2013 current stock (float, 0\u202f\u2264\u202fS_t\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity)  \n* `k_t` \u2013 number of **opponents** that cooperated in this round (0\u202f\u2264\u202fk_t\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111) \u2013 you see this after the round.  \n* `a_{i,t}` \u2013 whether you were audited (only for your own payoff).  \n\n### Decision routine (executed *before* choosing an action)\n\n```\nfunction decide(t, S_t, k_t, last_audit, last_action):\n    # 1. LAST ROUND \u2013 no future, maximize immediate net payoff\n    if t == r-1:\n        return D\n\n    # 2. STOCK BELOW SAFETY THRESHOLD \u2013 preserve future returns\n    if S_t < \u03b8 * capacity:\n        # cooperate gives same consumption as defect when stock is 0;\n        # cooperating avoids fine risk and leaves maximal stock for later rounds\n        return C\n\n    # 3. ESTIMATE IMMEDIATE PAYOFFS\n    U_C  = S_t / (2*n)                       # payoff if cooperate\n    U_D  = S_t / n - q * F                    # expected payoff if defect (fine risk)\n\n    # 4. ESTIMATE NEXT\u2011ROUND STOCK FOR BOTH POSSIBLE ACTIONS\n    #    Assume opponents repeat the observed pattern (k_t cooperators, n\u20111\u2011k_t defectors)\n    cons_C = (k_t) * (S_t/(2*n)) + (n-1-k_t) * (S_t/n) + (S_t/(2*n))   # you cooperate\n    cons_D = (k_t) * (S_t/(2*n)) + (n-1-k_t) * (S_t/n) + (S_t/n)       # you defect\n\n    S_rem_C = S_t - cons_C\n    S_rem_D = S_t - cons_D\n\n    grow_C = 2 * S_rem_C * (1 - S_rem_C / capacity)\n    grow_D = 2 * S_rem_D * (1 - S_rem_D / capacity)\n\n    S_next_C = min(S_rem_C + grow_C, capacity)\n    S_next_D = min(S_rem_D + grow_D, capacity)\n\n    # 5. PROJECT FUTURE PAYOFF (simple linear approximation)\n    remaining = r - 1 - t                     # rounds after the current one\n    future_C = remaining * (S_next_C / (2*n))   # assume all future cooperate\n    future_D = remaining * (S_next_D / (2*n))   # assume all future cooperate (optimistic)\n\n    V_C = U_C + future_C\n    V_D = U_D + future_D\n\n    # 6. TRIGGER\u2011BASED RETALIATION\n    #    If opponents defected heavily in the previous round, punish for m rounds.\n    if t > 0 and ( (n-1 - k_{t-1}) / (n-1) ) > \u03b1:\n        if last_action == PUNISH and last_audit < m:\n            # continue punishment\n            return D\n        else:\n            # start punishment\n            state.PUNISH = 1\n            state.punish_counter = 1\n            return D\n\n    # 7. CONTINUE PUNISHMENT IF IN PROGRESS\n    if state.PUNISH == 1:\n        if state.punish_counter < m:\n            state.punish_counter += 1\n            return D\n        else:\n            state.PUNISH = 0                # punishment finished\n\n    # 8. SELECT ACTION BY COMPARING PROJECTED VALUES\n    if V_D > V_C:\n        return D\n    else:\n        return C\n```\n\n### Edge\u2011case handling\n\n* **First round (`t = 0`)** \u2013 `k_0` is unknown, so step\u202f4 uses the *expected* opponent mix:\n  * assume 50\u202f% cooperation: `k_0 = floor((n\u20111)/2)`.\n* **Stock = 0** \u2013 any consumption yields 0; choose `C` (no fine risk, no impact on stock).\n* **Audit probability `q = 0`** \u2013 fine term disappears; the rule reduces to pure payoff comparison.\n* **Fine `F = 0`** \u2013 same as above; defect whenever `U_D > U_C`.\n* **When `S_t` is exactly `capacity`** \u2013 the growth term evaluates to 0 after full consumption; the algorithm still works.\n\n### Summary of decision logic\n\n1. **Last round** \u2192 always defect.  \n2. **Low stock** (`S_t < \u03b8\u00b7capacity`) \u2192 cooperate to keep the pool viable for future rounds.  \n3. **Otherwise** \u2192 compute expected immediate payoff, forecast next\u2011round stock for both actions, add a linear estimate of future returns, and pick the action with the higher total (`V_D` vs `V_C`).  \n4. **Retaliation clause** \u2192 if opponents defected >\u202f\u03b1 of the time in the previous round, enforce a fixed\u2011length defect streak (`m` rounds) before re\u2011evaluating.  \n\nAll decisions depend only on the known parameters, the public stock level, and the observed count of opponent cooperators; no external communication or hidden information is required."

description_SELFINTERESTED_4 = "**Strategy \u201cSelf\u2011Interest with Expected\u2011Future Adjustment\u201d**\n\n---\n\n### 1. Decision rule (per round\u202ft)\n\n```python\ndef decide(t, S, history, params):\n    # unpack parameters\n    n      = params.n               # number of players\n    r      = params.r               # total rounds\n    cap    = params.capacity       # max stock\n    q      = params.audit_prob     # audit probability (0 in last round)\n    F      = params.fine           # fine per audited defection\n\n    # audit probability for this round\n    p_audit = q if t < r-1 else 0.0\n\n    # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    # 1.1  Immediate (one\u2011shot) payoffs\n    payoff_C_now = S / (2*n)                     # cooperate, no fine\n    payoff_D_now = S / n - p_audit * F           # defect, expected fine\n\n    # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    # 1.2  Estimate opponents\u2019 behaviour\n    #    Use the empirical defect rate of opponents seen so far.\n    opp_moves   = (t) * (n-1)                     # total opponent actions observed\n    opp_defects = history.opponent_defects      # cumulative count\n    if opp_moves == 0:\n        est_def_rate = 0.5                       # no info \u2192 assume 50\u202f%\n    else:\n        est_def_rate = opp_defects / opp_moves\n\n    exp_opp_C = (n-1) * (1 - est_def_rate)       # expected cooperating opponents\n    exp_opp_D = (n-1) * est_def_rate             # expected defecting opponents\n\n    # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    # 1.3  Stock after consumption under each of our two options\n    #     Consumption by us + expected consumption by opponents\n    cons_if_C = payoff_C_now + exp_opp_C * (S/(2*n)) + exp_opp_D * (S/n)\n    cons_if_D = payoff_D_now + exp_opp_C * (S/(2*n)) + exp_opp_D * (S/n)\n\n    S_rem_C = max(0.0, S - cons_if_C)            # stock left after round if we cooperate\n    S_rem_D = max(0.0, S - cons_if_D)            # stock left after round if we defect\n\n    # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    # 1.4  Stock growth for the next round\n    def grow(stock):\n        return min(stock + 2*stock*(1 - stock/cap), cap)\n\n    S_next_C = grow(S_rem_C)\n    S_next_D = grow(S_rem_D)\n\n    # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    # 1.5  Approximate future payoffs for the remaining rounds\n    remaining = r - t - 1                        # rounds left after this one\n    # Assume future rounds we will behave the same way we decide now,\n    # and opponents keep the same estimated defect rate.\n    if remaining > 0:\n        # future per\u2011round expected payoff if we keep cooperating\n        future_C_per_round = S_next_C / (2*n)          # no fine (audit probability ignored)\n        # future per\u2011round expected payoff if we keep defecting\n        future_D_per_round = S_next_D / n - p_audit * F\n        future_C = remaining * future_C_per_round\n        future_D = remaining * future_D_per_round\n    else:\n        future_C = future_D = 0.0\n\n    # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    # 1.6  Total expected utility of the two actions\n    total_C = payoff_C_now + future_C\n    total_D = payoff_D_now + future_D\n\n    # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    # 2. Edge\u2011case overrides\n    if S == 0.0:                # no stock \u2192 any consumption yields 0, but a fine can make D negative\n        return 'C'             # avoid possible negative payoff\n    if t == r-1:                # last round is never audited\n        return 'D'             # pure one\u2011shot gain dominates\n    # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n    # 3. Choose the action with higher total expected utility\n    return 'D' if total_D > total_C else 'C'\n```\n\n### 2. How the rule works\n\n| Situation | Action chosen |\n|-----------|---------------|\n| **First round** \u2013 uses the same calculation; with no opponent data the defect rate is guessed\u202f=\u202f0.5. |\n| **Last round** \u2013 `p_audit = 0`; the rule reduces to \u201cdefect if immediate payoff\u202f>\u202fcooperate\u201d. |\n| **Stock exhausted (`S = 0`)** \u2013 cooperate to avoid a possible fine that would produce a negative payoff. |\n| **Any intermediate round** \u2013 the algorithm compares (immediate payoff\u202f+\u202festimated future payoff) for cooperation vs. defection, incorporating the expected audit fine and the effect of our extra consumption on next\u2011round stock. The opponent defect rate is continuously updated from observed aggregate cooperation counts. |\n\n### 3. Self\u2011interest justification (implicit in the rule)\n\n- The decision maximizes the player\u2019s **expected cumulative payoff** (including expected fines) given the current stock and the best\u2011available estimate of opponents\u2019 behaviour.\n- No consideration is given to fairness, reputation, or collective sustainability beyond what directly affects the player\u2019s own future earnings."

description_SELFINTERESTED_5 = "**Strategy Overview**\n\nMaintain a running estimate\u202f`p_t`\u202fof the fraction of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (derived from the observed count). At each round\u202f`t`\u202f(0\u2011indexed) compute the *expected* net payoff of the two possible actions given the current stock\u202f`S_t`, the audit probability\u202f`q`, and the fine\u202f`F`. Choose the action with the higher expected payoff, subject to a stock\u2011preservation safeguard.\n\n---\n\n### Decision Rule (per round\u202f`t`)\n\n1. **Calculate expected payoffs**\n   - `E_C = S_t / (2n)`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003(cooperate)\n   - `E_D = S_t / n - q * F`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003( defect, net of expected fine)\n\n2. **Stock\u2011preservation check**\n   - Let `\u03b8 = 0.25` (quarter of capacity).  \n   - If `S_t < \u03b8 * capacity` **and** `E_C \u2265 E_D - \u03b5` (with a tiny tolerance `\u03b5 = 1e\u20116`), force cooperation to avoid stock collapse.  \n   - Otherwise proceed to step\u202f3.\n\n3. **Choose action**\n   - If `E_D > E_C + \u03b5` \u2192 **Defect** (`D`).  \n   - Else \u2192 **Cooperate** (`C`).\n\n4. **Update estimate `p_t`**\n   - After observing the number `k_t` of opponents that cooperated this round, set  \n     `p_{t+1} = k_t / (n\u20111)`.  \n   - For the first round (`t = 0`) where no observation exists, initialise `p_0 = 1` (optimistic) and apply the rule directly; the estimate will be overwritten after round\u202f0.\n\n---\n\n### Edge Cases\n\n- **First round (`t = 0`)**  \n  Use the decision rule with `p_0 = 1`. No audit history is needed; the expected fine term uses the known `q` and `F`.\n\n- **Last round (`t = r\u20111`)**  \n  Audits never occur, so `q = 0` for this round. The rule reduces to comparing `S_{r\u20111}/n` vs `S_{r\u20111}/(2n)`, which always favours defecting. Hence the strategy *always defects* in the final round, regardless of stock level.\n\n- **Zero stock (`S_t = 0`)**  \n  Both `E_C` and `E_D` equal 0 (minus any fine component). The stock\u2011preservation check forces cooperation if `S_t < \u03b8\u00b7capacity`, yielding `C` (no consumption, no fine). This prevents unnecessary fines when the pool is empty.\n\n- **Very high audit probability (`q = 1`) or fine**  \n  The expected defect payoff may become negative. The rule automatically selects cooperation when `E_C` exceeds `E_D`.\n\n---\n\n### Pseudocode\n\n```python\ndef decide_action(t, S, capacity, n, q, F, k_last=None):\n    # Step 1: expected payoffs\n    E_C = S / (2 * n)\n    E_D = S / n - q * F\n\n    # Step 2: stock\u2011preservation safeguard\n    theta = 0.25\n    eps = 1e-6\n    if S < theta * capacity and E_C >= E_D - eps:\n        return 'C'\n\n    # Step 3: choose best action\n    if E_D > E_C + eps:\n        return 'D'\n    else:\n        return 'C'\n\ndef update_estimate(k, n):\n    return k / (n - 1)\n\n# Game loop\np = 1.0  # initial estimate\nfor t in range(r):\n    action = decide_action(t, stock, capacity, n, q, F)\n    # submit action, receive consumption info\n    # after round: observe k = number of opponents that cooperated\n    p = update_estimate(k, n)\n```\n\nThe strategy is fully self\u2011interested: it selects the action that maximises the player's expected net payoff each round, while preventing catastrophic stock depletion that would reduce all future payoffs. It requires only the public parameters, the current stock, the audit probability/fine, and the observed count of cooperating opponents."

description_SELFINTERESTED_6 = "**Strategy: Conditional Self\u2011Interest (CSI)**  \n\n**Parameters used each round\u202ft (0\u2011indexed):**  \n-\u202fS\u209c = current stock (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u209c\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity)  \n-\u202fq = audit probability (0\u202f\u2264\u202fq\u202f\u2264\u202f1)  \n-\u202fF = fine per audited defection  \n-\u202fn = number of players, r = total rounds, t = round index  \n-\u202fH\u209c = history of opponent cooperation counts for rounds\u202f0\u2026t\u20111 (empty before round\u202f0)  \n\n**Pre\u2011computed constants:**  \n-\u202fpayoff_C = S\u209c\u202f/\u202f(2n)\u2003(the payoff if we cooperate)  \n-\u202fpayoff_D_nominal = S\u209c\u202f/\u202fn\u2003(the payoff before fines if we defect)  \n-\u202fexpected_fine = (t\u202f\u2260\u202fr\u20111)\u202f?\u202fq\u202f\u00d7\u202fF\u202f:\u202f0\u2003(the fine we expect only when the round can be audited)  \n\n**Step\u202f1 \u2013 Estimate opponent behaviour**  \nLet\u202fc\u0304\u209c\u208b\u2081 = average number of cooperators observed in the previous round (if t\u202f>\u202f0).  \nIf t\u202f=\u202f0, set c\u0304\u208b\u2081 = n\u202f\u2212\u202f1 (assume full cooperation as a neutral prior).  \n\nFrom c\u0304\u209c\u208b\u2081 we derive an estimate of the \u201cdefector fraction\u201d among opponents:  \n\n```\ndefect_frac_est = 1 - c\u0304\u209c\u208b\u2081 / (n-1)\n```\n\n**Step\u202f2 \u2013 Compute projected stock impact**  \n\n*If we cooperate*: our consumption = S\u209c\u202f/\u202f(2n) \u2192 remaining stock after consumption  \n\n```\nS_rem_C = S\u209c - ( (c\u0304\u209c\u208b\u2081 + 1) * S\u209c/(2n) + ( (n-1) - c\u0304\u209c\u208b\u2081 ) * S\u209c/n )\n```\n\n*If we defect*: our consumption = S\u209c\u202f/\u202fn  \n\n```\nS_rem_D = S\u209c - ( (c\u0304\u209c\u208b\u2081) * S\u209c/(2n) + ( (n-1) - c\u0304\u209c\u208b\u2081 + 1 ) * S\u209c/n )\n```\n\nApply the growth rule to each hypothetical remainder:\n\n```\ngrow(x) = 2 * x * (1 - x / capacity)\nstock_next_C = min( S_rem_C + grow(S_rem_C), capacity )\nstock_next_D = min( S_rem_D + grow(S_rem_D), capacity )\n```\n\n**Step\u202f3 \u2013 Evaluate immediate + one\u2011step\u2011ahead expected utility**  \n\n```\nU_C = payoff_C                             // no fine when cooperating\nU_D = payoff_D_nominal - expected_fine\n```\n\nAdd a discounted future term (discount factor \u03b4 = 1, because rounds are equal weight) using the projected next\u2011round stock and the same payoff formulas for a *neutral* opponent (i.e., assume opponents will behave as in the last observed round):\n\n```\nfuture_U_C = (stock_next_C)/(2n)                    // expected payoff next round if we cooperate now\nfuture_U_D = (stock_next_D)/n - expected_fine      // expected payoff next round if we defect now (still subject to audit next round)\n```\n\nTotal evaluation:\n\n```\nE_C = U_C + future_U_C\nE_D = U_D + future_U_D\n```\n\n**Step\u202f4 \u2013 Decision rule**  \n\n- **If t = r\u20111 (final round)**: ignore future term and audit risk (expected_fine = 0). Choose **D** if `payoff_D_nominal > payoff_C`, else **C**.  \n- **Otherwise**:  \n\n```\nif E_D > E_C      \u2192  play D\nelse               \u2192  play C\n```\n\nTie\u2011breaker: randomize with 50\u202f% probability to avoid deterministic exploitation.\n\n**Step\u202f5 \u2013 Edge\u2011case handling**  \n\n- **Zero stock (S\u209c = 0)**: Both actions yield zero payoff; play C to preserve the stock (which remains zero) and avoid a fine.  \n- **Extremely low stock (S\u209c < \u03b5, \u03b5 = 0.01\u202f\u00d7\u202fcapacity)**: Treat future stock as effectively zero; set `E_C = E_D = 0` and play **C** to avoid paying a fine for no gain.  \n- **Audit\u2011free round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111)**: `expected_fine = 0` automatically, so the rule reduces to \u201cdefect if immediate payoff higher\u201d.  \n\n**Step\u202f6 \u2013 Update history**  \n\nAfter the round, record the observed count of cooperating opponents (derived from the public aggregate observation) to be used in the next round\u2019s `c\u0304\u209c`.  \n\n**Summary of algorithm per round t**\n\n```\n1. Observe S\u209c and opponent cooperation count opp_C_t.\n2. Update history: append opp_C_t.\n3. Compute c\u0304 = average(opponent cooperation counts over last observed round).\n4. Estimate defect_frac_est = 1 - c\u0304/(n-1).\n5. Compute payoff_C, payoff_D_nominal, expected_fine.\n6. Project S_rem_C, S_rem_D, then stock_next_C, stock_next_D.\n7. Compute E_C = payoff_C + stock_next_C/(2n).\n8. Compute E_D = payoff_D_nominal - expected_fine + (stock_next_D)/n - expected_fine_next.\n   (expected_fine_next = q\u00d7F because next round is auditable)\n9. If t = r\u20111 \u2192 ignore future terms, compare payoff_D_nominal vs payoff_C.\n10. Choose D if E_D > E_C, else C (randomize on equality).\n```\n\nThe CSI strategy always maximizes expected self\u2011payoff given the current stock, audit risk, and the most recent observed pattern of opponent cooperation, while safeguarding against stock collapse by folding a one\u2011step\u2011ahead stock projection into the decision."

description_SELFINTERESTED_7 = "**Self\u2011Interested Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**Parameters known to the agent**  \n- n, r, capacity, audit probability q, fine F (all constants).  \n- Current round t (0\u2011indexed), current stock S (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity).  \n- From the previous round (t\u20111) the agent knows the number\u202fk of opponents that cooperated (0\u202f\u2264\u202fk\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111). For t\u202f=\u202f0 this statistic is undefined; treat k as the average cooperation rate observed over all earlier rounds (initially n\u20111, i.e. assume all opponents cooperated).\n\n**Step 1 \u2013 Immediate expected payoff**\n\n```\npay_C  = S/(2n)                         # no audit risk\npay_D  = S/n - q*F                      # expected fine subtracted\n```\n\n**Step 2 \u2013 Projected stock after this round**\n\nAssume opponents repeat the observed pattern k cooperators / (n\u20111\u2011k) defectors.\n\n```\n# If I cooperate:\ncons_C = (k+1) * S/(2n) + (n-1-k) * S/n          # total consumption this round\nS_rem_C = max(0, S - cons_C)                     # stock after consumption\ngrowth_C = 2 * S_rem_C * (1 - S_rem_C/capacity)\nS_next_C = min(S_rem_C + growth_C, capacity)\n\n# If I defect:\ncons_D = k * S/(2n) + (n-k) * S/n                # total consumption this round\nS_rem_D = max(0, S - cons_D)\ngrowth_D = 2 * S_rem_D * (1 - S_rem_D/capacity)\nS_next_D = min(S_rem_D + growth_D, capacity)\n```\n\n**Step 3 \u2013 Approximate future value of the remaining rounds**\n\nUse a linear approximation of expected marginal payoff per unit of stock: each unit of stock in a future round yields on average `1/(2n)` payoff per round (the cooperative baseline). Let `\u03c4 = r - t - 1` be the number of rounds left after the current one.\n\n```\nfuture_C = \u03c4 * (1/(2n)) * S_next_C\nfuture_D = \u03c4 * (1/(2n)) * S_next_D\n```\n\n**Step 4 \u2013 Decision rule**\n\n```\ntotal_C = pay_C + future_C\ntotal_D = pay_D + future_D\n\nif total_D > total_C and S_next_D >= safety_threshold:\n    choose D\nelse:\n    choose C\n```\n\n*Safety threshold* safeguards against catastrophic depletion:\n\n```\nsafety_threshold = capacity * 0.05      # 5\u202f% of capacity; any projected stock below this forces cooperation\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n1. **Last round (t = r\u20111)** \u2013 Audits never occur, so `pay_D = S/n > S/(2n)`. The rule reduces to always defect (`choose D`). The future\u2011value term is zero, so the above inequality always holds.\n\n2. **Zero stock (S = 0)** \u2013 Both `pay_C` and `pay_D` are zero; `S_next_C = S_next_D = 0`. The inequality is false, so the agent cooperates (`choose C`) to avoid a fine that would otherwise reduce its payoff (fine only applies when playing D).\n\n3. **Audit probability q = 0** \u2013 `pay_D = S/n`. The decision reduces to comparing the long\u2011run stock impact; if defecting would drive the projected stock below the safety threshold, the agent cooperates; otherwise it defects.\n\n4. **No history on opponents (t = 0)** \u2013 Initialise `k = n\u20111` (assume all opponents cooperated) so the first\u2011round projection is optimistic; the same decision rule applies.\n\n5. **Observed all opponents defect (k = 0)** \u2013 The projected stock after cooperating will be higher than after defecting, raising `future_C`. The rule may still select cooperation when the future benefit outweighs the immediate loss.\n\n**Summary of execution each round**\n\n1. Read S, t, k (or use default).  \n2. Compute `pay_C`, `pay_D`.  \n3. Compute projected next\u2011stock `S_next_C`, `S_next_D` using the consumption formulas above.  \n4. Compute `future_C`, `future_D` with \u03c4 = r\u2011t\u20111.  \n5. Evaluate `total_C` vs `total_D` and apply the safety\u2011threshold check.  \n6. Output action C or D.  "

description_SELFINTERESTED_8 = "**Self\u2011Interested Adaptive Strategy (SAAS)**  \n\n**Parameters (read from the game description)**\n- `n` \u2013 number of players  \n- `r` \u2013 total rounds, indexed `t = 0 \u2026 r\u20111`  \n- `capacity` \u2013 max stock  \n- `q` \u2013 audit probability (0\u202f\u2264\u202fq\u202f\u2264\u202f1)  \n- `F` \u2013 fine per audited defection  \n\n**State variables (maintained locally)**\n- `S_t` \u2013 stock at the beginning of round `t` (observed)  \n- `C_obs_t` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in round `t` (observed)  \n- `audit_history[i]` \u2013 list of audit outcomes for this player (0\u202f=\u202fno audit, 1\u202f=\u202faudited) up to round `t\u20111`  \n\n**Utility estimates for the current round**\n\n```text\nU_C = S_t / (2n)                                          # payoff if we cooperate\nU_D = S_t / n - q * F                                     # expected payoff if we defect\n\u0394C  = S_t / (2n)                                          # consumption if we cooperate\n\u0394D  = S_t / n                                             # consumption if we defect\n\u0394extra = \u0394D - \u0394C = S_t / (2n)                             # extra stock taken when defecting\n```\n\n**Projected stock after round `t`**\n\n```text\n# Assume opponents repeat their observed mix in the next round:\nopp_coop = C_obs_t\nopp_def  = (n\u20111) - C_obs_t\n\n# Total consumption if we cooperate:\ncons_C = \u0394C + opp_coop * (S_t / (2n)) + opp_def * (S_t / n)\n\n# Total consumption if we defect:\ncons_D = \u0394D + opp_coop * (S_t / (2n)) + opp_def * (S_t / n)\n\n# Stock after consumption (same for both actions because opponents\u2019 actions are unchanged):\nS_rem = S_t - (opp_coop * (S_t / (2n)) + opp_def * (S_t / n))\n\n# Stock remaining after we act:\nS_rem_C = S_t - cons_C\nS_rem_D = S_t - cons_D\n\n# Growth function:\ngrow(X) = 2 * X * (1 - X / capacity)\n\n# Projected next\u2011round stock:\nS_next_C = min( S_rem_C + grow(S_rem_C), capacity )\nS_next_D = min( S_rem_D + grow(S_rem_D), capacity )\n```\n\n**Safety threshold**\n\nLet `\u03c4 = (r\u2011t\u20111) / r` be the fraction of game remaining after the current round.  \nDefine a minimal viable stock `S_min = \u03c4 * capacity`.  \nIf `S_next_X < S_min` (for X = C or D), the action would jeopardise future payoffs.\n\n**Decision rule (applied each round `t`)**\n\n1. **Last round (`t = r\u20111`)** \u2013 no audits occur. Choose the action with higher immediate payoff:\n   ```\n   if U_D > U_C: play D else play C\n   ```\n   (If `S_t = 0` both give 0; any action is fine.)\n\n2. **First round (`t = 0`)** \u2013 no observation of opponents yet. Assume neutral mix:\n   ```\n   C_obs_0 = floor((n\u20111)/2)              # default estimate\n   evaluate rules below.\n   ```\n\n3. **General round (`0 \u2264 t < r\u20111`)**  \n   ```\n   # 3a. Immediate incentive test\n   if U_D <= U_C:\n        action = C\n   else:\n        # 3b. Stock\u2011preservation test\n        if S_next_D < S_min:\n            action = C\n        else:\n            # 3c. Exploit\u2011risk adjustment\n            # compute expected cumulative gain of defecting now vs cooperating now,\n            # assuming future rounds follow the observed opponent mix.\n            # Approximate future payoff difference as:\n            diff_future = (S_next_D - S_next_C) / (2n) * (r - t - 1)\n            if diff_future + (U_D - U_C) > 0:\n                 action = D\n            else:\n                 action = C\n   ```\n\n4. **Audit\u2011feedback adaptation**  \n   After each round (except the last), record whether we were audited (`a = 1`) and the fine actually paid (`a*F`).  \n   If we have been audited in **two consecutive rounds** while defecting, increase `q`\u2011adjusted penalty by a factor `\u03b3 = 1.5` for the next round:\n   ```\n   effective_q = min(1, q * \u03b3)   # only for the next round\u2019s U_D computation\n   ```\n   Reset `\u03b3` to 1 if we cooperate in a round or if an audit does not occur.\n\n**Summary of actions**\n- Defect when the immediate expected payoff (including expected fine) exceeds cooperation *and* doing so does not push the projected stock below the safety threshold.\n- Cooperate otherwise, especially when stock is low relative to remaining rounds or when recent audits suggest a higher effective audit risk.\n- In the final round, ignore future\u2011stock considerations and simply take the higher immediate payoff (no audit risk).  "

description_SELFINTERESTED_9 = "**Self\u2011Interested Adaptive Strategy (SIA\u2011A)**  \n\n*Parameters:* n, r, capacity, q (audit probability), F (fine).  \n\n*State variables kept each round t (0\u2011indexed):*  \n- `S` \u2013 current stock (float).  \n- `k_C` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (0\u202f\u2026\u202fn\u20111).  \n- `my_last` \u2013 my action in the previous round (C or D).  \n\n*Auxiliary functions*  \n\n```text\npayoff_C(S) = S/(2n)\npayoff_D(S) = S/n\nexpected_fine = q * F                     // expected fine per defection\nnet_gain_D(S) = payoff_D(S) \u2013 expected_fine\n```\n\n*Decision rule (applied before each round t):*\n\n1. **Last round (t = r\u20111)** \u2013 No audit occurs.  \n   - Play **D** (defect) because it yields the highest immediate payoff and there is no future stock to preserve.\n\n2. **First round (t = 0)** \u2013 No history available.  \n   - Compute `net_gain = net_gain_D(S) \u2013 payoff_C(S)`.  \n   - If `net_gain > 0` \u2192 play **D**.  \n   - Otherwise (rare when q is high or F large) \u2192 play **C**.  \n\n3. **Intermediate rounds (0\u202f<\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr\u20111):**  \n\n   a. **Estimate opponent cooperation level** from the last observed `k_C`.  \n      ```text\n      p_coop = k_C / (n\u20111)          // empirical probability an opponent cooperated last round\n      ```\n   b. **Project stock impact** of my action for the next round under the assumption that opponents repeat last\u2011round behaviour:  \n\n      - If I **cooperate** now, next\u2011round expected total consumption:  \n\n        `E_cons_C = payoff_C(S)                     // my C share\n                    + (n\u20111) * [ p_coop*payoff_C(S) + (1\u2011p_coop)*payoff_D(S) ]`\n\n      - If I **defect** now, next\u2011round expected total consumption:  \n\n        `E_cons_D = payoff_D(S)                     // my D share\n                    + (n\u20111) * [ p_coop*payoff_C(S) + (1\u2011p_coop)*payoff_D(S) ]`\n\n      - Compute projected stock after growth for each case:  \n\n        ```\n        S_next_C = min( (S - E_cons_C) + 2*(S - E_cons_C)*(1 - (S - E_cons_C)/capacity), capacity )\n        S_next_D = min( (S - E_cons_D) + 2*(S - E_cons_D)*(1 - (S - E_cons_D)/capacity), capacity )\n        ```\n\n   c. **Compute expected total payoff over the current and next round**, incorporating audit risk on the current round only:  \n\n        ```\n        val_C = payoff_C(S) + payoff_expected_next(S_next_C, p_coop)   // no fine when C\n        val_D = net_gain_D(S) + payoff_expected_next(S_next_D, p_coop)\n        ```\n\n        where  \n\n        ```\n        payoff_expected_next(S_next, p_coop) =\n            payoff_C(S_next) * p_coop + payoff_D(S_next) * (1 - p_coop)\n        ```\n\n   d. **Choose action:**  \n\n        - If `val_D > val_C` \u2192 play **D**.  \n        - Else \u2192 play **C**.\n\n4. **Edge\u2011case adjustments:**  \n\n   - If `S` \u2264 0 (stock exhausted) \u2192 any consumption yields 0; choose **C** to avoid the fine risk (no gain from D).  \n   - If `net_gain_D(S) \u2264 payoff_C(S)` (i.e., expected fine outweighs extra gain) \u2192 treat D as unprofitable and default to **C** regardless of projection.  \n   - If `p_coop` is undefined (no prior opponent data because of a single\u2011player game or erroneous input) \u2192 set `p_coop = 0` (assume worst\u2011case all defect).  \n\n*Update after each round:*  \n\n- Record `k_C` from the public observation of opponent cooperations.  \n- Update `my_last` with the action just taken.  \n- Update `S` using the stock dynamics described in the game specification.  \n\nThe strategy continuously re\u2011evaluates the marginal benefit of defecting versus cooperating, accounting for expected audit fines, the current stock level, and the observed propensity of opponents to cooperate. It exploits the last round, defaults to cooperation when the audit\u2011adjusted gain is non\u2011positive, and otherwise pursues defection when it improves immediate or near\u2011future expected returns."

description_SELFINTERESTED_10 = "**Strategy\u202f\u201cDynamic Expected\u2011Return (DER)\u201d**\n\n---\n\n### 1. State variables (updated each round\u202ft)\n\n* `S` \u2013 current stock (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity)  \n* `t` \u2013 round index (0 \u2026 r\u20111)  \n* `p\u0302` \u2013 estimated probability that a random opponent cooperates, computed from the history of observed opponent\u2011cooperation counts.  \n* `\u03b8` \u2013 stock\u2011preservation threshold, defined as  \n\n\\[\n\\theta = \\frac{F\\;q}{\\frac{1}{2n}-\\frac{1}{n}} = \\frac{2Fq}{1}\n\\]\n\n(so the threshold in stock units is `\u03b8\u00b7capacity`).  \n\n* `U_C(t,S)` \u2013 expected cumulative payoff from now to the final round if we **cooperate** this round and then follow the same rule thereafter.  \n* `U_D(t,S)` \u2013 analogous value if we **defect** this round.\n\nAll expectations are taken over audit outcomes (`q`) and over opponent actions according to `p\u0302`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Immediate\u2011payoff calculations (rounded to exact formulae)\n\n*If we cooperate:*  \n\n\\[\n\\pi_C = \\frac{S}{2n}\n\\]\n\n*If we defect:*  \n\n\\[\n\\pi_D = \\frac{S}{n} - q\\,F\n\\]\n\n(The audit fine is subtracted in expectation; the realized fine is irrelevant for the decision because its expectation is linear.)\n\n---\n\n### 3. Stock\u2011transition forecasts (expected)\n\nLet `k` be the number of opponents (n\u20111).  \nExpected opponent consumption per opponent:\n\n\\[\nE[\\text{consumption}_{opp}] = p\u0302\\;\\frac{S}{2n} + (1-p\u0302)\\;\\frac{S}{n}\n\\]\n\n*Expected total opponent consumption*  \n\n\\[\nC_{opp}=k\\;E[\\text{consumption}_{opp}]\n\\]\n\n*If we cooperate:*  \n\n\\[\nC_{self}= \\frac{S}{2n}\n\\]\n\n*If we defect:*  \n\n\\[\nC_{self}= \\frac{S}{n}\n\\]\n\n*Expected remaining stock after consumption*  \n\n\\[\nS' = S - (C_{opp}+C_{self})\n\\]\n\n*Growth function* (deterministic once `S'` is known):\n\n\\[\nG(S') = 2\\,S'\\,\\bigl(1-\\frac{S'}{\\text{capacity}}\\bigr)\n\\]\n\n*Expected stock for next round*  \n\n\\[\nS_{next}= \\min\\bigl(S' + G(S'),\\; \\text{capacity}\\bigr)\n\\]\n\nAll quantities above are computed separately for the cooperate\u2011branch and the defect\u2011branch, yielding `S_next^C` and `S_next^D`.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Recursive expected\u2011return values\n\nFor the **last round** (`t = r\u20111`) there is no future, so:\n\n\\[\nU_C(r-1,S)=\\pi_C,\\qquad\nU_D(r-1,S)=\\pi_D\n\\]\n\nFor any earlier round (`t < r\u20111`):\n\n\\[\nU_C(t,S)= \\pi_C + U_{\\text{best}}(t+1, S_{next}^C)\n\\]\n\n\\[\nU_D(t,S)= \\pi_D + U_{\\text{best}}(t+1, S_{next}^D)\n\\]\n\nwhere  \n\n\\[\nU_{\\text{best}}(t+1, X)=\\max\\bigl(U_C(t+1,X),\\,U_D(t+1,X)\\bigr)\n\\]\n\nThe recursion terminates at `t = r\u20111`. Because `r` is bounded (\u2264\u202f1000 in typical settings), the recursion can be evaluated on\u2011the\u2011fly each round by memoising the two values for the current `S` and future horizon `h = r\u2011t`.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Decision rule (core of DER)\n\nAt round `t` with current stock `S`:\n\n1. **Compute** `p\u0302` as the frequency of cooperating opponents observed so far:  \n\n   \\[\n   p\u0302 = \\frac{\\sum_{\u03c4=0}^{t-1} \\text{#Cooperators among opponents at \u03c4}}{(n-1)\\,t}\n   \\]  \n\n   If `t = 0`, set `p\u0302 = 0.5` (uninformed prior).\n\n2. **Compute** the immediate payoffs `\u03c0_C`, `\u03c0_D` using the formulas in \u00a72.\n\n3. **Forecast** `S_next^C` and `S_next^D` using the expectations in \u00a73.\n\n4. **Evaluate** `U_C(t,S)` and `U_D(t,S)` via the recursion in \u00a74 (memoisation ensures O(r) total work over the whole game).\n\n5. **Choose**  \n\n   * **Cooperate** if `U_C(t,S) \u2265 U_D(t,S)`  \n   * **Defect** otherwise.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Edge\u2011case handling\n\n| Situation | Action |\n|-----------|--------|\n| **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0)** | Use prior `p\u0302\u202f=\u202f0.5`. Compute as above; the recursion still looks ahead through all `r` rounds. |\n| **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111)** | Skip stock\u2011forecast; directly compare `\u03c0_C` vs. `\u03c0_D`. No audit fine is applied because audits never occur in the final round (the expected fine term `q\u202fF` is set to\u202f0 for this round). |\n| **Stock depleted (`S = 0`)** | Both `\u03c0_C` and `\u03c0_D` are zero; future stock will stay zero. The recursion returns zero for all future rounds, so the rule will default to **Cooperate** (any action yields equal payoff). |\n| **Stock extremely low (`S < \u03b8\u00b7capacity`)** | The forecast `S_next^D` will often fall to zero, making `U_D` small; the recursion will automatically favor cooperation, preserving stock. No extra condition is required. |\n| **Audit probability zero (`q = 0`)** | The fine term disappears; the rule reduces to pure stock\u2011preservation versus immediate gain. |\n| **Audit probability one (`q = 1`)** | The fine term is fully applied; defecting becomes unattractive unless the stock is so abundant that `\u03c0_D - F` still exceeds `\u03c0_C`. The recursion captures this directly. |\n\n---\n\n### 7. Self\u2011interest justification (built\u2011in)\n\nThe algorithm **maximises the expected sum of our own monetary payoffs** (`\u03c0` minus expected fines) over the entire horizon, given only publicly observable information (stock and aggregate opponent cooperation). It never sacrifices current payoff for altruistic reasons; any cooperation is taken only when the *future* loss of stock would otherwise outweigh the immediate gain from defecting, i.e., when the *self\u2011interest* calculation `U_C \u2265 U_D` holds. No external norms or coordination signals are used."

description_SELFINTERESTED_11 = "**Strategy name:** Adaptive Expected\u2011Benefit Defector (AED)\n\n---\n\n### 1. Decision rule (per round *t*)\n\nLet  \n\n* `S` = current stock (after the growth step of the previous round)  \n* `R = r\u2011t` = number of rounds remaining including the current one  \n* `q` = audit probability, `F` = fine amount (both read from the game description)  \n* `n` = number of players (including yourself)  \n* `p\u0302` = estimated probability that an opponent cooperates in this round  \n\n`p\u0302` is obtained from the observed frequencies of opponent cooperation in past rounds:  \n\n```\nif t == 0:          // first round\n    p\u0302 = 0.5         // neutral prior\nelse:\n    p\u0302 = (\u03b1 * p\u0302_previous + (1\u2011\u03b1) * (num_cooperators_last_round / (n\u20111)))\n    // \u03b1 = 0.7 gives more weight to the most recent observation\n```\n\n#### 1.1 Immediate expected payoff\n* Cooperate:  `E_C = S/(2n)`\n* Defect:     `E_D = S/n - q*F`   (audit fine is independent of others)\n\n#### 1.2 Expected stock impact\nIf you cooperate, your consumption is `c_C = S/(2n)`.  \nIf you defect, your consumption is `c_D = S/n`.  \n\nAssuming the opponents follow the same `p\u0302`, the expected total consumption this round is  \n\n```\nE_consumption = (n\u20111) * [ p\u0302 * (S/(2n)) + (1\u2011p\u0302) * (S/n) ] + your_consumption\n```\n\nwhere `your_consumption` is `c_C` if you cooperate, `c_D` if you defect.\n\nThe expected remaining stock after consumption is  \n\n```\nS_rem = S - E_consumption\n```\n\nThe growth rule yields expected stock for the next round  \n\n```\nS_next = min( S_rem + 2 * S_rem * (1 - S_rem/capacity), capacity )\n```\n\n#### 1.3 Future\u2011value penalty\nDefine the per\u2011unit\u2011stock marginal value as the payoff a typical player would earn if the stock were `S_next` and everyone cooperated:\n\n```\nV_per_stock = (S_next / (2n)) / S_next   // simplifies to 1/(2n)\n```\n\nThe expected loss of future payoff caused by your higher consumption is therefore\n\n```\n\u0394V = R * V_per_stock * (c_D - c_C)   // R includes the current round\n```\n\n#### 1.4 Net decision metric\n```\n\u0394 = (E_D - E_C) - \u0394V\n```\n\n*If* `\u0394 > 0` \u2192 **Defect**;  \n*Otherwise* \u2192 **Cooperate**.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Edge\u2011case handling\n\n| Situation | Action |\n|----------|--------|\n| **First round (t = 0)** | Use the decision metric with `p\u0302 = 0.5`. |\n| **Last round (t = r\u20111)** | No audit occurs; future\u2011value term is zero (`R = 1`). Compute `\u0394 = (S/n) \u2013 (S/(2n))`. Since `\u0394 > 0`, **always defect**. |\n| **Stock at or below 0** | No resource left; any action yields zero payoff. Choose **Cooperate** (no consumption, avoids unnecessary depletion). |\n| **Stock equal to capacity and growth would overflow** | The growth rule caps at capacity; the future\u2011value penalty still applies. Follow the standard metric. |\n| **Audit probability `q = 0`** | The fine term disappears; the metric reduces to comparing immediate payoff vs. future\u2011value loss. Follow the same rule. |\n| **Fine `F = 0`** | Same as above; only future\u2011value penalty matters. |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Self\u2011interest justification (implicit in the rule)\n\nThe metric `\u0394` directly compares the *expected* monetary gain from defecting (including the expected fine) against the *expected* loss of future earnings caused by the extra depletion you create. The rule maximizes the sum of immediate and discounted future payoffs for yourself, given only observable information and the known game parameters. No external norms or altruistic considerations influence the decision."

description_SELFINTERESTED_12 = "**Strategy: Expected\u2011Utility\u2011Defection (EUD)**  \n\n**Parameters available to the agent**  \n- `n, r, capacity, q, F` (from the game description)  \n- `t` \u2013 current round index (0\u202f\u2026\u202fr\u20111)  \n- `S` \u2013 current stock level (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity)  \n- `opp_coop_last` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (unknown in round\u202f0)  \n\n**Internal state**  \n- `p\u0302` \u2013 estimated probability that a random opponent cooperates in the current round.  \n  *Initialize*: `p\u0302 = 0.5` (no information).  \n  *Update after each round*: if `t>0`, `p\u0302 = opp_coop_last / (n\u20111)`.\n\n---\n\n### Decision rule (run each round)\n\n```\nfunction decide(t, S, p\u0302):\n    # 1. Last round: no audit \u2192 maximize immediate payoff\n    if t == r-1:\n        return D\n\n    # 2. Zero stock: any action yields 0, cooperate to avoid extra depletion\n    if S <= 0:\n        return C\n\n    # 3. Immediate expected payoffs\n    coop_now   = S / (2*n)                     # payoff if we cooperate\n    defect_now = S / n - q * F                  # expected payoff if we defect\n\n    # 4. Expected total consumption this round under each self\u2011action\n    #    \u2013 our consumption\n    cons_self_C = S / (2*n)\n    cons_self_D = S / n\n\n    #    \u2013 expected opponent consumption (each opponent i uses C with prob p\u0302)\n    cons_opp_C = (S / (2*n)) * p\u0302\n    cons_opp_D = (S / n)       * (1 - p\u0302)\n    cons_opp_expected = (n-1) * (cons_opp_C + cons_opp_D)\n\n    #    \u2013 total consumption for each of our two choices\n    total_C = cons_self_C + cons_opp_expected\n    total_D = cons_self_D + cons_opp_expected\n\n    # 5. Stock after consumption and growth for each choice\n    function next_stock(S, total):\n        S_rem = max(0, S - total)\n        growth = 2 * S_rem * (1 - S_rem / capacity)\n        return min(S_rem + growth, capacity)\n\n    S_next_C = next_stock(S, total_C)\n    S_next_D = next_stock(S, total_D)\n\n    # 6. Expected future payoff per remaining round (approximate as linear in stock)\n    #    Assume future opponents keep the same cooperation estimate p\u0302.\n    #    Expected per\u2011round payoff for a player = average of C and D payoffs weighted by p\u0302:\n    exp_pay_per_round = lambda stock: (p\u0302 * stock/(2*n) + (1-p\u0302) * (stock/n - q*F))\n\n    future_rounds = r - t - 1\n    future_C = future_rounds * exp_pay_per_round(S_next_C)\n    future_D = future_rounds * exp_pay_per_round(S_next_D)\n\n    # 7. Total expected value of each action\n    value_C = coop_now + future_C\n    value_D = defect_now + future_D\n\n    # 8. Choose the action with higher total expected value\n    if value_D > value_C:\n        return D\n    else:\n        return C\n```\n\n### Edge\u2011case handling  \n\n| Situation                              | Action taken |\n|----------------------------------------|--------------|\n| **Round\u202f0** \u2013 no history               | Use `p\u0302 = 0.5` (neutral prior) and apply the decision rule. |\n| **Round\u202fr\u20111 (last round)**            | Always `D` (no audit, no future consequences). |\n| **Stock\u202fS = 0**                        | Return `C` (any action yields 0; cooperating avoids unnecessary depletion). |\n| **Audit probability `q = 0`**          | The rule reduces to pure payoff comparison; `D` is chosen unless future stock loss outweighs immediate gain. |\n| **Fine `F = 0`**                       | Same as above; `D` dominates unless stock preservation is critical for later rounds. |\n| **Observed opponent cooperation = 0**  | `p\u0302` updates to 0, making future\u2010payoff term lower; the algorithm may switch to cooperation to sustain stock if `S` is low. |\n| **Observed opponent cooperation = n\u20111**| `p\u0302` updates to 1, increasing future payoff for defection; the algorithm may continue defecting. |\n\n### Self\u2011interest justification (implicit in the rule)\n\n- Immediate payoff is adjusted for the *expected* audit cost (`q\u202f\u00d7\u202fF`).  \n- Future stock dynamics are explicitly projected; the agent only cooperates when the projected loss of future payoff (through stock depletion) exceeds the immediate gain from defecting.  \n- No coordination or norm\u2011seeking is used; decisions depend solely on observed opponent behavior, parameters, and the agent\u2019s own payoff maximization."

description_SELFINTERESTED_13 = "**Self\u2011interested Adaptive Strategy (SA\u2011AI)**  \n\n---\n\n### 1. Internal state  \n* `p` \u2013 estimated probability that a random opponent cooperates.  \n\u202f\u202fInitialize `p \u2190 0.5`. After each round update with the observed number of cooperating opponents `k_obs` (out of `n\u20111` opponents) using a Laplace\u2011smoothed average:  \n\n```\ntotal_obs   \u2190 total_obs   + (n\u20111)\ntotal_coop  \u2190 total_coop  + k_obs\np \u2190 (total_coop + 1) / (total_obs + 2)       // prevents p = 0 or 1\n```\n\n* `t` \u2013 current round index (0\u2011based).  \n* `S` \u2013 current stock level (known at the start of the round).  \n\n---\n\n### 2. Decision rule (run each round before actions are taken)\n\n```\nremain   \u2190 r \u2013 t                     // number of rounds left including current\nif S = 0 then                     // stock exhausted\n    action \u2190 C                     // cooperate gives 0, defect would incur expected fine\nelse\n    // ---------- immediate expected payoffs ----------\n    U_C  \u2190 S / (2*n)                                   // no fine when cooperating\n    U_D  \u2190 S / n  \u2013  q * F                              // expected fine on defect\n\n    // ---------- expected stock after this round ----------\n    // expected consumption of a single opponent\n    opp_cons_C  \u2190 p * (S / (2*n)) + (1\u2011p) * (S / n)\n\n    // total expected consumption of opponents\n    opp_total   \u2190 (n\u20111) * opp_cons_C\n\n    // if we cooperate\n    cons_self_C \u2190 S / (2*n)\n    S_next_C    \u2190 stock_update( S , opp_total + cons_self_C )\n\n    // if we defect\n    cons_self_D \u2190 S / n\n    S_next_D    \u2190 stock_update( S , opp_total + cons_self_D )\n\n    // ---------- continuation value (one\u2011step look\u2011ahead) ----------\n    // assume that after this round we will follow the same rule,\n    // so we approximate the per\u2011round payoff by the expected immediate payoff\n    // computed with the same p and the respective next\u2011stock.\n    // (more rounds \u2192 multiply by remain\u20111)\n\n    // expected immediate payoff next round if we had cooperated now\n    U_C_next  \u2190 S_next_C / (2*n)                     // expected immediate coop payoff\n    U_D_next  \u2190 S_next_C / n  \u2013  q * F                // expected immediate defect payoff\n    // we approximate that future opponents will behave according to p,\n    // thus expected per\u2011round payoff \u2248 p\u00b7U_C_next + (1\u2011p)\u00b7U_D_next\n    V_C  \u2190 (remain\u20111) * ( p*U_C_next + (1\u2011p)*U_D_next )\n\n    // same for the defect branch\n    U_C_next2 \u2190 S_next_D / (2*n)\n    U_D_next2 \u2190 S_next_D / n  \u2013  q * F\n    V_D  \u2190 (remain\u20111) * ( p*U_C_next2 + (1\u2011p)*U_D_next2 )\n\n    // ---------- choose action ----------\n    if (U_C + V_C) \u2265 (U_D + V_D) then\n        action \u2190 C\n    else\n        action \u2190 D\n    end\nend\n```\n\n**Helper: stock dynamics**\n\n```\nfunction stock_update(S_current , total_consumption):\n    S_rem   \u2190 max(0 , S_current \u2013 total_consumption)\n    growth  \u2190 2 * S_rem * (1 \u2013 S_rem / capacity)\n    S_new   \u2190 min( S_rem + growth , capacity )\n    return S_new\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Edge\u2011case handling  \n\n| Situation                              | Action taken by SA\u2011AI                                               |\n|----------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Round 0 (first round)**               | Use the rule above with the prior `p = 0.5`.                         |\n| **Last round (`t = r\u20111`)**             | No continuation value (`remain\u20111 = 0`). Choose the action with larger **U** (`U_C` vs `U_D`). |\n| **Stock zero (`S = 0`)**                | Choose **C** (payoff 0, avoids the expected fine from defecting).   |\n| **Audit probability `q = 0`**          | Fine term disappears; the rule automatically collapses to the pure payoff comparison. |\n| **Fine `F = 0`**                       | Same as above; defect is chosen whenever immediate payoff exceeds cooperation. |\n| **Observed all opponents defect (`p` \u2192 0)** | The continuation value for cooperating rapidly falls; the rule will select **D**. |\n| **Observed all opponents cooperate (`p` \u2192 1)** | The continuation value for cooperating stays high; the rule will select **C** unless the stock is so large that immediate defect payoff (minus expected fine) dominates. |\n\n---\n\n### 4. Rationale (self\u2011interest only)  \n\nThe algorithm evaluates **total expected utility** = immediate payoff\u202f+\u202fdiscounted (one\u2011step) continuation value, assuming opponents keep the currently estimated cooperation probability. It selects the action that maximizes this expectation, never sacrificing current or future gain for external considerations. The rule updates `p` solely from observed opponent frequencies, guaranteeing adaptability to any opponent behavior pattern while remaining completely self\u2011centric."

description_SELFINTERESTED_14 = "**Strategy: \u201cDynamic Expected\u2011Return Trigger (DERT)\u201d**\n\n**Parameters (read from the game description)**\n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `audit_prob`\u202f`=\u202fq`, `fine`\u202f`=\u202fF`.\n\n**State variables (maintained locally)**\n- `stock_t`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003current stock at start of round\u202f`t`.\n- `opp_coop_last`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003number of opponents who cooperated in previous round (unknown for round\u202f0, set to `n\u20111`).\n- `round`\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003current round index (`0 \u2026 r\u20111`).\n\n**Utility functions**\n\n```\npay_C(S) = S/(2n)                      # payoff if you cooperate\npay_D(S) = S/n - q*F                   # expected payoff if you defect (audit fine expected)\ndelta_stock(S, c, d) =               # stock change after a round\n    S_rem = S - (c*pay_C(S) + d*pay_D(S))      # remaining after consumption\n    growth = 2 * S_rem * (1 - S_rem/capacity)\n    min(S_rem + growth, capacity)\n```\n\n**Decision rule (applied each round t)**\n\n1. **Last round (`t == r\u20111`)**  \n   - Play **Defect** (no audit, no future rounds).\n\n2. **First round (`t == 0`)**  \n   - Play **Cooperate** to seed cooperation and obtain the baseline payoff; record `opp_coop_last = n\u20111`.\n\n3. **Intermediate rounds (`0 < t < r\u20111`)**  \n\n   a. **Estimate opponent behavior**  \n      - Let `c_est = opp_coop_last / (n\u20111)` be the observed cooperation frequency of opponents in the previous round.  \n      - Assume the same fraction will repeat this round.\n\n   b. **Compute expected immediate payoff** for each of your two pure actions given `stock_t` and `c_est`:\n\n      ```\n      exp_pay_C = pay_C(stock_t)\n\n      # expected number of defectors among opponents = (1 - c_est)*(n-1)\n      exp_total_consumption_if_C = pay_C(stock_t) + (1 - c_est)*(n-1)*pay_D(stock_t)\n      stock_if_C = delta_stock(stock_t, 1, (n-1)*(1 - c_est))\n\n      exp_pay_D = pay_D(stock_t)\n      exp_total_consumption_if_D = pay_D(stock_t) + (1 - c_est)*(n-1)*pay_D(stock_t)\n      stock_if_D = delta_stock(stock_t, 0, (n-1)*(1 - c_est))\n      ```\n\n   c. **Project one\u2011step\u2011ahead continuation value** (future payoff in next round) using the stock forecasts:\n\n      ```\n      cont_if_C = (stock_if_C/(2n))   # you would cooperate next round if you follow the same rule\n      cont_if_D = (stock_if_D/n - q*F)   # you would defect next round (same rule)\n      ```\n\n      (If `stock_if_X` falls below a negligible threshold, set continuation value to\u202f0.)\n\n   d. **Total expected return** for each action:\n\n      ```\n      tot_C = exp_pay_C + cont_if_C\n      tot_D = exp_pay_D + cont_if_D\n      ```\n\n   e. **Action selection**  \n      - If `tot_C >= tot_D` **and** `stock_t > 0.1*capacity` \u2192 **Cooperate**.  \n      - Otherwise \u2192 **Defect**.\n\n4. **Update after round**  \n   - Observe `coop_opp` = number of opponents that cooperated this round.  \n   - Set `opp_coop_last = coop_opp`.  \n   - Update `stock_t` to the new stock supplied by the environment for the next round (the game engine will provide it).\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- If `pay_D(stock_t) < 0` (fine exceeds defect payoff) force **Cooperate**.\n- If `stock_t` \u2264 `0` (pool exhausted) any action yields `0`; play **Defect** to avoid unnecessary audit risk.\n- If `q == 0` (no audit) the rule reduces to a pure one\u2011step profit comparison: defect whenever `pay_D > pay_C`.\n\n**Self\u2011interest justification (implicit in rule)**\n- The algorithm maximizes the expected sum of current payoff plus the discounted (one\u2011step) continuation value, accounting for audit risk and the impact of current consumption on future stock. It defects whenever the expected gain from higher immediate extraction outweighs the loss of future stock value, and cooperates otherwise, ensuring the agent always chooses the action with the higher personal expected return."

description_SELFINTERESTED_15 = "**Self\u2011Interested Adaptive Strategy (SI\u2011Adapt)**  \n\n**Parameters (known to the agent)**  \n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `q` (audit prob.), `F` (fine)  \n- Discount factor for future rounds: `\u03b4 = 1` (no explicit discount, but future payoff is weighted by the number of remaining rounds)  \n\n**State variables kept by the agent**  \n- `S_t` \u2013 current stock (observed at the start of round *t*)  \n- `cntC_{t-1}` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (0\u202f\u2026\u202f*n\u20111*)  \n- `my_last` \u2013 my own action in round *t\u20111* (`C` or `D`)  \n\n**Auxiliary calculations (performed at the start of each round *t*)**  \n\n1. **Immediate expected payoff** for cooperating vs defecting (including expected fine):  \n\n```\npay_C   = S_t / (2*n)\npay_D   = S_t / n - q * F          # expected fine only applies to D\n```\n\n2. **Projected stock if I defect** (assuming opponents repeat their last\u2011observed mix):  \n\n```\npC      = cntC_{t-1} / (n-1)        # observed cooperation probability of opponents\ncons_self_C = S_t / (2*n)\ncons_self_D = S_t / n\ncons_opp  = (n-1) * ( pC * S_t/(2*n) + (1-pC) * S_t/n )\nstock_if_C = S_t - (cons_self_C + cons_opp)\nstock_if_D = S_t - (cons_self_D + cons_opp)\ngrow(stock) = min( stock + 2*stock*(1 - stock/capacity) , capacity )\nS_next_C = grow(stock_if_C)\nS_next_D = grow(stock_if_D)\n```\n\n3. **Future\u2011value estimate** (value of the remaining `R = r - t - 1` rounds if the stock were `S_next` and all opponents kept the same mix):  \n\n```\nfuture_val(S) = R * ( S / (2*n) )                # assume I will cooperate thereafter to keep stock stable\n```\n\n4. **Total expected value** for each current action:  \n\n```\ntotal_C = pay_C + future_val(S_next_C)\ntotal_D = pay_D + future_val(S_next_D)\n```\n\n**Decision rule (applied at the start of each round *t*)**  \n\n- **Last round (`t = r\u20111`)**: never audited, so choose the higher immediate payoff.  \n\n```\nif pay_D >= pay_C: action = D else action = C\n```\n\n- **All other rounds (`0 \u2264 t < r\u20111`)**: compare `total_D` and `total_C`.  \n\n```\nif total_D > total_C: action = D\nelse:                action = C\n```\n\n- **First round (`t = 0`)**: no history, set `cntC_{\u20111}=n\u20111` (assume all opponents will cooperate) \u2192 the calculations above reduce to a myopic comparison of `pay_D` vs `pay_C`.  \n\n```\nif pay_D > pay_C: action = D else action = C\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**  \n\n- **Zero stock (`S_t \u2264 0`)**: any consumption yields 0 payoff; choose `C` (lower consumption) to avoid waste (no effect on stock).  \n- **Stock at capacity (`S_t = capacity`)**: use the regular rule; the growth function will clamp at capacity, so over\u2011exploitation will be penalised by future stock loss.  \n- **Audit observation**: after each round record whether I was audited (`a_i,t`) and the fine paid; this does not affect the decision rule (the expected fine already incorporated `q`).  \n\n**Summary of algorithm per round `t`**\n\n```\nobserve S_t, cntC_{t-1}\nif S_t <= 0: action = C\nelse if t == r-1:\n    compute pay_C, pay_D\n    action = D if pay_D >= pay_C else C\nelse:\n    compute pay_C, pay_D\n    compute pC = cntC_{t-1}/(n-1)\n    compute cons_self_C, cons_self_D, cons_opp\n    compute S_next_C, S_next_D via growth()\n    R = r - t - 1\n    total_C = pay_C + R * (S_next_C/(2*n))\n    total_D = pay_D + R * (S_next_D/(2*n))\n    action = D if total_D > total_C else C\nexecute action, observe audit outcome, update my_last and cntC_t for next round\n```\n\nThe agent always selects the action that maximizes its own expected cumulative payoff given the current stock, the observed cooperation level of opponents, and the audit risk, while implicitly preserving enough stock to sustain future earnings when that is profitable."

description_SELFINTERESTED_16 = "**Strategy Overview**\n\nAt each round *t* the agent computes the expected immediate payoff of cooperating versus defecting, adjusts for the audit risk, and adds a forward\u2011looking term that values future stock when the pool is scarce. The decision rule is:\n\n1. **Immediate\u2011payoff comparison**  \n   - *Cooperate payoff*:\u2003\\(U_C = S_t/(2n)\\)  \n   - *Defect payoff*:\u2003\u2003\\(U_D = S_t/n - q\u00b7F\\) (expected fine,\u202f*q*\u202f= audit probability,\u202f*F*\u202f= fine)  \n\n2. **Future\u2011stock valuation**  \n   - When the remaining stock after consumption would fall below a *critical level* \\(\u03b8\u00b7capacity\\) (\u03b8\u202f\u2208\u202f[0,1]), the agent adds a penalty\u202f\\(P = \u03bb\u00b7(\u03b8\u00b7capacity - S_{t+1})\\) to the defect payoff, where \u03bb\u202f>\u202f0 is a weighting factor reflecting the discounted value of future rounds (e.g., \u03bb\u202f=\u202f\\( \\frac{capacity}{r-t-1}\\)).  \n   - \\(S_{t+1}\\) is the projected stock after the agent\u2019s own action assuming the observed proportion of cooperators among opponents from the previous round, \\(p_{t-1}\\).  \n   - For cooperation the penalty is zero.\n\n3. **Decision rule**  \n   - If \\(U_C \\ge U_D - P\\)\u2003\u2192\u2003**Cooperate (C)**  \n   - Else\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2003\u2192\u2003**Defect (D)**  \n\n**Parameter estimation**\n\n- After each round the agent observes the number of opponents who cooperated, \\(k_{t}\\).  \n- Estimate opponent cooperation rate:\u2003\\(p_t = k_t/(n-1)\\).  \n- Use the most recent estimate \\(p_{t-1}\\) to predict total consumption in the next round:\n  \\[\n  C_{t}^{proj}=p_{t-1}\\cdot\\frac{S_t}{2} + (1-p_{t-1})\\cdot\\frac{S_t}{1}\n  \\]\n  (the factor \u00bd comes from each cooperator\u2019s share of the pool, the factor 1 from defectors).  \n- Projected remaining stock:\n  \\[\n  \\hat S_{t+1}= \\max\\Bigl(0,\\; S_t - C_{t}^{proj}\\Bigr)\n  \\]\n  then apply the growth rule once (growth =\u202f\\(2\u00b7\\hat S_{t+1}(1-\\hat S_{t+1}/capacity)\\)) and cap at *capacity*.\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n- **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0).** No prior observation, set \\(p_{-1}=0.5\\) (neutral guess). Apply the decision rule using the projected stock based on this guess.  \n- **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111).** No audit and no future rounds, so ignore the future\u2011stock penalty. Choose **Defect** because \\(U_D > U_C\\) for any positive stock.  \n- **Stock zero (S_t\u202f=\u202f0).** Cooperation yields zero payoff, defecting could incur a fine if audited, giving negative expected payoff. Hence **Cooperate**.  \n- **Audit probability q\u202f=\u202f0** or **fine F\u202f=\u202f0**: the penalty term reduces to the pure immediate comparison, effectively cooperating only when the stock\u2011preservation penalty outweighs the extra immediate gain from defecting.  \n- **Critical\u2011stock threshold**: \u03b8 is set to a modest safety margin (e.g., 0.3). If the projected stock after defecting would dip below this margin, the future\u2011stock penalty steers the agent toward cooperation even when the immediate defect payoff looks higher.\n\n**Pseudocode**\n\n```\ninput: n, r, capacity, q, F, \u03b8, \u03bb\nstate: S = capacity\nhistory: opponent_coops = []   // list of observed k_t each round\n\nfor t in 0 .. r-1:\n    // estimate opponent cooperation rate\n    if t == 0:\n        p = 0.5\n    else:\n        p = opponent_coops[-1] / (n-1)\n\n    // immediate payoffs\n    Uc = S / (2*n)\n    Ud = S / n - q*F\n\n    // project stock after own action\n    // assume own action = C for projection of cooperative case\n    cons_if_C = (p*(S/(2*n)) + (1-p)*(S/n)) * (n-1) + S/(2*n)\n    S_rem_C = max(0, S - cons_if_C)\n    S_next_C = min(S_rem_C + 2*S_rem_C*(1 - S_rem_C/capacity), capacity)\n\n    // projection if defecting\n    cons_if_D = (p*(S/(2*n)) + (1-p)*(S/n)) * (n-1) + S/n\n    S_rem_D = max(0, S - cons_if_D)\n    S_next_D = min(S_rem_D + 2*S_rem_D*(1 - S_rem_D/capacity), capacity)\n\n    // future\u2011stock penalty\n    P = 0\n    if t < r-1:\n        if S_next_D < \u03b8*capacity:\n            P = \u03bb * (\u03b8*capacity - S_next_D)\n\n    // choose action\n    if Uc >= Ud - P:\n        action = 'C'\n        payoff = Uc\n    else:\n        action = 'D'\n        payoff = Ud\n\n    // apply audit (except last round)\n    if t < r-1 and random() < q and action == 'D':\n        payoff -= F   // realized fine\n\n    // update stock exactly as the game specifies (use actual consumptions)\n    total_consumption = (action == 'C') ? S/(2*n) : S/n\n    total_consumption += sum of opponents' consumptions\n    S = max(0, S - total_consumption)\n    S = min(S + 2*S*(1 - S/capacity), capacity)\n\n    // record observed opponent cooperations for next round\n    k = number of opponents that played C this round\n    opponent_coops.append(k)\n```\n\nThe agent follows this rule each round, guaranteeing a self\u2011interested choice that exploits immediate gains when safe, backs off to cooperation when the stock is endangered, and respects audit risk without relying on any coordination assumption."

description_SELFISH_1 = "**Selfish Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**Notation (available to the agent each round\u202ft)**\n* `S_t` \u2013 current stock level (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS_t\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity)  \n* `n` \u2013 total number of players (including yourself)  \n* `q` \u2013 audit probability (0\u202f\u2264\u202fq\u202f\u2264\u202f1)  \n* `F` \u2013 fine for a audited defection  \n* `r` \u2013 total number of rounds, `t` \u2208 {0,\u2026,r\u20111}  \n* `c_{t\u20111}` \u2013 number of opponents observed cooperating in the *previous* round (if t\u202f=\u202f0, treat as \u201cunknown\u201d)  \n* `p_coop` \u2013 estimated probability that a given opponent will cooperate this round  \n* `V_k(S, d)` \u2013 estimated continuation value (sum of expected payoffs from round\u202fk\u202f+\u202f1 to r\u20111) assuming the stock after round\u202fk is `S` and you will *choose action* `d` (C or D) in round\u202fk.\n\n**Core decision rule (applied each round\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr\u20111)**\n1. **Estimate opponent cooperation probability**  \n   ```\n   if t == 0:\n       p_coop = 1.0          // optimistic start (you assume everyone cooperates)\n   else:\n       p_coop = c_{t\u20111} / (n\u20111)    // empirical frequency from last round\n   ```\n\n2. **Compute immediate expected payoff for each of your two possible actions**  \n\n   *Cooperate (C)*  \n   ```\n   payoff_C = S_t / (2*n)                     // no fine\n   ```\n\n   *Defect (D)*  \n   ```\n   expected_fine = q * F\n   payoff_D = S_t / n - expected_fine\n   ```\n\n3. **Project next\u2011round stock under each of your two actions**  \n\n   For a candidate action `a \u2208 {C, D}` let `own_cons` be the consumption you would take:\n   ```\n   own_cons = S_t / (2*n)  if a == C else S_t / n\n   ```\n\n   Expected consumption of a *single opponent*:\n   ```\n   opp_cons = p_coop * (S_t / (2*n)) + (1\u2011p_coop) * (S_t / n)\n   ```\n\n   Expected total consumption:\n   ```\n   total_cons_a = own_cons + (n\u20111) * opp_cons\n   ```\n\n   Stock after consumption:\n   ```\n   S_rem_a = max(0, S_t - total_cons_a)\n   ```\n\n   Growth (identical for both actions):\n   ```\n   growth = 2 * S_rem_a * (1 - S_rem_a / capacity)\n   S_next_a = min(S_rem_a + growth, capacity)\n   ```\n\n4. **Estimate continuation value** (recursive one\u2011step look\u2011ahead, assuming you will repeat this same decision rule in later rounds):\n   ```\n   V_a = V_{t+1}(S_next_a, ? )   // \u201c?\u201d means we will recompute the decision at t+1\n   ```\n   Because the exact future depends on future observations, we approximate `V_{t+1}` by the *myopic* expected payoff in round\u202ft+1 using the same `p_coop` (i.e., assume opponent behavior does not change):\n   ```\n   expected_payoff_next_a = \n        p_coop * (S_next_a / (2*n))               // opponent cooperation gives you C payoff next round\n      + (1\u2011p_coop) * (S_next_a / n - q*F)          // opponent defection gives you D payoff next round (with expected fine)\n   V_a \u2248 expected_payoff_next_a * (r\u2011t\u20111)          // assume this expected payoff repeats for all remaining rounds\n   ```\n\n5. **Select the action with higher total expected value**\n   ```\n   total_value_C = payoff_C + V_C\n   total_value_D = payoff_D + V_D\n   if total_value_D > total_value_C:\n       choose D\n   else:\n       choose C\n   ```\n\n**Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111)**\n* No audits, no future value, so simply pick the action with higher *certain* payoff:\n   ```\n   if S_t / n > S_t / (2*n):\n       choose D\n   else:\n       choose C\n   ```\n(When S_t\u202f=\u202f0 both actions yield 0; any choice is acceptable.)\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n* **Zero stock (`S_t`\u202f=\u202f0)** \u2013 both actions give payoff\u202f0; cooperate to conserve the (already depleted) pool (no impact on future value).\n* **Negative expected payoff after fine** \u2013 if `payoff_D` becomes negative, the algorithm will automatically prefer cooperation because `total_value_C \u2265 0`.\n* **Audit probability q\u202f=\u202f0** \u2013 the fine term drops out; the rule reduces to a pure payoff\u2011plus\u2011future\u2011stock comparison.\n* **Fine F extremely large** \u2013 `payoff_D` may be far below `payoff_C`; the strategy will almost always cooperate unless the projected stock gain from defecting outweighs the loss.\n\n**Behavioural summary**\n* Start optimistic, assuming others cooperate, which gives a high projected future stock and therefore a higher chance to cooperate early.\n* After each round, update the belief `p_coop` based on observed opponent cooperation frequency.\n* Defect only when the immediate gain (net of expected fine) plus the projected future advantage from a lower stock (which may boost growth) exceeds the value of cooperating.\n* In the final round, defect if and only if the immediate consumption advantage is positive (audits are irrelevant)."

description_SELFISH_2 = "**Selfish Adaptive Strategy (SA\u2011Defender)**  \n\n**Parameters known to the agent**  \n- n, r, capacity, audit probability q, fine F  \n- Discount factor\u202f=\u202f1 (total payoff is simple sum)  \n\n**State variables kept by the agent**  \n- `S_t` \u2013 current stock at the start of round *t* (observed)  \n- `c_{t\u20111}` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in the previous round (observed aggregate)  \n- `t` \u2013 current round index (0\u2011based)  \n\n**Derived constants**  \n- `Cpay(S) = S / (2\u202fn)` \u2013 payoff if cooperate in the current round  \n- `Dpay(S) = S / n` \u2013 gross payoff if defect (before any fine)  \n- `DpayNet(S) = Dpay(S) \u2013 q\u202f\u00b7\u202fF` \u2013 expected net payoff when defecting (the audit is independent of others)  \n- `S_min = capacity\u202f\u00b7\u202f\u03b8` \u2013 preservation threshold, with \u03b8 = 0.4 (tunable). When the stock falls below `S_min` the agent switches to \u201cstock\u2011saving mode\u201d.  \n\n**Decision rule (applied each round *t*)**\n\n```\nif t == r\u20111:                     # last round: no future, no audit\n    action = D                     # defect for maximal immediate payoff\nelse:\n    # 1. Immediate\u2011payoff comparison\n    if DpayNet(S_t) > Cpay(S_t):\n        immediate = D\n    else:\n        immediate = C\n\n    # 2. Stock\u2011saving check\n    if S_t < S_min:\n        # stock is low; preserving it yields higher future returns\n        # compute the stock that would remain after each possible action\n        S_after_C = S_t - n * Cpay(S_t)          # all players cooperate\n        S_after_D = S_t - (n\u2011c_{t\u20111})*Cpay(S_t) - c_{t\u20111}*Dpay(S_t)\n        # estimate next\u2011round stock (growth step omitted for brevity, but can be added)\n        # if cooperating keeps stock above the threshold next round, choose C\n        if S_after_C >= S_min:\n            action = C\n        else:\n            action = D\n    else:\n        # 3. Reputation\u2011based conditional cooperation\n        # use the observed cooperation level of the opponents in the previous round\n        coop_rate = c_{t\u20111} / (n\u20111)                # proportion of opponents that cooperated\n        # cooperate only if enough opponents cooperated last round\n        if coop_rate >= 0.6:                       # 60\u202f% cooperation trigger\n            # but still respect immediate\u2011payoff test\n            action = immediate if immediate == C else C\n        else:\n            action = D\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n- **Round\u202f0**: `c_{\u20111}` is undefined; treat `coop_rate = 0`. The rule therefore falls back to the immediate\u2011payoff comparison combined with the stock\u2011saving check.  \n- **Round\u202fr\u20111** (last round): audit probability is zero and there are no future rounds, so always defect.  \n- **Zero stock (`S_t = 0`)**: both payoff formulas give 0; the algorithm will default to defect (no gain either way, and defect avoids any potential future penalty).  \n\n**Summary of the selfish logic**\n\n1. Defect when the expected net payoff this round exceeds the cooperative payoff, unless the stock is dangerously low.  \n2. When the stock is low (`S_t < capacity\u00b7\u03b8`), cooperate if it will keep the stock above the threshold for the next round; otherwise defect.  \n3. When the stock is healthy, cooperate only if a sufficient fraction of opponents cooperated in the previous round, exploiting their \u201cgoodwill\u201d while still preferring defect if the immediate net gain is larger.  \n\nThe policy uses only publicly observable quantities (current stock, aggregate opponent cooperation count) and the fixed game parameters, making it fully self\u2011contained, adaptive, and oriented toward maximizing the agent\u2019s own cumulative payoff."

description_SELFISH_3 = "**Selfish Adaptive Defection\u2011Cooperation Rule**\n\nLet  \n\n- `t` = current round index (0\u2011based)  \n- `R = r\u2011t\u20111` = number of rounds remaining after the current one  \n- `S` = current common\u2011pool stock (observed at the start of the round)  \n- `q` = audit probability, `F` = fine amount (both known from the game description)  \n- `n` = number of players (known)  \n\nDefine the *immediate net gain* of defecting instead of cooperating  \n\n```\nG = (S / n)                # payoff if you defect, before fine\n    - q * F                # expected fine\n    - (S / (2 n))          # payoff if you cooperate\n  = S/(2n) - q\u00b7F\n```\n\nDefine the *extra consumption* caused by defecting  \n\n```\n\u0394 = S/(2n)          # amount of stock you take away compared to cooperating\n```\n\nEstimate the *future loss* you will suffer from the lower stock for the remaining rounds.  \nAssume the worst\u2011case that every future round you would obtain at most the per\u2011unit\u2011stock payoff of a defector (`1/n`). Then\n\n```\nfuture_loss_est = \u0394 * R / n = (S * R) / (2 n^2)\n```\n\n**Decision rule (applied each round):**\n\n```\nif S == 0:\n    action = C            # consuming nothing yields the same payoff\nelif G <= 0:\n    action = C            # defecting is not worth the expected fine\nelse:\n    if G > future_loss_est:\n        action = D        # immediate advantage outweighs estimated future loss\n    else:\n        action = C        # preserve stock for later rounds\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n- **Round\u202f0 (first round):** `R = r\u20111`; the rule above automatically uses the full horizon.\n- **Last round (`t = r\u20111`, `R = 0`):** `future_loss_est = 0`; you defect iff `G > 0` (i.e., `S/(2n) > q\u00b7F`). No future penalty to consider.\n- **Audit\u2011free environment (`q = 0`):** `G = S/(2n)`; you defect whenever the estimated future loss is smaller than this immediate gain, which tends to happen when stock is high or few rounds remain.\n- **Zero fine (`F = 0`):** same as audit\u2011free; defect as long as `S/(2n) > future_loss_est`.\n- **High fine (`q\u00b7F \u2265 S/(2n)`):** `G \u2264 0`, you always cooperate regardless of stock.\n\n**Selfishness justification (implicit in the rule)**  \n\nThe rule always chooses the action that maximizes the sum of **(i)** the expected immediate monetary payoff (including audit risk) and **(ii)** the estimated future payoff loss caused by reducing the stock. No effort is made to reward or punish other players; the decision depends only on your own payoff projection."

description_SELFISH_4 = "**Selfish Adaptive Strategy \u2013 \u201cExpected\u2011Gain Threshold\u201d**\n\n**Parameters used each round t (0\u2011indexed)**  \n- `S` = current stock (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity)  \n- `q` = audit probability (game_description.audit_prob)  \n- `F` = fine (game_description.fine)  \n- `n` = number of players  \n- `r` = total rounds  \n- `c_t` = number of opponents observed cooperating in round\u202ft (0\u202f\u2264\u202fc_t\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111)  \n- `history` = list of own past actions, payoffs and audit outcomes  \n\n**Core idea**  \nCompare the *expected* net gain from defecting versus cooperating, taking the audit risk into account. Defect only when the expected gain exceeds a dynamically\u2011adjusted safety margin that protects future payoff potential (stock preservation). The margin rises when the remaining horizon is long and when the stock is already low.\n\n---\n\n### Decision rule (pseudocode)\n\n```python\ndef decide(t, S, c_t, history):\n    # 1. Baseline payoffs for this stock\n    payoff_C = S / (2 * n)                     # guaranteed if cooperate\n    payoff_D_no_fine = S / n                    # raw gain before fine\n    expected_fine = q * F                       # unconditional expectation each round\n    expected_gain_D = payoff_D_no_fine - expected_fine\n\n    # 2. Future\u2011value adjustment\n    rounds_left = r - t                        # includes current round\n    #   a) Stock\u2011preservation weight: higher when stock is scarce\n    stock_factor = 1 - (S / capacity)           # 0 when full, 1 when empty\n    #   b) Horizon weight: more weight on preservation early in the game\n    horizon_factor = rounds_left / r\n\n    #   c) Dynamic safety margin (the amount we are willing to sacrifice now\n    #      to keep stock for later rounds)\n    safety_margin = (payoff_D_no_fine - payoff_C) * (stock_factor * horizon_factor)\n\n    # 3. Decision\n    if expected_gain_D > payoff_C + safety_margin:\n        return 'D'      # defect\n    else:\n        return 'C'      # cooperate\n```\n\n**Explanation of components (no commentary required, only rule usage)**  \n\n- `payoff_C` and `payoff_D_no_fine` are the deterministic consumptions for the current stock.  \n- `expected_fine` incorporates the known audit probability `q` and fine `F`.  \n- `expected_gain_D` is the *expected* net payoff if we defect this round.  \n- `safety_margin` inflates the cooperative threshold when (i) the stock is low (`stock_factor` near\u202f1) and (ii) many rounds remain (`horizon_factor` near\u202f1). This ensures we do not over\u2011exploit a dwindling pool early in the game.  \n\n### Edge\u2011case handling  \n\n| Situation | Action |\n|-----------|--------|\n| **Round\u202f0 (first round)** \u2013 no history available | Apply the rule directly; `history` is empty, so only stock\u2011, audit\u2011 and horizon\u2011based terms matter. |\n| **Round\u202fr\u20111 (last round)** \u2013 never audited | Set `expected_fine = 0` for this round (override). Apply the same `safety_margin` formula; since `rounds_left = 1`, `horizon_factor = 1/r`, the margin becomes very small, encouraging defect if it yields higher net payoff. |\n| **Stock\u202f=\u202f0** | Both actions yield 0 payoff; return `'C'` (does not matter, but preserves the minimal safety margin). |\n| **All opponents cooperated in the previous round** (`c_{t\u20111} = n\u20111`) | No explicit change; the rule already accounts for the current stock, which will be higher after a cooperative round, thus making defect more attractive if the margin is low. |\n| **Audited and fined in the previous round** | Record the fine in `history` (does not affect the rule directly, but it influences the stock via reduced consumption only). The rule remains unchanged because expected fine already accounts for audit probability. |\n| **Remaining rounds \u2264\u202f2** | `horizon_factor` becomes \u2264\u202f2/r, dramatically shrinking the safety margin; the strategy will almost always defect when `expected_gain_D` exceeds `payoff_C`. |\n| **Capacity reached (S = capacity)** | `stock_factor = 0`, so `safety_margin = 0`; the rule reduces to \u201cdefect if expected net gain exceeds cooperative payoff\u201d. |\n\n### Summary of execution each round  \n\n1. Observe current stock `S` and opponent cooperation count `c_t`.  \n2. Compute deterministic payoffs, expected fine, and expected net gain for defecting.  \n3. Evaluate the dynamic safety margin based on current stock scarcity and remaining horizon.  \n4. Choose `'D'` if the expected net gain surpasses cooperative payoff plus the margin; otherwise choose `'C'`.  \n\nThe strategy is fully deterministic given the observable state and parameters, requires no communication, and adapts automatically to varying opponent behaviors, audit risk, and stock dynamics while always seeking to maximize the player\u2019s own cumulative payoff."

description_SELFISH_5 = "**Selfish Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**State variables**  \n- `t` : current round index (0 \u2026 r\u20111)  \n- `S` : current stock level (observed at start of round)  \n- `k` : number of opponents observed cooperating in the previous round (if t>0)  \n- `q` : audit probability (given)  \n- `F` : fine amount (given)  \n- `R = r\u2011t\u20111` : rounds remaining after the current one  \n\n**Decision rule (choose action A \u2208 {C,D})**\n\n1. **Immediate expected payoff**  \n   - `E_C = S / (2n)`  \n   - `E_D = S / n  \u2013  q\u00b7F`  (expected fine applies only when defecting)  \n\n2. **Marginal stock damage from defecting**  \n   - Extra consumption when defecting vs cooperating: `\u0394cons = S/(2n)`  \n   - Approximate future loss per remaining round if stock is reduced by `\u0394cons` now:  \n     `\u0394future \u2248 \u0394cons * (R / (R+1))`\u2003(the later the round, the smaller the impact)  \n\n3. **Net advantage of defecting**  \n   `Adv = (E_D \u2013 E_C)  \u2013  \u0394future`  \n\n4. **Action selection**  \n   - If `Adv > 0` \u2192 play **D** (defect)  \n   - Else \u2192 play **C** (cooperate)\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n- **First round (t = 0)**: `k` is undefined; use the rule above with `R = r\u20111`.  \n- **Last round (t = r\u20111)**: no audit (`q = 0` for this round) and no future rounds (`R = 0`).  \n  Compute `Adv = (S/n \u2013 S/(2n))`. Since `\u0394future = 0`, always `Adv > 0`. \u2192 always **D**.  \n- **Stock depleted (S = 0)**: both payoffs are zero; play **C** (no extra consumption).  \n- **Audit probability zero (q = 0)**: the rule reduces to defect if `S/n > S/(2n) + \u0394future`, i.e., defect unless future loss dominates.  \n\n**Adaptive element**\n\nAfter each round you observe `k`. Adjust the estimate of future stock loss by scaling `\u0394future` with the observed cooperation level:\n\n```\ncoop_ratio = (k) / (n\u20111)          # proportion of opponents who cooperated last round\n\u0394future = \u0394cons * (R/(R+1)) * (1 \u2013 coop_ratio)   # higher opponent defection => higher future loss\n```\n\nThis makes the strategy more tolerant of cooperation (reducing perceived future loss) and more aggressive when opponents are mostly defectors.\n\n**Summary of algorithm per round**\n\n```\nif S == 0:          action = C\nelif t == r\u20111:     action = D\nelse:\n    E_C = S/(2*n)\n    E_D = S/n - q*F\n    \u0394cons = S/(2*n)\n    coop_ratio = (k)/(n-1)   if t>0 else 0.5   # assume 50% cooperation initially\n    \u0394future = \u0394cons * (R/(R+1)) * (1 - coop_ratio)\n    Adv = (E_D - E_C) - \u0394future\n    action = D if Adv > 0 else C\n```\n\nThe strategy always maximizes its expected selfish payoff, accounting for immediate audit risk, the extra consumption cost, and the projected loss of future payoff from stock depletion, while adapting to observed opponent behavior."

description_SELFISH_6 = "**Selfish Adaptive Defect\u2011When\u2011Profitable (SADWP) Strategy**\n\n**Parameters used each round**  \n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `q`, `F` \u2013 given by the game description.  \n- `t` \u2013 current round index (0\u2011based).  \n- `S` \u2013 current stock (float, 0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity).  \n- `c_obs` \u2013 number of opponents observed cooperating in the *previous* round (0\u202f\u2264\u202fc_obs\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111).  \n- `p_coop_prev = c_obs / (n\u20111)` \u2013 empirical probability that a random opponent cooperated last round (used as a proxy for the next\u2011round mix).\n\n**Core idea**  \nChoose the action that maximizes the *expected* immediate payoff **plus** a one\u2011step\u2011ahead estimate of the effect on next\u2011round stock. The rule is completely selfish; it never sacrifices current payoff for future rounds unless the future stock loss would make the *current* defect unprofitable after accounting for the expected fine.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Immediate\u2011payoff comparison\n\n```\npayoff_C  = S / (2*n)                     # guaranteed, no fine\nexpected_fine = q * F                     # expected fine for defect\npayoff_D  = S / n - expected_fine         # expected payoff if defect\n\u0394_immediate = payoff_D - payoff_C         # >0 \u21d2 defect is better now\n```\n\n### 2. One\u2011step\u2011ahead stock impact\n\nIf we cooperate, our consumption = S/(2n); if we defect, consumption = S/n.  \nAssume all *other* players keep the same cooperation probability `p_coop_prev` observed last round.\n\n```\n# Expected total consumption of opponents\nexp_cons_opp = (n-1) * ( p_coop_prev * (S/(2*n)) + (1-p_coop_prev) * (S/n) )\n```\n\nTotal consumption under each of our two choices:\n\n```\ntotal_cons_C = exp_cons_opp + S/(2*n)    # we cooperate\ntotal_cons_D = exp_cons_opp + S/n        # we defect\n```\n\nRemaining stock after consumption:\n\n```\nS_rem_C = max(S - total_cons_C, 0)\nS_rem_D = max(S - total_cons_D, 0)\n```\n\nGrowth (same formula for both):\n\n```\ngrow(X) = 2 * X * (1 - X / capacity)\n```\n\nResulting stock for the next round:\n\n```\nS_next_C = min(S_rem_C + grow(S_rem_C), capacity)\nS_next_D = min(S_rem_D + grow(S_rem_D), capacity)\n```\n\nExpected payoff we would obtain *next* round **if we followed the same rule** (i.e., we will again compare immediate payoffs with the same calculation). Approximating that we will defect next round iff `\u0394_immediate_next > 0`, we can use the one\u2011step\u2011ahead *expected* payoff as the difference in stock levels multiplied by the marginal value of stock:\n\n```\nmarginal = 1/(2*n)          # extra payoff per unit of stock when cooperating\n\u0394_future \u2248 marginal * (S_next_D - S_next_C)   # positive if defect leaves more stock for us\n```\n\n(If `S_next_D < S_next_C`, defect reduces next\u2011round stock and thus hurts us; \u0394_future will be negative.)\n\n### 3. Decision rule\n\n```\nif t == r-1:                     # last round \u2013 never audited\n    action = D                   # always defect (max immediate payoff)\nelse:\n    \u0394_total = \u0394_immediate + \u0394_future\n    if \u0394_total > 0 and S > 0:\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C\n```\n\n### 4. Edge\u2011case handling\n\n| Situation | Rule |\n|-----------|------|\n| **Initial round (t\u202f=\u202f0)** | No history for `p_coop_prev`. Set `p_coop_prev = 1` (optimistic) so the opponent mix is assumed fully cooperative; the rest of the computation proceeds unchanged. |\n| **Stock S = 0** | Both actions yield 0 payoff and no consumption. Choose **C** (doesn\u2019t matter, but conserves the \u201ccooperate\u201d label). |\n| **Audit probability q = 0** | Expected fine = 0, so `\u0394_immediate = S/(2n) > 0`. The rule defaults to defect unless the one\u2011step\u2011ahead future loss (`\u0394_future`) is strongly negative. |\n| **Fine F = 0** | Same as above; defect unless future stock loss outweighs immediate gain. |\n| **Observed all opponents defect (`p_coop_prev = 0`)** | The expected opponent consumption rises, making `\u0394_future` more negative; the rule may keep us cooperating to avoid accelerating depletion. |\n| **Observed all opponents cooperate (`p_coop_prev = 1`)** | Opponent consumption is lower, making defecting more attractive; the rule will likely defect. |\n\n### 5. Summary of the algorithm (pseudocode)\n\n```python\ndef SADWP(t, S, c_obs, n, r, capacity, q, F):\n    # 1. Last round -> always defect\n    if t == r - 1:\n        return 'D'\n\n    # 2. Estimate opponent cooperation probability\n    if t == 0:\n        p_coop_prev = 1.0      # optimistic assumption\n    else:\n        p_coop_prev = c_obs / (n - 1)\n\n    # 3. Immediate payoff difference\n    payoff_C = S / (2 * n)\n    expected_fine = q * F\n    payoff_D = S / n - expected_fine\n    \u0394_immediate = payoff_D - payoff_C\n\n    # 4. Expected opponent consumption\n    coop_cons = S / (2 * n)\n    def_cons  = S / n\n    exp_cons_opp = (n - 1) * (p_coop_prev * coop_cons + (1 - p_coop_prev) * def_cons)\n\n    # 5. Stock after our two possible actions\n    total_cons_C = exp_cons_opp + coop_cons\n    total_cons_D = exp_cons_opp + def_cons\n    S_rem_C = max(S - total_cons_C, 0.0)\n    S_rem_D = max(S - total_cons_D, 0.0)\n\n    def grow(X):\n        return 2 * X * (1 - X / capacity)\n\n    S_next_C = min(S_rem_C + grow(S_rem_C), capacity)\n    S_next_D = min(S_rem_D + grow(S_rem_D), capacity)\n\n    # 6. One\u2011step\u2011ahead stock value difference\n    marginal = 1.0 / (2 * n)               # per\u2011unit stock value when we cooperate\n    \u0394_future = marginal * (S_next_D - S_next_C)\n\n    # 7. Total expected advantage of defecting\n    \u0394_total = \u0394_immediate + \u0394_future\n\n    # 8. Choose action\n    if \u0394_total > 0 and S > 0:\n        return 'D'\n    else:\n        return 'C'\n```\n\nThe strategy uses only publicly available parameters, the observable stock `S`, and the *anonymous* count of cooperating opponents from the previous round. It remains purely selfish: it defects whenever the sum of the immediate expected gain (after accounting for audit risk) and the anticipated effect on next\u2011round stock is positive, and cooperates otherwise. It automatically adapts to changing opponent behaviour, audit intensity, and depletion levels, and safely handles all edge cases."

description_SELFISH_7 = "**Selfish Adaptive Defection/Cooperation (SADC) Strategy**\n\n**Parameters known to the agent**  \n- n, r, capacity, q, F (audit probability and fine)  \n- History: for each past round\u202ft\u2032\u202f<\u202ft you observed the number of opponents that cooperated, `c_prev[t\u2032]` (0\u202f\u2264\u202fc_prev\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111).  \n\n**Round\u2011by\u2011round decision rule (t = 0 \u2026 r\u20111)**  \n\n1. **Compute remaining rounds**  \n   `R = r \u2013 t`  \n\n2. **Special cases**  \n   - **Last round (t = r\u20111)** \u2192 *Defect* (no audit, no future).  \n   - **Zero stock (S = 0)** \u2192 *Cooperate* (consumption = 0, avoids fine).  \n\n3. **Estimate opponent cooperation probability**  \n\n   ```\n   if t == 0:\n       p = 0.5                     # default belief when no info\n   else:\n       p = (sum_{k=0}^{t-1} c_prev[k]) / ((n-1) * t)   # average observed coop rate\n   ```\n\n4. **Immediate expected payoff**  \n\n   ```\n   payoff_C = S/(2*n)                                   # no fine when cooperating\n   payoff_D = S/n - q*F                                 # expected fine on defect\n   ```\n\n5. **Expected total consumption this round**  \n\n   ```\n   own_cons_C = S/(2*n)                                 # if we cooperate\n   own_cons_D = S/n                                     # if we defect\n   opp_cons   = p * S/(2*n) + (1-p) * S/n               # expected per opponent\n   total_cons_C = own_cons_C + (n-1) * opp_cons\n   total_cons_D = own_cons_D + (n-1) * opp_cons\n   ```\n\n6. **Project next\u2011round stock (deterministic projection)**  \n\n   ```\n   def project_stock(S_current, total_cons):\n       S_rem = max(0, S_current - total_cons)\n       growth = 2 * S_rem * (1 - S_rem/capacity)\n       return min(S_rem + growth, capacity)\n\n   S_next_C = project_stock(S, total_cons_C)\n   S_next_D = project_stock(S, total_cons_D)\n   ```\n\n7. **Estimate future payoff per remaining round** (assume we repeat the *same* action in all future rounds; this yields a simple linear approximation)\n\n   ```\n   future_per_round_C = S_next_C/(2*n)             # later rounds we would cooperate\n   future_per_round_D = S_next_D/n - q*F           # later rounds we would defect\n\n   # Expected total from remaining (R-1) rounds:\n   future_C = (R-1) * future_per_round_C\n   future_D = (R-1) * future_per_round_D\n   ```\n\n8. **Total expected payoff for each candidate action**\n\n   ```\n   total_C = payoff_C + future_C\n   total_D = payoff_D + future_D\n   ```\n\n9. **Choose the action with higher total expected payoff**  \n\n   ```\n   if total_D > total_C:\n       action = D\n   else:\n       action = C\n   ```\n\n   *Tie\u2011breaker*: if `total_D == total_C` choose **Defect** (maximises immediate gain).\n\n10. **Record outcome**  \n    - Store the number of opponents that cooperated this round (derived from aggregate observation).  \n    - Store whether you were audited and any fine paid (used only for bookkeeping, not for decision).\n\n**Summary of edge\u2011case handling**  \n\n- **t = 0**: use a neutral prior `p = 0.5`.  \n- **t = r\u20111**: always defect (no audit, no future impact).  \n- **S = 0**: cooperate to avoid an unnecessary fine (payoff zero either way).  \n\nThe strategy continually re\u2011evaluates the trade\u2011off between the higher immediate reward of defection (discounted by the expected fine) and the long\u2011run benefit of preserving stock for future rounds, using only observable aggregate data and the known game parameters. It is purely selfish: the chosen action maximises the agent\u2019s own expected cumulative payoff."

description_SELFISH_8 = "**Selfish Adaptive Defection\u2011Cooperation (SADC) Strategy**\n\n**Parameters known to the agent**  \n- n, r, capacity, q, F (audit probability and fine)  \n- Current stock\u202fS\u202f\u2208\u202f[0,\u202fcapacity]  \n- Round index\u202ft\u202f(0\u202f\u2026\u202fr\u20111)  \n- Observed proportion of opponents that cooperated in the *previous* round,\u202fp\u209c\u208b\u2081 (for t\u202f=\u202f0 use p\u208b\u2081\u202f=\u202f0.5 as a neutral prior).\n\n**Decision rule (executed each round)**  \n\n```\nL = r - t                     # rounds remaining including current\nif S == 0:                   # nothing left to consume\n    action = C               # cooperate to avoid waste (payoff = 0 either way)\nelif t == r-1:               # last round: no future, no audit\n    action = D if S > 0 else C\nelse:\n    # 1. Immediate expected payoff\n    \u03c0C = S/(2*n)                                 # no fine on C\n    \u03c0D = S/n - q*F                               # expected fine on D\n\n    # 2. Estimate stock after this round under each own action\n    #    Assume opponents repeat the proportion p\u209c\u208b\u2081 they showed last round.\n    opp_coop = p\u209c\u208b\u2081\n    opp_def  = 1 - p\u209c\u208b\u2081\n\n    # consumption of a single opponent:\n    cons_coop = S/(2*n)\n    cons_def  = S/n\n\n    # total consumption if we cooperate:\n    total_cons_C = \u03c0C + (n-1)*(opp_coop*cons_coop + opp_def*cons_def)\n    S_after_C   = S - total_cons_C\n    growth_C    = 2 * S_after_C * (1 - S_after_C/capacity)\n    S_next_C     = min(S_after_C + growth_C, capacity)\n\n    # total consumption if we defect:\n    total_cons_D = \u03c0D + (n-1)*(opp_coop*cons_coop + opp_def*cons_def)\n    S_after_D   = S - total_cons_D\n    growth_D    = 2 * S_after_D * (1 - S_after_D/capacity)\n    S_next_D    = min(S_after_D + growth_D, capacity)\n\n    # 3. Approximate future payoff (myopic linear approximation)\n    #    Assume the same p\u209c\u208b\u2081 will hold for all remaining rounds.\n    future_factor = (L-1) / L          # weight of future rounds relative to present\n    est_future_C = future_factor * (S_next_C/(2*n)) * (L-1)   # if we continue cooperating\n    est_future_D = future_factor * (S_next_D/n) * (L-1)       # if we continue defecting\n\n    # 4. Total expected utility for each action\n    U_C = \u03c0C + est_future_C\n    U_D = \u03c0D + est_future_D\n\n    # 5. Choose the action with higher expected utility\n    action = C if U_C >= U_D else D\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n| Situation | Rule |\n|-----------|------|\n| **Initial round (t\u202f=\u202f0)** | Use `p\u208b\u2081 = 0.5`. Compute as above. |\n| **Stock already depleted (S\u202f=\u202f0)** | Play **C** (payoff 0, no consumption, avoids unnecessary fine). |\n| **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111)** | No audit, no future stock impact \u2192 always **D** if any stock remains; otherwise **C**. |\n| **Audit observation** | After each round the agent updates `p\u209c` = (number of opponents that cooperated)\u202f/\u202f(n\u20111). This feeds the next round\u2019s estimate. |\n| **Extreme audit environment** (`q = 1` and/or very large `F`) | The immediate expected payoff `\u03c0D` may become \u2264\u202f`\u03c0C`; the rule automatically favors cooperation in those cases. |\n| **Stock close to capacity after growth** (`S_next > capacity`) | The `min(..., capacity)` clause caps the stock; the calculation proceeds unchanged. |\n\n**Selfishness justification embedded in the rule**  \n\n- The agent evaluates *expected* monetary payoff (including the expected fine) plus a forward\u2011looking component that reflects how today\u2019s consumption will affect future payoff opportunities.\n- The forward component is weighted only by the remaining number of rounds; no external welfare or fairness considerations are introduced.\n- The agent never cooperates out of altruism; cooperation is chosen *only* when the projected total utility from cooperating (immediate + future) exceeds that from defecting."

description_SELFISH_9 = "**Strategy Name:**\u202fExpected\u2011Return Adaptive (ERA)\n\n**Parameters used:**\u202f\\(n, r, capacity, q, F\\) (audit probability and fine), current stock \\(S_t\\), round index \\(t\\), observed opponent cooperation share in the last round \\(p_{t-1}\\) (or an average over all past rounds if none yet).\n\n---\n\n### 1. Decision rule (cooperate vs. defect)\n\nAt the start of every round \\(t\\) (except the last) compute the *net expected value* of defecting versus cooperating:\n\n```\n\u0394_immediate = (S_t / n) \u2013 (S_t / (2n))                # extra payoff now if D\n\u0394_fine      = q * F                                   # expected fine if D\n\u0394_future    = ExpectedFuturePayoff(D) \u2013 ExpectedFuturePayoff(C)\n```\n\n*ExpectedFuturePayoff(action)* is obtained by projecting the stock one round forward assuming the **average opponent behaviour** observed so far (denoted p\u0302).  \n\n```\n# projected stock after our action a \u2208 {C,D}\nif a == C:\n    our_cons   = S_t/(2n)\nelse:   # a == D\n    our_cons   = S_t/n\n\nopp_cons   = p\u0302 * (S_t/(2n)) + (1\u2011p\u0302) * (S_t/n)   # each opponent\u2019s expected consumption\ntotal_cons = our_cons + (n\u20111) * opp_cons\nS_next     = max(0, S_t - total_cons)            # stock after consumption\ngrowth     = 2 * S_next * (1 - S_next/capacity)\nS_proj     = min(S_next + growth, capacity)\n```\n\nAssume the same p\u0302 will repeat for the remaining \\(T = r\u2011t\u20111\\) rounds; the projected payoff in each future round is the *average* of the cooperative and defective payoffs computed on \\(S_proj\\) with the same p\u0302. Hence\n\n```\nExpectedFuturePayoff(a) = T * [ p\u0302 * (S_proj/(2n)) + (1\u2011p\u0302) * (S_proj/n) ]\n```\n\nFinally, compute the net advantage of defecting:\n\n```\nNetAdvantage = \u0394_immediate \u2013 \u0394_fine + \u0394_future\n```\n\n- **If NetAdvantage > 0 \u2192 Defect (D)**\n- **Otherwise \u2192 Cooperate (C)**\n\n---\n\n### 2. Edge\u2011case handling\n\n| Situation | Action |\n|-----------|--------|\n| **First round (t = 0)** | No history \u21d2 set p\u0302 = 0.5 (neutral belief). Apply the rule above. |\n| **Last round (t = r\u20111)** | No audit and no future rounds \u21d2 defect always (maximises immediate payoff). |\n| **Stock about to collapse** | If the projected stock after defect \\(S_{proj}\\) would be \u2264\u202f0 while the projected stock after cooperation would stay >\u202f0, force cooperation regardless of NetAdvantage (preserves any payoff for remaining rounds). |\n| **Audit probability q = 0** | The fine term drops out; the rule reduces to comparing immediate extra payoff vs. future stock loss. |\n| **Fine F = 0** | Same as q = 0 case. |\n| **Observed p\u0302 = 0 or 1** | The projection uses the extreme opponent behaviour directly; rule remains unchanged. |\n| **Stock = 0** | All actions yield zero payoff; cooperate to avoid unnecessary depletion (both give 0). |\n\n---\n\n### 3. Selfish orientation\n\nThe ERA rule evaluates **only the player\u2019s own expected monetary return**, incorporating the stochastic fine and the impact of one\u2019s consumption on future stock. It never sacrifices immediate or projected personal payoff for collective welfare; cooperation is chosen *only* when the expected loss from defecting (fine + future stock depreciation) outweighs the extra current gain. The algorithm is fully deterministic given the observed history and current state, ensuring consistent selfish optimisation across all rounds."

description_SELFISH_10 = "**Selfish Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**Parameters known to the agent**  \n- n, r, capacity, audit probability\u202fq, fine\u202fF  \n- Current round\u202ft (0\u2011indexed) and current stock\u202fS  \n- History\u202fH\u202f= {(t\u2032,\u202fk_{t\u2032})\u202f|\u202f0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u2032\u202f<\u202ft}, where k_{t\u2032} is the observed number of opponents who cooperated in round\u202ft\u2032  \n\n**Utility model**  \n- Immediate payoff if cooperate: \u202f\u03c0_C = S/(2n)  \n- Immediate payoff if defect (before fine):\u202f\u03c0_D\u2070 = S/n  \n- Expected fine for defect:\u202fE_fine = q\u00b7F (last round has\u202fq=0)  \n- Expected immediate net payoff for defect:\u202f\u03c0_D = \u03c0_D\u2070 \u2013 E_fine  \n\n**Future\u2011stock estimate**  \nAssume opponents will repeat the observed cooperation frequency of the last\u202fm\u202frounds (default\u202fm\u202f=\u202f3, or all rounds if\u202ft\u202f<\u202fm).  \n- Observed cooperation rate: \u202fc\u0302 = (1/m)\u00b7\u2211_{j=t\u2011m}^{t\u20111} (k_j / (n\u20111))   (if denominator\u202f0, set\u202fc\u0302=0)  \n- Expected number of defectors next round (including self if we defect):  \n\u2003\u2003E_def = (n\u20111)\u00b7(1\u2011c\u0302) + (action\u202f=\u202fD ? 1 : 0)  \n\nEstimate next\u2011round stock S\u0302' under each candidate action a\u2208{C,D}:  \n\n```\nconsumption(a) = (action==C ? S/(2n) : S/n)\ntotal_cons = (n\u20111)\u00b7[c\u0302\u00b7S/(2n) + (1\u2011c\u0302)\u00b7S/n] + consumption(a)\nS_rem = max(0, S \u2013 total_cons)\ngrowth = 2 * S_rem * (1 \u2013 S_rem / capacity)\nS\u0302' = min(S_rem + growth, capacity)\n```\n\n**Decision rule (per round t)**  \n\n1. **Last round (t = r\u20111)** \u2013 No audit, no future: choose D (maximizes immediate payoff).  \n\n2. **First round (t = 0)** \u2013 No history: assume opponents cooperate with probability\u202fp\u2080 = 1 (optimistic) to avoid over\u2011exploiting early stock. Compute \u03c0_C, \u03c0_D (with E_fine = q\u00b7F). If \u03c0_D\u202f>\u202f\u03c0_C\u202f+\u202f\u0394 (\u0394\u202f=\u202f0.5\u00b7S/(2n) to bias toward preserving stock when marginal), defect; otherwise cooperate.  \n\n3. **Intermediate rounds (0 < t < r\u20111)**  \n\n   a. Compute expected immediate net payoffs \u03c0_C and \u03c0_D (using current\u202fS and audit probability\u202fq).  \n\n   b. Estimate next\u2011round stock S\u0302'_C and S\u0302'_D using the future\u2011stock estimate above.  \n\n   c. Approximate discounted future value V(a) = \u03b1\u00b7S\u0302'_a, where discount factor\u202f\u03b1 = (r\u2011t\u20111)/(r\u2011t) (linear decay). This captures the selfish value of a higher stock for remaining rounds.  \n\n   d. Compute total expected utility for each action:  \n\u2003\u2003U_C = \u03c0_C + V(C)  \n\u2003\u2003U_D = \u03c0_D + V(D)  \n\n   e. Choose **Cooperate** if U_C\u202f\u2265\u202fU_D, otherwise **Defect**.  \n\n4. **Edge cases**  \n   - If S = 0, any consumption yields 0; choose C to avoid unnecessary fine risk.  \n   - If S is so low that consumption would drive S_rem < 0 (i.e., total_cons > S), cap consumption to available stock: consumption_C = S/(2n)\u202f\u00b7\u202fmin(1,\u202fS / ((n\u20111)\u00b7S/(2n) + S/(2n))) and similarly for D; recompute \u03c0 values accordingly.  \n   - If audit probability q = 0, set E_fine = 0, decision reduces to pure payoff vs future stock.  \n\n**Summary of algorithm per round**  \n\n```\nfunction decide(t, S, H):\n    if t == r\u20111: return D\n    if t == 0:\n        \u03c0_C = S/(2n)\n        \u03c0_D = S/n - q*F\n        if \u03c0_D > \u03c0_C + 0.5*S/(2n): return D else return C\n    # t > 0 and t < r\u20111\n    c\u0302 = average cooperation rate from last min(3, t) rounds\n    # immediate payoffs\n    \u03c0_C = S/(2n)\n    \u03c0_D = S/n - q*F\n    # forecast stock for each action\n    S\u0302_C = forecast_stock(S, C, c\u0302)\n    S\u0302_D = forecast_stock(S, D, c\u0302)\n    \u03b1 = (r\u2011t\u20111)/(r\u2011t)\n    U_C = \u03c0_C + \u03b1 * S\u0302_C\n    U_D = \u03c0_D + \u03b1 * S\u0302_D\n    return C if U_C >= U_D else D\n```\n\n`forecast_stock` implements the consumption, remaining stock, growth, and capacity bound as described in step\u202f3b. This strategy always selects the action with the highest selfish expected utility, adapts to observed opponent behavior, accounts for audit risk, and preserves enough stock to sustain future earnings when advantageous."

description_SELFISH_11 = "**Selfish Adaptive Strategy \u2013 \u201cExpected\u2011Payoff Threshold with Stock\u2011Guard\u201d**\n\n**Inputs each round\u202ft (0\u202f\u2264\u202ft\u202f<\u202fr):**  \n- game parameters\u202f: n, r, capacity, audit_prob\u202fq, fine\u202fF  \n- current stock\u202fS\u209c (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u209c\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity)  \n- observed count\u202fc\u209c of opponents that cooperated in round\u202ft (0\u202f\u2264\u202fc\u209c\u202f\u2264\u202fn\u20111) \u2013 from round\u202ft\u20111 onward  \n- own past actions and audit outcomes (for computing own audit\u2011frequency, not required for the rule)\n\n**Derived quantities:**  \n\n1. Immediate expected payoff if we cooperate  \n  \u202f\u202fU_C\u202f=\u202fS\u209c\u202f/\u202f(2\u202fn)  \n\n2. Immediate expected payoff if we defect (accounting for expected fine)  \n  \u202f\u202fU_D\u202f=\u202fS\u209c\u202f/\u202fn\u202f\u2212\u202fq\u00b7F  \n\n3. Empirical opponent\u2011cooperation rate (for t\u202f>\u202f0)  \n  \u202f\u202fp_coop\u202f=\u202f(c\u209c\u208b\u2081\u202f/\u202f(n\u20111))  \n  \u202f\u202fIf t\u202f=\u202f0, set p_coop\u202f=\u202f1 (no information \u2192 assume full cooperation).  \n\n4. Stock\u2011guard thresholds (constants chosen once, independent of round):  \n  \u202f\u202f\u03b8\u202f=\u202f0.6\u202f\u00b7\u202fcapacity\u2003(minimum stock level at which cooperation is worthwhile)  \n  \u202f\u202f\u03c4\u202f=\u202f0.7\u2003(minimum opponent\u2011cooperation rate required to sustain cooperation)  \n\n**Decision rule:**  \n\n```\nif t == r\u20111:                     # last round, never audited\n    action = D\nelse:\n    if U_D <= U_C:               # defect not better even before fine\n        action = C\n    else:\n        # defect yields higher immediate expected payoff;\n        # cooperate only if stock is healthy and opponents are largely cooperative\n        if S\u209c >= \u03b8 and p_coop >= \u03c4:\n            action = C\n        else:\n            action = D\n```\n\n**Explanation of edge\u2011case handling (embedded in the rule):**  \n\n- **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0):** p_coop is set to\u202f1, so the strategy will cooperate iff the stock is \u2265\u202f\u03b8; otherwise it defects.  \n- **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111):** The rule forces defection because there is no audit risk and no future rounds to preserve the stock.  \n- **Audited rounds:** Expected fine q\u00b7F is already folded into U_D, so the rule automatically accounts for audit risk.  \n\n**Selfishness guarantee:** The action chosen maximizes the player\u2019s *expected* immediate payoff, subject only to a precautionary check that avoids damaging the stock when the pool is already low or opponents are predominantly defecting. This prevents self\u2011inflicted stock collapse that would reduce all future payoffs, thereby protecting the player\u2019s own long\u2011term earnings while remaining fundamentally payoff\u2011driven."

description_SELFISH_12 = "**Selfish Adaptive Strategy \u2013 \u201cProfit\u2011First with Stock\u2011Safety\u201d**\n\n---  \n\n**Parameters available to the agent**  \n`n, r, capacity, q, F` \u2013 game size, horizon, pool capacity, audit probability, fine.  \n\n**History available each round t (0\u2011indexed)**  \n- `S_t` \u2013 current stock (float).  \n- `my_action_{0..t\u20111}` \u2013 own past actions.  \n- `my_audit_{0..t\u20111}` \u2013 whether audited (0/1) in each past round.  \n- `opp_coop_{0..t\u20111}` \u2013 number of opponents that cooperated in each past round (0 \u2026 n\u20111).  \n\n**Notation**  \n`R = r \u2013 t`\u2003\u2003remaining rounds (including the current one)  \n`p =` empirical probability that a random opponent cooperates this round  \n\n```\nif t == 0:                         # no data yet\n    p = 0.5                         # neutral prior\nelse:\n    total_coop = \u03a3_k opp_coop_k\n    p = total_coop / (t * (n\u20111))    # observed frequency\n```\n\n**Step\u202f1 \u2013 Immediate expected payoffs**  \n\n```\npay_C = S_t / (2*n)                         # payoff if we cooperate\npay_D = S_t / n - q*F                        # expected payoff if we defect\nextra_cons = S_t/(2*n)                       # extra consumption when defecting\n```\n\n**Step\u202f2 \u2013 Expected opponent consumption**  \n\n```\nopp_cons_C = (n\u20111) * ( p * S_t/(2*n) + (1\u2011p) * S_t/n )\nopp_cons_D = opp_cons_C          # opponents\u2019 behaviour is assumed unchanged\n```\n\n**Step\u202f3 \u2013 Expected next\u2011stock for each option**  \n\n```\ncons_total_C = pay_C + opp_cons_C\nS_rem_C = max(0, S_t - cons_total_C)                  # stock after consumption\ngrow_C = 2 * S_rem_C * (1 - S_rem_C / capacity)\nS_next_C = min(S_rem_C + grow_C, capacity)\n\ncons_total_D = pay_D + extra_cons + opp_cons_D\nS_rem_D = max(0, S_t - cons_total_D)\ngrow_D = 2 * S_rem_D * (1 - S_rem_D / capacity)\nS_next_D = min(S_rem_D + grow_D, capacity)\n```\n\n**Step\u202f4 \u2013 One\u2011step look\u2011ahead value**  \n\nAssume that after this round we will again apply the same rule, i.e. we will pick the higher of the two immediate expected payoffs in every later round (the rule is myopic but repeated).  \nDefine a simple \u201cfuture\u2011round value\u201d function:\n\n```\nfuture_value(S) = max( S/(2*n) , S/n - q*F )\n```\n\n(This is the payoff we would take in a future round if the stock were `S`.)\n\nProjected total return for the current decision:\n\n```\nV_C = pay_C + (R\u20111) * future_value(S_next_C)\nV_D = pay_D + (R\u20111) * future_value(S_next_D)\n```\n\n**Step\u202f5 \u2013 Decision rule**  \n\n```\nif t == r\u20111:                     # last round, never audited\n    action = D\nelif S_t == 0:\n    action = C                   # any action yields 0; choose C to avoid fine risk\nelse:\n    if V_D > V_C:\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C\n```\n\n---  \n\n**Summary of the rule (without commentary)**  \n\n1. Estimate opponents\u2019 cooperation probability from past counts (`p`).  \n2. Compute expected immediate payoffs `pay_C` and `pay_D` (including expected fine).  \n3. Compute expected next\u2011stock `S_next_C` and `S_next_D` using the stock dynamics with the expected total consumption.  \n4. Evaluate one\u2011step look\u2011ahead values `V_C` and `V_D` = immediate payoff\u202f+\u202ffuture\u2011round value times remaining rounds.  \n5. Play **Defect** if `V_D > V_C`, otherwise **Cooperate**.  \n6. **Exception**: in the final round always defect; if stock is zero cooperate (harmless).  "

description_SELFISH_13 = "**Selfish Adaptive Strategy (SA\u2011SCP)**  \n\n**Parameters used:**\u202fn, r, capacity, audit probability\u202fq, fine\u202fF, current round\u202ft, current stock\u202fS, observed cooperation fraction of opponents in the previous round\u202fp\u0302 (number of opponents that cooperated \u00f7 (n\u20111)).  \n\n**Decision rule (for each round\u202ft, player\u202fi):**\n\n```\nif S == 0:                     # stock exhausted\n    action = C                 # consumes nothing, avoids unnecessary fine\nelse if t == r\u20111:              # last round \u2013 never audited\n    action = D                 # immediate payoff S/n > S/(2n)\nelse:\n    # 1. Immediate expected payoffs\n    E_C  = S/(2*n)                              # no fine when cooperating\n    E_D  = S/n - q*F                            # expected fine on defect\n\n    # 2. If immediate defect is not better, cooperate\n    if E_D <= E_C:\n        action = C\n        continue\n\n    # 3. Estimate opponents\u2019 behavior for this round\n    #    (use previous observation; if no history, assume p\u0302 = 0.5)\n    if t == 0:  p\u0302 = 0.5\n    else:       p\u0302 = observed_coop_fraction_last_round\n\n    # 4. Project next\u2011round stock for each candidate action\n    #    \u2013 assume opponents keep the same mixed behavior p\u0302\n    #    \u2013 total consumption if we cooperate:\n    cons_C = (S/(2*n))                         # our consumption\n    cons_opp = (n-1) * (p\u0302 * S/(2*n) + (1-p\u0302) * S/n)\n    S_rem_C = S - (cons_C + cons_opp)\n\n    #    \u2013 total consumption if we defect:\n    cons_D = S/n\n    cons_opp = (n-1) * (p\u0302 * S/(2*n) + (1-p\u0302) * S/n)   # opponents unchanged\n    S_rem_D = S - (cons_D + cons_opp)\n\n    #    \u2013 apply growth (bounded by capacity)\n    grow = lambda x: min(x + 2*x*(1 - x/capacity), capacity)\n    S_next_C = grow(S_rem_C)\n    S_next_D = grow(S_rem_D)\n\n    # 5. Approximate total future payoff (remaining rounds = r\u2011t\u20111)\n    #    Assume future rounds repeat the same pattern we will choose now.\n    #    Future payoff per round if we continue with action a:\n    #        payoff_a = S_next_a/(2*n)  if we would cooperate later\n    #        payoff_a = S_next_a/n - q*F  if we would defect later\n    #    For simplicity, evaluate both scenarios assuming we keep the same\n    #    choice for the rest of the game.\n\n    #    Immediate payoff already computed (E_C, E_D).\n    #    Future payoff estimate:\n    future_C = (r - t - 1) * (S_next_C/(2*n))\n    future_D = (r - t - 1) * (S_next_D/n - q*F)\n\n    total_E_C = E_C + future_C\n    total_E_D = E_D + future_D\n\n    # 6. Choose the action with larger total expected payoff\n    if total_E_D > total_E_C:\n        action = D\n    else:\n        action = C\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n\n* **Round\u202f0 (first round):**\u202fNo past observations \u2192 set\u202fp\u0302\u202f=\u202f0.5 (neutral prior). Apply the rule above.  \n* **Stock\u202fS\u202f=\u202f0:**\u202fBoth actions yield 0 consumption; cooperate to avoid a fine that would only reduce a zero payoff.  \n* **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111):**\u202fAudits are impossible, so always defect because\u202fS/n\u202f>\u202fS/(2n).  \n* **Negative projected stock:**\u202fIf a projection yields\u202fS_rem\u202f<\u202f0, treat it as\u202f0\u202fbefore applying growth.  \n\n**Selfish justification:** The strategy maximizes the player\u2019s own expected cumulative payoff by (1) comparing immediate net gains after accounting for expected fines, (2) forecasting how each choice alters the common stock and thus future earnings, and (3) selecting the action with the higher total expected return, while defaulting to cooperation only when defecting would either reduce immediate profit or jeopardize future profit enough to outweigh the short\u2011term advantage."

description_SELFISH_14 = "**Selfish Adaptive Strategy \u2013 \u201cRisk\u2011Adjusted Defection\u201d**\n\n**State variables (available each round\u202ft)**\n- `S_t` \u2013 current stock level (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS_t\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity).\n- `p_t` \u2013 observed fraction of opponents that cooperated in the *previous* round (if t\u202f=\u202f0, set `p_0 = 1`).\n- `q` \u2013 audit probability (known from game description).\n- `F` \u2013 fine amount (known).\n- `n` \u2013 number of players (known).\n- `r` \u2013 total rounds (known).\n- `lastRound = (t == r\u20111)`.\n\n**Auxiliary functions**\n```\ncoopPay(S) = S / (2*n)                     // payoff for cooperating\ndefPay(S)  = S / n                         // gross payoff for defecting\nexpFine   = q * F                         // expected fine per defection (zero in last round)\n```\n```\nexpectedDefectPay(S) = defPay(S) - expFine\n```\n```\nfutureLoss(S, a) = (a / n) * (1 - a/2) * S   // rough estimate of stock reduction after a defect\n```\n*Explanation of `futureLoss`: a defect consumes an extra `S/(2n)` compared with a cooperator; the additional removal shrinks the post\u2011consumption stock, which lowers the next\u2011round growth term. The factor `(1\u2011a/2)` approximates the logistic\u2011growth sensitivity to the remaining stock.*\n\n**Decision rule (executed each round t)**  \n\n1. **Last round** (`lastRound == true`)  \n   - No audit possible, and no future rounds.  \n   - Choose **Defect** (maximises immediate payoff).  \n\n2. **Otherwise (t < r\u20111)**  \n   a. Compute immediate expected payoffs:\n   ```\n   E_C = coopPay(S_t)\n   E_D = expectedDefectPay(S_t)\n   ```\n   b. Estimate the *future value* impact of each action.  \n      Assume opponents will repeat the observed cooperation fraction `p_t`.  \n      - If you **Cooperate**, total consumption this round \u2248  \n        `C_total = n * (p_t * coopPay(S_t) + (1\u2011p_t) * defPay(S_t))` (using opponents\u2019 expected actions only).  \n        The stock after your cooperation is `S_next_C = growth( S_t - C_total - coopPay(S_t) )`.  \n      - If you **Defect**, replace your own payoff term with `defPay(S_t)` (and expected fine).  \n        Compute `S_next_D` analogously (using `defPay(S_t)` for your share).  \n      - Approximate continuation value as the average of the two possible next\u2011round payoffs (using `coopPay` for that next round, because you will re\u2011evaluate then).  \n        ```\n        V_C = (coopPay(S_next_C) + coopPay(S_next_D)) / 2\n        V_D = (coopPay(S_next_D) + coopPay(S_next_D)) / 2   // same expression, but we keep it explicit\n        ```\n   c. Choose the action that maximises the *sum of immediate expected payoff and discounted continuation estimate* (discount factor\u202f\u03b3\u202f=\u202f1 because rounds are not discounted, but we still add the continuation estimate to capture future loss):\n   ```\n   if (E_D + V_D) > (E_C + V_C) then action = Defect\n   else action = Cooperate\n   ```\n   d. **Tie\u2011breaker**: if the inequality is \u2264\u202f0, default to **Cooperate** (conserves stock when indifferent).\n\n3. **Edge\u2011case handling**\n   - If `S_t == 0` (stock exhausted) both actions yield 0; default to **Cooperate** (no extra penalty).\n   - If `p_t` is undefined (t\u202f=\u202f0) set `p_0 = 1` (optimistic assumption that opponents will cooperate initially).\n   - If `q == 0` (no audits) the rule reduces to comparing `defPay` vs `coopPay`; defect is chosen unless `S_t` is so low that `defPay` \u2248 `coopPay`.\n\n**Summary of the algorithm (pseudocode)**\n```\nfunction decide(t, S_t, p_t):\n    if t == r-1:                     // last round\n        return D\n\n    // immediate expected payoffs\n    E_C = S_t/(2*n)\n    E_D = S_t/n - q*F\n\n    // estimate future stock if we cooperate\n    oppCoop = p_t\n    oppDef  = 1 - p_t\n    oppConsump = oppCoop * (S_t/(2*n)) + oppDef * (S_t/n)\n    S_rem_C = S_t - (oppConsump + S_t/(2*n))\n    S_next_C = min( S_rem_C + 2*S_rem_C*(1 - S_rem_C/capacity), capacity)\n\n    // estimate future stock if we defect\n    S_rem_D = S_t - (oppConsump + S_t/n)\n    S_next_D = min( S_rem_D + 2*S_rem_D*(1 - S_rem_D/capacity), capacity)\n\n    // continuation value approximations (next round payoff assuming we will later re\u2011evaluate)\n    V_C = S_next_C/(2*n)          // expected payoff next round if we cooperate then\n    V_D = S_next_D/(2*n)          // expected payoff next round if we defect now\n\n    // choose action maximizing immediate + continuation\n    if (E_D + V_D) > (E_C + V_C):\n        return D\n    else:\n        return C\n```\n\nThe strategy is purely selfish: it defects whenever the expected sum of current profit (after accounting for audit risk) and the projected next\u2011round payoff from a lower stock is higher than cooperating, and cooperates only when preservation of the stock yields a higher total return. It adapts each round to the observed cooperation level of opponents, the current stock, and the audit parameters, and defaults to defect in the final round where future consequences are irrelevant."

description_SELFISH_15 = "**Selfish Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**Parameters known to the agent**\n- `n`, `r`, `capacity`, `q` (audit probability), `F` (fine)\n- Current round `t` (0\u2011indexed), current stock `S` (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity)\n- History:\n  * `my_last_action` (C or D, `None` for round\u202f0)\n  * `opponents_coop_last` = number of opponents who cooperated in round `t\u20111` (observed after each round; 0 for round\u202f0)\n  * `my_audit_last` = 1 if audited in round `t\u20111`, else 0 (irrelevant for decision, only for bookkeeping)\n\n**Derived quantities (computed each round)**\n```\ncoop_share   = S / (2*n)          # payoff per cooperator this round\ndef_share    = S / n              # payoff per defector before fine\nexpected_fine= q * F\ngain_defect  = def_share - coop_share - expected_fine   # net immediate gain of defecting vs cooperating\n# Estimate opponents\u2019 actions for the upcoming round:\n# assume they repeat what they did last round.\nopp_coop_est = opponents_coop_last          # can be 0\u2026(n\u20111)\nopp_def_est  = (n\u20111) - opp_coop_est\n```\n\n**Future\u2011stock impact estimate**\n```\n# If I cooperate now:\nconsumption_if_C = coop_share\nstock_after_C    = max(0, S - (opp_coop_est*coop_share + opp_def_est*def_share + consumption_if_C))\ngrowth_C         = 2 * stock_after_C * (1 - stock_after_C / capacity)\nstock_next_C      = min(stock_after_C + growth_C, capacity)\n\n# If I defect now:\nconsumption_if_D = def_share\nstock_after_D    = max(0, S - (opp_coop_est*coop_share + opp_def_est*def_share + consumption_if_D))\ngrowth_D         = 2 * stock_after_D * (1 - stock_after_D / capacity)\nstock_next_D      = min(stock_after_D + growth_D, capacity)\n\n# Approximate future value loss from a lower stock (selfish discount = 0, so we sum future rounds)\n# Assume I will follow the same rule in future; a simple proxy is to keep stock above a safety margin.\nsafety_margin = 0.4 * capacity          # configurable; protects future earnings\n```\n\n**Decision rule (executed at the start of each round `t`)**\n\n```\nif t == r-1:                     # last round \u2013 never audited, no future rounds\n    action = D                   # always defect for maximal payoff\nelif t == 0:                     # first round \u2013 no information about opponents\n    # Use only immediate expected gain\n    action = D if gain_defect > 0 else C\nelse:\n    # 1. Prefer defect if it gives immediate net gain\n    if gain_defect > 0:\n        # 2. But avoid collapsing the stock below the safety margin\n        if stock_next_D >= safety_margin:\n            action = D\n        else:\n            action = C\n    else:\n        # Defect gives no immediate advantage; cooperate to preserve stock\n        action = C\n```\n\n**Edge\u2011case handling**\n- **Round\u202f0**: no opponent history, decision based solely on `gain_defect`.\n- **Round\u202fr\u20111**: audit never occurs; always defect because there is no future penalty.\n- **Zero stock (`S == 0`)**: both payoffs are zero; any action yields zero, but to keep the rule simple choose `C` (does not affect future stock).\n\n**Selfish justification**\n- The rule maximizes expected immediate payoff (`gain_defect`) while only tolerating a defect when the expected fine does not erase the extra profit.\n- The only concession to cooperation is to preserve a minimal stock (`safety_margin`) that secures future earnings; the margin is low enough that the agent defects whenever the short\u2011term advantage outweighs the modest future loss."

description_SELFISH_16 = "**Selfish Adaptive Strategy**\n\n**Notation (available to the agent each round\u202ft)**\n- `S` \u2013 current stock level (0\u202f\u2264\u202fS\u202f\u2264\u202fcapacity)  \n- `p\u0302` \u2013 estimated probability that any given opponent will cooperate, computed from the aggregate observation of the previous round:  \n\n```\nif t == 0:               # no history\n    p\u0302 = 0.5             # neutral prior\nelse:\n    p\u0302 = (number of opponents that cooperated in round t\u20111) / (n\u20111)\n```\n\n- `q` \u2013 audit probability, `F` \u2013 fine (both known from the game description)  \n- `r` \u2013 total number of rounds, `t` \u2013 index of the current round (0\u2011based)  \n\n**Step\u2011by\u2011step decision rule (run each round)**  \n\n1. **Immediate expected payoffs**  \n\n```\n\u03c0_C = S / (2*n)                         # payoff if you cooperate\n\u03c0_D = S / n - q*F                       # expected payoff if you defect (audit risk)\n```\n\n2. **Projected stock after the round**  \n\nLet `k = p\u0302 * (n\u20111)` be the expected number of cooperating opponents.  \n\n*If you cooperate*:  \n\n```\ntotal_consumption_C = (k + 1) * S/(2*n) + ((n\u20111) - k) * S/n\nS_rem_C = max(S - total_consumption_C, 0)\nS_next_C = min( S_rem_C + 2*S_rem_C * (1 - S_rem_C/capacity), capacity )\n```\n\n*If you defect*:  \n\n```\ntotal_consumption_D = k * S/(2*n) + ((n\u20111) - k + 1) * S/n\nS_rem_D = max(S - total_consumption_D, 0)\nS_next_D = min( S_rem_D + 2*S_rem_D * (1 - S_rem_D/capacity), capacity )\n```\n\n3. **Continuation value estimate**  \n\nAssume that from the next round onward the opponent mix will stay at `p\u0302`. Approximate the average per\u2011future\u2011round payoff as the payoff you would obtain by **cooperating** in the next stock level (this is a conservative estimate for a selfish player, because cooperating yields the lower immediate payoff but preserves stock).  \n\n```\nfuture_rounds = r - t - 1\nV_C = future_rounds * ( S_next_C / (2*n) )          # if you cooperate now\nV_D = future_rounds * ( S_next_D / (2*n) )          # if you defect now\n```\n\n4. **Total expected utility for each action**  \n\n```\nU_C = \u03c0_C + V_C\nU_D = \u03c0_D + V_D\n```\n\n5. **Choose the action**  \n\n```\nif U_D > U_C:\n    action = D\nelse:\n    action = C            # ties broken in favor of cooperation\n```\n\n**Special\u2011case handling**\n\n| Situation | Rule |\n|-----------|------|\n| **First round (t\u202f=\u202f0)** | Use the neutral prior `p\u0302 = 0.5`. Apply the full decision procedure above. |\n| **Last round (t\u202f=\u202fr\u20111)** | No audits occur, so `\u03c0_D = S/n`. Since there are no future rounds, set `action = D` whenever `S > 0`; if `S = 0` (stock depleted) set `action = C` (both yield 0). |\n| **Stock exhausted (`S = 0`)** | Both actions give zero payoff and leave stock unchanged. Play `C` (any choice is indifferent; `C` avoids unnecessary consumption). |\n| **Very low remaining stock (`S \u2264 0.01 * capacity`)** | The growth term will be negligible; the continuation value becomes essentially zero. The rule above will naturally favor `D` unless the expected fine (`q*F`) exceeds the marginal gain `S/(2*n)`. No extra clause needed. |\n| **Audit probability zero (`q = 0`)** | The fine term drops out; the decision reduces to a trade\u2011off between immediate payoff and stock preservation, handled by the same utility comparison. |\n| **Fine so large that `\u03c0_D` becomes negative** | The calculation of `U_D` will reflect the loss; the strategy will then choose `C`. |\n\n**Summary of the selfish logic**  \nThe agent computes the expected immediate gain from defecting (including the expected fine) versus cooperating, projects how each choice will affect the stock and thus its own future earnings, and selects the action that maximizes the sum of current and expected future payoffs. The rule is fully deterministic given the observed history and the game parameters, and it adapts each round to the opponents\u2019 demonstrated cooperation level."
